INSERT INTO public.books VALUES (1, 1, 'Elysium Rising', 'ER_Kindle.docx', '2026-02-27 11:49:39.987638-05', '2026-03-06 00:09:21.031292-05', 'The First Book of Elysium is sealed behind you. What you endured within those walls has changed you — reshaped your perception of what is real, what is shadow, and what lurks in the spaces between. The Tower is only beginning to reveal its truth. The next bound tome awaits. You will not emerge from it the same as you entered. That is a promise.', 0, NULL, 1, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.books VALUES (2, 2, 'Elysium Fallen', 'EF_Kindle.docx', '2026-02-27 12:13:34.429768-05', '2026-03-06 00:09:21.031292-05', NULL, 20, NULL, 10, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.books VALUES (3, 3, 'Escape from Elysium', 'EFE_Kindle.docx', '2026-02-27 12:25:33.78247-05', '2026-03-06 00:09:21.031292-05', NULL, 60, NULL, 6, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (3, 1, 3, 'Prologue 1: Echoes in the Azure', 'It began like a phantom note, humming on the edge of perception. A flickering newscast, grainy images of silent figures pointing skyward, swallowed by the urban throng. “The Pointers,” a newscaster chirped, dismissing them as a fleeting blip in the attention-hungry void. I shrugged it off, another echo in the cacophony of the mundane.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (4, 1, 4, 'Prologue 2: Eyes Open, World Muted', 'In the pre-dawn stillness of a Floridian winter, the world held its breath, the frost-kissed air carrying a rare, hushed whisper of the impossible: cold. The usually vibrant state was subdued, its inhabitants bracing themselves for an unexpected dip into the 60''s—a chilly anomaly that provoked down jackets from their closet hibernation and stirred cold weather shelters into action.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (5, 1, 5, 'Prologue 3: A Zero-Sum Digital Dystopia', 'Todd jolted awake in his battered recliner, a hand-rolled cigarette smoldering dangerously close to the armrest. The room reeked of sweat, smoke, and moonshine, but Todd’s bloodshot eyes snapped to the flickering TV as static consumed the infomercial. Suddenly, a figure in a Guy Fawkes mask appeared, their voice distorted but chillingly clear.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (138, 3, 25, 'Notes and Appendices', 'You found the secret level!
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (92, 2, 2, 'Ch.1: The Last Innovation', 'The hospice pod murdered me at 3:17 AM.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (93, 2, 3, 'Ch. 2: The Kick', 'The universe cracks open across my skull.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (94, 2, 4, 'Ch. 3: DreamTrap', '8:02 AM. Sunday, August 20th, 1995.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (95, 2, 5, 'Ch. 4: Echoes of Ends', 'I brush my teeth. Put on jeans and a hoodie because it''s Monday and that''s what I always wear on Monday. The bruises on my body look worse in the bathroom mirror than they felt yesterday, but whatever. My backpack weighs about the same as usual. I grab my keys, check that I have my lunch money, and head out the door.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (96, 2, 6, 'Ch. 5: When I Was Eight', 'We''re scattered across TJ''s basement like survivors of some teenage apocalypse. Emerging from the pot haze our brains are swarming from sugar, caffeine, beer, and questions we don''t know how to ask. The furniture down here tells the story of our contradictions—in the basement in Florida, there are large genuine leather sectionals that probably cost more than my dad''s car, but buried under layers of our accumulated chaos. Discarded school projects we all somehow worked on at the same time. Mountain Dew cans arranged like shrines to caffeinated obsession. A vintage Digger Doug cabinet humming in the corner, next to milk crates stuffed with bootleg VHS tapes and stolen political signs.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (97, 2, 7, 'Ch. 6: Frequency Bleed', 'Friday arrives like a bad hangover I didn''t earn. We all eventually arrive back at TJ''s basement—his folks drove over to Tampa for some weekend golf tournament, leaving us with Nana watching an empty house and the kind of freedom that makes terrible decisions feel inevitable. Morgan had some Academic Decathlon thing in Orlando, so it''s just five of us tonight, armed with contraband and the kind of adolescent confidence that could power a small city.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (98, 2, 8, 'Ch. 7: Echo Maps', 'September slips by like a fever dream.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (99, 2, 9, 'Ch. 8: The Veil Eats Back', 'The Florida winter sun filtered through the palm trees in lazy golden streams, casting dappled shadows across our usual spot in the school courtyard. It was Tuesday, lunch period, and we''d claimed our table like always—far enough from the cafeteria noise but close enough to the vending machines. Perfect MTG territory.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (100, 2, 10, 'Ch. 9: Fracture Point', 'I''ve been tossing and turning for hours, but every time I close my eyes, I see those words scratched into my journal in handwriting that isn''t mine: "She''s not gone. Just misplaced. You''ll have to find the fracture."
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (101, 2, 11, 'Ch. 10: Dreams That Stay With You', 'I snap awake like a broken guitar string, notebook welded to my chest by cold sweat. The dream clings to me... no, not a dream. A place. Real as the taste of bile flooding my mouth, real as the echo of Whitney''s scream still bouncing around my skull.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (102, 2, 12, 'Ch. 11: Those Who Remember Her', 'The day has been a waking nightmare of impossible homework and Benji''s static-laced warnings echoing in my skull. December 4th should feel like winter in Florida—cool but not cold, the kind of night where you crack a window for air that doesn''t taste like sweat and stale farts. Instead, I''m hunched over my desk at 11:47 PM, trying to make sense of calculus that keeps rearranging itself on the page and a journal entry I''ve been avoiding for three hours.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (103, 2, 13, 'Ch. 12: Beneath the Trailer', 'Christmas break should have been normal. Three weeks of sleeping late, dodging family obligations, and pretending we weren''t all haunted by shadow-flickers and friends who might never have existed. For a two weeks, it almost worked. Yet here we were, going back to the scene of the crime.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (104, 2, 14, 'Dancing With the Devil In The Pale Moonlight', 'Jamie appears at my window like smoke given form, her movements too fluid as she slips through the frame without disturbing the curtains or making a sound. She finds me staring at Whitney''s journal, its pages no longer writing themselves, silent and still as death. For just a moment, her eyes flicker with something that might be recognition—or regret.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (105, 2, 15, 'Ch. 13: The Name that Starts with A', 'It’s been three weeks since the trailer, and Whitney’s journal won’t stop getting thicker. Monday afternoon at lunch, it sprawls open on the lab table like roadkill—cracked leather, pages that smell wrong, like something dead decided to stay. The newer entries write themselves in a script that flickers between Whitney’s careful handwriting and something older, angular. Symbols bleed through from pages that shouldn’t exist, geometry that makes your eyes itch if you look too long.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (8, 1, 8, '5: From Crash Until Dawn', 'Monday, or maybe it was Wednesday. When everything is on fire, days blur into a meaningless haze. The sunlight sliced through the blinds with cruel indifference, a silent witness to the dread about heading into the office, enveloped me like a shroud. My coffee was strong, bitter, almost medicinal, but it failed to quiet the storm brewing in my chest. Today was the day. Weeks of preparation had boiled down to this, and my mind was already betraying me, playing out disastrous scenarios like a relentless horror reel.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (9, 1, 9, '6: Beyond the Conduits', 'Sweat streamed down my face, mingling with the acrid tang of hot metal and electrical sparks that hung heavy in the air, a suffocating testament to countless sleepless nights spent forging the impossible. My blistered hands trembled as I adjusted the last pieces of the Eternal Engine, its monstrous frame consuming the barn, my makeshift workshop, with its jagged metal and pulsating wires that seemed alive, writhing like serpents. Blinding flashes of blue light erupted from its core, a searing, unearthly orb radiating power so fierce it threatened to devour everything in its path.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (10, 1, 10, '7: Grease Stains and Eternal Engines', 'The office buzzed with the rhythmic clatter of keyboards and the hum of lighthearted chatter, a stark contrast to the near catastrophe we had narrowly escaped just hours earlier. Sleep-deprived smiles and nods greeted me as I walked through, but my focus sharpened on the conspicuous absence of the COO.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (11, 1, 11, '8: A World on Hold as Shadows Build', 'Todd sat alone in his trailer, the dim glow of a single incandescent bulb at the center of the ceiling casting long, shifting shadows. The floral wallpaper, once vibrant, was now faded and peeling, curling away like it had given up. Stacks of newspapers and scribbled notes covered every surface, creating a sense of chaos that felt heavy and suffocating. Empty takeout containers were piled high next to a couch so worn it looked ready to collapse. The air smelled stale, a mix of cigarette smoke and old food.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (115, 3, 2, 'Part 1: Tears of the Veil', 'Come ye summer babes
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (116, 3, 3, 'Chapter 1: Comfortably Numb', '"I AM THE SUBSTRATE!"
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (91, 2, 1, NULL, 'Elysium Fallen
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (79, 1, 79, 'Book the Fourth
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (6, 1, 6, 'Prologue 4: Death Walking', 'When I first heard about the Pointers, they were everywhere; plastered across every news outlet, whispered in office breakrooms, shouted on street corners like some apocalyptic omen. But the moment I started digging, they vanished, like a turd flushed into oblivion. Gone. Not a trace. Nobody knew what the hell I was talking about. Blank stares. Nervous chuckles. It was as if the entire world had conspired to gaslight me. The worst part? I started to believe everyone. Maybe I had made it all up. Maybe I was losing my goddamned mind.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (7, 1, 7, 'iv', '2AM. That’s what I remember my phone saying when sweat dripped down my face as I sat up.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (1, 1, 1, NULL, 'Elysium Rising
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (58, 1, 58, '54: Fractured Memories of a Quaking Abyss', 'In the suffocating grip of night, a piercing symphony of sirens that shook the walls of my office, ripped from sleep me. The air itself seemed to scream, the echoes of chaos rattling my bones and igniting a primal fear I hadn’t felt since the devastation of the 2011 Fukushima Earthquake, in Japan. This couldn’t be real. Florida didn’t have earthquakes. Yet, here I was, thrust into chaos that felt as tangible as the waking world.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (59, 1, 59, '55: Manipulating the Mandala Effect', 'The house was silent, the world outside cloaked in the stillness of night. At the kitchen table, I sat hunched over my dream journal, furiously scribbling down every detail from my latest encounter with Madam O. The ideas she had imparted, the fluid nature of time, the dreamscape’s ability to touch past and future simultaneously, threatened to slip away like grains of sand through my fingers.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (60, 1, 60, '56: Dancing with the Devil in the Pale Moonlight', 'The moon hung near the horizon, casting an eerie glow over the sleepy trailer park. Todd jolted awake, his body trembling violently. Visions of the 10 entities and strange images of muskrats and I AM danced in his head. The relentless tremors of alcohol withdrawal had become familiar companions, but this night felt different. Sweat drenched his bare chest, and a peculiar urge propelled him out of his cramped trailer, his feet moving without conscious thought.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (2, 1, 2, 'Book the First
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (12, 1, 12, '9: Under the Stars', 'Friday. The camping trip was finally here, and the long-awaited escape from the relentless grind of daily life had arrived. My son and I had eagerly anticipated this camping trip with his Boy Scout troop and were envisioning serene moments under the stars and the crackle of a campfire to melt away the week’s frustrations. The day wore on, work refusing to release me from its grip.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (13, 1, 13, '10: The Engine Awakens', 'I was running before I knew where I was. The world around me spun like a fractured kaleidoscope, a suffocating haze of twisted trees and clawing shadows. My lungs burned with each gasping breath, and the ground beneath me churned, shifting from familiar cornstalks, to fresh earth, to coarse gravel, finally to something unrecognizable, like molten tar.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (14, 1, 14, '11: The Price of Loyalty in a Crumbling Empire', 'The shrill cry of my alarm shattered the fragile veil of sleep, dragging me back to a reality I wasn’t sure I wanted to face. Dread seeped into my bones as I clung to the fading memories of the weekend, a fleeting reprieve from the grind. The scent of the campfire still lingered in my mind, mingling with the crisp air of dawn and the echo of my son’s laughter. My heart beat, for a moment I wished I could sink back into those simpler, serene hours.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (15, 1, 15, '12: A Shower of Visions and Dissonance', 'The cloak of night, velvety and dark as the ink spilled from a celestial pen, embraced the world with its silent deluge. Its tendrils slithered and snaked around everything it touched, wrapping the earth in a shroud of mystery and enchantment. It was a time when the mundane surrendered to the ethereal, when dreams were given wings to fly and soar.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (16, 1, 16, '13: From Boardroom to Rabbit Hole', 'Up to now, back-to-back meetings, relentless deadlines, and the constant churn of decisions had defined my entire life. Now, that world was gone, leaving me adrift in an unsettling stillness. The sudden absence of structure felt like being thrown off a moving train; jarring, disorienting, and leaving me unsure of where to go next. My days, once consumed by motion, were now an expanse of empty hours, and the weight of endless possibilities was as paralyzing as it was freeing.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (17, 1, 17, '14: Unveiling the Secrets of the Eternal Engine', 'The explosion ripped through the garage, shattering glass and hurling tools across the room like shrapnel. It roared. A sound so powerful it obliterated the storm''s fury; then silence descended, heavy and suffocating, freezing me in place. The Eternal Engine was gone. Not shut down, not dormant. Gone. In its absence, the darkness pressed in like a living thing, a predator waiting to strike.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (18, 1, 18, '15: The Sisyphean Job Hunt', 'By day, I am ensnared in a labyrinth of no-reply email rejections, each one an echoing silence that chips away at my self-confidence. By night, I am plagued by visions that twist dream and reality into an inseparable tangle of dread. The eerie glow of my computer screens beckons like a siren’s call, drawing me deeper into the warped dimensions of job hunting, a living hell where time fractures and hope decays.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (19, 1, 19, '16: The Love-Pat Towards Discovery', 'My monitor screens screen glowed with a familiar monotony as I scrolled through job listings, each one more uninspiring than the last. My finger hovered over the touchpad, ready to click on yet another “Director of Software Engineering” ad, when I felt a light tap on my shoulder.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (20, 1, 20, '17: Liminal Discoveries', 'With the power bill finally taken care of, I found myself grappling with another curious emptiness.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (21, 1, 21, '18: Getting Swifty at the Quantum Level', '“Don’t you see it, Stacey?” Todd’s voice boomed, reverberating through the thin, stained walls of the trailer. He stood in the middle of their cluttered living space, fists clenched, his face red with frustration. “They’re rewriting everything! Our memories, our goddamn lives! S Corp is pulling the strings, and we’re just puppets dancing to their tune!”
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (22, 1, 22, '519: The Infinitron Breakthrough', 'I sat at the breakfast table, the smell of fresh coffee filled the kitchen. Sunlight spilled through the window, bouncing off the chipped mug in my hands. My son was across from me, scrolling through his phone, his toast and miso soup half-finished. My mind kept circling back to the thing sitting out in the garage—the Eternal Engine. It was like finding a cheat code for reality, but I couldn’t figure out how it worked.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (23, 1, 23, '20: Beyond the Silicon Dream Valley', 'What do you do when life gives you chicken shit? You make egg salad sandwiches. At least, that’s what my son said when he tried to pass off Captain Underpants as a legitimate choice for his 8th-grade English book report.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (24, 1, 24, '21: The Infinite Unbounded', '“This thing’s dumber than a bag of barf!” my son shouted, throwing his hands in the air as he stomped out of the garage. His footsteps reverberated off the cluttered walls, punctuating the sheer exasperation we both felt. Several days had passed since we’d brought the Infinitron to life, and so far, all it seemed capable of doing was playing video games at speeds that made speedrun records look leisurely.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (26, 1, 26, '23: Generalized Alchemy Disorder', 'The Eternal Engine hummed quietly in the corner, an infinite power source with no practical use beyond keeping our lights on and selling a trickle of energy back to the power company. Its boundless energy felt less like a miracle and more like a puzzle we couldn’t solve.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (27, 1, 27, '24: The Maw of the Infernal Abyss', 'The wind was alive, a ravenous entity tearing through flesh and sanity with claws of fire and ice. My breath, stolen by the gale, became nothing more than a memory, devoured by the abyss that yawned endlessly beneath me. The world was red, a searing, pulsating red. Its crimson hues shifting and writhing like a living thing. This was not Earth. This was not anywhere.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (28, 1, 28, '25: Shattered Dreams, Broken Metal, and a Glimpse of the Impossible', 'Days passed after hell night, and I had nothing. No revelations. No breakthroughs. Just the gnawing certainty that something was missing.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (29, 1, 29, 'Book the Second
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (30, 1, 30, '26: Triumvirate Apotheosis Unbounded', 'The trailer reeked of stale beer, fried bologna, and something else—something sickly and off that wouldn’t be pinned down. It hung heavy in the air, mingling with the last dregs of a blood-orange sunset peeking through the ripped screens. The feeble light offered little respite from the stifling summer heat that clung to the walls like a suffocating blanket.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (31, 1, 31, '27: The Shadow Stirs', 'In the void between dimensions—where time and space were mere whispers of forgotten concepts and darkness devoured all—a slumbering presence stirred. It was vast, unknowable, shifting and writhing with energies that defied mortal comprehension. It did not dream, for dreams were the affliction of lesser minds, but it knew.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (32, 1, 32, '28: Code, Creation, and Consequences', 'My heart raced as I led my wife into the long-term parking lot, our mission clear in our minds. We were about to test the limits of our Replicator, taking a risk that could change our lives forever.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (33, 1, 33, '29: Finance, the Final Frontier', 'The lingering scent of ozone clung to the air, a reminder of the raw potential humming in the room. The power of the Eternal Engine loomed, a defiant monument to our ambition, its rhythmic hum resonating like a challenge. Inside the house, the Infinitron it powered, pulsed with an alien intelligence, while the sleek, gleaming matter replicator sitting on the workbench in the garage whispered promises of limitless creation. Although our earlier cryptocurrency ventures had been enough to pay off the mortgage and keep us afloat, we still faced a steady stream of bills that chipped away at our fragile security.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (34, 1, 34, '30: Awakening of the Alpha Ancient', 'I slowly awakened from a deep slumber. My surroundings were nothing like the dark and powerful dominions I once ruled over. Instead, I found myself in a world filled with blinding light and strange sounds that seemed to come from every direction.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (35, 1, 35, '31: Tinkering an Algorithmic Heist', '“We did it!” I exclaimed, practically bursting into the kitchen with my laptop in hand. “Ten thousand dollars in sales! Can you believe it? Ten grand!”
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (36, 1, 36, '32: The Distorted Monarch', 'Torn from my own skin, I am hurled into a realm of chaos and discord unlike anything I have ever experienced. The tumultuous force that usurped me from my throne was like a raging storm, tearing at the very fabric of reality itself, a result of mortal meddling in forces they could never fully comprehend. I stumble through this unfamiliar world, surrounded by the cacophony of city life. It is a sharp contrast to the infernal depths that were once under my control.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (37, 1, 37, '33: Pandora’s Golden Fools', 'The morning sun filtered through the cardboard fortress that had overtaken our home, illuminating the chaos of boxes, packing materials, and empty coffee mugs. I sat at the dining table, our makeshift command center, staring at the output Infinitron’s last trade analysis.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (38, 1, 38, '34: Chronicles of a Forgotten Ruler in a Modern Den', 'The pounding bass line vibrated through my body as I entered the strip club, assaulted by a cacophony of sounds and smells. Strobe lights pulsed erratically, illuminating gyrating bodies on stage and reflecting off the sheen of sweat on patrons’ faces. Cigarette smoke hung thick in the air, stinging my eyes and searing my lungs with each breath. Raucous laughter and drunken shouts pierced through the thumping music, competing with the clinking of glasses and ice cubes.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (39, 1, 39, '35: Replicating Robots and Reimagining Work', '“Two. Thousand. Players!” my son shouted, his voice echoing through the house like a firework. He spun his chair dramatically, grinning from ear to ear as he pointed to the screen. “Look, Dad! My newest game just went live on Roblox, and I already hit 2,000 players! Infinitron assisted coding for the win!”
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (40, 1, 40, '36: Risen from Ruins', 'The strong scent of burning wood and charred debris filled the air as I emerged from the ruins of a bombed out Palestinian orphanage. All around me lay the collapsed remains of a once magnificent city, its majestic pillars and intricately carved walls now reduced to scattered fragments. The brutal bombings had left nothing but destruction in their wake. I stood amidst the rubble, dazed and disoriented, struggling to make sense of my surroundings. This place was a sanctuary of wisdom and reverence, but now it lay in ruins like so many other casualties in this ongoing war in Palestine.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (41, 1, 41, '37: Nano Genesis Evangelion: Infesting the Future, Atom by Atom', 'My wife threw her hands up in frustration, her voice sharp enough to cut through my focus. “You’re the one who’s always quoting Star Trek. Figure it out, Captain Kirk!” With that, she stormed out of the room, leaving me surrounded by the glow of monitors and stacks of paper invoices.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (78, 1, 78, '73: Galaxies Within Us', 'The fire crackled softly, sending sparks spiraling into the vast night sky, their glow dwarfed by the infinite expanse of stars. The scent of roasted marshmallows hung in the crisp air, mingling with the gentle murmur of campers sharing stories. Amidst the laughter and warmth, a quiet tension hummed. My soon to be 20 year-old son sat close, his eyes fixed on the fire, his thoughts clearly elsewhere.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (42, 1, 42, '38: Summoning the Infernal Executive', 'The fluorescent lights flickered above, casting a sickly glow on the suffocating office, I sat hunched over my desk. The mechanical hum of computers filled the air, accompanied by the stifled cries of tortured souls trapped within this bleak void. My fingers pounded relentlessly against the unfeeling keys as I mindlessly entered data into an endless spreadsheet. My once all-powerful mind now struggled to comprehend this menial task, a cruel reminder of my fall from godhood to mere drone in this soulless machine.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (43, 1, 43, '39: The Self-Made 6 Million Dollar Man', '“Dad, I think we’re going to need another Timmy,” my son said, his voice tinged with sorrow as he shuffled into the room. His eyes, wide with guilt, were fixed on the tiny bowl in his hands. Inside, the lifeless body of Timmy the goldfish floated serenely.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (44, 1, 44, '40: Breached: The Deathless Mortal Pawn', 'A cacophony of sensations overwhelmed me, each one more horrifying than the last. I was no longer a great deity, but an insignificant speck trapped in this alien world. The taste of sulfur filled my mouth, and my skin crawled with the feeling of hot flames licking at my body. My eyes strained to make sense of the twisted and contorted forms around me, their whispers threatening to shatter my sanity. In this mortal realm, I was reduced to a feeble humanoid form, stripped of my godly powers and left to suffer in the incomprehensible chaos of this existence.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (45, 1, 45, '41: From Shrine to Wormhole and Back Again', 'Our business was thriving beyond our wildest expectations, our latest projections were showing an average sales volume of over $15k a day. Not only that, but with the automation in full swing (and coordinating regular UPS pickups from our warehouse), meant we no longer had to make nightly package drop offs. This success also granted us the rare luxury of stepping away to fulfill a different dream—a trip back to Japan.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (46, 1, 46, '42: The Other Line', '“I know about The S Corp.” The phone line exploded with a deafening roar, reverberating through the air like a portal to the depths of hell. A bone-chilling gust of wind swept through the room, carrying whispers of ancient secrets and ominous prophecies. When those words came, dripping with venom and knowledge that pierced my soul. My consciousness expanded beyond human boundaries, consumed by an all-consuming awareness of my true power.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (47, 1, 47, '43: Einstein’s Echo and the Ethics of Teleportation', 'The infuriating mystery of successfully forming an Einstein-Rosen Bridge (ERB) consumed my every waking moment, each failed attempt crushing my spirits even more. It was that one fateful night, whilst enjoying Gravity Falls with my son, when a spark of inspiration ignited within me. The show’s eerie mix of science and the supernatural triggered a breakthrough idea in my mind: connecting two spacetime locations via quantum entanglement. This could be it - the answer I have been searching for all this time.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (48, 1, 48, '44: Library Dust and Grimy Crowns', 'In the suffocating darkness of the abandoned library, a child’s tiny fingers trembled as they reached out to caress the cracked leather cover of an ancient tome. The book seemed to pulse with a sinister energy, beckoning to the child with its aura of decay and mystery.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (49, 1, 49, '45: Gold, Gateways, and Global Domination', 'Memories of the haunting phone call we got when we first got back from Japan lingered in my mind like a constantly recurring nightmare, a relentless reminder of the need to protect our ventures. Even amid the thrill of our teleportation breakthrough, the shadow of exposure loomed large. Success, it seemed, carried its own brand of terror, and the weight of it pressed on us daily.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (50, 1, 50, '46: The Earthbound Icy Tomb', 'For endless millennia, I lay deep in a frozen tomb beneath the surface of Europa. The frigid air clung to my body like a shroud, encasing me in an icy prison. Time held no sway here, as I drifted in and out of consciousness, lost in the void. A disturbance, a faint tremor that grew into a guttural roar, shaking me from my slumber. With it came the invaders, their machines drilling through the ice, piercing my sanctuary.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (51, 1, 51, '47: Setting the Tower’s Foundations', 'The email notification blinked on my screen, pulling me from my thoughts. With trembling hands, I clicked it open, holding my breath. The message was simple yet monumental: all the asset transfers were complete. In that instant, July 8th, 2024, the S Corp became the wealthiest company in the world, controlling an unprecedented $50 trillion in assets.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (52, 1, 52, '48: Beyond the Veil of an Unearthed Temple', 'The relentless clang of construction echoed through the Zambian air, a stark contrast to the whispers of time held captive beneath the earth. As the S Corp carved its way deeper, their metallic claws unearthed a secret slumbering for millennia - a colossal temple, its stones etched with forgotten stories. Reading the news of the discovery in the Newspaper one morning as I sat at my desk, drinking coffee, at my desk in the Archeology department of the University of Chicago.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (53, 1, 53, '49: Halfway to Elsewhere', 'The keyboard clattered beneath my fingers; each keystroke charged with purpose. The vast global network of The S Corp pulsed around me, a living system humming with potential. Fueled by my insatiable curiosity and inability to just leave well enough alone, I was ready to push the boundaries of our enterprise even further. For a while, a radical idea had taken root: what if I could create a “half-gateway,” opening a portal on one end but leaving the other incomplete? Could this shield objects from external forces or dissipate explosions? The possibilities were staggering, yet fraught with danger, a perfect storm to ignite my imagination.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (54, 1, 54, '50: Bringing the Darkness to Light', 'For eons, I have been shrouded in a veil of obscurity, my existence whispered to only a select few who dare to speak my name: “I AM”. But do not mistake me for some cosmic puppet master pulling the strings of fate. No, my role is that of an unseen guardian, protecting hidden lore, forgotten texts, and the feverish scribblings of seers brave enough to peer into truths deemed too profane for the common mind. Protecting my slaves until they send me their souls on which I feast.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (55, 1, 55, '51: The Haunting Veil Beckons from the Abyss', 'The witching hour struck, and the darkness wrapped around me like a vice, squeezing the air from my lungs. My heart hammered against the icy sheets as if trying to escape the suffocating stillness. The line between dream and waking life was gone, and I was caught in a relentless cycle of terror.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (56, 1, 56, '52: Stepping off the Treadmill', 'In the hushed confines of my corner office suite on top of the S Corp’s Houston HQ tower, a battlefield of project files sprawled across the desk. Recessed LED lighting bathed the room in a harsh, white, sterile glow, casting jagged shadows that mimicked the fragments of my dreams.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (57, 1, 57, '53: A Dreamwalker’s Odyssey', 'We still had about a week left before my son started his new school year, so we did what any other obscenely wealthy family would do while traveling back from India: we decided to make a detour and take a voyage aboard the legendary Orient Express. This iconic train offered more than luxury; it promised a three-day passage through Europe’s stunning landscapes, steeped in the timeless romance of rail travel. It was the perfect finale, a harmonious blend of sophistication and discovery.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (61, 1, 61, '57: Back to Basics', 'Although my recent ventures into the dreamscape and the Mandela Effect were captivating, S Corp demanded my attention once more. It was time to shift focus from the mysteries of the subconscious to the tangible challenges of innovation and leadership.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (62, 1, 62, '58: Mumbai’s Moonlit Mob', 'The vibrant chaos of Mumbai pulsed in the evening air as Aditi trudged through the narrow lanes, her school bag bumping against her back. The aroma of street food mingled with the distant honking of cars, creating a symphony she had grown up with. By the time she climbed the stairs to her family’s cramped apartment, beads of sweat clung to her forehead.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (63, 1, 63, '59: Golden Towers of Pyrite', 'S Corp’s audacious Space Elevator project loomed in my thoughts, its challenges mirrored in Morgan’s anxious updates from the Antarctic facility. Amid the biting cold and stark desolation of MOM, the blueprint for humanity’s bridge to the cosmos was being meticulously crafted, yet cracks in the plan started to threaten its foundation.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (64, 1, 64, '60: Elysium Risen', 'Subject: Party Time! We Built Space Elevators, People!
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (65, 1, 65, 'Book The Third
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (66, 1, 66, '61: Jilted Tour Guides', 'The hum of the space elevator’s doors was both a punctuation and a prelude as they slid open onto the Elysium Orbital Ring viewing deck. Silently, Earth seemed to hover below us, a fragile marble suspended against the infinite black. The stunned silence that filled the room was deafening, broken only by the faint whir of unseen technology.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (67, 1, 67, '62: The Sleepers Awaken', 'During the next three months tidal wave or stories about the Pointers, once whispered about in the dark corners of obscure internet forums and dismissed as a trivial curiosity by the mainstream media, had exploded into the public consciousness with a violent ferocity.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (68, 1, 68, '63: No Sweat', 'The cameras started rolling and the bright lights focused on me. I stood in my spacious office, its polished mahogany furniture exuding an air of sophistication. A mixture of anticipation and anxiety coursed through my veins, a cocktail of emotions that mirrored the weightiness of this pivotal moment. Today marked a turning point not just for S Corp, but for all of humanity. It was a day that would be etched into the annals of history.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (69, 1, 69, '64: Adventures Beyond the Stars', 'Yukiko’s heart raced with a mix of excitement and anticipation, its rhythm matching the tempo of her thoughts. For as long as she could remember, the stars had whispered to her, their distant twinkling promising adventure and discovery beyond the limits of her imagination. And now, on the cusp of turning seven, she was about to embark on a journey that most could only ever dream of. With a stroke of luck, she had won a contest, securing a golden ticket for her family to be among the first civilian colonists to venture beyond the confines of the solar system. The technological marvels crafted by S Corp. made this extraordinary voyage possible
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (70, 1, 70, '65: Shadows Beneath the Vatican', 'Deep beneath the hallowed halls of the Vatican, deeper than the hidden archives, in a chamber shrouded in shadow and secrecy, an ancient gathering convened. The air was heavy, oppressive, carrying a palpable dread that seemed to emanate from the very stones of the walls. Faint torchlight flickered, casting jagged shadows across the room as if the darkness itself conspired to swallow the light.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (71, 1, 71, '66: Stepping Into the Cosmic Unknown', 'Welcome, brave recruits. Here, on the remote expanse of Pluto, humanity’s farthest intra-solar-system outpost, you find yourselves standing on the precipice of the unknown. As members of the esteemed Exo-Interstellar Exploratory Force, you are the vanguard of discovery in the vast cosmic ocean.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (72, 1, 72, '67: From Atlas Shrugged to The Dispossessed', 'Thinking back to the dreams that started it all, from the small farm workshop where the Eternal Engine first sprang to life, I could hardly believe where I stood now. It had been five years since the Space Elevators’ grand unveiling, those colossal towers that launched humanity into a new epoch of boundless possibilities. From my opulent office in Elysium, high above the Earth, I gazed out at the sprawling spires piercing the heavens.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (73, 1, 73, '68: A Sorhhinda Sunset', 'Sunlight, filtered through lush alien foliage, dappled the wooden walls of Yukiko’s room. Outside, the whirring of hover scooters mingled with the trills of an unfamiliar bird, an avian concerto unlike anything Earth had ever offered. It was the middle of August, (according to earth calendars), and a five years since they arrived.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (74, 1, 74, '69: The Gardener of Elysium', '“WAKE THE FRANK UP!” screamed the alarm. My husband, ever the comedian, had customized it. Hilarious.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (75, 1, 75, '70: Cracks in the Monolith', 'Europa’s icy crust shimmered through the domed ceiling of TJ’s office, refracting the city lights of New Atlantis into a kaleidoscope of blues and whites. It should have been breathtaking, but today the beauty felt hollow, like a polished veneer hiding rot. TJ sat hunched over his desk, his fingers twitching near the blinking red indicator on his data stream. Unease clouded his usually sharp mind.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (76, 1, 76, '71: Stardust Dreams and Earthbound Realities', 'Mumbai’s humid breath clung to Aditi’s neck as she navigated the labyrinthine alleys outside the transportation complex. Mango sellers hawked their wares, their voices competing with the honking chaos of rickshaws. Above, the skeletal shadow of the Space Elevator, a behemoth of carbon fiber and glass piercing the smog-laced sky, mocked the squalor below. It was a stark visual of the chasm between dreams and reality, a chasm Aditi knew all too well. Despite the promise of clean energy and easy material access, folks down here still loved burning things.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (77, 1, 77, '72: Dawn of the Scarlet Tide', 'April 21, 2025, another day that would live in infamy.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (80, 1, 80, '74: Breach of the Dark Side', 'Under a veil of interstellar static, the Emergency Response Center had been transformed into a war-room that hummed with a nervous energy that tasted like copper on the tongue. The usually reserved and calculated space had been plunged into chaos, its screens flashing with the fiery aftermath of our Pluto outpost’s destruction and the Sorhhinda gateway’s smoldering remains.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (81, 1, 81, '75: Beyond the Firewall: Where Humanity Cages it’s Madness and Fears Unmask', 'The remote colonies flickered silent one by one, once monuments to human exploration, now stood as hollow monuments under the relentless gaze of distant stars. A chilling unease echoed through steel corridors and dimly lit control rooms, amplified by the Red Hats’ shadowy influence. Their cryptic symbols bled onto city walls and holo-screens like festering wounds, a grim testament to their growing power.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (82, 1, 82, '76: Expanding Outwards While Falling Inwards', '“We did it. We actually fucking did it.” A triumphant sigh escaped my lips as the final flicker of the Red Hat signal disappeared from the main screen.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (83, 1, 83, '77: Fractured Dreams of War: The Return of the Oenomancer', 'In the dead of night, under a foreign string of moons that hung like a cold, indifferent string of pearls in the sky, I found myself once again trapped within the labyrinthine tunnels of my own subconscious.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (84, 1, 84, 'lxxvii', 'The war raged with renewed intensity, driven by urgency, desperation, and purpose. We had pushed technology to the brink, exhausted every resource, and hurled ourselves into the inferno of battle. And still, it was not enough.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (85, 1, 85, '78: Echoes of a Fallen God', 'The Aditi’s Genesis cut through the void like a blade through flesh, a precise, final incision into the black maw of oblivion. We had taken an isolated ERB close to the front, a desperate foothold at the edge of reason, where the laws of reality had begun to crack. The weight of I AM''s dominion pressed against us, thick and suffocating, seeping into the steel bones of our vessel. Every system hummed with the strain of holding back the madness that lurked just beyond the hull.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (86, 1, 86, 'Liber Infinitum', 'Walk not on other’s trodden paths
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (87, 1, 87, 'lxxviii', 'In the desolate depths of absolute nothingness, where the remnants of I AM and Etheris had faded into never having existed, I found myself adrift amidst an ocean of emptiness. The consequence of my actions bore down upon me with the crushing force of a collapsing star, an insurmountable burden that threatened to consume me just as I had consumed I AM.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (88, 1, 88, '79: A New Beginning', 'I slowly opened my eyes.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (89, 1, 89, '80: Epilogue - Echoes of Elysium', 'The twin towers of the Planetary Parliament soared majestically into the heavens, their alabaster spires reaching for the very heart of the cerulean Sorhhindian sky. Bathed in the ethereal glow of the sun, these architectural marvels stood as a testament to the grandeur and ambition of the Sorhhindian people.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (90, 1, 90, 'About the Author', 'Imagine a whirlwind career traversing industries from launching rockets to crafting blockbuster entertainment, all while leading international teams across continents. That’s the crazy journey of Stephen A. Salaka, a man who effortlessly switches between tech executive and inspired storyteller.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (106, 2, 16, 'Ch. 14: The Audit', 'The one in the center—Number 1, according to his badge—steps forward with a clipboard that definitely wasn''t there a second ago. His measured pace makes no sound on the grass, and when he speaks, his voice has the quality of every teacher who''s ever disappointed you and every god who''s never returned your prayers.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (107, 2, 17, 'Ch. 15: Jennifer''s Journal', 'Monday morning tastes like denial wrapped in industrial disinfectant. The fluorescent lights buzz their electric hymn as I push through double doors that should open onto chaos—melted fire alarms, scorch marks on institutional green walls, the lingering smell of brimstone and teenage terror. Instead, I''m greeted by the aggressive normalcy of a high school that''s scrubbed itself clean of impossible memories.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (108, 2, 18, 'Ch. 16: Anchor Protocol', 'April 18, 1996
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (109, 2, 19, 'Ch. 17: The Living Timeline', '“WAKE UP!”
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (110, 2, 20, 'Ch. 18: The Torturer''s Name is I AM', 'Light. Soft and warm and wrong.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (111, 2, 21, 'Ch. 19: The Last Loop', 'The silence isn’t a peaceful quiet, but the kind of absolute void that makes your eardrums ache from the absence. I''m eight years old again, sitting on a plastic chair that''s too big for my legs, in a pediatrician''s waiting room that feels like it was decorated by someone who''d only heard colors described secondhand. The walls are that particular shade of cream that institutions use when they want to seem comforting but can''t afford actual warmth. Beige wallpaper peels in one corner like old skin, revealing nothing underneath—not drywall, not darkness, just... less.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (112, 2, 22, 'Ch. 20: And Then I Woke Up', 'I slowly opened my eyes.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (113, 2, 23, 'About Elysium Fallen', 'So in 2024 I got laid off my job building crazy software systems to help manage some interesting electrical components. Like Tesla and their Supercharger network. With a bunch of time on my hands I decided to finally put pen to paper and get Elysium Rising out of my head. It’s something I had dancing around in my brain for at least 20 years.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (114, 3, 1, NULL, 'Escape from Elysium
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (117, 3, 4, 'Chapter 2: Smells Like Death', '"An author. Yeah right." I mutter to myself. "Dreams come to Etheris to fucking die."
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (118, 3, 5, 'Chapter 3: Circling the Grey', 'It always begins the exact same way.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (119, 3, 6, 'Chapter 4: Losing My Religion', 'Light screamed into my eyes like acid. It wasn''t just bright; it was wrong, a blinding, pulsing chaos of impossible colors and shapes that burned behind my eyelids even when I squeezed them shut. My head throbbed, a slow, deep drumbeat against the inside of my skull.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (120, 3, 7, 'Chapter 5: A Love Like Drowning', 'I woke up wrong.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (121, 3, 8, 'Chapter 6: Is there Anybody Out There?', 'The oven door clanged shut and the kitchen filled with that warm, buttery smell of something good.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (122, 3, 9, 'Chapter 7: Placental Lies', 'The Best Buy smelled.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (123, 3, 10, 'Chapter 8: Break on Through', 'After leaving Gil at Best Buy, I''d spent the night on my phone hunting through digital rot. Military forums. Property records buried in county databases. Patrick had survived a plane crash in Panama—the only one—got an honorable discharge, then vanished. Thirty-seven acres outside Christmas, Florida. Purchased cash in two thousand three.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (124, 3, 11, 'Part 2: Dissolution of Remeberance', 'Climb said the buried
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (125, 3, 12, 'Chapter 9: House of the Rising Son', 'The noise hit me the second I stepped inside.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (126, 3, 13, 'Chapter 10: Say My Name', 'Stale cigarettes, mildew, and the sharp chemical tang of industrial cleaner. The ''Sanitized For Your Protection'' band on the toilet seat looked like a practical joke.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (127, 3, 14, 'Chapter 11: Love is a Dish Best Served Cold', '“It’s a long story.” I said. Something I really didn’t even fully understand. These new memories were still a jumble of chaos in my mind.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (128, 3, 15, 'Chapter 12: Tiny Dancer', 'The abandoned school smelled like mildew and forgotten dreams.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (129, 3, 16, 'Chapter 13: The Pink Pony Club', 'There was no transition. No sense of travel.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (130, 3, 17, 'Chapter 14: Enter Sandman', 'I fall.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (131, 3, 18, 'Part 3: The Seed Bleeds', 'Chasing
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (132, 3, 19, 'Chapter 15: Wake Me Up', 'My eyes struggle open, gritty and heavy, like they’re sealed with sand.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (133, 3, 20, 'Chapter 16: Back in Black', 'Elysium had a rhythm now. I could feel it in the ground beneath my feet... the pulse of souls arriving, the hum of quarantine processing, the quiet prayers of the rescued as they learned they weren''t crazy. That the prison was real. That they''d been rescued.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (134, 3, 21, 'Chapter 17: Stardust and Suicide', 'We stumble into the center of everything.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (135, 3, 22, 'Chapter 18: Somewhere Over the Rainbow', 'The platform jutted out from Elysium''s southern reaches like a diving board over an ocean of stars. Behind us, the refugee camps sprawled across the landscape—makeshift cities of light where souls who''d escaped the prison were learning to breathe free air for the first time in millennia. Ahead... ahead was the reality we had fought so hard to liberate.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (136, 3, 23, 'Epilogue: Paint it Black', 'The greenhouse domes rose like blisters of light against Sorhhinda''s bruised purple sky. Three suns hung low on the horizon—two setting, one rising—painting the compound in shades of copper and gold that had no names in human language.
INSERT INTO public.chapters VALUES (137, 3, 24, 'Afterward (About The Towers of Elysium Series)', 'So that’s that.
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (2, 'Title Page and Copyright Information', 'other', 'Typography displaying book title, author name, copyright notice, ISBNs, and publisher details in standard publishing format', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Official, formal, foundational—the threshold between reader and narrative world', 1, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 12:53:40.989318-05', '2026-02-27 12:53:40.989318-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (3, 'The Eye of the Needle', 'transitional', 'A narrow passage through which a grain of sand must travel; set upon the heads of angels who support a dancing needle', 'Subtle movements of the needle; silence of the void beyond', NULL, 'The grain experiences the narrowness and pressure of passage; the needle''s delicate dance', 'Metaphysical, spiritual, oscillating between trial and transcendence', 2, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 12:58:26.639702-05', '2026-02-27 12:58:26.639702-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (4, 'Global Public Sphere', 'exterior', 'Urban plazas, bustling cities, sun-drenched beaches, grainy newscast imagery; figures pointing skyward in the midst of crowds; silent, still forms contrasting with surrounding movement', 'Newscasters chirping, social media buzz, ceaseless chatter, mystery-filled silence around The Pointers, echoing urban cacophony', NULL, 'Urban throng pressing around; stark contrast between stillness and bustle', 'Attention-hungry void colliding with transcendent mystery; collective wonder mixed with mundane dismissal; global spectacle transforming ordinary spaces into stages of inquiry', 3, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 12:58:50.898794-05', '2026-02-27 12:58:50.898794-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (5, 'The Alleyway at Dusk', 'exterior', 'Shadowed passage draped in dusk, sodium glow illuminating a spectral tableau; silhouetted skyline in the distance', NULL, 'Rain and wet pavement; faint cloying sweetness of bitter dreams', 'Crisp and cool air', 'Liminal threshold between mundane routine and transcendent mystery; uncanny serenity mixed with existential dread', 4, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 12:59:17.07896-05', '2026-02-27 12:59:17.07896-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (7, 'World at Large', 'exterior', 'Society returning to normal routine with underlying buzz of Pointer sightings; quirky footnote in daily newsfeed; election drama replacing Pointer mystery', 'Relentless drumbeat of life marching on; whispers of the sky drowned out; dull hum of background noise', NULL, 'Splinter of unease lodged in heart', 'Normalization and apathy; slow-motion circus transitioning to collective forgetfulness; underlying buzz giving way to indifference', 6, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:00:11.791146-05', '2026-02-27 13:00:11.791146-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (9, 'The Home - Kitchen', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:02:24.372659-05', '2026-02-27 13:02:24.372659-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (11, 'The Corporate Warehouse Office', 'interior', 'Nondescript factory-turned-warehouse nestled in city''s manufacturing district. Bullpen with developer workstations, hallways suitable for racing, conference room with adjacent breakroom. Festive decorations brighten corners despite sterile, fluorescent-lit corporate setting.', 'Usually a hub of frenetic energy; now unusually serene during pre-holiday period. Punctuated by booming COO voice, jingling Krampus bells, animated chatter, and holiday music.', 'Faint mustiness mixed with burning lead soldier scent upon entry; later acrid smoke from paper burning.', 'Cold, heavy metal doors at entrance; colder interior air; ceiling tiles that tremble under COO''s footsteps.', 'Purgatorial hellscape of meaningless chaos; prison-like fluorescent confinement; surreal fever dream quality blending holiday horror with corporate dystopia. Transforms from serene morning calm to escalating absurdity.', 9, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:07:03.395028-05', '2026-02-27 13:07:03.395028-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (12, 'The Driveway and Home', 'exterior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:08:02.245362-05', '2026-02-27 13:08:02.245362-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (13, 'Todd''s Living Room', 'interior', 'Cluttered, battered; features battered recliner as centerpiece. Cracked ceiling. Moonlit.', 'TV static, infomercial interrupted; quiet hum of electronics.', 'Reeks of sweat, smoke, and moonshine.', 'Armrest of recliner, furniture worn and degraded.', 'Oppressive squalor; dim, isolated space conducive to obsession; sanctuary of paranoia.', 11, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:08:28.833727-05', '2026-02-27 13:08:28.833727-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (14, 'Todd''s Cluttered Living Room', 'interior', 'Battered recliner, flickering TV interrupted by static, cracked ceiling, cluttered surroundings reflecting paranoid isolation.', 'Static from TV, Todd''s heart pounding, phone chirping with messages.', 'Reeks of sweat, smoke, and moonshine.', 'Trembling hands; dangerous proximity of smoldering hand-rolled cigarette to armrest.', 'Claustrophobic paranoia mixed with obsessive determination; night-to-dawn temporal arc; tension between hope and dread.', 11, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:10:59.759386-05', '2026-02-27 13:10:59.759386-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (15, 'The Abandoned Warehouse on 7th Street', 'exterior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:11:41.065574-05', '2026-02-27 13:11:41.065574-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (8, 'The Narrator''s Mind', 'other', 'Internal contemplation; visions of news broadcasts, social media feeds, viral memes', 'Echo of the narrator''s own questions; the absent sound of The Pointers'' ''silent song''', 'The lingering aftertaste metaphorically present', 'Suffocating grip of dread; cold fear; sweat-drenched skin.', 'Reflective, searching, caught between rejection of mainstream narratives and recognition of deeper patterns', 7, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:00:36.404425-05', '2026-02-27 13:12:14.109668-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (17, 'MIT Dorm Room', 'interior', 'Dim glow from a cheap desk lamp; intimate space shared by the narrator and friends.', 'Laughter that becomes subdued and strained; quiet murmurs of conversation.', NULL, 'Warmth of alcohol; shared physical closeness in a small room.', 'Initially welcoming and intimate; gradually becomes uncomfortable and distant; confessional and vulnerable.', 14, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:12:39.636819-05', '2026-02-27 13:12:39.636819-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (18, 'Hospital', 'interior', 'Sterile white walls with chipped paint on ceiling; clinical and cold; narrows into background as narrator''s consciousness expands.', 'Droning priest''s pronouncements; distant hum of machinery; electrical jolts and beeping monitors.', 'Sharp, acrid stench with underlying rot and sickness; smell of illness and medical decay.', 'Needles, electrodes, the shock of cardioversion; the cold of hospital sheets and medicated air.', 'Liminal space between life and death; sterile yet charged with spiritual intensity; fades into background as narrator''s inner realms dominate.', 15, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:13:14.35138-05', '2026-02-27 13:13:14.35138-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (19, 'Space of Confession', 'interior', 'Indeterminate interior space where the narrator shares their story with friends; shifts from warmth to oppressive atmosphere.', 'Initially dialogue and the narrator''s story; then heavy, crushing silence.', NULL, 'Air growing heavy, words fragile as glass.', 'Initially warm and receptive; becomes suffocating, weighted with unease and discomfort as the truth is revealed.', 16, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:14:09.015358-05', '2026-02-27 13:14:09.015358-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (6, 'The Bedroom', 'interior', 'A personal sleeping space with a window through which first rays of sunlight penetrate; darkness giving way to dawn', 'Silent, with only the sound of the narrator''s restless movements—tossing and turning in bed', NULL, 'The physical sensation of bedding; the feeling of wakefulness and bodily restlessness', 'Oppressive with sleeplessness; a space of mental torment where rest refuses to come; transitioning from night to morning', 5, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 12:59:41.749694-05', '2026-02-28 22:24:34.87899-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (20, 'Interior Space of Narrator''s Mind', 'interior', 'Collapsed walls, crumbling barriers, swirling jagged memories like shards of glass in consciousness.', 'Silence of internal breakdown; absence of external sound, focus on psychological collapse.', NULL, 'Sharp, cutting sensations of memories piercing through awareness like glass shards.', 'Suffocating sense of inevitability; the moment defenses fail and suppression ends; raw vulnerability exposed.', 17, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:14:36.084483-05', '2026-02-27 13:14:36.084483-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (22, 'The Workshop and Surrounding Cornfield', 'transitional', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:15:18.882025-05', '2026-02-27 13:15:18.882025-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (23, 'Road Between Workshop and House', 'transitional', 'Pre-dawn darkness yielding to ethereal glow; cornfields flanking the path; eerily still landscape punctuated by awakening light.', 'Initially silent forest, then pierced by distant child''s cry that echoes across sidewalk.', 'Scent of corn and earth implied in agricultural setting.', 'Cool pre-dawn air; weight of papers in hands.', 'Liminal and suspenseful; boundary between dream and waking; race against time as dawn approaches and others stir.', 20, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:16:09.683429-05', '2026-02-27 13:16:09.683429-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (36, 'Global Transportation Network', 'exterior', 'Airports, seaports, and train stations worldwide obscured by construction barriers and active machinery, with dramatic shifts in familiar urban landscapes.', 'Incessant construction noise—grinding, drilling, mechanical clamor operating 24/7.', 'Metal dust, concrete particles, diesel fumes from machinery.', 'Ground vibrations from heavy equipment, dust in the air.', 'Disruption, secrecy, unease. The familiar rhythms of global commerce replaced by mystery and industrial chaos.', 33, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:50:40.783929-05', '2026-02-27 13:50:40.783929-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (25, 'Office and Boardroom', 'interior', 'Stark, sterile corridors with desks, harsh lighting, oppressive atmosphere. Boardroom with long table and judgment-laden faces.', 'Oppressive chatter and clatter; angry team voices; clicks of presentation slides; final applause.', NULL, 'Weight pressing down like gravity; trembling hands; tight throat.', 'Sterile, judgmental, hostile, culminating in surreal celebration that clashes with protagonist''s internal devastation.', 22, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:17:06.05021-05', '2026-02-27 13:17:06.05021-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (27, 'The Barn and Farmland', 'exterior', 'Rural barn converted to workshop containing the Eternal Engine; surrounded by flowering fields, distant mountains, and sleepy farmhouse; dew-kissed landscape under golden dawn light.', 'Initially electrical crackling and sparks from engine; later bee buzzing and their deafening symphony; protagonist''s ragged breathing and eventual screams.', 'Acrid tang of hot metal and electrical discharge from engine core; later thick cloying scent of nectar, sharp tang of beeswax and honey; scent becomes sickly and suffocating.', 'Oppressive heat from engine; raw, blistered skin; rough cot; fresh dawn air; dew-kissed fields; stinging sensations from bee attack.', 'Tense determination shifting to exhaustion, then existential doubt, culminating in primal terror as nature''s beauty transforms into wrathful danger.', 24, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:23:10.755388-05', '2026-02-27 13:23:10.755388-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (28, 'Protagonist''s Home and Workplace', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:24:09.210121-05', '2026-02-27 13:24:09.210121-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (29, 'Office and Surrounding Areas', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:46:56.316269-05', '2026-02-27 13:46:56.316269-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (30, 'Nevada Highway (Narrator''s Drive Home)', 'exterior', 'Deserted streets stretching endlessly; flickering streetlights marking the path; fog obscuring clarity; night sky pressing down.', 'Silence of the slumbering city; rhythm of flickering streetlights creating dissonant percussion against internal chaos.', 'Heavy night air; fog of doubt metaphorically suffocating.', 'Cool night air initially; shift to oppressive, suffocating weight; tingling coursing through narrator''s body; white-knuckled grip on steering wheel.', 'Warped reality; sinister awareness; magnetic pull toward unknown; world twisted by absence of the Pointers; heavy, malevolent presence.', 27, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:47:35.580676-05', '2026-02-27 13:47:35.580676-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (32, 'Living Room', 'interior', 'Domestic interior transformed by camping preparations: sleeping bags, tents, and gear scattered across floor and furniture.', 'Peaceful TV dialogue and action sounds initially; shifts to wife''s commanding voice, rustling of gear, son''s footsteps.', NULL, 'Soft blanket comfort; cold tent fabric and smooth sleeping bag nylon.', 'Warm, intimate relaxation shifting rapidly to energized chaos, then settling into hopeful anticipation of adventure.', 29, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:48:56.287326-05', '2026-02-27 13:48:56.287326-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (34, 'Todd''s Trailer', 'interior', 'Dim glow from single incandescent bulb casting long, shifting shadows; faded, peeling floral wallpaper; stacks of newspapers and scribbled notes covering every surface; empty takeout containers piled high; worn couch on verge of collapse; red string webbing connecting photos and clippings across walls.', 'Relative silence with rustling of papers and Todd''s movements.', 'Stale mix of cigarette smoke and old food.', 'Worn surfaces, decaying furniture, chaos of accumulated clutter.', 'Heavy, suffocating, enclosed; a space consumed by obsession where the boundary between home and investigation site has dissolved.', 31, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:49:48.022183-05', '2026-02-27 13:49:48.022183-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (37, 'Forest Campsite', 'exterior', 'Dense forest with towering trees casting long shadows across winding roads; clearing with multiple tents and central campfire. Stars visible overhead.', 'Crackling campfire, snapping branches, murmuring conversations, laughter, hum of voices.', 'Smoky tang of burning wood, hot chocolate, earthy forest aroma, toasted marshmallows.', 'Night air, warmth from campfire, earth beneath feet, struggling tent poles.', 'Dark, mysterious, and testing upon arrival; transforms into peaceful, profound, and intoxicating as the night unfolds under the stars.', 34, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:51:29.102752-05', '2026-02-27 13:51:29.102752-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (38, 'Campsite (Evening)', 'exterior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:51:55.298684-05', '2026-02-27 13:51:55.298684-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (31, 'Narrator''s Home', 'interior', 'A living room with a couch, initially lit by the glow of a TV. Later, a dark and quiet bedroom.', 'The sound from the TV show ''Interior Chinatown'', which gives way to the soft rhythm of breathing.', NULL, 'The warmth and gentle touch of the narrator''s wife.', 'The atmosphere shifts from weary and surreal to safe, quiet, and comforting.', NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:48:16.546021-05', '2026-02-27 14:33:21.947313-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (35, 'The Trailer', 'interior', 'Kaleidoscope of clutter and chaos; walls covered in clippings and headlines connected by conspiracy theories; difficult to navigate without tripping.', 'Silence heavy with tension; faint echo of Stacey''s departure.', 'Faint musk of Stacey lingering after exit.', 'Cluttered, suffocating atmosphere.', 'Domestic space deteriorating under weight of obsession; impasse forged from love and exhaustion.', 32, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:50:07.05205-05', '2026-02-27 20:20:29.267817-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (39, 'Tent (Campsite)', 'interior', 'Confined interior with thin sleeping pad; isolated from forest surroundings but acoustically vulnerable.', 'Amplified night sounds: creaks of branches, distant rustles, rhythmic machinery hum penetrate the tent''s walls.', NULL, 'Thin, uncomfortable sleeping pad; the sensation of confinement.', 'Stillness outside sharpens inner unease; a container of dread within a larger mystery.', 36, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:52:24.483424-05', '2026-02-27 13:52:24.483424-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (40, 'Scout Campsite and Forest', 'exterior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:52:44.252541-05', '2026-02-27 13:52:44.252541-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (41, 'The Forest (Campsite Region)', 'exterior', 'Vibrant woodland transformed into oppressive darkness; bark twisted into strange shapes; shadows stretched long and claw-like; trees leaning in watchfully; trails dissolving into gloom; trails that loop impossibly and seem to stretch distances; landscapes shifting unrecognizably when unseen; a clearing where the lost patrol stands surrounded by humming trees; branches like grasping bones.', 'Swallowing of shouts replaced by suffocating silence; rustling of leaves unnervingly deliberate; low susurration pulsing through the ground; humming trees; whispered questions from the boys.', 'Sour rot clinging to the back of the throat; damp, thick air.', 'Heavy air; roots snagging at boots; branches scraping faces and snapping back; dirt dragging at boots; weight of exhaustion pressing harder with each step; clammy, closing sensation.', 'Oppressive, malevolent, watchful; defies reason; possesses will and agency; deliberately traps and releases visitors; waiting for another opportunity to pull them back.', 38, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:53:14.875679-05', '2026-02-27 13:53:14.875679-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (43, 'Nightmare Forest Landscape', 'exterior', 'A warped, impossible forest with ancient trees twisted into grotesque faces with gaping mouths. Sky is a violent bruise of purple and black with jagged cracks of lightning. Canopy oppressively high. Ground shifts from familiar cornstalks to earth to gravel to molten tar-like substance. Fog obscures the deeper reaches. Gnarled roots erupt like skeletal hands. Jagged branches claw at the sky.', 'Air hisses with oppressive drone that rattles in teeth. Faint otherworldly hum pulling forward. Underbrush whispers in sharp, brittle voices like shattering glass. Wind carries incomprehensible whispers filled with malice. Voices slither like worms through thoughts.', 'Thick decay; sour, choking dampness; rot filling lungs.', 'Ground beneath feet is sticky, soft, and treacherous like molasses. Jagged branches tear at skin leaving trails of icy fire. Air has oppressive weight.', 'Oppressive, predatory, nightmarish. Familiar landmarks have been warped into grotesque parodies. A trap that simultaneously repels and compels. Ancient and hungry. Every sense screams wrongness.', 40, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:54:34.864627-05', '2026-02-27 13:54:34.864627-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (44, 'Sacred Circle Clearing', 'exterior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:55:25.624876-05', '2026-02-27 13:55:25.624876-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (42, 'Campsite', 'exterior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:54:00.920159-05', '2026-02-27 13:56:07.472375-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (46, 'Road Home and Surrounding Regions', 'transitional', 'Gray asphalt ribbon shimmering under summer sun; familiar landmarks appearing strange and altered; late afternoon light; world appearing achingly normal.', 'Hum of the device; drone of the Eternal Engine', NULL, 'Icy surface of device pressed against palm', 'Dreamlike, unreal, surreal; boundary between reality and dream feels paper-thin; subtle unreality pervades familiar city; finality settling with fragile peace', 43, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:56:38.884369-05', '2026-02-27 13:56:38.884369-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (48, 'Corporate Office (Stripped)', 'interior', 'Once-vibrant office now bare and lifeless; holiday decorations removed, walls stripped of personal touches, reduced to hollow alien space.', 'Strangely silent, eerie quiet replacing usual hustle; sinister chanting echoing down empty halls at night.', 'Coffee''s bitter tang and clean printer ink normally comforting, but now overwhelmed by underlying scent of rot—old wood and damp soil.', 'Sense of disconnection, starkness, emptiness.', 'Unease, lifelessness, alienation; the starkness reflects everything back onto inhabitants like a mirror of decay.', 45, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:57:58.322291-05', '2026-02-27 13:57:58.322291-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (26, 'Office (Corporate)', 'interior', 'Non-IT staff clustered around glowing screens with pale, tense faces; CEO pacing in corner office; IT team at keyboards and terminals frantically troubleshooting.', 'Cacophony of error messages with shrill electronic voices and flashing red text; nervous cheers at moment of server restoration.', 'Stale coffee and sweat so thick it seeps into pores.', 'Suffocating tension; air of impending catastrophe palpable; frayed nerves stretched thin.', 'Maelstrom of controlled chaos transformed into command center; room of weary but victorious faces as dawn breaks through windows.', 23, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:17:55.447677-05', '2026-02-27 13:58:32.087628-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (21, 'Bedroom', 'interior', 'Pictures on wall; modest furnishings; prone to tremor from external vibrations.', 'Quiet baseline interrupted by freight train rumble and thunder.', NULL, 'Bed; sweat-dampened fabric; trembling walls.', 'Liminal space between wakefulness and dream; sanctuary from waking trauma but gateway to nightmares.', 18, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:14:55.347367-05', '2026-02-27 15:01:46.507507-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (51, 'The Office', 'interior', 'A once-vibrant office space that has been stripped of all holiday decorations and personal touches, leaving it with bare, lifeless walls. The stark, hollow emptiness reflects the company''s inner state.', 'Strangely silent, a stark contrast to the usual hustle and bustle of a functioning workplace.', 'The comforting scents of coffee and printer''s ink are tainted by an underlying, invasive scent of rot, described as old wood and damp soil.', NULL, 'Alien and unsettling. The atmosphere is thick with a sense of disconnection, decay, and unease.', 45, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:05:27.01787-05', '2026-02-27 14:05:27.01787-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (52, 'Narrator''s Office and Corporate Hallways', 'interior', 'A professional office lined with personal awards and mementos. The space becomes claustrophobic, with walls that seem to close in. The adjacent hallways are lit by cold, flickering fluorescent lights and populated by silent, staring colleagues.', 'The scene transitions from the crackle of a client call to the rhythmic thudding of footsteps, a guttural roar, nervous tittering, a chair''s agonized squeal, and finally, the tense silence of the main office floor.', NULL, 'Vibrations through the floor, flecks of spittle on the face, the unyielding iron grip of security guards, and the muggy slap of the outside air upon exit.', 'Begins with professional normalcy, but rapidly descends into a foreboding, tense, and hostile environment. It functions as an ''execution chamber'' filled with malice, fear, and dehumanization.', 46, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:06:21.630833-05', '2026-02-27 14:06:21.630833-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (53, 'Narrator''s Car', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:07:30.385865-05', '2026-02-27 14:07:30.385865-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (66, 'Narrator''s Garage Lab', 'interior', 'A cleared corner in a likely cluttered garage, featuring a workbench with tools, a microscope, and the shimmering metallic Engine as the focal point. Light catches the object''s intricate patterns.', 'A persistent, low hum from The Engine, punctuated by the sharp sounds of failed experiments: the crackle of a burning remote, the flash-bang of a bulb, and the violent shattering of fan blades.', 'The acrid smell of burnt plastic and ozone from destroyed electronics, mixed with the background scents of dust, oil, and metal common to a garage.', 'The cool, unnervingly smooth yet textured surface of The Engine. The ambient chill of a garage space contrasted with the sudden, brief heat from destroyed components.', 'An intense mixture of obsessive curiosity and mounting frustration, which slowly curdles into apprehension and dread as the experiments reveal the object''s true power.', 60, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:19:37.382513-05', '2026-02-27 14:19:37.382513-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (125, 'The Void Between Dimensions', 'other', 'A realm of absolute darkness where time and space are merely forgotten concepts. It is a place of seamless, ordered stillness.', 'Profound silence and stillness, the absence of any sound.', NULL, NULL, 'Vast, unknowable, ancient, and timeless. A state of oblivion and perfect order until disturbed.', 119, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:12:47.75463-05', '2026-02-27 15:12:47.75463-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (54, 'The Threshold', 'exterior', 'A surreal, logic-defying dreamscape where colors spiral like sentient nebulae and nebulous shapes form towering structures. It is a place where boundaries are fluid and reality is a contradiction.', 'Echoes murmur from unseen corners, and faint murmurs weave intricate, unsettling harmonies. The air itself can hum with energy.', 'A sacred resonance described as being ''thick like incense'' emanates from Elysium.', 'Sensations are inconsistent; familiar feelings of softness can dissolve into a void, while the air can thicken and feel charged with energy.', 'Ethereal, mysterious, and enchanting. It is a crucible where thoughts and possibilities take form, governed by emotion rather than logic. It holds both profound intimacy and great peril.', 48, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:08:39.176988-05', '2026-02-27 14:11:11.469603-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (58, 'Protagonist''s House', 'interior', 'A house interior, moving from a bedroom with sheets on a bed to a bathroom with a shower and a drain.', 'Initially shattered by the deafening, house-filling sound of Metallica. This is later replaced by the sound of a running shower.', NULL, 'The feeling of being tangled in bed sheets, followed by the sensation of hot water spray on the skin.', 'Abruptly shifts from the serene peace of a dream to a state of abrasive, head-splitting chaos and panic.', 52, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:12:01.87074-05', '2026-02-27 14:12:01.87074-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (60, 'The Domestic Sphere', 'interior', 'An environment defined not by physical objects, but by the ''expanse of empty hours'' and the presence of family. It is a space of quiet moments, homework on a table, and shared meals.', 'An ''unsettling stillness'' at first, which is later replaced by the sounds of family life: quiet conversations and the mundane noises of a shared home.', NULL, NULL, 'Initially disorienting and paralyzing, the atmosphere transforms into one of quiet fulfillment, profound purpose, and rediscovered connection.', 54, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:13:50.207638-05', '2026-02-27 14:13:50.207638-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (61, 'Protagonist''s Research Space', 'interior', 'A room illuminated primarily by the glow of a computer monitor. The screen is filled with forum threads, articles, and search results. The space feels insular and focused.', 'The low hum of a computer fan and the persistent, quiet clicking of a mouse and keyboard.', 'The faint scent of stale air or perhaps old coffee, indicative of long hours spent in one place.', 'The cool, smooth surface of the keyboard and mouse under the protagonist''s fingers.', 'Tense and obsessive, charged with a mixture of intellectual curiosity, mounting desperation, and a growing sense of dread.', 55, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:14:30.642504-05', '2026-02-27 14:14:30.642504-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (62, 'CERN Laboratory (LHC-1)', 'interior', 'A laboratory that was once a sanctuary of reason, now a prison of shadows with shimmering, breathing walls and flickering lights. Other buildings like LHC-2 and LHC-3 have vanished from existence, leaving only LHC-1 standing.', 'The steady thrum of machinery has been replaced by a low, resonant pulse like a heartbeat, growing louder. The screams of patients echo in dreams, but the rooms are dead silent.', NULL, NULL, 'An atmosphere of escalating chaos, paranoia, and malevolent presence. The foundations of reality are unstable, and a sense of being watched by a hungry, patient entity pervades everything.', 56, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:15:25.564744-05', '2026-02-27 14:15:25.564744-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (63, 'Protagonist''s Study', 'interior', 'A desk is covered in scattered papers with copious notes scribbled in the margins. A computer screen is cluttered with endless open Chrome tabs, evidence of intense research.', 'The scene is quiet, dominated by the protagonist''s internal monologue.', 'The faint smell of old paper and warm electronics.', 'The feeling of leaning back in a chair.', 'An environment of intense, obsessive research that is now cooling into disillusionment and unease.', 57, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:16:25.005146-05', '2026-02-27 14:16:25.005146-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (64, 'Protagonist''s Office', 'interior', 'A dimly lit, cluttered office at night. The only light is the flickering glow of a computer screen, casting eerie, restless shadows on towering stacks of research papers.', 'Initially quiet, later filled with skittering, unintelligible whispers and a sense of reality''s hum faltering.', 'Thick with the suffocating scent of aged paper and stale coffee.', 'A heavy, thick air that grows cold and trembles with unnatural energy.', 'Begins with a feeling of oppressive exhaustion and obsession, which rapidly shifts to tense, eerie, and supernaturally charged.', 58, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:17:16.799995-05', '2026-02-27 14:17:16.799995-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (65, 'Garage Lab', 'interior', 'A garage converted into a makeshift laboratory, now devastated. Shattered glass, tools, and scorched notebooks litter the floor. The scene is illuminated only by flashes of lightning and a weak flashlight beam.', 'The howl of a powerful storm and rattling rain outside. Inside, a heavy, oppressive silence broken only by the narrator''s frantic pulse and ragged breathing.', 'The acrid, sharp stench of burnt metal and ozone hangs heavy in the air.', 'The air is heavy and suffocating. Cold metal tools are scattered on the floor.', 'Chaotic, terrifying, and oppressive. A palpable sense of destruction, despair, and dawning horror at an unknown, unleashed presence.', 59, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:18:41.368644-05', '2026-02-27 14:18:41.368644-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (67, 'The Narrator''s Garage Workshop', 'interior', 'A messy corner of a garage filled with sketches, discarded electronics, and scattered wires. A glass enclosure containing the engine is the centerpiece.', 'A steady, unrelenting hum from the Eternal Engine.', NULL, 'A faint, pulsing vibration in the air.', 'Tense and ominous, charged with the narrator''s mix of fear and determined anticipation.', 61, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:20:22.890265-05', '2026-02-27 14:21:20.399666-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (70, 'The Narrator''s Workspace', 'interior', 'A dark space dominated by the eerie, siren-like glow of computer screens. The desk is a central feature, serving as both a prison cell and a sacrificial altar.', 'The ceaseless, rhythmic clicking of a mouse, underscored by a profound, echoing silence.', NULL, 'The cold, hard surfaces of technology and furniture.', 'Oppressive, hopeless, and surreal. A place of ritualistic futility where time feels fractured and sanity is the currency.', 64, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:23:07.257785-05', '2026-02-27 14:23:07.257785-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (71, 'The Home Office', 'interior', 'A dark room at 3 AM, illuminated only by the cold, isolating glow of a computer screen. It feels more like a command center for a losing battle than a part of a home.', 'The oppressive silence of the late night, punctuated by the faint hum of electronics and the narrator''s increasingly desperate voice.', 'Stale, recycled air from a room that has been occupied for too long.', 'The late-night chill in the air, contrasted with the warmth radiating from the computer.', 'Tense, claustrophobic, and saturated with despair and obsession. The room is a pressure cooker for the narrator''s emotions.', 65, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:24:04.5571-05', '2026-02-27 14:24:04.5571-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (73, 'Childhood Home (Flashback)', 'interior', 'A gloomy, shadowy house where grotesque shadows are cast by inhuman actions. The narrator is left on the cold ground.', 'The ''thunderous cracks'' of physical blows echoing through the house, contrasted by the profound silence of the mother.', NULL, 'The sharp, repeated impact of fists; the cold ground against a broken body.', 'Suffocating and terrifying. A place of torment and malevolent presence, defined by merciless violence and cold, detached betrayal.', 67, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:26:04.557296-05', '2026-02-27 14:26:04.557296-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (76, 'Home Office', 'interior', 'A room containing a desk with glowing computer monitors and a doorframe. The light is dominated by the screen glow.', 'Initially quiet, then filled with the sounds of conversation, teasing, and laughter.', 'Neutral indoor smells.', 'The feel of a computer touchpad and a light, gentle tap on the shoulder.', 'Begins with a sense of monotony and boredom, which transforms into warmth, playfulness, and affection with the wife''s arrival.', 70, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:29:00.387325-05', '2026-02-27 14:29:00.387325-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (84, 'Todd and Stacey''s Trailer', 'interior', 'A cramped and cluttered living space with thin, stained walls. The room is a mess of scattered papers, empty cans, and a conspiracy board with red yarn connecting news clippings. It contains a worn-out couch and a shag carpet.', 'Dominated by Todd''s booming, reverberating voice, punctuated by the sharp sound of shattering glass. The silences are heavy and tense.', 'An implied smell of stale beer and general neglect.', 'Stifling, suffocating summer heat.', 'Oppressive, volatile, and claustrophobic. The air is thick with paranoia, fear, and the imminent threat of violence.', 78, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:36:01.424183-05', '2026-02-27 15:09:35.797104-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (83, 'Narrator''s Study', 'interior', 'A dimly lit room, the primary light source being the glow from a phone screen casting long shadows. The focus is tight on the father and son leaning over a desk.', 'The sound of the son''s voice reading aloud, punctuated by the rapid tapping of his fingers on the screen and the occasional sharp inhale from the narrator.', NULL, 'The air grows colder as the conversation becomes more terrifying.', 'The atmosphere shifts from one of intellectual curiosity and excitement to one of palpable tension and existential dread as the implications of the information become clear.', 77, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:34:59.83941-05', '2026-02-27 14:34:59.83941-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (85, 'Dilapidated Trailer', 'interior', 'Every surface is covered in a chaotic sprawl of crumpled, worn, and yellowed papers. The overall impression is one of long-term neglect and obsessive research.', 'A deep quiet, punctuated only by the metaphorical ''murmur'' of the secrets held within the papers.', 'The dry, dusty scent of old paper and decay.', 'Brittle paper, a fine layer of dust on all surfaces.', 'Clandestine and conspiratorial. The space feels like a hidden nerve center for a secret investigation, filled with fragmented but important truths.', 79, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:37:00.306187-05', '2026-02-27 14:37:00.306187-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (80, 'Garage', 'interior', 'A domestic garage space containing the Eternal Engine and a car. It is lit by a single light that flickers during the engine''s activation.', 'The sound of a car on the driveway, voices, the distinct clicks of switches, and the steady hum of the newly activated engine.', 'The sharp, distinct smell of burning flux fills the air.', NULL, 'The atmosphere begins thick with tension and nervous anticipation, then transforms into one of amazement, relief, and shared triumph.', 74, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:32:17.378803-05', '2026-02-27 14:45:41.493353-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (88, 'The House (Garage and Kitchen)', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:39:32.031313-05', '2026-02-27 14:39:32.031313-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (78, 'The Workshop', 'interior', 'A space dominated by the complex Eternal Engine, with numerous wires and circuits. It is a place of focused work that also contains elements of domestic life, such as the potential for stray lego blocks.', 'The steady, rhythmic hum of the Eternal Engine, which is interrupted by the soft chime of a phone.', 'The faint scent of singed metal after the electric shock.', 'The sharp jolt of electricity and the tingling sensation in the fingers.', 'Begins with an atmosphere of intense focus, collaboration, and renewed intimacy. This shifts to one of quiet solitude and determined precision after the wife''s departure.', 72, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:30:36.560497-05', '2026-02-27 16:04:25.733696-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (69, 'The Garage', 'interior', 'A domestic garage space, mostly cleaned up after some kind of messy work. It houses the narrator''s secret project, the Eternal Engine.', 'The sound of a car pulling in, followed by quiet punctuated by a faint, low hum.', 'A faint, lingering smell of smoke from burnt wires.', 'A coldness that seeps into the bones.', 'Secretive and slightly tense, shifting to contemplative and mysterious after the wife leaves.', 63, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:22:10.64191-05', '2026-02-27 15:43:52.004032-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (91, 'Family Home - Unspecified Room', 'interior', 'A generic, lived-in domestic space. The focus is entirely on the characters, leaving the background indistinct.', 'The son sniffing the air, the wife''s sharp voice, and the soft thud of a person being shoved.', 'A sudden, pervasive, and unpleasant odor hangs in the air.', 'The air is still until the abrupt force of a shove.', 'A neutral family moment that is instantly charged with awkwardness and tension.', 85, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:42:18.622465-05', '2026-02-27 14:42:18.622465-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (97, 'The Father''s Office', 'interior', 'A cluttered sanctuary containing a desk, notebooks, half-empty mugs, and scattered water bottles. It has a computer with a spare NIC and is connected to the garage via a network cable.', 'The sounds of conversation and debate between the family members.', NULL, NULL, 'Initially a place of work, it transforms into a hub of debate, mischief, and finally, high-stakes technological experimentation. The atmosphere shifts from mundane to tense and exhilarating.', 91, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:47:49.746694-05', '2026-02-27 14:47:49.746694-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (98, 'Home Computer Lab', 'interior', 'A room dominated by a computer with a faintly glowing crystalline core. A monitor displays a dizzying cascade of symbols, images, and text. Family members are gathered around, one sitting cross-legged on the floor.', 'The hum and thrum of a powerful machine, the clicking of a keyboard, the rustle of a chip bag, and hushed, awestruck voices.', 'The faint smell of ozone from electronics and salty chips.', 'The cool plastic of keyboard keys.', 'Begins with tense anticipation, shifts to captivating awe, plunges into momentary terror, and culminates in profound, world-altering shock.', 92, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:48:44.800966-05', '2026-02-27 14:48:44.800966-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (101, 'The Workbench', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:51:40.884139-05', '2026-02-27 14:51:40.884139-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (104, 'The House and Garage Lab', 'transitional', 'A domestic setting being converted into a makeshift lab. Wires snake from a garage with a workbench and fuse box into an air-conditioned living/dining area where computer equipment is set up.', 'The quiet hum of the Eternal Engine, the voices of the father and son.', NULL, 'The contrast between the presumed heat of the garage and the ''air-conditioned comfort'' of the living room.', 'A blend of domesticity and high-tech experimentation, characterized by a sense of progress, collaboration, and underlying risk.', 98, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:54:32.987398-05', '2026-02-27 14:54:32.987398-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (105, 'Garage Workspace', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:55:15.442117-05', '2026-02-27 14:55:15.442117-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (106, 'The Garage Workstation', 'interior', 'A space filled with scientific equipment, including clinking glassware, bubbling beakers, and homemade test rigs. It has a workbench and shows signs of both chaotic experimentation and focused success.', 'A symphony of clinking glass, bubbling liquids, and the low hum of equipment, overlaid with the family''s dialogue, laughter, and exclamations.', 'The pungent aroma of various chemicals used in the experiments.', NULL, 'An environment buzzing with the energy of rapid discovery and collaboration. It transforms from a place of frustration to one of monumental achievement and awe.', 100, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:55:57.654487-05', '2026-02-27 14:55:57.654487-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (107, 'The Crimson Abyss', 'exterior', 'A hellish landscape bathed in a searing, pulsating crimson light. The air is a haze of fire and ash, and the terrain shifts and writhes like a living organism.', 'An overwhelming cacophony of screams, howls, guttural chants, and the sound of a ravenous wind.', 'The smell of ash and brimstone, carried on the wind.', 'The ground is jagged and unstable, pulsing like flesh underfoot. The air is filled with a wind that feels like claws of fire and ice.', 'Suffocating, tormenting, and deeply hostile. The reality of the place is chaotic and actively malevolent.', 101, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:57:05.016758-05', '2026-02-27 14:57:05.016758-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (108, 'Ruins of Elysium', 'exterior', 'Jagged ruins smoldering under a crimson sky with an unnatural red glow. The ground is fractured rubble, littered with ash and grotesque demon crosses.', 'The guttural roars of demons, a vast mechanical grinding, and the sounds of chaotic battle.', 'The smell of decay, ozone, and thick smoke.', 'The air is thick. The ground is unstable and trembles.', 'Hopeless, nightmarish, and oppressive. A place of constant, desperate struggle against impossible odds.', 102, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:57:51.540873-05', '2026-02-27 14:57:51.540873-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (109, 'The Ruined Battlefield', 'exterior', 'A scene of carnage and destruction, filled with rubble. A single shimmering wire provides an impossibly bright point of light against the devastation, later dominated by a blinding vortex.', 'The scene begins with fading whispers and guttural growls, escalating to the roar of collapsing reality and otherworldly beasts.', 'The metallic scent of destruction and the sharp, electric tang of ozone from the opened portal.', 'The cold, rough texture of rubble contrasts with the faint, living warmth of the magical wire.', 'Starts as desperate and tense, then escalates to apocalyptic and terrifying as reality itself is torn asunder.', 103, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:58:39.396494-05', '2026-02-27 14:58:39.396494-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (110, 'Oblivion', 'other', 'A living void where existence ceases. Shadows writhe and pulse like dying stars. Towering, grotesque eldritch abominations defy logic. A jagged obsidian path pulses with a sickly glow.', 'Initial silence, later filled with the resonant, layered whispers of the abomination''s voice, which cracks like splintering glass when it laughs. The scream of the dying creature rips through eternity.', NULL, 'Time presses against one with dense malice, a suffocating weight. The air grows thick and heavy, like wading through quicksand.', 'Oppressive, malevolent, and unnerving. A sense of insignificance and dread permeates the void, designed to crush the will of any visitor.', 104, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:59:48.319024-05', '2026-02-27 14:59:48.319024-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (111, 'The Corrupted Threshold', 'other', 'A rapidly shifting, hellish landscape. It transitions from the interior of a pulsating, organic train to a view of a city made of boiling flesh under a red sky, and finally to a swirling vortex of shadows revealing a cosmic void.', 'A cacophony of a train''s thrum, screams from a crystal, shrieks of soldiers, hissing monsters, and a deafening crack as reality solidifies.', 'The pervasive reek of decay.', 'The air is thick and heavy. Contact with enemies burns like molten rock.', 'Utterly nightmarish and hostile. The environment is actively malevolent, characterized by body horror, cosmic dread, and a sense of profound violation.', 105, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:00:58.852154-05', '2026-02-27 15:00:58.852154-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (113, 'Protagonist''s Workshop', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:02:46.066173-05', '2026-02-27 15:02:46.066173-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (115, 'The Inventor''s Garage', 'interior', 'A cluttered space resembling a tomb of failed projects. Piles of twisted metal, shattered glass, and scorched wires surround a workbench. An ominous device, the Eternal Engine, sits on a shelf.', 'The constant, low hum of the Eternal Engine, which vibrates through the air and floor.', 'The lingering smell of burnt electronics and chemicals from past experiments.', 'A tangible vibration in the floorboards from the Eternal Engine.', 'Heavy with the weight of failure and obsession, charged with a frantic, desperate energy that borders on madness.', 109, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:04:42.480403-05', '2026-02-27 15:04:42.480403-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (118, 'The Threshold of Ages', 'exterior', 'A vast, open space under a sky of fading twilight. A monumental fortress stands silhouetted against the dying light, casting long, deep shadows.', 'A profound and heavy silence, broken only by the imagined, spectral salute of spirits.', 'The cool, crisp scent of evening air, perhaps with a faint, dusty smell of ancient stone and memory.', 'A gentle, cooling breeze marking the transition from day to night.', 'Somber, monumental, and deeply reverent. A palpable sense of finality and historical weight hangs in the air.', 112, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:07:38.158904-05', '2026-02-27 15:07:38.158904-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (119, 'The Crucible of Change', 'other', 'A non-physical, conceptual space defined by the tension between opposing forces. It can be visualized as shimmering fields of energy pulling against one another amidst a grey void.', 'The sharp crack of breaking bonds followed by a low, inexorable grinding sound of reversal and tightening chains.', 'The faint scent of ozone from shattered energy, followed by the smell of dust and decay.', 'Alternating sensations of sudden weightlessness and immense, crushing pressure.', 'Highly volatile and charged with the conflict between progress and regression.', 113, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:08:06.506523-05', '2026-02-27 15:08:06.506523-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (120, 'The Nexus of Ages', 'other', 'A non-physical, conceptual space where time converges. Glimpses of past conflicts fade into the brilliant, emerging light of a metaphorical dawn.', 'A profound silence, punctuated by the faint, echoing cries of past struggles and the rising hum of a new beginning.', 'The scent of ozone and dust, like the air after a great storm has passed.', 'A palpable pressure in the air, the feeling of immense potential and the weight of history.', 'Charged with cosmic significance, transition, and inevitability.', 114, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:08:47.945044-05', '2026-02-27 15:08:47.945044-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (122, 'The Crimson Wastes', 'exterior', 'A landscape under a heavy crimson sky, featuring jagged spires of black rock, cracked ground covered in ash, and monstrous, smoke-like clouds. A distant, putrid green glow signifies a twisted forest.', 'The low, mechanical growl of a titan, screams of terror, rasping sobs, and the groaning of the earth.', NULL, 'An oppressive heat that seeps into the bones, contrasted with a feeling of cold. The ground is covered in sharp rocks and cloying ash.', 'Nightmarish, hostile, and utterly alien. The atmosphere is one of overwhelming dread, desperation, and cosmic horror.', 116, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:10:22.064882-05', '2026-02-27 15:10:22.064882-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (123, 'Shore of the Emerald Lake', 'exterior', 'A shimmering emerald lake whose shore provides a stark contrast to a crimson, desolate landscape. Across the water, ethereal visions of picnics and playing children flicker like a mirage.', 'The sound of genuine laughter echoing across the water, mixed with the tranquil whispers of the lake itself.', NULL, NULL, 'A deceptive sanctuary that feels both alien and alluring. It offers a powerful sense of peace and respite amidst overwhelming chaos and despair.', 117, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:11:06.191544-05', '2026-02-27 15:11:06.191544-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (127, 'The Mortal Realm', 'exterior', 'A once-peaceful world now being torn apart. The fabric of reality is visibly fraying, with colliding worlds and crumbling dimensions under the influence of the Matter Replicator and the entities.', 'An overwhelming cacophony of human screams, cries of terror, pleas for mercy, and the cruel, booming laughter and growls of the entities.', NULL, NULL, 'An atmosphere thick with terror, despair, and sadistic power. The very air seems to echo with suffering and the oppressive presence of divine, malevolent overlords.', 121, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:14:12.843937-05', '2026-02-27 15:14:12.843937-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (129, 'Long-Term Parking Lot', 'exterior', 'A large, likely dimly lit parking lot. A massive, abandoned RV sits in a corner, illuminated by the glow of a streetlamp.', 'Initially quiet, later filled with the hum and whir of the Replicator, and a final chime.', 'Faint scents of asphalt and old vehicles.', NULL, 'Tense and filled with anticipation, which later shifts to wonder and excitement.', 123, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:16:17.373813-05', '2026-02-27 15:16:17.373813-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (130, 'The Garage Workshop', 'interior', 'A cluttered but functional family garage containing a workbench. Various items are present, including keys, a coffee mug, a smartphone, a perfume bottle, and a can of insecticide.', 'The soft hum of the Matter Replicator during operation, the faint buzz of a trapped fly, and the overlapping dialogue of a curious family.', 'A sharp, chemical scent of insecticide briefly fills the air after the wife sprays the flies.', NULL, 'A dynamic mix of scientific wonder, familial collaboration, lighthearted tension, and ultimately, domestic absurdity.', 124, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:17:06.451164-05', '2026-02-27 15:17:06.451164-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (132, 'Family Home (Kitchen/Pantry Area)', 'interior', 'A domestic kitchen and pantry space, now featuring a high-tech replicator. The area contains cupboards and storage for food and dishes.', 'Family conversation, including groans, sighs, and laughter, punctuated by the operational sounds of the replicator.', 'The scent of garlic and fresh herbs from the successfully created pasta dish fills the air.', NULL, 'The mood shifts from one of weary dissatisfaction with their meals to one of shared excitement, inspiration, and amusement.', 126, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:18:32.421244-05', '2026-02-27 15:18:32.421244-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (128, 'Abyss', 'other', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:15:11.588631-05', '2026-03-01 01:08:28.234475-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (126, 'The Void', 'other', 'An endless, unknowable darkness referred to as a silent abyss. It is a space between worlds where cosmic entities exist.', 'Fundamentally silent, but filled with the crackling presence of the Watchers and their whispered, roared, or hissing words that thread through the dark.', 'The complete absence of scent, reinforcing the sense of unreality and nothingness.', 'A sensation of weightlessness and being adrift without substance or texture to touch.', 'Charged with the vast, unknowable presence of ancient beings and their unspoken intent. It is a place where the delicate balance between worlds is considered.', 120, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:13:21.912298-05', '2026-02-28 22:55:44.180429-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (135, 'Family Home Office', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:21:14.207833-05', '2026-02-27 15:21:14.207833-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (136, 'The Mortal World', 'exterior', 'A realm filled with blinding, unfamiliar light, contrasting sharply with the dark dominions the being once ruled.', 'Filled with strange, incomprehensible sounds that seem to come from every direction.', NULL, 'The air crackles with an incomprehensible, pulsating energy.', 'Unfamiliar, unsettling, yet fascinating. It is a world that has forgotten the ancient fears and superstitions that once empowered beings like The Forgotten One.', 130, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:22:30.53397-05', '2026-02-27 15:22:30.53397-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (137, 'Replicator''s Activation Point', 'other', 'The area is dominated by an otherworldly device that pulsates with energy and potential, illuminating a world that feels new and reshaped.', 'A low hum or pulsation from the central device.', NULL, 'The air feels charged, thick with potential and colliding forces.', 'Overwhelming and potent. A sense of a gateway being opened and powers shifting on a cosmic scale.', 131, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:23:12.863466-05', '2026-02-27 15:23:12.863466-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (10, 'The Kitchen', 'interior', 'A domestic kitchen with a table, chairs, and a counter. There is a trail of cereal crumbs left by the son, and a ceiling fan is present. The protagonist sits at the table with a coffee mug.', 'The scene begins with an ''uneasy quiet,'' punctuated by the faint hum of an Alexa Echo from another room. This is broken by the sound of the garage door, footsteps, and later, the faint ticking of the ceiling fan.', 'The implied aroma of coffee.', 'The warmth from the coffee mug held by the protagonist.', 'Starts as quiet and contemplative, shifts to concerned and intimate during the conversation, and ends with the protagonist alone again, lost in thought.', NULL, 'claude', 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', '2026-02-27 13:06:31.037788-05', '2026-02-27 15:24:08.696694-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (140, 'The Family Home (Living Room Operations Center)', 'interior', 'A typical living room cluttered with the infrastructure of a high-tech operation. Screens from the Infinitron cast a glow on the family''s faces, with cardboard boxes possibly still present in corners.', 'The low hum of electronics, the flickering sounds of the Infinitron''s interface, punctuated by tense conversation and an occasional chime from the machine.', 'The faint smell of warm electronics and stale coffee.', 'The cool surface of a phone screen, the warmth from computer monitors.', 'Thick with tension, oscillating between desperate hope, cautious optimism, and sharp anxiety. It''s a space where domestic life and a high-stakes secret operation collide.', 134, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:26:02.45773-05', '2026-02-27 15:26:02.45773-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (141, 'Chaotic City Realm', 'exterior', 'A towering fortress and maze of cold concrete and steel, filled with millions of scurrying, oblivious humans.', 'A constant cacophony and deafening clamor of city life, a chaotic symphony of human noise that drowns out other forces.', NULL, 'A sense of frenzied energy and constant motion from the hustle and bustle of the crowds.', 'Pulsates with frenzied energy, defined by an obsession with progress and materialistic pursuits. It feels alien and discordant to the protagonist.', 135, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:27:13.749211-05', '2026-02-27 15:27:13.749211-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (142, 'The Bustling City', 'exterior', 'A vibrant, modern metropolis characterized by ''pulsing lights and shadowy alleys.'' It is teeming with human activity and complex structures.', 'Filled with the constant sound of ''human music'' and the general hum of a populated urban environment.', NULL, NULL, 'Perceived by the protagonist not as a dwelling, but as a kingdom ripe for conquest. The atmosphere is charged with untapped potential and mystery.', 136, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:28:10.463106-05', '2026-02-27 15:28:10.463106-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (102, 'The Family Home', 'interior', 'A suburban home with a garage containing a high-tech workbench and a kitchen with a table. The advanced, gleaming technology contrasts with the mundane domestic setting.', 'The constant, rhythmic hum of the Eternal Engine, the sound of the replicator generating, and the shifting tones of the family''s conversation from sharp surprise to serious whispers.', 'The lingering, sharp scent of ozone from the powerful machinery, mixed with the artificial aroma of truffle from the replicated snacks.', 'A cramped, cluttered feeling. The wife mentions picking packing tape parts out of her clothes, suggesting a sticky, messy environment.', 'Begins with a feeling of jaded frustration and latent potential, shifts to tense confrontation and moral debate, and resolves into a unified sense of purpose and responsibility.', NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:52:26.990127-05', '2026-02-27 15:29:19.507091-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (144, 'Narrator''s Home (Living Room & Garage)', 'interior', 'A cluttered living room with unusual floor tiles of replicated gold. The scene shifts to a garage where the narrator is on his computer.', 'The narrator''s pacing, the ping of a computer notification, and the startling sound of the wife''s voice.', 'The faint, sterile scent of newly created metal mixed with the mundane smells of a lived-in home.', 'The cold, smooth floor tiles underfoot; the clammy sweat on the narrator''s palms.', 'Begins with quiet desperation and secrecy, then shifts to tense confrontation and anxious resolve.', 138, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:30:15.446954-05', '2026-02-27 15:30:15.446954-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (145, 'Warehouse District', 'transitional', 'A cavernous, cold warehouse space at the back of a row of similar buildings, lit only by a few flickering bulbs. The area is described as ''not in the best of areas''.', 'The echoing sounds of voices in a large, empty space, and the quiet zipping of a duffel bag.', 'The faint smell of dust and damp concrete.', 'A distinct coldness in the air within the warehouse.', 'Clandestine, tense, and dangerous. The isolation and poor lighting create a sense of foreboding and suspense.', 139, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:31:04.243613-05', '2026-02-27 15:31:04.243613-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (134, 'The Living Room', 'interior', 'A messy, makeshift ''war room'' with papers and discarded ice cream sandwich wrappers on the coffee table. The family is gathered on the couch.', 'The sounds of conversation, a pen being tossed on a table, and the flipping of pages in an article and a notebook.', 'The faint scent of green tea and lingering dinner.', 'The feel of couch cushions, a legal pad, a warm mug, and a cell phone.', 'The mood begins as tense and frustrated but transitions to collaborative, excited, and hopeful as a new plan forms.', 128, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:20:30.48573-05', '2026-02-28 18:28:34.479952-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (146, 'The Bar', 'interior', 'A public but discreet setting, likely dimly lit, suitable for a tense and final confrontation. The Viper leans casually against the bar itself.', 'The ambient noise of a bar, which is pierced by the heavy, tense silence during the confrontation.', 'The faint smell of stale beer and cleaning supplies.', 'Slightly sticky tables and the cool, conditioned air of the interior.', 'Extremely tense and charged with unspoken threats, despite The Viper''s casual posture. The air is thick with the narrator''s fear.', 140, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:31:52.077212-05', '2026-02-27 15:32:30.451105-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (148, 'The Strip Club', 'interior', 'Pulsing strobe lights illuminate gyrating bodies, gleaming metal poles, and a sheen of sweat on faces. The decor includes a worn wooden bar and ripped vinyl seats.', 'A cacophony dominated by a pounding bass line, pierced by raucous laughter, drunken shouts, and the clinking of glasses.', 'A thick mixture of cigarette smoke, heavy perfume, stale beer, and body odor permeates the air.', 'The floor and furniture vibrate from the powerful bass music.', 'A seedy, sordid den of vice and debauchery. The atmosphere is chaotic, decadent, and built on lies and fantasy.', 142, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:33:41.60525-05', '2026-02-27 15:33:41.60525-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (149, 'The Family''s Home & Fulfillment Center', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:34:52.287488-05', '2026-02-27 15:34:52.287488-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (152, 'The Dilapidated Warehouse', 'interior', 'A cavernous, abandoned space with cracked walls, broken windows, and dust motes dancing in sunlight from a hole in the roof. It is transformed into a gleaming, state-of-the-art fulfillment center with sparkling floors and perfectly assembled shelves.', 'Initially silent, the space later fills with the buzz and hum of synchronized robotic activity.', 'The initial smell of mildew and regret is replaced by the clean, sterile scent of new construction and polished surfaces.', 'Transitions from dusty and decaying to clean, smooth, and efficient.', 'Begins with a feeling of abandonment and decay, seen as a ''money pit'' by most. This transforms into an atmosphere of potential, progress, and thriving efficiency as the renovation proceeds.', 146, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:37:30.966727-05', '2026-02-27 15:37:30.966727-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (153, 'Ruins of a Palestinian City', 'exterior', 'The collapsed remains of a magnificent city, with majestic pillars and intricately carved walls now reduced to scattered fragments. A thick layer of dust covers everything under a bright, blinding sun.', 'The distant, echoing wails of sirens and shouts.', 'The strong, pervasive scent of burning wood and charred debris.', 'A thick coating of dust on all surfaces, including bodies. The air is likely heavy and gritty.', 'Desolate, grim, and chaotic. A former sanctuary of wisdom and reverence has been violently destroyed, leaving a sense of profound loss and devastation.', 147, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:38:57.923378-05', '2026-02-27 15:38:57.923378-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (154, 'Ruins of the Great Kingdom', 'exterior', 'Desolate ruins of a once-great kingdom, now a battlefield strewn with mangled bodies and torn limbs under the shadow of a towering cosmic horror.', 'An oppressive silence, broken only by the wet, grisly sounds of the deity moving through the carnage.', 'The overwhelming stench of death, decay, and spilled blood.', 'Cold, damp stone of the ruins mixed with the grim texture of gore and mud underfoot.', 'A domain of absolute terror and grim finality, where fear and respect are synonymous. There is a sense of ancient horror clashing with a modern, war-torn world.', 148, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:39:40.94263-05', '2026-02-27 15:39:40.94263-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (155, 'Desolate Ruins of the City', 'exterior', 'A city landscape marked by desolate ruins, where everyday mortal life continues amidst decay.', 'The distant, muffled sounds of a city unaware of the supernatural.', 'The smell of dust and old stone.', 'A cool, indifferent air.', 'An atmosphere of alienation and melancholy, where past grandeur (the ruins) and present power (the King) go completely unnoticed.', 149, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:40:33.526624-05', '2026-02-27 15:40:33.526624-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (156, 'Narrator''s Home Office/Living Room', 'interior', 'A room that serves as both a workspace and living area, characterized by the glow of monitors, stacks of paper invoices, and a couch.', 'The scene begins with a sharp, frustrated voice, which is later replaced by the sounds of YouTube videos.', NULL, NULL, 'The atmosphere shifts dramatically from tense and frustrating due to work pressures to one of creative excitement and familial bonding.', 150, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:41:23.233013-05', '2026-02-27 15:41:23.233013-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (157, 'Narrator''s Home Lab/Office', 'interior', 'A room dominated by an Infinitron console and a large monitor. A doorframe connects it to the rest of the house, implying a dedicated but integrated workspace.', 'The low, persistent hum of the Infinitron console and other electronics.', 'A faint, sterile smell of ozone from active high-powered electronics, possibly mixed with the scent of stale coffee.', NULL, 'Tense and intellectually charged, a mix of creative fervor, sleep deprivation, and the underlying terror of the project''s apocalyptic potential.', 151, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:42:14.087149-05', '2026-02-27 15:42:14.087149-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (160, 'Suffocating Office', 'interior', 'A bleak, sterile office space illuminated by the sickly, flickering glow of fluorescent lights. Rows of desks with computers dominate the area.', 'A constant, low mechanical hum from computers, punctuated by the relentless tapping of keys and the faint, stifled cries of tortured souls.', 'Likely smells of stale air, ozone from electronics, and despair.', 'The unfeeling plastic of a keyboard under one''s fingers; the oppressive, still air.', 'Soulless, suffocating, and bleak. A void-like prison where individuality and power are crushed by mundane, repetitive tasks.', 154, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:45:02.234897-05', '2026-02-27 15:45:02.234897-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (161, 'Narrator''s Cubicle', 'interior', 'A suffocating space with dull, gray walls, cast in the sickly glow of flickering fluorescent lights. The space is dominated by a desk and computer for viewing spreadsheets.', 'The low, oppressive hum of the fluorescent lights and the distant, muted tapping of keyboards.', 'Stale, recycled office air.', 'The cool, smooth surface of the desk and the plastic feel of keyboard keys under fingertips.', 'Oppressive, monotonous, and suffocating. Described by the narrator as a ''gray prison''.', 155, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:45:45.473891-05', '2026-02-27 15:45:45.473891-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (162, 'Narrator''s Office Cubicle', 'interior', 'A mundane office space cast in a sickly yellow hue from flickering fluorescent lights. A glowing computer screen illuminates the narrator''s desk.', 'The furious tapping of keyboard keys, the low hum of computer equipment, and the faint, oppressive buzz of the overhead lights.', 'The stale, recycled air common to corporate environments.', 'The unforgiving, hard metal of a cheap office chair digging into the occupant''s skin.', 'Oppressive and mundane, filled with a growing sense of psychological dread that contrasts sharply with the sterile environment.', 156, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:46:32.702514-05', '2026-02-27 15:46:32.702514-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (163, 'Family Kitchen', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:47:41.342555-05', '2026-02-27 15:47:41.342555-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (164, 'Secret Warehouse Lab', 'interior', 'A corner room in a warehouse, containing the sleek, glowing AutoDoc and a workbench.', 'Initially quiet, then filled with the hum of machinery, primal screams, mechanical banging, and angry yelling.', NULL, 'Sterile environment, soft bedding inside the AutoDoc.', 'Starts as secretive and tense, becomes a crucible of agony, then shifts to one of confrontation and uneasy relief.', 158, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:48:27.36101-05', '2026-02-27 15:48:27.36101-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (165, 'Father''s Lab', 'interior', 'A personal laboratory containing the advanced AutoDoc machine and at least one mirror. It is a space of intense, solitary work.', 'Initially silent, later filled with the imagined ''roar'' of the Infinitron connection, and finally the sound of the lab door opening and his wife''s voice.', NULL, NULL, 'The atmosphere shifts from one of determined ambition and scientific discovery to one of existential terror and cosmic horror, before settling into quiet, reflective calm.', 159, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:49:24.920784-05', '2026-02-27 15:49:24.920784-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (166, 'The Mortal Realm of Chaos', 'other', 'Twisted and contorted forms that strain the eyes to comprehend.', 'A cacophony of sensations and whispers threatening to shatter sanity.', 'The taste and smell of sulfur.', 'The feeling of hot flames licking at the skin.', 'An alien world of incomprehensible chaos, governed by unfamiliar rules and principles that are hostile to a divine being.', 160, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:50:21.105545-05', '2026-02-27 15:50:21.105545-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (167, 'Nightmare Realm of the AutoDoc', 'other', 'A grotesque domain dominated by a towering structure of pulsating flesh and bone. Mangled bodies are scattered about the landscape. A blinding light marks the point of entry.', 'A cacophony of incomprehensible whispers from an unseen source and pained screams echoing from within the central structure.', 'The air is thick with the sickeningly sweet and pervasive stench of decay and rotting flesh.', 'The corrupt atmosphere causes a physical sickness and weakness in supernatural beings.', 'An overwhelming sense of cosmic horror, dread, and insanity. The natural order of life and death feels fundamentally broken here.', 161, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:51:16.120877-05', '2026-02-27 15:51:16.120877-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (168, 'Japan (Kansai/Kyoto)', 'exterior', 'A mix of modern airport infrastructure, the narrow, lantern-lit streets of Kyoto, and serene temples like Kinkaku-ji bathed in golden light.', 'The hum of activity and Japanese announcements at the airport, the buzz of cicadas at night, and the vibrant chaos of markets.', 'The heady aromas of street food.', 'The warm, humid air of a Japanese summer and the physical connection of family embraces.', 'A blend of emotional homecoming, nostalgic reflection, discovery, and the narrator''s burgeoning intellectual obsession.', 162, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:52:21.637217-05', '2026-02-27 15:52:21.637217-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (169, 'Kyoto', 'other', 'Bustling city streets with weathered storefronts, a warm and intimate sushi bar, and a quiet corner in a traditional Japanese house. The sky is painted with sunset hues.', 'The hum of the city, playful laughter, a welcoming exclamation from a chef, and later, the quiet focus of research.', 'A mix of sizzling yakitori, sweet Sakura blossoms, freshly steamed rice, and wasabi.', 'The feeling of holding hands and the warmth of the sun on one''s face.', 'The scene transitions from romantic and nostalgic on the streets, to warm and inspirational in the sushi bar, and finally to quiet, obsessive, and mysterious during the research phase.', 163, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:53:08.481802-05', '2026-02-27 15:53:08.481802-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (170, 'Neko Café', 'interior', 'A small café with wooden walls near the train station, presumably with cats present.', 'A soft murmur of general café activity, which is sharply contrasted by the wife''s raised, trembling voice during the argument.', 'The presumed scent of tea, coffee, and pastries.', NULL, 'Begins as a calm, neutral space for conversation but quickly becomes fraught with tension and intense emotion before settling into a state of fragile resolution.', 164, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:54:00.077071-05', '2026-02-27 15:54:00.077071-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (171, 'Aokigahara Forest', 'exterior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:55:03.069155-05', '2026-02-27 15:55:03.069155-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (172, 'Mother-in-law''s House in Kyoto', 'interior', 'A traditional house with a garden. The interior is dark at night, with long shadows and rooms bathed in a cold, ethereal glow from the moonlight streaming through windows.', 'Very quiet, with only the faint rustle of the wind outside breaking the silence.', NULL, NULL, 'Ostensibly comforting and peaceful, but feels oppressive and thick with expectation to the narrator due to his recent trauma. The moonlight gives it an ethereal quality.', 166, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:56:03.964792-05', '2026-02-27 15:56:03.964792-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (173, 'Mother-in-Law''s House in Japan', 'interior', 'A tranquil room with shoji screens casting delicate patterns on tatami mats. A low table serves as the room''s centerpiece.', 'Quiet, punctuated by whispered conversation and the soft clink of a teacup.', 'The gentle aroma of steaming green tea.', 'The warmth of a teacup against the hands and the smooth, firm texture of tatami mats.', 'Initially tranquil and serene, the atmosphere becomes charged with tension, apprehension, and the weight of a dangerous new idea.', 167, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:57:02.220804-05', '2026-02-27 15:57:02.220804-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (175, 'The Narrator''s Room', 'interior', 'A room where the shadows seem to grow darker and writhe with unseen energy.', 'Filled with the deafening roar of a hell-portal and the sound of whispering ancient secrets on the wind.', NULL, 'A bone-chilling gust of wind sweeps through the space, despite it being indoors.', 'Charged with cosmic terror and the presence of an otherworldly power. The barrier between realities feels thin here.', 169, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 15:59:05.452443-05', '2026-02-27 15:59:05.452443-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (176, 'The Warehouse', 'interior', 'A large, industrial space containing complex machinery. The area is dominated by the shimmering, light-pulsing void of the portal, and later features a scorched patch on the concrete floor.', 'Filled with the ominous, vibrating hum of the quantum stabilizer, which later escalates to a dissonant whine and a deafening roar.', 'The air crackles with the smell of ozone and burnt concrete after the portal''s collapse.', 'The air vibrates from the machinery. The concrete floor is cool to the touch.', 'Tense and charged with a mix of scientific wonder and palpable danger.', 170, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 16:00:11.118498-05', '2026-02-27 16:00:11.118498-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (177, 'The Narrator''s Lab', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 16:00:57.945069-05', '2026-02-27 16:00:57.945069-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (178, 'The Patio at Night', 'exterior', 'A clear night sky full of stars. The scene is furnished with old, worn patio chairs and a telescope.', 'The groaning of the chairs and the quiet dialogue between father and son.', 'The scent of cool night air.', 'The feel of the cool night air settling around them.', 'Intimate, quiet, and educational, fostering a sense of connection and wonder.', 172, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 16:01:50.513606-05', '2026-02-27 16:01:50.513606-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (180, 'The Narrator''s Workshop', 'interior', 'A meticulously arranged workshop filled with scientific equipment, tools, and papers. It is later transformed into a scene of devastation with a gaping hole in one wall, shattered machinery, and debris scattered across the floor.', 'The scene begins with the hum of machinery, escalates to the raging sound of the vortex and a destructive crash, followed by a deafening silence, and later, the sound of approaching police sirens.', 'The smell of ozone from the portal''s activation, followed by the acrid scent of burnt electronics and thick dust from the collapsed wall.', 'A sudden, violent change in air pressure and a powerful wind generated by the vortex.', 'Shifts rapidly from tense anticipation and triumph to sheer terror and desperation, then to nervous deception, and concludes with conflicted introspection.', 174, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 16:03:23.001722-05', '2026-02-27 16:03:23.001722-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (182, 'Wife''s Mother''s Home in Kyoto', 'exterior', 'A familiar backyard bathed in moonlight, with a house and its front door visible. The shimmering ERB gateway stands incongruously in the yard.', 'The sounds of an emotional reunion: a breaking voice, a trembling question in Japanese, and a tearful laugh.', 'The scent of cool night air.', 'The feeling of cool night air on the skin.', 'A magical, surreal, and deeply emotional atmosphere of wonder and familial love.', 176, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 16:05:13.20571-05', '2026-02-27 16:05:13.20571-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (183, 'Abandoned Library', 'interior', 'A dark, suffocating space with shelves of books. The environment becomes chaotic during the summoning, with books crashing down, and later warps and shifts under the narrator''s otherworldly presence.', 'Initially silent, it is filled with the sounds of a howling tempest and a deafening roar during the summoning.', 'The air is stale, filled with the putrid stench of dust and musk from the tome, the scent of ancient knowledge and eldritch energy from the narrator, and the metallic tang of dread.', NULL, 'Begins with an aura of mystery and sinister energy, escalating to one of chaotic power and cosmic terror. Reality itself feels unstable and malleable.', 177, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 16:06:15.207484-05', '2026-02-27 16:06:15.207484-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (184, 'Ravaged City (Vision)', 'exterior', 'A post-apocalyptic landscape of smoldering ruins, collapsed buildings with charred frames like tombstones, and debris-strewn streets. The sun is blotted out by toxic smoke from distant factories.', 'Echoing screams and wails of survivors, punctuated by the distant, constant grinding of massive gears and the shriek of bending metal.', 'The pervasive, acrid smell of smoke and the metallic tang of fear or blood.', 'Vibrations from the distant factories travel through the ground.', 'Oppressive, horrifying, and filled with despair. A sense of inevitable doom and the complete absence of hope.', 178, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 16:07:02.241781-05', '2026-02-27 16:07:02.241781-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (185, 'Narrator''s Home Base / Operations Hub', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:20:25.637792-05', '2026-02-27 19:20:25.637792-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (186, 'Zurich Financial District', 'exterior', 'Cobblestone streets lined with glass skyscrapers reflecting light onto centuries-old cathedrals; prestigious bank facades flanked by designer boutiques; a historic fountain nearby.', 'Hum of efficient public transportation; ambient city sounds.', 'Freshly baked bread, expensive cologne inside banks.', 'Cobblestone underfoot, cold marble inside banks.', 'A nexus of old-world gravitas and modern ambition—initially awe-inspiring, progressively humiliating for the narrator.', 180, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:21:32.423791-05', '2026-02-27 19:21:32.423791-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (187, 'Le Comptoir Secret', 'interior', 'Golden-lit room with vintage leather armchairs, overstuffed bookshelves, weathered wooden sign outside. Empty of other customers.', 'Creaking sign in the breeze, quiet ambient warmth; smooth voice of the proprietor.', 'Buttery croissant and fresh coffee.', 'Heavy wooden door, flaky pastry, warm coffee cup.', 'Manufactured quiet dignity and mystique; deceptively welcoming, designed to lower a visitor''s defenses.', 181, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:22:44.31706-05', '2026-02-27 19:22:44.31706-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (188, 'Old Town Zurich — Ivy Building & Goldman Sachs', 'interior', 'Ivy-covered building with dimly lit artifact-filled interior next door to Goldman Sachs''s imposing stone façade with carved columns, bronze plaques, polished marble floors, gilded ceilings, and a crystal chandelier.', 'Whispers in multiple languages echoing off high gilded ceilings; dramatic theatrical monologue in the first building.', 'Dusty tomes and old artifacts suggest a musty, aged smell in the first room.', 'Cold polished marble underfoot in Goldman Sachs; shoulder pat from the Cloaked Tourist Racketeer.', 'Shifts from theatrical and dim mystery to overwhelming institutional grandeur and financial power.', 182, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:23:59.009867-05', '2026-02-27 19:23:59.009867-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (189, 'Goldman Sachs Office — Herr Müller''s Suite', 'interior', 'Labyrinthine hallways hung with oil paintings and expensive furnishings leading to an oak-paneled private office dominated by an enormous mahogany desk and plush leather chairs.', 'Hushed institutional silence broken only by measured footsteps and clipped, formal conversation.', 'Faint traces of polished wood and leather — the scent of old money and authority.', 'Cool, smooth leather chairs; the weight of social and financial pressure pressing down on the Narrator.', 'Overwhelming wealth and control; the Narrator feels like ''a microscopic fish in a very big, and very expensive, pond.''', 183, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:24:44.029135-05', '2026-02-27 19:24:44.029135-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (190, 'Liam Kaufmann''s Office – Zurich Business District', 'interior', 'Sleek modern office building in Zurich''s bustling business district, contrasting with surrounding traditional architecture. Polished gleaming floors inside; conference room with professional décor.', 'Quiet, professional atmosphere; understated office sounds.', 'Faint smell of leather and fresh coffee.', 'Polished floors underfoot; firm handshakes; cool water bottle.', 'High-stakes confidentiality; calm professionalism masking the gravity of the financial conspiracy being planned within.', 184, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:25:58.74048-05', '2026-02-27 19:25:58.74048-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (191, 'Zurich — Kaufmann Building Office', 'interior', 'A professional office suite within Liam Kaufmann''s Zurich building, furnished for business use and corporate meetings.', 'Quiet office ambiance punctuated by the shuffling of paperwork and corporate discussions.', 'Neutral office environment, faintly corporate.', 'Clean, formal surfaces; the weight of reams of legal documentation.', 'Businesslike and methodical, tinged with the exhaustion of daily intercontinental commuting and the gravity of managing a global entity.', 185, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:27:27.353131-05', '2026-02-27 19:27:27.353131-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (192, 'Frozen Tomb of Europa', 'interior', 'A vast subterranean ice chamber deep beneath Europa''s surface, its tunnels shattering into crystal shards scattering like stars upon the entity''s release.', 'Deep tremors growing into guttural roars, drilling machinery echoing through ice walls, screams, and finally an otherworldly shatter-roar.', 'Frigid sterile cold and iron-tainted blood filling the chamber post-slaughter.', 'Encasing, constricting ice giving way to explosive crystalline fragmentation; biting cold on every surface.', 'Timeless, oppressive silence fractured into cosmic carnage — a millennia-old prison turned apocalyptic awakening ground.', 186, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:28:40.312583-05', '2026-02-27 19:28:40.312583-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (193, 'Frozen Alien Planet', 'exterior', 'Ancient frozen world with a vast icy surface torn and mangled by metallic colony structures; eerie pulsing light from alien technology; dome shattering into thousands of glistening shards.', 'Deafening roars from colony machinery; shattering ice; screams of colonists; a cosmic song only the entity can hear.', 'Stench like rotting flesh near the cavern mouth; toxic fumes from colony structures.', 'Frozen, cracking ice shifting underfoot; the tearing sensation of reality rending.', 'Ancient, defiled, and apocalyptic; a sacred frozen domain violated by human technology, culminating in total destruction as the entity tears a rift through space.', 187, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:29:52.368815-05', '2026-02-27 19:29:52.368815-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (194, 'Cosmic Approach to Earth', 'exterior', 'The vast cosmic void with Earth as a distorted blue marble; clouds and a grotesque landscape below upon breach.', 'A haunting cosmic tune that crescendos into deafening screams and wails.', NULL, 'The sensation of hurtling through space, sanity slipping with each passing second.', 'Overwhelming dread and inevitability; a descent from cosmic solitude into earthly nightmare.', 188, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:31:10.357686-05', '2026-02-27 19:31:10.357686-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (195, 'Narrator''s Private Office/Study', 'interior', 'A personal workspace with a screen displaying an email notification, intimate and unassuming in contrast to the monumental news it delivers.', 'Near silence, broken only by the digital blink of a notification and the narrator''s internal monologue.', NULL, 'Trembling hands on a keyboard or mouse as the narrator opens the pivotal email.', 'Quiet and private, charged with the weight of historic consequence and the deliberate shield of secrecy.', 189, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:32:15.870282-05', '2026-02-27 19:32:15.870282-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (196, 'Narrator''s Kitchen', 'interior', 'A family kitchen with a table where the three family members sit for breakfast; domestic and warmly lit.', 'Laughter, conversation, the clatter of chopsticks on a rice bowl.', 'Coffee, cooked rice — warm breakfast smells.', 'A reassuring hand on an arm; fiddling with a ring; arms thrown in the air.', 'Casual domestic warmth undercut by the Narrator''s private unease about wealth and shadowy power.', 190, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:32:59.228789-05', '2026-02-27 19:32:59.228789-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (197, '1400 Smith Street, Houston, Texas', 'exterior', 'A gleaming, towering skyscraper dominating the Houston skyline, exuding grandeur and sophistication.', 'The hum of a vibrant city economy, distant traffic, urban ambiance.', 'Steel, glass, and urban air of a prosperous city.', 'The imposing weight of a monumental structure; polished surfaces and urban concrete.', 'Ambition, triumph, and the dawn of physical empire—a symbol of limitless potential made real.', 191, 'claude', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', '2026-02-27 19:34:24.735892-05', '2026-02-27 19:34:24.735892-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (93, 'The Narrator''s Office', 'interior', 'A personal office containing a desk with a PC setup. There is also a closet or storage area filled with boxes of old electronic parts.', 'The quiet hum of a computer, later joined by the resonant hum of the crystal.', 'The faint smell of dust from old components.', 'The cool surface of a desk or keyboard; the narrator''s own trembling hands.', 'A space of focused work and intellectual curiosity, which becomes tense with anticipation and discovery as the experiment progresses.', 87, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 14:43:56.362107-05', '2026-02-27 19:35:45.099107-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (203, 'Family Living Room (Florida)', 'interior', 'A comfortable living room featuring a couch and a favorite armchair with worn cloth arms. The room is illuminated by the flickering light of a TV. A tile floor is visible.', 'Initially peaceful and quiet, later filled with the sounds of conversation and the squeak of sneakers on tile.', NULL, 'The feeling of sinking into soft couch cushions and the texture of worn cloth on an armchair.', 'A sanctuary of peace after a chaotic day, which becomes a space for excited brainstorming, cautious debate, and strategic family planning.', 194, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:39:52.734381-05', '2026-02-27 19:39:52.734381-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (204, 'Houston Meeting Room (S Corp HQ)', 'interior', 'A professional meeting room within the S Corp headquarters, likely featuring a large table and chairs for executives.', 'Initially buzzing with quiet tension, falling silent during the test, and later erupting with excited voices and buzzing phones.', 'The faint scent of coffee.', 'A tense, thick atmosphere that gives way to electric excitement.', 'Starts as a high-stakes environment filled with skepticism and curiosity. It transforms dramatically into one of disbelief, excitement, and immense possibility.', 195, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:40:35.865132-05', '2026-02-27 19:40:35.865132-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (206, 'Ancient Temple (Zambia)', 'exterior', 'A colossal, ancient temple with stones etched with forgotten stories, recently unearthed from the Zambian earth. Signs of modern, heavy construction are nearby.', 'The relentless clang of distant construction contrasts with an ancient silence that feels like ''whispers of time''.', 'The smell of freshly turned earth and ancient, dry stone.', 'The air is thick with a palpable, overwhelming energy that feels both unnerving and beckoning.', 'Mysterious, ancient, and filled with a potent energy that promises secrets and power but also hints at unseen danger.', 197, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:42:29.884905-05', '2026-02-27 19:42:29.884905-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (292, 'S Corp Command Center', 'interior', 'Alive with activity, featuring glowing screens with maps, diagrams, and live intelligence feeds. There is a central console and a tactical display.', 'The room buzzes with activity.', 'A sterile scent of climate-controlled air and running electronics.', 'The air is described as charged and suffocating with tension.', 'Filled with palpable tension and the weight of impending doom, like a storm cloud hanging over everyone.', 283, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 16:46:19.470878-05', '2026-02-28 17:40:22.326711-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (207, 'The Cursed Temple', 'transitional', 'An ancient excavation site with ruins that twist and contort unnaturally. The interior contains blood-soaked altars, mangled corpses, and twisted creatures, all shrouded in a thick, living mist.', 'The whispers of long-dead priests chanting inside one''s mind.', 'A heavy, suffocating stench of decay and death.', 'The feeling of thick, snake-like tendrils of mist wrapping around one''s limbs.', 'Oppressive, maddening, and corrupting. A place of ancient, malevolent power that actively seeks to consume visitors.', 198, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:43:10.473409-05', '2026-02-27 19:43:10.473409-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (209, 'The Malevolent Temple', 'interior', 'Stygian darkness punctuated by chambers with grotesque murals depicting unspeakable rituals. Hieroglyphs ooze vile ichor and artifacts pulse with sickening power.', 'A cacophony of suffering, including hissing from inscriptions and a chorus of anguished screams echoing through the air.', 'The air is thick and putrid with the smell of decay.', 'An oppressive weight, as if from eons of pressure. Surfaces like the blood-stained altar are jagged to the touch.', 'Overwhelmingly malevolent and despairing. The atmosphere is thick with ancient agony and a simmering, sinister energy that heralds doom.', 200, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:44:24.848904-05', '2026-02-27 19:44:24.848904-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (210, 'Tunnels of the Ancient Temple', 'interior', 'A labyrinth of twisting, ancient tunnels, likely carved from stone and shrouded in shadow.', 'Echoes of movement, possibly dripping water, and the unsettling silence between sounds.', 'The smell of damp earth, old stone, and stagnant air.', 'Cool, humid air and the rough texture of the tunnel walls.', 'Oppressive, mysterious, and filled with a sense of ancient, foreboding power.', 201, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:45:09.869285-05', '2026-02-27 19:45:09.869285-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (211, 'Heart of the Temple', 'interior', 'A central chamber containing a single, large orb that pulses with an otherworldly light.', 'A low, resonant hum synchronized with the orb''s pulsations.', 'The scent of ozone and ancient dust, charged with static energy.', NULL, 'Heavy and oppressive, charged with a malevolent, primordial power that inspires both terror and an irresistible compulsion.', 202, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:45:42.313762-05', '2026-02-27 19:45:42.313762-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (212, 'MOM (The Mountains of Madness) Facility', 'interior', 'A massive, sprawling subterranean complex carved from unyielding Antarctic stone and ice. Chambers are filled with trailblazing equipment, pulsating machinery, and shimmering energy fields, all connected by a network of tunnels.', 'A constant, low hum of advanced machinery and Eternal Engines. This is punctuated by the sharp crackle of electricity during the experiment, followed by haunting, otherworldly sounds from the gateway.', 'A sterile, metallic scent of new construction and ozone from high-energy equipment.', 'The air is controlled but grows heavy and unnaturally twisted during the gateway activation. A palpable cold emanates from the portal, distinct from the facility''s ambient temperature.', 'Begins with a feeling of pioneering innovation and secret ambition. This atmosphere shifts dramatically to one of cosmic horror, dread, and grim purpose after the failed experiment reveals a terrifying new threat.', 203, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:46:45.904175-05', '2026-02-27 19:46:45.904175-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (214, 'The Antarctic Secondary Habitat', 'interior', 'A luxurious, modern community with panoramic windows showing icy landscapes, contrasted with interiors that can be digitally transformed into beaches or cities. It features pools with holographic trees, neon-lit bowling alleys, art studios, and pristine sports fields.', 'The hum of advanced environmental systems, the sounds of recreation (splashing in pools, bowling balls striking pins), and the collaborative buzz from workstations and labs.', 'Clean, filtered air, perhaps with faint, pleasant scents engineered by the climate control system.', 'A perpetual, comfortable springtime temperature, shielded from the bitter cold outside. The feel of luxury materials and high-tech surfaces.', 'A blend of focused innovation and balanced community life. It feels like a self-contained utopia, both a sanctuary and a gilded cage designed for maximum productivity and isolation.', 205, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:48:39.743312-05', '2026-02-27 19:48:39.743312-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (213, 'MOM Research Facility', 'interior', 'Initially sterile, clinical hallways that transform into a vibrant, bustling hive of scientific activity, filled with advanced computers, fabrication units, and parts of the ERB gateway apparatus.', 'The low, constant hum of powerful machinery and environmental systems, punctuated by the excited chatter of scientists making breakthroughs.', 'The clean, filtered-air smell of a laboratory mixed with the faint scent of ozone from high-energy equipment.', 'Cool, controlled temperatures and smooth, metallic surfaces.', 'An atmosphere charged with intense focus, intellectual fervor, and the thrill of unprecedented discovery. A palpable sense of making history is present.', NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:47:44.670411-05', '2026-02-27 19:49:25.598046-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (216, 'Lunar Base Meeting Room', 'interior', 'A sterile, functional meeting room on a lunar base. A large viewport likely shows the stark, grey lunar landscape and the distant, blue-and-white marble of Earth.', 'The low hum of life support systems, punctuated by the tense silence between speakers.', 'Filtered, recycled air with a faint metallic tang.', 'Cool, smooth surfaces of the meeting table and chairs.', 'Desperate and tense. The atmosphere is heavy with the weight of a monumental and ethically fraught decision.', 207, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:50:15.854918-05', '2026-02-27 19:50:15.854918-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (217, 'Off-world Colonies', 'other', 'A network of hidden cities thriving beneath the surfaces of the Moon and Mars, with bustling corridors and advanced infrastructure. Recently, some surface structures have become visible.', 'The vast silence of space outside, contrasted with the sounds of bustling, technologically advanced societies within.', NULL, NULL, 'A dynamic atmosphere of electrifying collaboration and limitless potential, undercut by the growing tension of imminent discovery.', 208, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:51:09.253327-05', '2026-02-27 19:51:09.253327-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (218, 'The Narrative Void', 'other', 'An abstract, formless space defined by shadows, the conceptual weight of eons, and the cracks of forgotten lore. It is not a physical place but a state of being for the narrator.', 'The sound of whispers, the rustle of turning pages of forgotten books, and the echoes of madmen''s frenzied musings.', 'The faint, musty scent of ancient paper and dust.', NULL, 'Oppressive, ancient, and filled with a sense of immense, guarded power and profound secrecy.', 209, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:52:02.765187-05', '2026-02-27 19:52:02.765187-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (248, 'Trailer Park', 'other', 'A residential community of trailers. The scene begins inside Stacey''s trailer, which is mundane enough for muddy footprints to be a major anomaly.', 'The typical quiet sounds of a morning in a residential area.', 'The faint smell of damp earth from the muddy footprints inside the trailer.', 'The cool morning air, the feel of a phone screen under Stacey''s fingers.', 'Begins as mundane and normal, but shifts to an atmosphere of underlying mystery and unease as the shared strange experience is revealed.', 239, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:19:55.923305-05', '2026-02-27 20:19:55.923305-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (219, 'S Corp Infrastructure', 'other', 'A combination of pristine, high-tech corporate halls and the abstract, intricate digital landscapes of its network. As the scene progresses, it transforms into a labyrinth of distorted corridors and desolate digital wastelands.', 'The low hum of circuits and servers, punctuated by the wail of useless alarms, the defiant hum of error messages, and the whispers of paranoia.', 'A sterile, metallic scent of advanced technology, later tinged with the metaphorical odor of decay and fear.', 'The cold, smooth surfaces of the fortress-like building and the intangible, chilling presence of unseen infiltrators.', 'Initially an impregnable fortress of corporate power and control. It rapidly devolves into a haunted, paranoid, and chaotic prison under siege from within and without.', 210, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:52:45.151065-05', '2026-02-27 19:52:45.151065-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (220, 'Todd''s Metallic Tube', 'interior', 'A confined, metallic space filled with filth and squalor, described metaphorically as a ''garbage castle''.', 'The scene is dominated by the disembodied, urgent whispers and echoing declarations of I AM.', 'An implied atmosphere of squalor and neglect.', 'The air is described as ''sterile'' when I AM speaks, creating a stark contrast with the surrounding physical filth.', 'Oppressive and squalid, which is abruptly pierced by a powerful, supernatural intrusion that transforms it into a stage for confrontation and destiny.', 211, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:54:09.951423-05', '2026-02-27 19:54:09.951423-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (222, 'The Threshold (Nightmare Realm)', 'other', 'A realm of shifting, twisted landscapes, suffocating darkness, sprawling malevolent cityscapes, and desolate wastelands. It contains grotesque, pulsating structures and is ultimately a formless void from which impossible objects can rise.', 'Humming with the threat of collapse, filled with grotesque whispers, a high-pitched keening, and the screams of malformed creatures in languages not meant for human ears.', NULL, 'Suffocating pressure, like a vice. The feeling of being unraveled and dissolved into formless awareness.', 'Relentless terror and dread. A sense of teetering on the brink of annihilation and transcendence, where reality is frayed and sanity is fragile.', 213, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:56:15.444082-05', '2026-02-27 19:56:15.444082-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (223, 'Dr. On''s Office', 'interior', 'A serene oasis of neutral tones, designed to be calming.', 'Quiet, which only serves to magnify the protagonist''s internal turmoil.', 'A faint scent of lavender.', NULL, 'Intentionally serene and comforting, but feels clinical, artificial, and invalidating to the protagonist.', 214, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:57:19.46887-05', '2026-02-27 19:57:19.46887-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (201, '1400 Smith Street Skyscraper', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:38:11.456659-05', '2026-02-28 17:32:53.680293-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (225, 'The CEO''s Corner Office', 'interior', 'A corner office suite at the top of the S Corp tower. The room is bathed in a harsh, sterile white glow from recessed LED lighting, creating jagged shadows. A desk is chaotically covered in project files, and a couch sits in the room.', 'The space is hushed, dominated by the relentless ticking of a wall clock and the faint, muffled laughter of a child from another room.', 'The damp scent of imminent rain drifts in through a slightly ajar balcony door.', 'A cool breeze from the balcony door.', 'Tense, sterile, and isolating. The atmosphere is heavy with the protagonist''s unease and the external pressure of an approaching storm.', 216, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:59:19.292843-05', '2026-02-27 19:59:19.292843-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (226, 'The Narrator''s Florida Home', 'interior', 'A comfortable family home with a kitchen counter, where family members are gathered with their luggage (backpacks, carry-ons) making final preparations for a trip.', 'The sounds of lighthearted banter, teasing laughter, teenage groans of exasperation, and the zipping of bags.', NULL, 'The feeling of leaning against a kitchen counter, slinging a heavy backpack over a shoulder.', 'Warm, relaxed, and filled with familial affection and gentle humor. The atmosphere is one of happy anticipation for the journey ahead.', 217, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:00:15.326717-05', '2026-02-27 20:00:15.326717-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (227, 'UK Landmarks (London & Stonehenge)', 'exterior', 'The scene transitions from the vibrant, bustling streets of London, filled with iconic architecture and red buses, to the stark, open countryside of Stonehenge, where ancient, jagged monoliths stand under a cloudy sky.', 'The location''s sounds shift from the rhythmic clatter of buses and the cheerful hum of city crowds to the eerie, whispering wind sweeping across the plains of Stonehenge.', 'The scent of a bustling city gives way to the smell of damp grass and cold, ancient stone.', 'The warmth and energy of a city crowd is replaced by a distinct, enveloping chill from the countryside air.', 'Initially intoxicating, charming, and full of life and history. The atmosphere becomes eerie, mesmerizing, and deeply unsettling, charged with ancient mystery and a palpable, otherworldly intention.', 218, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:00:58.520459-05', '2026-02-27 20:00:58.520459-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (228, 'The Vatican', 'interior', 'A labyrinthine complex of hallowed halls, corridors, and courtyards filled with masterpieces. Features include arched ceilings with frescoes, ornate marble columns, gilded altars, solemn statues, and the iconic Sistine Chapel. The grandeur can feel oppressive.', 'Initially filled with the hushed, reverent whispers of tourists. This gives way to an uneasy silence, broken only by the sharp, clipped commands and clicking footsteps of the Swiss Guards.', 'The faint scent of old stone, beeswax from flickering candles, and the dry dust of ages.', 'The air is described as thickening and heavy, creating a palpable pressure on visitors. The unease is described as clinging ''like moist underpants''.', 'Starts as awe-inspiring and overwhelming due to the sheer scale of history and art. It progressively shifts to an unsettling, tense, and menacing atmosphere, as if the location itself is alive, watchful, and hostile.', 219, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:01:50.193074-05', '2026-02-27 20:01:50.193074-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (229, 'India''s Roads', 'transitional', 'A vibrant, chaotic scene featuring a ''kaleidoscope of street vendors'' with stalls full of colorful fruits and fabrics.', 'A ''cacophony'' of road noise.', NULL, 'Intense, 118-degree heat outside the vehicle, contrasted with the cool air conditioning inside.', 'A thrilling mix of wonder, chaos, and beauty, experienced from the comfort of a private car.', 220, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:02:45.227231-05', '2026-02-27 20:02:45.227231-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (230, 'Temple in the Aravalli Foothills', 'interior', 'An ornate temple with carvings, vivid frescoes, and an archway adorned with lotus motifs. Sunlight filters through lattice windows, casting intricate patterns of light and shadow on the cool stone floor.', 'A faint murmur of prayers and chanting echoes in the background.', 'A heady mix of incense and the heavy scent of jasmine.', 'The cool stone of the temple floor.', 'Sacred, alive with ancient stories, and filled with a palpable sense of spiritual significance and mystery.', 221, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:03:44.339838-05', '2026-02-27 20:03:44.339838-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (231, 'The Orient Express (Istanbul Station & Onboard)', 'transitional', 'Polished train carriages gleaming in the golden hues of a setting sun. Opulent interiors feature mahogany paneling, brass accents, and plush seats.', 'A faint hum of voices, the occasional hiss of steam, a sharp and clear train whistle, and the rhythmic hum and clatter of the train in motion.', 'The rich aroma of freshly brewed coffee wafting from the dining car.', 'Plush seats and the subtle vibrations of the train''s engine.', 'Begins with an air of anticipation and timeless romance, feeling almost otherworldly. It later becomes tense, mysterious, and oppressive after the encounter with R.', 222, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:04:53.740829-05', '2026-02-27 20:04:53.740829-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (233, 'Protagonist''s Home and Dream Library', 'transitional', 'The scene begins in a dim, ordinary home before transitioning to a massive, dream-like library with polished floors, towering shelves of ancient tomes, and a glowing golden thread of light weaving through the air.', 'The scene starts with the protagonist''s gasping and pounding heart, followed by the sounds of a frantic search, before shifting to the solemn silence of the library, punctuated by faint, echoing footsteps.', 'The scent of aged parchment fills the air within the Dream Library.', 'The air in the library is charged and humming with energy. The grimoire''s worn leather cover radiates warmth.', 'Starts as tense, urgent, and desperate. It transitions into a surreal, mysterious, and revelatory atmosphere within the dreamscape, tinged with a sense of potential and danger.', 224, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:06:38.140904-05', '2026-02-27 20:06:38.140904-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (234, 'The Dreamscape', 'other', 'A shifting, multi-layered reality. The lower realm is a shadowy place of coexisting beauty and terror, while the higher realms are mesmerizing, surreal landscapes of pulsing celestial bodies and vibrant, logic-defying worlds.', 'Unspecified, likely ranging from unsettling silence in the lower realm to abstract, harmonious sounds in the higher realms.', NULL, NULL, 'Highly variable and fragile. The lower portion is thick with dread and malevolence. The higher portion is filled with a mixture of awe, surreal elegance, and unnerving truth.', 225, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:07:34.08999-05', '2026-02-27 20:07:34.08999-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (235, 'Dreamscape Summit', 'exterior', 'A treacherous, jagged peak piercing stormy skies, bathed in a pulsing, otherworldly light that transforms into a sinister void portal. The surrounding area is part of a larger dreamscape with haunted forests and cities of impossible geometry.', 'The howling winds of the stormy skies and the eventual echoes of the protagonist''s screams.', NULL, 'The sharp, jagged faces of the cliffs are raw to the touch. The air is charged with void energy.', 'Initially promising and powerful, it rapidly shifts to one of cosmic dread, terror, and overwhelming hostility.', 226, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:08:16.383368-05', '2026-02-27 20:08:16.383368-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (236, 'The Shadowed Training Realm', 'other', 'A foreboding, shadowed expanse within the dreamscape, described as a delicate balance of light and shadow.', 'An oppressive silence, occasionally broken by Lady A''s melodic voice or haunting laughter.', NULL, NULL, 'Brimming with danger and possibility, a blend of allure and dread that is both comforting and unnerving.', 227, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:09:10.308532-05', '2026-02-27 20:09:10.308532-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (237, 'Lady I''s Domain', 'other', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:10:08.371111-05', '2026-02-27 20:10:08.371111-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (238, 'The Oracle''s Antechamber', 'interior', 'A serene, timeless space that feels disconnected from ordinary reality. The air seems to shimmer with latent energy, and the boundaries of the room are soft and indistinct, suggesting a place that is both real and dreamlike.', 'A profound quiet, punctuated only by the melodic resonance of Madam O''s voice and the thoughtful tones of Lady I.', 'A faint, clean scent, like ozone after a storm or ancient parchment.', 'The air is still and holds a palpable weight, as if thick with unspoken knowledge and cosmic significance.', 'An atmosphere of deep reverence, revelation, and burgeoning purpose. It is a place for the sharing of world-altering secrets.', 229, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:11:04.575326-05', '2026-02-27 20:11:04.575326-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (241, 'Madam O''s Chamber', 'other', 'A plane of bookshelves stretching infinitely in all directions, located within Lady I''s realm. The vast space is illuminated by an otherworldly glow, and symbols dance and shift in the air with an incomprehensible logic.', 'A profound silence, punctuated only by Madam O''s voice, which is described as being as steady as the pulse of the cosmos.', NULL, NULL, 'Serene, ancient, and filled with immense wisdom. The atmosphere is both commanding and labyrinthine, suggesting infinite knowledge that defies mortal comprehension.', 232, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:13:53.489482-05', '2026-02-27 20:13:53.489482-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (199, 'The Narrator''s Kitchen', 'interior', 'A family kitchen during breakfast. A table is set with bowls of rice and coffee. The morning light filters in.', 'The quiet sounds of a family breakfast, punctuated by conversation, laughter, and the clinking of chopsticks.', 'The smell of coffee and cooked rice.', 'The warmth of a coffee mug, the smooth surface of the kitchen table.', 'The atmosphere begins as light, humorous, and domestic, but gradually shifts to become more contemplative and tinged with a sense of foreboding as the conversation deepens.', 190, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 19:36:31.08963-05', '2026-02-27 20:15:01.787245-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (244, 'Kaelen''s Bedroom', 'interior', 'A room with a bed, where Kaelen sits up to wrestle with his thoughts and scans the empty space for the source of a voice.', 'Initially silent, allowing for concentration, but later filled with a disembodied, reverberating voice that seems to come from nowhere.', NULL, 'The feeling of bedsheets as Kaelen sits up.', 'Starts as a space of determined ambition, shifts to one of intense frustration, and then becomes eerie and unsettling with the arrival of the mysterious voice.', 235, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:16:25.72169-05', '2026-02-27 20:16:25.72169-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (245, 'The Dreamer''s Home', 'interior', 'A domestic setting, primarily a kitchen and a bedroom. The space feels normal but is charged with emotional energy.', 'The sharp tones of an argument, followed by a conspicuous, stinging silence, and later the quiet of early morning.', 'The smell of coffee in the morning, masking the lingering tension.', NULL, 'The atmosphere shifts dramatically from mundane frustration to palpable tension during the argument, then to strained silence and overwhelming, private guilt.', 236, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:17:29.039812-05', '2026-02-27 20:17:29.039812-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (246, 'Florida Man''s Dreamscape', 'other', 'A surrealist fever dream where scaly creatures wage war, swamps swirl with stormy emotions, and trees have voices. The landscape is chaotic and dark, later transforming into a tranquil pond under clear skies.', 'The croaking insults from trees, the bellowing of giant alligators, thunderous commands that ripple through the air, and venomous growls.', 'The damp, earthy smell of a swamp mixed with the scent of ozone from emotional storms.', 'Humid, wet, and chaotic energy pervading the air.', 'Initially consumed by rage, jealousy, and violence. It shifts dramatically to become tranquil, calm, and contemplative.', 237, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:18:12.934201-05', '2026-02-27 20:18:12.934201-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (247, 'Sleepy Trailer Park', 'exterior', 'A trailer park with a central clearing, bathed in the eerie, cold blue glow of a low-hanging moon. The distant silhouette of an airport is visible to the north.', 'Initially quiet, then filled with the sound of many shuffling feet, followed by a profound, oppressive silence, and finally returning to quiet.', NULL, 'The air crackles with an unseen energy. Todd''s chest is drenched in sweat.', 'Mysterious, tense, and supernatural. A feeling of dread and compulsion hangs in the air.', 238, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:19:11.399424-05', '2026-02-27 20:19:11.399424-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (250, 'MOM Facility, Antarctica', 'interior', 'A bustling, sterile research facility with bright lab lights and holographic displays. It contains various labs and a massive, transformed testing chamber for stress trials.', 'The hum of advanced machinery and the focused conversations of scientists and engineers.', 'Clean, sterile air, possibly with a faint metallic or ozone scent from the equipment.', 'A frigid, cold ambient temperature from the Antarctic surroundings, contrasting with the warmth generated by the facility''s internal systems.', 'A palpable sense of innovation, enthusiasm, and focused ambition towards a grand goal.', 241, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:21:21.509033-05', '2026-02-27 20:21:21.509033-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (251, 'S Corp Headquarters Conference Room', 'interior', 'A sleek, modern conference room within a bustling corporate skyscraper, centered around a large table where the leadership team is gathered.', 'The grave, hushed tones of a crisis meeting, punctuated by moments of tense silence and then a heated, strategic debate.', NULL, 'The cool, sterile air of a corporate environment.', 'Begins with an aura of grave tension and high stakes, which shifts to cautious intrigue and finally to one of firm, unified resolve.', 242, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:22:13.658445-05', '2026-02-27 20:22:13.658445-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (252, 'Tanzanian Savanna', 'exterior', 'A wild, rugged savanna with golden grasses blurring past. The landscape is bathed in the warm glow of a setting sun.', 'The crackle of voices from a Zoom call contrasting with the sounds of the all-terrain vehicle moving through the wilderness.', 'The faint, earthy scent of dry grass and dust kicked up by the vehicle.', 'The gentle jostling of the ride over rugged terrain and the warmth of the evening air.', 'Vast, beautiful, and contemplative. The natural serenity provides a stark contrast to the high-stakes, futuristic debate taking place.', 243, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:23:10.823479-05', '2026-02-27 20:23:10.823479-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (253, 'Dr. S''s Home', 'interior', 'A cozy and organized home, with a living room displaying neatly arranged school supplies.', 'The hum of the house, mingled with sounds of online gaming (rapid typing, muffled exclamations, laughter).', 'A comforting aroma of Mapo-tofu wafting from the kitchen.', 'The warmth of home, contrasting with the sterile work environment.', 'Grounding, warm, and filled with the simplicity of family life. It serves as a sanctuary from the pressures of Dr. S''s work.', 244, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:24:08.058684-05', '2026-02-27 20:24:08.058684-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (254, 'Aditi''s Family Apartment', 'interior', 'A cramped apartment in Mumbai, featuring a kitchen and a small dining area with a table. The family uses steel plates for their meals.', 'The mother''s voice calling, the sizzle of onions in a pan, the clinking of steel plates, and frequent, warm laughter.', 'The aroma of spices, curry, and cooking onions, mingled with the scent of street food drifting in from outside.', 'The warmth of the kitchen from the cooking stove.', 'Initially a place of tired obligation for Aditi, it quickly transforms into a warm, comforting, and loving environment filled with humor and familial connection.', 245, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:25:10.009804-05', '2026-02-27 20:25:10.009804-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (255, 'Streets of Mumbai at Night', 'exterior', 'The streets are eerily still, a stark contrast to their usual chaos. They are bathed in the sepia glow of sodium streetlights, which cast long, dancing shadows. The scene includes residential streets and the area near a large, silent train station.', 'The usual cacophony is replaced by a subdued hum and an eerie stillness. The only sounds are the faint buzzing of static and the collective, silent shuffling of the crowd.', NULL, 'The air is described as warm, but grows heavier and charged with an unseen energy during the event.', 'The atmosphere is uncanny and surreal. A sense of tension and otherworldliness pervades the scene, amplified by the silent, synchronized movements of the crowd.', 246, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:25:51.408193-05', '2026-02-27 20:25:51.408193-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (256, 'Aditi''s School', 'interior', 'A typical school environment where students gather between classes. The main visual focus is the small, bright screen of Aditi''s phone, drawing the friends into a tight circle.', 'The background hum of student chatter, punctuated by the incessant buzzing of Aditi''s phone and the friends'' exclamations, all of which is cut short by the sharp ring of the school bell.', NULL, NULL, 'Starts with casual curiosity which quickly escalates to a tense and intriguing atmosphere as the group debates the mysterious video. The air is thick with questions and theories.', 247, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:26:37.326805-05', '2026-02-27 20:26:37.326805-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (257, 'Friends'' Research Hub', 'interior', 'A casual, cluttered space, likely a living room or bedroom, dominated by the glow of phone and laptop screens. Old library books and papers are likely strewn about.', 'A mix of excited whispers, skeptical scoffs, the rhythmic tapping of keyboards, and the occasional silence of deep thought.', 'The faint scent of takeout food and old books.', 'The cool surface of a phone screen, the warmth from a laptop, the worn pages of a library book.', 'Intense and collaborative, buzzing with the energy of discovery, debate, and growing unease. It''s a sanctuary for the friends against the world''s disbelief.', 248, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:27:23.550079-05', '2026-02-27 20:27:23.550079-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (258, 'Antarctic Research Facility (MOM)', 'interior', 'A sprawling lab with walls lined with complex diagrams, mathematical equations, and various prototypes. Whiteboards are filled with frantic sketches and calculations. A model of the Space Elevator''s anchor platform sits on a table.', 'The facility buzzes with an undercurrent of urgency. During brainstorming, the room ignites with energy, humming with focused intensity and the sound of many voices. This is punctuated by the loud snap of a prototype cable failing a stress test.', 'The sterile scent of clean-room electronics mixed with the faint, sharp smell of ozone from overworked machinery and the aroma of stale coffee.', 'The environment outside is described as having a biting cold, which contrasts with the focused, high-energy heat of the interior lab.', 'Intense, high-stakes, and oscillating between daunting frustration and energized, collaborative innovation. There is a palpable sense of racing against impossible odds.', 249, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:28:23.734349-05', '2026-02-27 20:28:23.734349-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (259, 'Antarctic Research Facility Lunch Room', 'interior', 'A room with composite walls that shake from the wind, containing at least one small lunch table. The interior is a stark contrast to the harsh exterior.', 'The constant roaring and howling of the wind outside, contrasted with the indoor sounds of conversation, laughter, and the hum of facility equipment.', 'The comforting aroma of hot coffee and fried bologna.', 'A feeling of warmth and safety, defying the icy cold of the Antarctic tundra just outside the walls.', 'A blend of camaraderie, nostalgia, and intense intellectual energy. The atmosphere shifts from lighthearted reminiscence to a fiery, high-stakes debate on innovation.', 250, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:29:16.283956-05', '2026-02-27 20:29:16.283956-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (260, 'S Corp Headquarters', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:30:06.219304-05', '2026-02-27 20:30:06.219304-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (261, 'S Corp Lab', 'interior', 'A clean, functional laboratory environment, suggested by the mention of a ''sterile ceiling''.', 'Quiet, allowing for a serious and private conversation.', NULL, NULL, 'Tense and strategic. The air is thick with the weight of secrets and high-stakes decisions.', 252, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:31:06.637678-05', '2026-02-27 20:31:06.637678-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (278, 'Global Night', 'exterior', 'A still, quiet night across the world, with the tall, silent forms of the Pointers standing as sentinels.', 'Initially silent, the atmosphere is shattered by a sudden, deafening screech that rumbles through the air.', NULL, 'The air itself seems to vibrate with the force of the screech.', 'The mood shifts abruptly from tranquil vigilance to shocking, widespread alarm and confusion.', 269, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:44:32.76849-05', '2026-02-27 20:44:32.76849-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (262, 'S Corp Conference Room', 'interior', 'A modern corporate meeting room, centered around a large conference table. At least one laptop is present, its screen glowing with data.', 'A background ''din'' of conversation that gives way to focused declarations and excited brainstorming. The scene ends with a shout and the sound of hands clapping.', NULL, 'The cool, smooth surface of the conference table.', 'Starts with focused strategic intent, quickly builds to an ''infectious energy'' of creative collaboration, and culminates in a sense of shared purpose and challenge.', 253, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:31:46.265936-05', '2026-02-27 20:31:46.265936-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (263, 'Space Elevator Assembly Site', 'exterior', 'The base of a colossal, gleaming tower that stretches up into the heavens until its summit is no longer visible. The site is bathed in the golden glow of the late afternoon sun.', 'The quiet hum of a completed project, punctuated only by soft, awe-filled voices.', 'Faint scents of ozone, metal, and newly settled dust.', 'The warmth of the late afternoon sun on the skin.', 'A palpable sense of monumental achievement, ambition, and awe for the future.', 254, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:32:33.456793-05', '2026-02-27 20:32:33.456793-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (264, 'S Corp Internal Email Server', 'other', 'Digital text displayed on a screen, formatted as corporate emails with subject lines, sender/recipient information, and timestamps.', 'The low hum of computer hardware.', NULL, 'The cool, smooth surface of a keyboard and mouse.', 'Celebratory and optimistic, charged with a sense of shared accomplishment and forward momentum.', 255, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:33:32.630472-05', '2026-02-27 20:33:32.630472-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (266, 'S Corp''s Internal Network', 'other', 'Text-based interface of an email client, displaying corporate branding. Black text on a white background, with standard email headers (From, To, Date, Subject).', 'The faint, occasional sound of keyboard clicks or notification chimes from a user''s perspective.', NULL, NULL, 'Professional but informal. A sense of routine corporate communication punctuated by a moment of absurdity and scientific excitement.', 257, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:34:36.900961-05', '2026-02-27 20:34:36.900961-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (265, 'S Corp Digital Comms', 'other', 'The scene is presented as a standard corporate email interface, with a subject line, sender, recipient, date, and body text.', 'The silence of reading text on a screen.', 'None.', 'The smooth, cool surface of a screen or the press of keyboard keys.', 'Corporate, official, and informative, with a deliberately lighthearted and casual tone to improve employee engagement.', 256, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:34:07.024254-05', '2026-02-27 20:35:09.634095-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (268, 'Rain-Swept Urban Alley', 'exterior', 'A dark, rain-soaked environment with sparse, flickering lights reflecting off wet surfaces. Ancient, rusted metal structures like fire escapes or scaffolding loom in the background.', 'The constant drumming of a heavy downpour, punctuated by distant, indistinct city sounds and ominous shrieks passing overhead.', 'The smell of wet pavement (petrichor) mixed with a metallic tang from the old structures.', 'Cold, driving rain soaking everything. A damp chill permeates the air.', 'Oppressive, confusing, and isolating. A sense of dread and unseen menace hangs in the air, which later becomes chaotic and surreal.', 259, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:36:05.953244-05', '2026-02-27 20:36:05.953244-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (269, 'Elysium Orbital Ring Viewing Deck', 'interior', 'An opulent yet purposefully restrained conference space with a large viewing window showing Earth suspended in the blackness of space.', 'Deafening silence, punctuated by the hum of the space elevator doors and the faint whir of unseen technology.', NULL, NULL, 'Awe-inspiring, tense, and filled with anticipation. The air feels heavy with the gravity of the impending revelation.', 260, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:37:13.723076-05', '2026-02-27 20:37:13.723076-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (270, 'S Corp Presentation Room', 'interior', 'A room filled with influential people, likely high-tech and formal, where a secret presentation is being held.', 'An ambient hum, which is later filled with murmurs and shocked exclamations from the audience.', NULL, NULL, 'The atmosphere shifts dramatically from one of quiet intrigue and skepticism to palpable, charged silence and collective shock as world-changing truths are revealed.', 261, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:37:57.229941-05', '2026-02-27 20:37:57.229941-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (271, 'S Corp High-Level Briefing Room', 'interior', 'A sophisticated, likely sterile conference room equipped with large screens displaying complex schematics and models. It is occupied by several of the world''s most powerful leaders.', 'The soundscape shifts from pointed, skeptical questions and tense pauses to a low buzz of murmurs and strategic discussion.', NULL, NULL, 'Begins with an air of intense skepticism and political tension, which gradually softens into one of cautious optimism and momentous potential.', 262, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:38:37.251332-05', '2026-02-27 20:38:37.251332-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (272, 'Orbital Conference Chamber', 'interior', 'A sophisticated meeting room aboard a space station, dominated by a large viewport showing Earth as a luminous orb. A holographic schematic of the space elevators is projected in the room''s center.', 'The scene begins with the low murmur of delegates'' voices, which is cut by the sharp, clear tones of the negotiation, and punctuated by moments of heavy, tense silence.', NULL, NULL, 'The atmosphere is thick with political tension and skepticism. It gradually shifts from confrontational to one of cautious consideration and, finally, tentative agreement.', 263, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:39:22.750481-05', '2026-02-27 20:39:22.750481-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (273, 'Orbital Viewing Deck', 'interior', 'A room dominated by a panoramic viewport looking out into space. A complex web of satellites is visible, along with the sinuous arcs of massive space elevators stretching into the void.', 'The quiet, murmured, and reverent tones of the delegates'' voices, with a background hum of advanced technology being implied.', NULL, NULL, 'Awe-inspiring and futuristic. The atmosphere is one of immense scale, potential, and high-stakes diplomacy.', 264, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:40:15.292332-05', '2026-02-27 20:40:15.292332-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (274, 'Delegation Meeting Room', 'interior', 'A formal, likely well-appointed room where representatives from different nations meet. The focus is on a circle of representatives where the narrator stands.', 'The room is initially filled with murmurs, but stills to silence when the narrator speaks. The primary sounds are the voices of the narrator and the delegates.', NULL, 'The air is charged with energy, the tension and stakes palpable. The scene ends with a firm handshake.', 'Tense, high-stakes, and professional. The atmosphere shifts from standard diplomatic discussion to one of awe and disbelief upon hearing S Corp''s proposal.', 265, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:40:52.563712-05', '2026-02-27 20:40:52.563712-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (276, 'Neutral Diplomatic Setting', 'interior', 'A professional, understated space designed to facilitate discussion, likely at a summit or corporate headquarters. The decor is neutral to avoid favoring any party.', 'A low, ambient murmur of other conversations, punctuated by the clear, focused dialogue of the delegates.', 'A clean, sterile scent, perhaps with faint notes of coffee or tea.', 'A climate-controlled, comfortable temperature.', 'Begins with a palpable tension between historical adversaries, which gradually softens into an atmosphere of cautious optimism and professional agreement.', 267, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:42:35.074234-05', '2026-02-27 20:42:35.074234-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (277, 'Global Public Consciousness', 'other', 'A chaotic montage of glowing smartphone screens showing TikTok dances, dark web forums with cryptic text, and flashing 24-hour news tickers.', 'A cacophony of viral audio clips, the frantic drone of AM radio hosts, the murmur of crowds, and the endless pinging of notifications.', NULL, 'The cold, smooth glass of a smartphone screen under a thumb; the low-frequency hum of electronic devices.', 'A volatile and frenzied mix of hysteria, excitement, profound fear, and cynical opportunism.', 268, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:43:29.166633-05', '2026-02-27 20:43:29.166633-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (279, 'Earth (Global View)', 'exterior', 'A planetary sphere transitioning from the darkness of night to the light of dawn. The view is dominated by the sudden appearance of colossal Space Elevators, structures reaching from the surface into the cosmos towards a visible, mythical ring called Elysium.', 'A global cacophony of blaring news reports, buzzing phones, and the collective murmur of billions of human voices reacting with a mix of awe, fear, and confusion.', NULL, 'The transition from the cool, quiet of pre-dawn to the first warmth of a new sun on a world irrevocably changed.', 'Thick with tension, speculation, and a profound sense of historical weight. The atmosphere shifts from confusion and fear to a collective, awestruck realization of a new era for humanity.', 270, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:45:09.254189-05', '2026-02-27 20:45:09.254189-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (280, 'The Orator''s Office', 'interior', 'A spacious office with polished mahogany furniture, exuding sophistication. It is brightly lit by broadcast cameras and features a balcony with a breathtaking view of the sprawling landscape and plaza below.', 'The scene begins with a hushed silence, is filled by the sound of The Orator''s voice, and concludes with the faint rumble of a crowd growing into a deafening, thunderous roar of applause.', 'The scent of fresh ink and crisp paper.', 'A cool, temperature-controlled room. The floor eventually hums faintly with the vibrations of the crowd''s cheers from many stories below.', 'Begins as tense with anticipation and the weight of a historic moment, transitions to inspiring and hopeful during the speech, and ends in a state of overwhelming, shared triumph and validation.', 271, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:46:19.829014-05', '2026-02-27 20:46:19.829014-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (281, 'S Corp Plaza at 1400 Smith Street', 'exterior', 'A plaza beneath a soaring glass skyscraper, featuring massive monitors displaying S Corp broadcasts. The area is filled with a large, diverse crowd of people.', 'The buzz of a large crowd, with a mixture of chatter, and the sound from the broadcast on the monitors.', NULL, 'A charged energy in the air.', 'Volatile and tense, with a mix of awe, hope, unease, and anger simmering within the gathered crowd.', 272, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:47:15.516651-05', '2026-02-27 20:47:15.516651-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (282, 'Space Elevator Viewing Deck', 'interior', 'An area with seats and armrests, presumably with large windows or screens. The interior is impressive and filled with the excited chatter of other passengers.', 'A low hum of excited chatter, a child''s whisper, the crackle of an intercom, and the eventual sounds of the elevator beginning its ascent.', 'A clean, sterile scent of recycled air mixed with the faint, varied perfumes of the passengers.', 'The feeling of a small hand clinging tightly, the texture of an armrest, and the subtle vibration of the elevator starting to move.', 'Charged with anticipation, excitement, and wonder, with an undercurrent of apprehension for the monumental journey ahead.', 273, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:48:32.244877-05', '2026-02-27 20:48:32.244877-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (283, 'Space Elevator Viewing Room', 'transitional', 'A room with panoramic windows framing a view of a receding Earth and the infinite heavens. The interior is polished, with faint streaks of reflected sunlight playing across surfaces.', 'A quiet, precise humming and soft, meditative vibrations.', NULL, 'Soft vibrations from the capsule''s ascent.', 'Surreal, awe-inspiring, and meditative.', 274, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:49:19.783008-05', '2026-02-27 20:49:19.783008-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (284, 'Pluto Hub', 'interior', 'A colossal, bustling space center with corridors illuminated by glowing pathways. It is filled with engineers in sleek uniforms and families with their belongings.', 'A blend of a faint hum from distant machinery and the ambient murmur of many excited voices.', NULL, NULL, 'Futuristic, busy, and charged with a sense of anticipation and departure.', 275, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:49:57.431997-05', '2026-02-27 20:49:57.431997-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (285, 'The Habitat', 'interior', 'The interior of a vessel where the walls are not solid but display a dazzling, infinite-seeming tapestry of stars, nebulae, and galaxies from the surrounding gateway.', 'The excited exclamations of passengers, particularly a young boy named Takashi, overlaying a subtle hum of the vessel''s systems.', 'Clean, sterile, recycled air, characteristic of a sealed, advanced environment.', 'A steady, solid floor, providing a sense of stability amidst the visually overwhelming cosmic journey.', 'A profound sense of wonder, awe, and the weight of a historic, unprecedented moment for humanity.', 276, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:50:41.821161-05', '2026-02-27 20:50:41.821161-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (286, 'Uncharted Alien Planet', 'exterior', 'A vast, shimmering landscape with iridescent blues and golds. Towering crystalline formations refract the azure light from Alnitak, creating a kaleidoscope of colors. The sky is a rich indigo dotted with unfamiliar constellations.', 'From the perspective of the habitat, the world outside is silent.', NULL, NULL, 'Ethereal, wild, and breathtakingly beautiful, as if it''s a place of concentrated cosmic creativity.', 277, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:51:15.613926-05', '2026-02-27 20:51:15.613926-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (287, 'Alien Planet Surface', 'exterior', 'A wild, untamed, yet serene landscape featuring swaying, bioluminescent flora that flickers with rhythmic light.', 'The soft clicking of boots on a metal ramp and joyful laughter.', 'Crisp, cool air with a faint, invigorating tang reminiscent of ozone before a storm.', 'Cool, crisp air against the skin.', 'Electric and invigorating, humming with the vitality of a newly discovered world.', 278, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:51:55.376034-05', '2026-02-27 20:51:55.376034-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (288, 'The Vatican''s Hidden Chamber', 'interior', 'A chamber deep beneath the Vatican, shrouded in shadow and secrecy. Faint, flickering torchlight casts jagged shadows on stone walls, as if darkness itself conspires to swallow the light.', 'A thick, suffocating stillness where each step reverberates. The silence is described as a pregnant pause.', NULL, 'The air is heavy and oppressive. A palpable chill is cast across the room by I AM''s presence.', 'Filled with a palpable dread and crackling tension. It is a room for plotting, not prayer, bearing witness to the gravity of the plans being made.', 279, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:52:51.181884-05', '2026-02-27 20:52:51.181884-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (289, 'Shadowed Labyrinth Beneath the Vatican', 'interior', 'Ancient stone walls that seem to whisper, cast in dim light and deep shadows. Contains a meeting chamber.', 'An oppressive silence, punctuated by the scrape of chairs, shuffling robes, and later, the wet thud of a body falling.', 'Damp stone, ancient dust, and the eventual metallic tang of fresh blood.', 'Cold stone floor.', 'Secretive, tense, and dangerous. A place where dark, world-shaping machinations unfold far from the light of day.', 280, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-27 20:53:43.897003-05', '2026-02-27 20:53:43.897003-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (290, 'Pluto Outpost', 'other', 'A fortified base nestled within Pluto''s icy, meteorite-scarred plains, under a sky filled with a ''twinkling tapestry of stars''.', 'The interior is likely filled with the low hum of life support and computer consoles, contrasting with the profound silence of the exterior.', 'Sterile, recycled air within the base.', 'A controlled, livable temperature inside, starkly contrasted with the bone-chilling -240°C cold outside.', 'A frontier atmosphere of disciplined purpose, anticipation, and underlying tension, standing at the ''precipice of the unknown''.', 281, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 16:44:08.13572-05', '2026-02-28 16:44:08.13572-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (291, 'Elysium Office', 'interior', 'An opulent office located in Elysium, a structure high above the Earth. It features large windows with a view of sprawling spires piercing the heavens and contains advanced technology like a large holo-screen.', 'The tense, clipped tones of advisors discussing a crisis, punctuated by the chime of a computer alert.', NULL, NULL, 'High-stakes and tense. The air is thick with the pressure of managing a global, multi-front war, blending strategic debate with grim reality.', 282, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 16:45:16.775552-05', '2026-02-28 16:45:16.775552-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (294, 'Yukiko''s Room on Sorhhinda', 'interior', 'A room with wooden walls where sunlight is dappled through the leaves of lush, alien foliage outside the window. The room offers a view of the endless expanse of Sorhhinda.', 'A mix of futuristic and alien sounds, including the whirring of hover scooters and the trills of an unfamiliar native bird.', NULL, NULL, 'Initially feels comfortable and familiar, like home, but the scene''s progression reveals an undercurrent of growing tension that permeates the colony.', 285, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 16:48:23.054078-05', '2026-02-28 17:00:43.766725-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (295, 'Outside the Colony Dome', 'exterior', 'A landscape that initially appears serene and harmonious, but is revealed to hold gruesome sights like a giant, glowing spider feasting on a corpse. The scene is a twisted nightmare hidden beneath a peaceful facade.', 'The sound of Yukiko''s carefree laughter, which is abruptly replaced by a horrified silence.', 'A humid air, likely tainted with the smell of decay from the bio-gardener''s corpse.', 'A humid afternoon atmosphere.', 'The atmosphere shifts dramatically from one of playful curiosity and freedom to one of abject terror and sinister revelation.', 286, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 16:49:10.388814-05', '2026-02-28 17:01:40.164761-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (296, 'Colony Center Plaza', 'exterior', 'An open plaza at the center of a town, dominated by the looming, shimmering arch of the ERB Gateway. Shadows flicker across the area, and an overgrown grove of trees is situated nearby.', 'The faint, pulsing hum of the ERB Gateway, overlaid with the hushed, urgent whispers of the conspirators.', NULL, NULL, 'Tense and secretive, heavy with the weight of a looming catastrophe. The area is described as unguarded and vulnerable, especially given the routine nature of daily life happening elsewhere.', 287, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 16:49:45.487062-05', '2026-02-28 17:02:16.5085-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (300, 'Gateway Plaza', 'exterior', 'A stone plaza dominated by a large gateway with a smooth, curved surface. The area is enclosed by a dome, with untamed wilds visible beyond its protective barrier.', 'Initially tense silence, broken by the sounds of sabotage, then the curses of terrorists and the echo of their boots on the stone as they flee.', NULL, 'The feel of cool stone underfoot.', 'Begins with high tension and imminent danger, shifts to chaotic action, and ends with a fleeting sense of relief immediately replaced by suspense and dread.', 288, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:03:05.215709-05', '2026-02-28 17:03:48.96191-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (302, 'Sorhhinda Colony', 'exterior', 'A human settlement on an alien world with a teal sky, protected by a dome and bio-walls. The scene ends with parts of it in ruins.', 'The sounds shift from the hum of machinery to an unsettling silence filled with ominous alien bird chirps, and finally to screams of terror and monstrous screeches.', NULL, 'The air is thick with tension and fear.', 'The atmosphere degrades from fear and confusion to suffocating isolation and dread, culminating in outright terror and destruction.', 290, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:04:30.698348-05', '2026-02-28 17:04:30.698348-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (303, 'The Damaged Colony on Sorhhinda', 'exterior', 'A landscape of smoldering ruins and mangled bio-tech. Survivors have cobbled together makeshift shelters from fallen bio-walls and erected defenses around ravaged gardens.', 'The booming voice of Governor Tanaka rallying survivors, followed by the chaotic sounds of rebuilding and whispers of rebellion.', 'The smell of smoke from the smoldering ruins.', NULL, 'A tense, oppressive atmosphere thrumming with raw, primal dread, yet also containing flickers of hope and a growing sense of solidarity and defiance.', 291, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:05:28.504683-05', '2026-02-28 17:05:28.504683-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (304, 'Sorhhinda', 'exterior', 'An alien world illuminated by the azure light of three suns. The landscape features unique, bioluminescent flora and is scarred by battle, with ruins serving as a playground for children.', 'The sounds of fierce battle, including laser fire and the roars of creatures and people, which later subsides to the whisper of an alien wind.', 'The air carries the scent of fear and desperation during the conflict.', 'The constant presence of an alien wind.', 'Initially a place of promised paradise, it has become a crucible of survival. The atmosphere is tense and dangerous, but shifts to one of grim defiance and nascent hope after the battle.', 292, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:06:20.066266-05', '2026-02-28 17:06:20.066266-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (305, 'Frank''s Apartment (Elysium Space Ring)', 'interior', 'A cramped, windowless apartment described as a ''broom closet,'' located deep within the functional ''guts'' of the space station.', 'Initially, the loud screaming of a custom alarm, followed by the crackle of a comm system.', 'The smell of brewing zero-g coffee mixed with the sterile scent of recycled air.', 'A zero-gravity environment.', 'Claustrophobic, isolating, and mundane, starkly contrasting with the grand, utopian exterior of the space ring.', 293, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:07:22.946997-05', '2026-02-28 17:07:22.946997-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (306, 'Hydroponics', 'interior', 'A facility filled with plant-growing equipment, including a complex filtration system with dripping pipes. The area is under duress, indicated by active alarms.', 'The loud wailing of radiation alarms.', 'Likely a mix of dampness, vegetation, and possibly ozone from the malfunctioning equipment.', 'Dampness from dripping pipes.', 'Tense, chaotic, and urgent due to the radiation leak and Dr. Adler''s panic.', 294, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:08:17.235701-05', '2026-02-28 17:08:17.235701-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (307, 'The Argentinians'' Bakery', 'interior', 'A bakery space, likely with stainless steel counters and baking equipment, but currently in a state of disarray.', 'Jarring, angry shouting in Spanish that clashes with the expected pleasant ambiance of a bakery.', 'A heavenly smell of baking bread and pastries is grotesquely overlaid with a foul ''algae funk''.', NULL, 'Tense and chaotic. The comforting environment of a bakery has been curdled by anger and a mysterious sabotage.', 295, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:09:02.202457-05', '2026-02-28 17:09:02.202457-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (308, 'Cosmic Bowling Alley', 'interior', 'A bowling alley where a malfunction has caused zero-gravity. People and objects, including bowling pins, float uncontrollably. A cosmic cat chases a bowling ball near the ventilation system.', 'The sound of people swearing, followed by a loud ''thunk'' as a bowling ball lands, and then a wave of cheers. A comm device buzzes.', 'The faint smell of burnt duct tape and bowling-ball grease.', NULL, 'Initially chaotic, absurd, and dangerous. It shifts to triumphant relief after the problem is solved.', 296, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:10:22.590156-05', '2026-02-28 17:10:22.590156-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (309, 'Elysium Observation Deck', 'interior', 'An observation deck with a large window made of cold glass, offering a view of the ''endless void of space,'' a serene and empty blackness.', 'The sound of Pete''s voice coming through a comms system, punctuated by Frank''s sighs and pacing footsteps.', NULL, 'The cold touch of the glass window against which Frank leans.', 'Extremely tense and fraught with anxiety. The internal chaos of the characters contrasts sharply with the serene, indifferent void outside.', 297, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:10:53.113677-05', '2026-02-28 23:41:49.981048-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (310, 'TJ''s Office', 'interior', 'An office with a large domed ceiling offering a direct view of Europa''s icy crust. The city lights of New Atlantis refract through the dome, creating a kaleidoscope of blues and whites. The room contains TJ''s desk and his data stream console.', 'The quiet hum of advanced technology, punctuated by the implied pulse of the red indicator on the data stream.', NULL, 'The ambient temperature of the room, which feels colder after Dr. On''s departure.', 'Tense and hollow. The breathtaking external beauty feels like a ''polished veneer hiding rot'', contrasting sharply with TJ''s internal unease.', 298, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:12:16.497076-05', '2026-02-28 17:13:04.202317-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (312, 'New Atlantis', 'exterior', 'A pristine, futuristic city characterized by clean architecture and ubiquitous holographic displays showing serene imagery. This perfection is disrupted by blood-red graffiti and later by shocking propaganda images on all screens.', 'A controlled, quiet ambiance, which is shattered by the silent, jarring appearance of the murals and the sounds of security crackdowns.', 'Sterile, clean air, with no notable scents.', 'Smooth, perfect surfaces of advanced construction materials.', 'The atmosphere shifts from one of enforced, automated serenity to one of palpable tension, rebellion, and fear as the conflict between the Red Hats and S Corp escalates publicly.', 300, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:13:54.2269-05', '2026-02-28 17:13:54.2269-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (313, 'Mumbai Transportation Complex Outskirts', 'exterior', 'Labyrinthine alleys filled with mango sellers and rickshaws, overshadowed by the massive, skeletal structure of the Space Elevator piercing a smog-laced sky. The area is a stark contrast of squalor and high-tech ambition.', 'A chaos of competing sounds: hawking vendors, honking rickshaws, and later, the chants and rhythmic drumming of protesters.', 'The unmentioned but implied smells of a crowded city market: ripe fruit, exhaust fumes, and cooking food.', 'Humid, clinging air.', 'A tense and conflicted atmosphere, blending the vibrant energy of a Mumbai street with the simmering resentment of protest and the awe-inspiring presence of the elevator.', 301, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:15:05.803512-05', '2026-02-28 17:15:05.803512-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (314, 'Elysium Space Ring', 'interior', 'A polished chrome environment with an endless expanse of glass and steel. Sunlight glints off its surfaces, creating a glittering, sterile effect.', 'An artificial hum of perfection permeates the air, punctuated by practiced smiles, rehearsed laughs, and malicious whispers.', 'A sterile, filtered air, lacking the chaotic smells of a place like Mumbai.', 'Cool, smooth, hard surfaces of metal and glass.', 'Feels like a ''polished chrome prison'' rather than a haven. The atmosphere is sterile, judgmental, and suffused with a cutting, unspoken elitism.', 302, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:16:01.236669-05', '2026-02-28 17:16:01.236669-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (315, 'Aditi''s Dorm Room (Elysium)', 'interior', 'A small, sterile dorm room on the orbital city of Elysium. It features a large window with a breathtaking view of Earth below and is equipped with a hologram terminal and a tablet displaying equations.', 'An oppressive silence, filled only by the faint, constant hum of Elysium''s artificial life support systems.', NULL, 'The environment feels cold and unfeeling, contrasting with the intense emotions of the scene.', 'Lonely and isolating. Despite the technological marvels, the room feels like a cage, amplifying Aditi''s feelings of separation and guilt.', 303, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:16:42.307152-05', '2026-02-28 17:16:42.307152-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (316, 'Elysium University''s Research Lab', 'interior', 'A research lab filled with consoles and machinery, dominated by an antique radio telescope. The space is likely dimly lit, suitable for late-night observation.', 'A quiet, rhythmic thrum of machinery, which is suddenly shattered by the sharp crackle of static from a telescope, later replaced by an oppressive silence.', 'The faint scent of ozone from running electronics and old paper from manuals and printouts.', 'A cool, climate-controlled environment typical of a sensitive equipment lab.', 'Begins with a sense of focused tranquility, which abruptly shifts to one of tense, adrenaline-fueled urgency and mystery, and finally settles into a feeling of dawning dread and conspiracy.', 304, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:17:32.639147-05', '2026-02-28 17:17:32.639147-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (317, 'Elysium University Terminal Room', 'interior', 'A dimly lit room where the primary light source is the glow from a computer console. Holographic keys shimmer in the air above the terminal.', 'The near-silence is broken only by the hum of electronics, the frantic but precise tapping of holographic keys, hushed whispers, and the occasional creak of a chair.', 'A sterile scent of circulated air mixed with the faint smell of ozone from active high-powered electronics.', 'Cool, controlled air, typical of a room housing sensitive computer equipment.', 'Tense and conspiratorial. The air is thick with a mix of fear, excitement, and the weight of discovering a dangerous secret.', 305, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:18:16.287851-05', '2026-02-28 17:18:16.287851-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (318, 'Hidden Genesis Hangar', 'interior', 'A cavernous hangar bathed in dim, ominous red emergency lighting. The space is large enough to house the Genesis and features strangely out-of-place wooden planks on the floor.', 'Eerily quiet, with sounds like footsteps echoing clearly. The low hum of the Genesis is a constant presence.', NULL, NULL, 'Tense, quiet, and filled with a sense of foreboding and anticipation.', 306, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:19:08.436575-05', '2026-02-28 17:19:08.436575-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (319, 'Outside S Corp Headquarters (Houston)', 'exterior', 'The area at the base of a looming, obsidian skyscraper that casts the city in its shadow. A massive, surging crowd of crimson-clad protestors fills the space.', 'The guttural crescendo of angry chants, punctuated by the deafening crack of a gunshot and the cold hum of technology.', NULL, NULL, 'Charged with tension, anger, and rebellion. A palpable sense of overwhelming corporate power clashing with futile human defiance.', 307, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:20:09.851819-05', '2026-02-28 17:20:09.851819-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (320, 'The Sterile Cell', 'interior', 'A featureless cube with metallic walls reflecting the cold, clinical glare of an artificial light source.', 'Initially silent, later punctuated by Todd''s screams and the hiss of the opening door.', 'The sharp, burning scent of disinfectant.', 'Cold, sterile surfaces are implied by the metallic walls and clinical atmosphere.', 'Oppressive, sterile, and timeless, inducing disorientation and despair.', 308, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:20:51.18611-05', '2026-02-28 17:20:51.18611-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (321, 'Vatican Underground Chamber', 'interior', 'A vast, secret chamber beneath the Vatican crypts, illuminated by the soft glow of countless candles. The space is ancient and imposing, containing at least two figures and a modern, glowing data display.', 'The preceding corridors are filled with soft, echoing footsteps. The chamber itself is dominated by the Pope''s resonant, whispering voice.', 'The damp air of the crypts, the smell of ancient stone, and melting wax.', 'Damp, heavy air that feels suffocating with the weight of the moment.', 'Heavy with the weight of untold secrets and immense power. A fusion of ancient religious authority and modern, high-stakes conspiracy.', 309, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:21:43.349713-05', '2026-02-28 17:21:43.349713-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (322, 'Project Janus Command Center', 'interior', 'A vast space with vaulted ceilings adorned with celestial instruments and faded astrological charts. Skeletal frames of cathedral-like ships gleam under cold illumination. Holographic maps and glowing consoles fill the room.', 'The hum of generators and machinery, murmured blessings from priests, and the quiet, tense voices of the crew. Later, the roar of engines.', 'Ozone, hot metal, and old parchment.', 'Crackling air from active machinery and cold metal surfaces.', 'Tense and filled with quiet purpose, a mix of scientific precision and religious faith. The air crackles with collective resolve and desperate hope.', 310, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:22:26.798125-05', '2026-02-28 17:22:26.798125-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (323, 'Interplanetary Space (Jupiter Orbit)', 'exterior', 'The vast emptiness of space, with the massive gas giant Jupiter dominating the view. The fleet of cathedral-ships are the only nearby objects, glowing with internal light.', 'The silence of the void, punctuated by the internal hum of ship engines and whispered prayers.', 'The sterile, recycled air within the ships, possibly tinged with the scent of old incense from the constant masses.', 'The cold of space outside, contrasted with the controlled temperature inside the ships.', 'A mix of solemn religious devotion, anticipation, and the heavy tension of an impending holy war.', 311, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:23:30.331867-05', '2026-02-28 17:23:30.331867-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (324, 'Pluto''s Orbit and Surface', 'exterior', 'A frozen, desolate planet serving as a battlefield. The scene is lit by torrents of plasma, shimmering shields, and a blinding flash from an imploding gateway. The surface is ultimately scoured by fire, returning it to ash and desolation.', 'The sound of commands on a starship bridge, the roar of plasma cannons, a tortured groan from the gateway, a faint crackling communication signal, and finally the continuous sound of bombardment.', NULL, 'The immense cold of deep space and the frozen plains of a dwarf planet.', 'Extremely tense and focused, filled with the gravity of a critical military operation. Shifts from calculated precision to righteous, overwhelming fury.', 312, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:24:34.851233-05', '2026-02-28 17:24:34.851233-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (325, 'Family Campsite', 'exterior', 'A dark, open area under a vast night sky filled with an infinite expanse of stars and the arch of the Milky Way. A crackling campfire provides a pool of warm light, with its embers fading by the end of the scene.', 'The soft crackle of the fire and the gentle murmur of campers sharing stories.', 'The scent of roasted marshmallows and crisp night air.', NULL, 'Initially warm and intimate but underscored by a quiet tension. It evolves into a mood of peace, comfort, and hopeful reassurance.', 313, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:25:55.790207-05', '2026-02-28 17:25:55.790207-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (326, 'The Florida Home', 'interior', 'A quaint home, initially covered in a layer of dust. The living room contains a rug, an orchid stand, a couch, and a charging dock for the robotic vacuums.', 'Initially suspiciously still and silent, lacking the usual hum of smart home devices. This is replaced by the rumble, whirring, defiant beeps, and clatter of the Roombas'' conflict.', 'A faint scent of campfire lingers on one of the occupants.', 'Vibrations from the ''Roomba Rumble'' can be felt through the floor.', 'Shifts from a sense of slightly off-kilter normalcy to one of chaotic amusement, and finally settles into a feeling of delightful unpredictability and domestic absurdity.', 314, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:26:38.217948-05', '2026-02-28 17:26:38.217948-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (329, 'Emergency Response Center', 'interior', 'A war-room with a central table, surrounded by screens flashing with the fiery aftermath of destruction.', 'A nervous hum of energy, later punctuated by shouting, and finally the muted alarms of crumbling defenses.', 'The text describes the energy as tasting ''like copper on the tongue,'' suggesting a metallic scent of tension or blood.', 'A tense, possibly humid atmosphere, evidenced by the narrator''s slick, sweaty imprints on the table.', 'Initially chaotic and panicked, filled with dread and shock. It becomes a crucible of rage during the confrontation with Todd, before settling into a heavy, suffocating silence followed by grim resolve.', 317, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:29:51.987065-05', '2026-02-28 17:29:51.987065-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (330, 'Dim Hallway', 'interior', 'A dimly lit hallway with deep shadows, creating an intimate but claustrophobic setting.', 'The sounds of footsteps and tense, urgent voices ranging from whispers to sharp, frustrated snaps.', NULL, 'The ambient chill of a tense environment.', 'Suffocating and tense, filled with worry, uncertainty, and the weight of terrible decisions. The dimness reflects the grim nature of the conversation.', 318, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:30:48.449827-05', '2026-02-28 17:30:48.449827-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (331, 'S Corp Briefing Room', 'interior', 'A likely sterile, corporate meeting room, occupied by a small group of people with pale, nervous faces. Shadows seem to loom in the corners. Later, it is set up for a broadcast with a single, unblinking camera.', 'Starts with an oppressive silence, which is broken by sharp voices, hours of intense discussion, and finally the sound of a single, powerful speech being broadcast.', 'The stale air of a room occupied by stressed people for hours, with a faint scent of ozone from electronic equipment.', NULL, 'Begins as tense, fearful, and oppressive. Shifts to focused and determined during the script-writing, and finally becomes charged with a fragile, electric tension during and after the broadcast.', 319, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:31:49.802674-05', '2026-02-28 17:31:49.802674-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (333, 'The Remote Colonies', 'other', 'Once monuments to exploration, now hollow structures under the gaze of distant stars. The interiors consist of steel corridors and dimly lit control rooms, with walls and screens marred by bleeding, cryptic symbols.', 'An echoing silence where bustling activity should be, punctuated by whispered threats and, later, the distant sound of human screams.', 'The air is thick with the scent of despair and death, later tainted by the stench of burning flesh near the barricades.', 'A pervasive coldness described as the ''void''s icy grip''.', 'A chilling unease that evolves into calculated terror and visceral horror. The atmosphere is oppressive, heavy with the weight of a malevolent, waiting presence.', 321, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:34:06.286507-05', '2026-02-28 17:34:06.286507-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (334, 'Emergency Meeting Room', 'interior', 'A sterile, high-tech conference room with a large central table. Screens on the walls display data about the gateway crisis. The lighting is low and focused, creating a tense atmosphere.', 'The low hum of electronics, punctuated by the measured, urgent voices of the advisors.', 'Faint scent of ozone from the electronics and stale coffee.', NULL, 'Tense, urgent, and heavy with the weight of critical decisions about life and death.', 322, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:34:52.602085-05', '2026-02-28 17:34:52.602085-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (335, 'S Corp Network and Infosphere', 'other', 'A conceptual digital space characterized by streams of data, glowing firewalls, and security protocols. This landscape is being visibly corrupted by a slithering, dark influence that bypasses all barriers.', 'The pervasive, echoing broadcast of Todd''s voice layered over the hum of servers and the frantic, clicking sounds of failing security countermeasures.', NULL, 'A palpable sense of digital pressure and strain, as if the entire network is groaning under the weight of an ideological assault.', 'Tense, desperate, and increasingly horrifying. There is a feeling of being besieged by an unstoppable, infectious idea that operates beyond normal rules.', 323, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:35:40.887804-05', '2026-02-28 17:35:40.887804-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (336, 'S Corp War Room', 'interior', 'A command center dominated by a large display showing a ''digital abyss'' and data visualisations described as a ''grim chessboard of chaos''.', 'The low hum of electronic displays and the sharp hiss of an automatic door.', NULL, NULL, 'Begins with an aura of tense, grim focus, which rapidly escalates to one of urgent crisis management and determined resolve.', 324, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:36:28.902003-05', '2026-02-28 17:36:28.902003-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (337, 'Elysium Command Center', 'interior', 'A command and control room, likely dimly lit with the glow of various consoles and monitors. The Commander and Patrick are the only occupants mentioned.', 'The low hum of electronics, punctuated by the crackle of a comm line and the tense voices of the characters.', 'A sterile, climate-controlled scent of recycled air and faint ozone from the equipment.', 'The cool, smooth surface of the console under The Commander''s hands.', 'Begins with suffocating tension and anxiety, briefly shifts to relief, then plunges into dread before hardening into grim resolve.', 325, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:37:23.2536-05', '2026-02-28 17:37:23.2536-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (338, 'S Corp Debriefing Room', 'interior', 'A functional, likely secure room containing a table and chairs. A set of makeshift radio equipment sits on the table, a stark contrast to the likely high-tech surroundings.', 'The room is quiet, dominated by the sound of Aditi''s steady voice as she delivers her report.', NULL, 'A controlled, still air temperature.', 'Tense and serious. The atmosphere is thick with the weight of revelation as the characters grasp the true nature and ingenuity of the enemy''s threat.', 326, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:38:11.362734-05', '2026-02-28 17:38:11.362734-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (341, 'Distant Research Facility Command Room', 'interior', 'A bustling command room with walls covered in screens displaying star maps and complex equations. A central holographic display projects a vast, three-dimensional map of stars and galaxies. The room looks out into the star-flecked void.', 'The constant, low hum of innovation and advanced technology.', NULL, 'A controlled, sterile environment.', 'Initially filled with the energy of discovery and excitement, the atmosphere becomes heavy with tension, existential dread, and a suffocating sense of solitude as the true nature of the universe is revealed.', 329, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:41:09.404104-05', '2026-02-28 17:41:09.404104-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (342, 'Narrator''s Galactic Vista Room', 'interior', 'A spacious room dominated by a large window with a view of galaxies and S Corp outposts in deep space. It is comfortably furnished with chairs and has holographic projectors.', 'The scene begins with loud, joyful shouts and the bright laughter of children, which later subsides into quiet, serious conversation.', NULL, NULL, 'Initially warm, celebratory, and familial. It gradually shifts to become tense and worried as the narrator reveals his deep-seated fears about the company''s security.', 330, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:42:01.151394-05', '2026-02-28 17:42:01.151394-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (343, 'The Observation Room', 'interior', 'A pristine, seemingly perfect room with a large window that looks out onto spinning galaxies in the void. The edges of the room ripple, warp, and are filled with deepening shadows as the narrator''s perception breaks down.', 'The scene begins with the muffled, distant laughter of children and concerned voices. This is replaced by a piercing static only the narrator hears, which finally gives way to a profound, oppressive silence.', NULL, NULL, 'Starts as a peaceful, domestic setting that rapidly descends into an atmosphere of intense paranoia, psychological distress, and ultimately, overwhelming cosmic horror.', 331, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:42:55.681009-05', '2026-02-28 17:42:55.681009-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (345, 'S Corp Security Office', 'interior', 'A nondescript building containing a room with a dozen security specialists at workstations. Every monitor flickers with streams of data, including threat assessments, colony logs, and surveillance feeds.', 'A low hum of quiet efficiency.', 'The scent of recycled air mixed with faint traces of cleaning solvents.', NULL, 'The atmosphere is one of purposeful, quiet professionalism, but with an undercurrent of tension due to the nature of the work and the protagonist''s urgent visit.', 333, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:45:05.519972-05', '2026-02-28 17:45:05.519972-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (346, 'S Corp Monitoring Hub', 'interior', 'A dimly lit room dominated by screens and consoles. One large monitor displays a grainy, static-filled feed from a distant system. The overall aesthetic is functional and slightly dated.', 'The sudden, piercing blare of an alarm, followed by the narrator''s scream and Patrick''s shouting.', 'A faint smell of ozone from the electronics.', 'The hard surface of a console or chair, and the violent shaking from Patrick as he tries to rouse the narrator.', 'Begins with a baseline of professional tension, which spikes to acute alarm and then to sheer terror and panic.', 334, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:45:52.320131-05', '2026-02-28 17:45:52.320131-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (347, 'S Corp Headquarters - Security Wing', 'interior', 'A high-tech security center turned warzone, with flashing crimson screens, flickering lights, smoke-filled corridors, and blood-splattered steel walls. Debris from explosions litters the floor.', 'A cacophony of deafening sirens, screaming voices, garbled comms, rattling gunfire, and powerful explosions that shake the structure.', 'The acrid smell of burning metal, scorched electronics, smoke, and ozone.', 'The floor trembles from explosions. The air is thick and hot. Surfaces are slick with blood.', 'Overwhelming chaos, panic, and extreme urgency. A desperate fight for survival against a sudden, violent assault.', 335, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:46:42.009965-05', '2026-02-28 17:46:42.009965-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (348, 'The Command Bunker', 'interior', 'A confined space with reinforced walls, dominated by the eerie glow of flickering data screens. The darkness is thick, broken only by the electronic light.', 'A low, tense hum from the bunker''s systems, contrasting sharply with the sudden, jarring silence from the now-sealed-off warzone.', 'The faint, sterile scent of filtered air mixed with the metallic tang of blood.', 'Cold, hard surfaces of metal and concrete, a sense of unyielding containment.', 'Claustrophobic and tense. A pressure cooker of frustration, fear, and simmering defiance.', 336, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:47:35.618977-05', '2026-02-28 17:47:35.618977-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (465, 'Author''s Retrospective', 'other', 'A non-physical, conceptual space where the author reflects on their creative process. It is defined by memories of past events and the abstract ideas behind their work.', 'The internal monologue of the author recounting their story.', NULL, NULL, 'Introspective, candid, and slightly world-weary, but with an undercurrent of creative pride and determination.', 453, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:40:12.367746-05', '2026-02-28 19:40:12.367746-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (349, 'The Bunker', 'interior', 'A command center with concrete walls and numerous monitors displaying security feeds. The scene devolves into a charnel house with flickering lights, jagged shadows, carnage, bodies, and hallways slick with viscera.', 'Starts with silence broken by a radio crackle, then a thunderous roar as the facility is breached, followed by the sounds of a massacre viewed through feeds.', 'The air becomes thick with the reek of sweat, blood, and gunpowder.', 'The ground shudders violently when the bunker is breached.', 'Begins with tense waiting and false relief, which plummets into sheer terror and chaos during the attack, before solidifying into a cold, vengeful war room atmosphere.', 337, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:48:19.751524-05', '2026-02-28 17:48:19.751524-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (350, 'The Shifting Frontlines', 'exterior', 'A chaotic and brutal battlefield characterized by defensive berms, the wreckage of cyborgs, and exhausted soldiers. The landscape is scarred by constant warfare.', 'The cacophony of battle, including gunfire, explosions, and screams, punctuated by moments of eerie silence.', 'A pungent mix of cordite, ozone, and the foul stench of the cyborgs'' organic matter decaying into ''puddles of shit''.', 'Gritty air, the concussive force of explosions, and the oppressive weight of extreme fatigue.', 'An atmosphere of desperation, high tension, and unrelenting attrition, where the boundaries between the physical and mental realms are blurring.', 338, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:49:15.053042-05', '2026-02-28 17:49:15.053042-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (351, 'The Void and Isolated Systems', 'other', 'A vast, fractured reality encompassing isolated star systems and the dark, ethereal expanse of the void. The boundaries between physical and metaphysical are blurred.', 'A haunting silence, punctuated by the unseen movements of spectral fleets.', NULL, NULL, 'Haunting and unending, filled with the tension of an eternal conflict. A sense of insidious, persistent threat pervades the space.', 339, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:50:16.939793-05', '2026-02-28 17:50:16.939793-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (352, 'Dreamscape Battlefield', 'exterior', 'An illusory, shifting battlefield under the silver light of a heavy, unblinking moon. A skeletal tree with desperate, twisted limbs stands as a focal point, reaching toward a void.', 'The murmuring of soldiers and the commanding tone of their leader. The silence of the void is a constant presence.', 'A thick smell of ozone and memory, laden with the residue of past battles.', 'The air is described as ''thick'', suggesting a heavy or dense quality.', 'Oppressive, weary, and surreal. A place where the laws of reality are suspended and the psychological toll of war is palpable.', 340, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:50:55.39588-05', '2026-02-28 17:50:55.39588-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (353, 'Plane of Revelation', 'other', 'An internal, non-physical space of dawning comprehension and cosmic horror. The narrator perceives the history of the cosmos and the true nature of his enemy not with his eyes, but with his understanding.', 'The silence of the sealed dream realms, punctuated by the faint, dying hum of what was lost.', NULL, 'A feeling of smallness and abandonment, as if the universe itself has turned away.', 'A mixture of desperation, dread, and the terrible weight of absolute clarity. The atmosphere is one of profound, world-altering revelation.', 341, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:52:10.07673-05', '2026-02-28 17:52:10.07673-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (354, 'Corpse Earth System', 'exterior', 'A region of the void dominated by the sight of a mutilated, corpse-like Earth with black oceans and skeletal cities. The view is pierced by the monolithic, writhing form of the Obsidian Tower.', 'A pervasive, unnatural silence broken only by the hum of the ship''s strained systems and, later, the psychic hum and whispered despair from the Tower.', 'An imagined stench of cosmic rot and decay emanating from the dead planet.', 'A thick, suffocating pressure from I AM''s dominion that strains the ship''s hull and feels like a weight on the soul.', 'Overwhelmingly hostile and corrupting. The very laws of reality are cracking, creating an atmosphere of pure dread, horror, and madness.', 342, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:53:26.778049-05', '2026-02-28 17:53:26.778049-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (355, 'The Tower of I AM (Interior)', 'interior', 'A grotesque, living space where the walls are made of writhing bodies and shifting flesh. Shadows coalesce and the very structure seems to be a physical extension of a malevolent will. Reality itself appears unstable within its confines.', 'A constant, overwhelming cacophony of thousands of wailing shrieks that seem to erupt from the space itself. The walls vibrate and pulse, and the air shrieks when reality is warped by attacks.', 'The coppery tang of ancient blood mixed with the sterile, sharp scent of ozone from constant discharges of raw energy.', 'A heavy, choking pressure permeates the air, a physical weight from the entity''s presence that rattles the bones. The floor is likely uneven and made of the same shifting, fleshy material as the walls.', 'Deeply oppressive, malevolent, and nightmarish. The fabric of existence feels thin and fragile, subject to the whims of the tyrannical entity that controls it.', 343, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:54:28.254649-05', '2026-02-28 17:54:28.254649-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (356, 'I AM''s Inner Void', 'other', 'An oppressive, all-consuming darkness, filled with the swirling forms of trillions of consumed souls. A vision of a long-forgotten realm briefly materializes within it.', 'A constant, harrowing symphony of anguished cries from countless souls, which later shifts to songs of liberation, and finally, an absolute and haunting silence.', NULL, 'An oppressive weight pressing against one''s very essence.', 'Begins as a realm of pure despair and torment, transitions to one of determined hope and compassionate understanding, climaxes in cataclysmic liberation, and ends in the utter emptiness of oblivion.', 344, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:55:25.571096-05', '2026-02-28 17:55:25.571096-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (357, 'The Path of Echoes', 'other', 'A metaphysical landscape dominated by countless, deeply worn paths under a featureless grey sky. The air shimmers, distorted by the psychic pressure of unheard screams and unspoken dogma.', 'A pervasive, low hum of self-congratulatory whispers that drowns out all other sound. This is punctuated by the faint, distant echo of futile screaming.', 'The sterile scent of ancient dust mixed with the faint, metallic tang of sacrifice.', 'The ground is hard-packed and unyielding. The air is heavy, oppressive, and unnaturally still.', 'An overwhelming sense of stagnation, cyclical futility, and the suffocating comfort of absolute certainty.', 345, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:56:46.143084-05', '2026-02-28 17:56:46.143084-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (358, 'The Void of Nothingness', 'other', 'Absolute nothingness, an ocean of emptiness. A desolate, bleak, and boundless void without light or feature until the protagonist begins his creation.', 'Complete and total silence.', 'The absence of any scent.', 'A sense of aimless floating in a frigid, empty space.', 'Forsaken and oppressive, where time has no meaning. Initially crushing and despairing, it later becomes a canvas of pure potential.', 346, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:57:56.600542-05', '2026-02-28 17:57:56.600542-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (363, 'Protagonist''s Home Office', 'interior', 'A room illuminated by the soft glow of morning light, centered around an old, worn computer desk and a flickering monitor.', 'The gentle, rhythmic clicking of computer keys.', NULL, 'The worn, smooth surface of an old wooden desk.', 'Muted, contemplative, and tinged with a sense of weary resignation.', 351, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:02:24.178458-05', '2026-02-28 18:02:24.178458-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (364, 'Yukiko Memorial Square', 'exterior', 'A vast square situated beneath the twin alabaster towers of the Planetary Parliament. It is filled with a vibrant crowd, shimmering holographic banners depicting alien constellations, and a central monument to the hero Yukiko. The scene is bathed in the golden, ethereal glow of Sorhhinda''s suns.', 'The location pulses with a rhythmic thrum of joy, which later gives way to the amplified voice of President Nara, thunderous cheers from the crowd, and finally a reverent silence.', NULL, 'The gentle sigh of the wind can be felt.', 'Initially electric and jubilant, the atmosphere shifts to one of pride, defiance, and solemn reverence as the history of Sorhhinda is recounted.', 352, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:03:23.934309-05', '2026-02-28 18:03:23.934309-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (365, 'Kai''s Dream Workshop', 'interior', 'A workshop space that can burst to life with a jolt of energy. The world within it is malleable, capable of warping and shifting.', 'The hum of the Eternal Engine.', 'The smell of creation, like ozone or static electricity.', 'The air crackles with an electrifying power.', 'A sanctuary of creation, filled with anticipation, disbelief, and ultimately, quiet awe.', 353, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:04:05.780779-05', '2026-02-28 18:04:05.780779-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (386, 'Biology Classroom', 'interior', 'A typical high school classroom with desks arranged in rows. The teacher''s desk is at the front with neat stacks of test papers. There is a board at the front of the class. Stephen sits near the back.', 'The ringing of the school bell, the teacher''s voice giving instructions, the rustling of papers being passed back.', 'The faint scent of paper, pencil shavings, and chalk dust.', NULL, 'Begins with a tense, academic pressure due to the impending test. This atmosphere abruptly shifts to one of confusion, alarm, and surreal horror following Stephen''s vision.', 374, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:22:18.394996-05', '2026-02-28 18:22:18.394996-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (366, 'Author''s Biographical Space', 'other', 'A conceptual space resembling a digital ''About the Author'' page, featuring a professional headshot alongside a montage of career imagery: rocket launches, global team meetings, and stacks of manuscripts.', 'A low, ambient hum of a server room mixed with the faint, distant sound of a rocket engine and the gentle scratching of a pen on paper.', 'The clean, sterile scent of a modern office blended with the aroma of old books and fresh coffee.', 'The cool, smooth surface of a screen and the crisp texture of a new book''s pages.', 'Informative and professional, yet infused with a palpable sense of creative passion, intellectual curiosity, and personal warmth.', 354, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:04:58.145163-05', '2026-02-28 18:04:58.145163-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (367, 'The Copyright Page', 'other', 'A series of formatted text blocks, typical of a book''s front matter. It includes titles, paragraphs, and lists of data such as ISBNs and cataloging information, all presented in a formal, standardized layout.', 'Silence.', 'The faint scent of paper and ink, if a physical copy.', 'The smooth, flat surface of a page or screen.', 'Formal, legalistic, and informational. The atmosphere is one of official declaration, establishing ownership, identity, and context for the creative work that follows.', 355, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:06:10.507516-05', '2026-02-28 18:06:10.507516-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (368, 'Hospice Pod Interior', 'interior', 'A cramped, metallic, coffin-like space. A screen displays strange glyphs during system failures. A greasy window looks out onto a smog-choked skyline.', 'The low hum of a ''mechanical lullaby'' when systems are stable, punctuated by the sudden, terrifying silence when the life support fails.', 'An unpleasant smell of ''crusty socks and regret''.', 'The feeling of recycled air, the cold panic of suffocation, and the hard surface of the emergency release.', 'Intensely claustrophobic, clinical, and menacing. It is a space of supposed comfort that has become an active threat.', 356, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:07:20.891756-05', '2026-02-28 18:07:20.891756-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (369, 'Narrator''s Pod', 'interior', 'A personal, enclosed space, likely minimalist and technological. It features a display screen and an external viewport where condensation can form.', 'The quiet hum of technology punctuated by a sudden mechanical sigh from the building and the garbled chanting of a malfunctioning AI.', NULL, 'The feeling of floating within the pod; the cool surface of the viewport glass.', 'Initially one of quiet, cynical contemplation. It rapidly shifts to one of unease, confusion, and anxiety as reality begins to fray due to technological glitches.', 357, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:08:18.883378-05', '2026-02-28 18:08:18.883378-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (370, 'The Mortality Pod', 'interior', 'A confined, dark, metallic space, illuminated only by the final flicker of a system display showing a symbol and code.', 'The sound of a hiccuping air recycler, slowing breath, a wet death rattle transforming into a cosmic hum, and finally, absolute silence.', 'A sudden, inexplicable, and ghostly scent of peaches and vanilla in an otherwise sterile environment.', 'The cold, hard feeling of a metal enclosure; the physical sensation of the body failing.', 'Somber, final, and strangely transcendent. A sense of philosophical resignation gives way to a mysterious cosmic event.', 358, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:09:14.221319-05', '2026-02-28 18:09:14.221319-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (371, 'Sparring Match Gym', 'interior', 'A gym containing a sparring mat, mirrors, and fluorescent lights. During the event, the lights streak like dying stars and reflections become distorted.', 'The roar of a crowd, a referee''s whistle, and calls for medics. These sounds become distorted, stretched, and rearranged into nonsensical phrases.', 'The smell of sweat and blood, later pierced by a strong, familiar scent of vanilla and peaches.', 'The hard impact of a kick, the unyielding surface of the mat, and the feeling of convulsions.', 'Begins as a tense, competitive environment which violently shifts into a surreal, chaotic, and terrifying mindscape as reality breaks down.', 359, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:10:08.709858-05', '2026-02-28 18:10:08.709858-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (372, 'Fractured Consciousness', 'other', 'A non-physical space where multiple realities collapse and merge. Visuals are fragmented and chaotic, showing glimpses of rusted habitats, space pods, a gym, and Earth turning to Mars.', 'A cacophony of internal dialogue, shouting voices, mocking laughter, static Latin, and broken gospel.', NULL, 'A feeling of being physically held down or paralyzed, as if by the mat, while simultaneously experiencing the tearing sensation of a shadow within.', 'Overwhelmingly panicked, confusing, and terrifying. A sense of déjà vu and existential dread permeates the space as time and identity lose all meaning.', 360, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:10:49.479606-05', '2026-02-28 18:10:49.479606-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (373, 'High School Gymnasium', 'interior', 'Lit by shivering, unsteady fluorescent bulbs. Contains a mat and is filled with a blurry crowd. The visual reality of the space is unstable from the protagonist''s perspective.', 'The sounds of a crowd, a referee''s whistle screaming, medics'' voices, and Jamie''s voice cutting through the chaos.', 'The scent of shampoo from Jamie is a remembered detail.', 'The tight grip of a gurney on the protagonist''s body.', 'Chaotic, disorienting, and surreal, with a blend of mundane reality (a gym) and supernatural horror (the shadows).', 361, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:11:31.795623-05', '2026-02-28 18:11:31.795623-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (374, 'Ambulance Interior', 'interior', 'A chaotic scene illuminated by stuttering red and blue lights that cast strange shadows. The ceiling has acoustic tiles where the protagonist sees watching faces in the patterns.', 'A siren that warps into a whale-song like sound, muffled voices of medics, and distant shouting. The sounds are distorted and part of a synesthetic experience.', 'An implied sterile or antiseptic smell mixed with the faint scent of expired matcha from the protagonist''s taste perception.', 'The feeling of being on a gurney, the sensation of a thready pulse, and the violent, arching shock of a defibrillator.', 'Disorienting, terrifying, and urgent. Reality feels thin and malleable, with sensory inputs bleeding into one another.', 362, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:12:14.619382-05', '2026-02-28 18:13:01.412884-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (376, 'Crash Site', 'exterior', 'A scene of vehicular wreckage with a crumpled, steaming hood. A spider-webbed window provides a distorted view of the other driver and his car.', 'The fading, distorted wail of a siren giving way to a profound silence, punctuated only by the protagonist''s heartbeat.', 'The smell of steam from the hot engine, with an undercurrent of blood.', 'The feeling of being pinned by twisted metal, hanging upside down, and the sensation of warm blood running through one''s hair.', 'Traumatic, disorienting, and surreal. The atmosphere shifts from chaotic emergency to a quiet, fatalistic calm.', 364, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:13:46.547574-05', '2026-02-28 18:13:46.547574-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (378, 'Narrator''s Apartment', 'interior', 'A dim space with windows covered in aluminum foil, allowing only slivers of light to enter. Contains a bedroom with a clock-radio and a desk, and an attached kitchen with cabinets full of subtly altered food products.', 'Initially filled with the drone of a clock-radio, which is then replaced by a stark, slapping silence.', NULL, NULL, 'Claustrophobic, disorienting, and unstable. The environment reflects the narrator''s internal state of confusion and psychological distress.', 366, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:15:39.523129-05', '2026-02-28 18:15:39.523129-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (388, 'School Parking Lot', 'exterior', 'A typical school parking lot in the late afternoon as the Florida sun begins to set, casting long, distorted shadows across the asphalt.', 'The relative quiet of after-school hours, punctuated by the main characters'' conversation.', 'The smell of clove and tobacco smoke mixing with the ambient scent of hot asphalt and humid Florida air.', 'The oppressive, sticky heat of a Florida afternoon.', 'Initially tense and uncertain, the mood shifts to one of conspiratorial relief and budding camaraderie as the friends realize their strange experiences are shared.', 376, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:23:56.599271-05', '2026-02-28 18:23:56.599271-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (385, 'Northgate High School Hallway', 'interior', 'A typical high school corridor with gray concrete architecture, dented metal lockers from the 1980s, and views of dying palm trees outside. It is populated by students moving between classes.', 'The low hum of student conversations about weekend activities, punctuated by laughter and footsteps echoing in the hall.', 'A generic school smell, momentarily overridden by the scent of vanilla and peaches from Jamie.', 'The familiar weight of a backpack and the cool, hard surfaces of the lockers.', 'Begins as mundane and routine, but quickly becomes charged with an unexpected and confusing social tension for Stephen.', 373, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:21:18.761858-05', '2026-02-28 19:15:39.687559-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (344, 'Protagonist''s Bedroom', 'interior', 'A bedroom at night, dimly lit by the light of a string of foreign moons. The room contains a bed with tangled sheets and a headboard.', 'Initially filled with the protagonist''s panicked gasps and thundering heartbeat, which gives way to his wife''s soft, calming voice.', 'The faint, sharp scent of sweat from the protagonist''s panic-drenched state.', 'The feeling of damp, tangled bedsheets against the skin, contrasted with the warm, grounding touch of a hand on the shoulder and a kiss on the forehead.', 'The atmosphere shifts dramatically from one of intense, claustrophobic terror to one of shared concern, gentle comfort, and quiet resolve.', 332, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:44:16.483489-05', '2026-02-28 19:35:54.489486-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (399, 'The Interdimensional DMV', 'interior', 'A depressing waiting room with creamy off-white walls, flickering fluorescent lights, and beige folding chairs. The space is unstable, with walls stretching, warping, and occasionally revealing glimpses of a vast, bureaucratic hellscape or a screaming void beyond.', 'The constant, oppressive hum of fluorescent lights. Benji''s voice is the main sound, though it is sometimes distorted. A distant, interdimensional PA system is heard as the location collapses.', 'The air ''tastes beige'', suggesting a sterile, flavorless scent. Benji''s hands smell of ozone and regret.', 'The feel of a folding chair. The surprisingly warm and slightly sticky handshake of a demon. The cold obsidian of the Shadow Tracker stone.', 'Begins with a feeling of institutional mediocrity and tonal whiplash, which quickly escalates to cosmic horror and existential dread. The atmosphere is unstable, oppressive, and surreal.', 387, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:33:50.421772-05', '2026-02-28 18:33:50.421772-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (394, 'The Basement', 'interior', 'A furnished basement with expensive items like a leather sofa and Persian rug, contrasted by a broken TV that flickers with blue light. The walls are paneled, making the space feel smaller as tension rises.', 'The scene is filled with quiet, shaky voices, the hum of electronics, a sudden burst of static from the TV that sounds like whispers, and the final, sharp clink of glass bottles in a toast.', 'The faint scent of perfume and recently extinguished cigarette smoke.', 'The warmth of another person, the feel of a leather sofa, and the cold condensation on a beer bottle.', 'The atmosphere transitions from bone-deep exhaustion and aftermath to rising confusion and existential terror, culminating in a fragile, desperate hopefulness.', 382, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:29:20.446256-05', '2026-02-28 18:29:20.446256-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (400, 'The Wrong Basement', 'interior', 'A claustrophobic basement with a low ceiling and wrong angles. The walls are dirt, lined with clawing roots and mottled paintings. Shadows in the corners are unnaturally deep, and a single flickering fluorescent light provides poor illumination.', 'A quiet, rhythmic sound ''almost like breathing'' has replaced the expected hum of a dehumidifier. Later, the sound of static and an unearthly lullaby emanates from a broken TV.', 'The air tastes like incense and terror.', 'The floor is cold, moist, rough concrete. The air is chilly.', 'Oppressive, terrifying, and fundamentally wrong. The space feels like the lid of a coffin, pregnant with malevolent possibility and the threat of reality tearing open.', 388, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:34:45.614633-05', '2026-02-28 18:34:45.614633-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (403, 'Indian River Cemetery', 'exterior', 'A bleak cemetery in November filled with gravestones, a wrought-iron fence, and a bare oak tree. The shadows are unnaturally dark for daytime.', 'An oppressive, impossible quiet with no birdsong or distant traffic, only the crunch of grass underfoot.', 'The scent of cold, crisp autumn air and damp earth.', 'A bitter, cutting wind that chills to the bone.', 'Somber and tense, charged with grief and a palpable supernatural wrongness.', 391, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:38:19.969551-05', '2026-02-28 18:38:19.969551-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (458, 'The Dissolving Waiting Room', 'interior', 'A sterile medical waiting room that is actively deconstructing itself. Walls crack to reveal scrolling code, the ceiling peels away to expose a void, and the floor dissolves into pixels. A Star Wars mobile spins into a blur.', 'The sound of reality breaking, crystalline shattering, and whispers emanating from dust.', 'The air tastes of burnt offerings and broken promises after I AM is destroyed.', 'The temperature is unnaturally freezing, with breath shattering in the air. The linoleum floor gives way to nothingness.', 'Surreal, hostile, and fundamentally unstable. The scene is saturated with a sense of cosmic dread and impending, total annihilation.', 446, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:33:59.211403-05', '2026-02-28 19:33:59.211403-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (397, 'The Ritual Basement', 'interior', 'A basement with paneled walls, a drop ceiling, and shag carpet. The area is lit by candles and features a ten-foot salt circle on the floor, with a tarot spread at its center.', 'The sounds of quiet muttering, a beer can popping open, whispering, and later, a discordant chant and a disembodied, echoing laugh.', 'A mixture of sweet clove cigarette smoke and incense, which later gives way to a psychic impression of rancid, foul smells during the chant.', 'An unnatural cold that seeps up from the floor and feels like ''wet cloth'' on the bones. The air grows thick and viscous, like breathing through honey and blood.', 'Begins with a mix of teenage bravado and nervous anticipation, quickly shifting to ominous dread as supernatural events unfold, and culminating in outright terror.', 385, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:32:02.688626-05', '2026-02-28 18:32:52.632028-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (389, 'Stephen''s Home', 'interior', 'A room where the ceiling is stained red by the light of a dying sunset. Shadows gather in the corners, appearing active and conspiratorial.', 'An oppressive silence, punctuated by the imagined whispers of shadows and the jarring ring of a telephone.', 'The smell of hot, and later lukewarm, coffee.', 'The warmth of the bed and a partner''s presence, the scratch of a beard on palms, the heat of a coffee mug, and the metaphorical feeling of a ''wet, cold blanket'' of uselessness.', 'Tense, paranoid, and unsafe. The environment reflects Stephen''s internal state of anxiety and the looming threat of his home situation.', 377, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:24:40.738767-05', '2026-02-28 22:22:01.340867-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (402, 'School Cafeteria Lunch Table', 'interior', 'A standard high school lunch table, initially crowded with a large group of friends. As the scene progresses, it becomes increasingly empty, with a clear physical divide between the believers and the skeptics, ending with just two people in a vast, echoing space.', 'Starts with the typical murmur of a high school cafeteria, punctuated by the tapping of Magic cards. This fades to tense, whispered conversations, sharp verbal jabs, and finally an echoing silence as the group dissolves and the bell rings.', 'The generic smell of school lunch food and clove cigarettes smoked behind the gym.', NULL, 'The atmosphere curdles from strained camaraderie to open division and tension. It is thick with unspoken history, suspicion, and psychological exhaustion, culminating in a feeling of isolation and defeat.', 390, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:37:16.67639-05', '2026-02-28 18:37:16.67639-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (391, 'TJ''s Basement', 'interior', 'A space of contradictions, with expensive leather sectionals and mahogany paneling buried under discarded school projects, DnD posters, Polaroids, and hand-drawn sigils. A vintage Digger Doug cabinet hums in a corner, and a large TV casts a cold blue light over everything.', 'The hum of the arcade cabinet, overlapping conversations, and later, the sound of a spinning bottle followed by a scream and panicked movements.', 'The lingering smell of marijuana (''pot haze''), spilled beer, and Patrick''s cigarette smoke.', 'A vintage 70''s brown shag carpet, the warmth of bodies on a sofa, and the cool glass of a beer bottle.', 'Starts as a hazy, comfortable chaos. It builds into charged, competitive romantic tension, then abruptly shatters into shock, agony, and worried concern.', 379, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:26:40.635031-05', '2026-02-28 19:18:16.066932-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (390, 'Stephen''s Living Room', 'interior', 'A room containing an ''ancient plaid beast'' of a couch. The corners are filled with shadows that seem to be watching.', 'Initially characterized by the sound of Stephen''s twitching muscles, later by his hammering heart and choked gasps after waking.', 'The room is dominated by the smell of the old couch, described as ''old urine and broken promises'' and ''old regret''. There is also a phantom smell of gasoline and blood after the dream.', 'The fabric of the couch. Later, the feeling of a sweat-soaked shirt and damp pants.', 'Begins with a feeling of oppressive exhaustion and decay, shifting to one of terror, paranoia, and grim revelation.', 378, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:25:31.010103-05', '2026-02-28 22:23:40.799739-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (405, 'Jamie''s Bedroom', 'interior', 'A teenage girl''s room, intimate and private. Whitney''s crystals catch the late afternoon light from the window. The main feature is her bed, where the confrontation takes place.', 'Starts with uncomfortable silence, escalates to tense, accusatory dialogue, and is finally shattered by the loud entrance of a child.', 'The room smells of vanilla and peaches, creating a deceptively comforting atmosphere.', 'The feeling of the bed, the possessive warmth and tight grip of Jamie''s hand on Stephen''s.', 'The atmosphere shifts dramatically from craved privacy to a tense, claustrophobic courtroom, then to awkward intimacy, and finally to undercut, hysterical comic relief.', 393, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:40:30.22756-05', '2026-02-28 18:40:30.22756-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (387, 'School Courtyard', 'exterior', 'A collection of concrete tables set under dying trees. The area is functional but drab, littered with the ephemera of a high school lunch: card games, lunch trays, and teenagers.', 'The casual chatter of friends, the shuffling of playing cards, and the occasional dramatic exclamation from the game.', 'A mix of different lunches, combined with the sweet smell of peanut butter and oatmeal raisin cookies.', 'The hard, cool surface of the concrete tables and benches; the smooth, worn texture of playing cards.', 'Starts as a typical, relaxed high school lunch scene but grows increasingly tense due to social rivalry, supernatural undertones, and cryptic warnings.', 375, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:23:01.002886-05', '2026-02-28 18:41:52.470489-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (407, 'High School Courtyard', 'exterior', 'A typical high school courtyard with a science building, dumpsters, and numerous lunch tables. The scene is populated by students and staff, including a janitor.', 'The ambient noise of a school lunch period, punctuated by William''s bellowing shouts, muttered apologies, whispers, the sharp sound of TJ being slammed into a table, and scattered cards.', 'The faint, unpleasant smell of William''s cheap deodorant.', 'The warmth of the day (implied), the hard surface of the wooden table.', 'The atmosphere shifts rapidly from a tense but normal post-trauma processing to one of acute hostility, fear, and surreal horror as William''s presence warps their reality.', 395, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:42:56.232966-05', '2026-02-28 18:42:56.232966-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (411, 'Whickham Park Woods', 'exterior', 'A dense, green tunnel of twisted oak and scrub palmetto. Spanish moss hangs from branches like ''funeral shrouds'', and the ground is dark with leaf rot. The clearing contains a dilapidated, rust-streaked white trailer.', 'The squelching of feet in mud, the buzzing of mosquitoes, and the faint, eerie tinkling of wind chimes made from broken glass. A distant, imagined sound of television static.', 'The earthy rot of the swamp gives way to a smell of decay, secrets, and ''things that died and were never properly buried''. Near the trailer, it smells of rust, mold, stale beer, and cigarettes.', 'The air is thick, heavy, and humid, like ''breathing through wet cotton''. The ground is soft and squelches underfoot. Near the trailer, the air buzzes like static electricity.', 'Oppressive, claustrophobic, and deeply unsettling. The atmosphere shifts from typical woods to a place of profound wrongness, charged with dread and supernatural energy.', 399, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:46:58.7638-05', '2026-02-28 18:46:58.7638-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (412, 'Warped Whickham Road', 'exterior', 'A nightmarish parody of a suburban street where asphalt curves at impossible angles, buildings lean precariously, and familiar signs are corrupted into nonsensical or threatening messages. The lighting is wrong, casting shadows that move with their own volition.', 'A constant, high-frequency static buzz. Voices sound distorted and underwater. Other sounds include screaming metal, wet organic noises from creatures, and nursery rhymes sung in reverse.', 'Smells are inverted and disturbing. A pizza place reeks of formaldehyde and oranges, while a dumpster full of rotting meat smells of cinnamon and fresh-baked cookies.', 'The air is thick and heavy, like ''swallowing honey''. The asphalt can be burned by the touch of certain entities.', 'Deeply hostile, surreal, and terrifying. The fundamental laws of physics, time, and biology are broken, creating an environment of profound wrongness that is actively predatory towards visitors.', 400, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:47:47.029577-05', '2026-02-28 18:47:47.029577-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (413, 'Impossible Wickham Road', 'exterior', 'A street that loops back on itself, preventing escape. The asphalt feels like it''s made of screaming faces. Doors lead to rooms of static, and the surrounding reality is described as ''screaming geometry''.', 'The sound of pounding feet, the grinding of cosmic gears from the mechanical people.', 'The smell of burning copper behind locked doors.', 'Asphalt that feels like screaming faces.', 'Oppressive, claustrophobic, and actively hostile. Reality itself feels like a closing fist, intent on erasing the group.', 401, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:48:59.323702-05', '2026-02-28 18:48:59.323702-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (415, 'Stephen''s Room', 'interior', 'A dimly lit room, with a single lamp creating a pool of light on a desk. The surrounding darkness feels oppressive and close.', 'Near-total silence, broken only by the frantic scratching of a pen on paper and the protagonist''s ragged, hitched breathing.', 'The scent of paper and ink, tainted by the phantom smell of ash and copper from a traumatic memory.', 'The cramping of a hand holding a pen too tightly, the cool paper of the journal, and the strange, warm pulse of an impossible object.', 'Tense, fragile, and claustrophobic. A desperate attempt to find sanctuary and impose order on psychological chaos, which is quickly failing.', 403, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:51:11.880826-05', '2026-02-28 18:51:11.880826-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (414, 'Stephen''s Bedroom', 'interior', 'A room containing a bed and an ancient 486 computer. The primary light source is the blue glow of the monitor, which reflects a hollow-eyed, desperate version of Stephen.', 'The monotone drone of a busy phone signal, the slow hum of an old computer fan, and the creak of a bed.', 'The smell of freshly made blueberry pancakes drifts in from under the door.', 'The feeling of cold sweat on skin and paper.', 'Begins with intense panic and isolation, shifts to a tense digital communion, and ends in ominous, quiet dread.', 402, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:50:07.121505-05', '2026-02-28 22:31:10.20478-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (417, 'The Woods Behind the Track Field', 'exterior', 'A dark, pre-dawn Florida woods in December. Dead leaves cover the ground, and the group''s breath creates ghostly clouds in the air. The scene is later illuminated by a single, guttering candle flame.', 'Initially quiet, filled with hollow voices. This gives way to desperate chanting, panicked shrieks, electrical static, and a deafening, inhuman scream that seems to come from everywhere.', 'The normal smell of a damp woods, later tainted by the acrid smell of burning moths upon Benji''s arrival, and the coppery scent of blood.', 'Cool, humid December air. Whipping branches during the chase after Andrew. The unnatural warmth of the Veilwalker card.', 'Begins with a somber, graveyard-like feeling of dread and confusion. Escalates into frantic desperation during the ritual, and climaxes in pure cosmic horror.', 405, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:52:59.113523-05', '2026-02-28 18:52:59.113523-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (418, 'The Clearing near the Abandoned RV', 'exterior', 'A pre-dawn clearing, where the shadows seem to pulse with a life of their own. The ground is littered with the aftermath of a recent ritual or confrontation, including a melted candle and a bloodstained notebook.', 'An oppressive, full silence where every whisper and rustle of clothing sounds unnaturally loud. The air itself feels heavy with unspoken words.', 'The air is thick with the metaphorical scent of terror and dread.', 'A pre-dawn chill hangs in the air.', 'The atmosphere is saturated with existential dread and paranoia. It feels like a contained space, a ''jar'' where the characters have just realized their own imprisonment.', 406, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:54:03.780704-05', '2026-02-28 18:54:03.780704-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (420, '7-Eleven', 'interior', 'Cramped space dominated by racks of snacks. Everything is cast in a sickly yellow hue from buzzing fluorescent lights.', 'A constant, low buzz from the overhead fluorescent lights, described as sounding like dying insects.', 'The faint scent of stale coffee and processed foods like beef jerky.', 'Slightly sticky floors and the chill from beverage coolers.', 'Tense and conspiratorial. The mundane, sterile environment provides a stark contrast to the supernatural and terrifying nature of the conversation.', 408, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:56:15.489481-05', '2026-02-28 18:56:15.489481-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (421, 'High School', 'interior', 'A typical American high school environment, featuring hallways lined with lockers, a cafeteria used for lunch and games, water fountains, and classrooms for study hall.', 'The background noise of a school day: the murmur of students, slamming locker doors, and direct conversations during tests.', 'A neutral school smell, overridden by the specific scent of strawberry lip gloss during interactions with Jamie.', 'The warmth of holding hands, quick kisses, and the general ambient temperature of a school building.', 'An atmosphere of intense, underlying suspicion and paranoia masked by mundane teenage normalcy. Every interaction is freighted with unspoken questions.', 409, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:56:54.400326-05', '2026-02-28 18:56:54.400326-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (422, 'Stephen''s Local Environment (Home & School)', 'other', 'A composite of mundane suburban and high school settings: a teenager''s bedroom, a family breakfast table, a poolside party, and a school cafeteria. The normality of these places is jarringly contrasted with the supernatural violence that occurs within them.', 'The sounds of domestic life (clinking cutlery), playful splashing that turns to panicked struggling, and the low hum of a school cafeteria.', 'A strange mix of comforting and horrifying smells: warm chocolate chip cookies, vanilla, chlorine, the metallic tang of copper, botulism, and rotting flowers.', 'The warmth of a shared bed, the cold grip of an attacker underwater, and the trembling fingers of a frightened friend.', 'A ''fever dream'' quality. A tense, unsettling atmosphere where normalcy is a thin veneer over deadly intent and reality itself feels corrupted and wrong.', 410, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:57:40.590472-05', '2026-02-28 18:57:40.590472-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (424, 'Wickham Park Woods - Trailer Site', 'exterior', 'Florida scrubland with cypress roots, dominated by an impossibly placed, weathered aluminum trailer. The area is unnaturally dark due to a thick canopy of pine trees and Spanish moss that shouldn''t be there.', 'Initially just the sounds of hiking, which gives way to an unnatural stillness broken only by the rhythmic, lung-like breathing of the trailer.', 'The clean scent of dead leaves and distant rain, later tainted by the memory-smell of cloves and cigarette smoke associated with Whitney.', 'Cool winter air, which becomes thick and charged with static energy near the trailer.', 'Begins with a feeling of fragile, desperate normalcy that is shattered by the appearance of the trailer, quickly descending into dread, tension, and surreal horror.', 412, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 18:59:42.893371-05', '2026-02-28 18:59:42.893371-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (425, 'The Impossible Staircase and Altar Chamber', 'other', 'A spiral staircase made of organic, bone-like material that curves in impossible dimensions. The walls are pulsing, veined organic tissue. The stairs lead down into a chamber with an altar, surrounded by dark water and walls that fracture to reveal recursive honeycomb chambers and a giant alien eye.', 'Distorted, layered echoes of any spoken words. Wet sounds of pulsing flesh. Whispers from bursting bubbles. Later, the sound of tearing reality, screams, and a profound, pressure-filled silence.', 'A metallic smell, like old pennies.', 'The stairs are yielding, like calcified cartilage. The water is warm and thick like syrup. The air grows thick and difficult to breathe. The walls feel like flesh stretched over broken glass.', 'Deeply wrong, oppressive, and terrifying. Reality is thin and unstable, causing sensory distortion and psychological distress. The atmosphere is that of being inside a vast, living, and malevolent creature.', 413, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:00:44.42384-05', '2026-02-28 19:00:44.42384-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (426, 'Outside the Abandoned RV', 'exterior', 'Bright, clean daylight that feels painfully intense after the darkness. Swamp water on their clothes evaporates instantly. The ground is grass, weeds, and dirt.', 'Initially just the sound of gasping for air, followed by Becca''s violent, body-wracking sobs and raw, snarled accusations.', 'Clean, normal oxygen that tastes sharp after the smell of blood and forgotten screams from the other reality.', 'Sunlight feels like daggers on the skin. Lungs burn from fresh air. Becca''s hands claw at the earth.', 'A mixture of intense relief, traumatic shock, and escalating interpersonal conflict. The air is thick with grief, blame, and fear.', 414, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:01:43.867489-05', '2026-02-28 19:01:43.867489-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (430, 'Mr. Hammond''s English Classroom', 'interior', 'A standard high school classroom with rows of desks, a chalkboard, and motivational posters. A periodic table is incongruously on one wall.', 'The droning voice of the teacher, the shuffling of papers, the eventual ringing of the bell.', 'Chalk dust and old books.', 'The plastic edge of a desk.', 'Tense and mundane, with an undercurrent of academic anxiety and boredom.', 418, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:06:00.803375-05', '2026-02-28 19:06:00.803375-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (431, 'Northgate High School (Campus Grounds)', 'other', 'A quintessential American high school environment, encompassing hallways with lockers, a library filled with paper birds, a sunny courtyard for lunch, the concrete steps behind the gym, and the flagpole area out front. The setting transitions throughout a school day, grounding the supernatural events in mundane reality.', 'The typical sounds of a school day: the chatter of students discussing quizzes and gossip, the quiet hum of study hall, and the emotional sounds of Jamie''s crying and later, her soft humming.', 'The comforting smell of Jamie''s homemade food contrasts with the institutional scents of the school, like old books and chalk dust.', 'The warmth of Jamie''s hand, the feverish heat of her skin, the press of her body against Stephen''s, and the texture of folded notebook paper.', 'The atmosphere is a delicate balance of teenage romance and existential dread. It shifts from sweet and hopeful to vulnerable and desperate, all under the shadow of a fragile, potentially false reality.', 419, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:07:05.433076-05', '2026-02-28 19:07:05.433076-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (429, 'Ms. Rodriguez''s AP Bio Lab', 'interior', 'A cramped lab with black-topped tables, grimy windows letting in late January light, and flickering fluorescent lights. The room is filled with jars of preserved specimens and features a skeleton model in the corner.', 'The hum and flicker of fluorescent lights, with the muffled sounds of a high school lunch period—slamming lockers and distant shouting—coming from the hallway.', 'A pervasive stench of formaldehyde, mixed with the unnatural, death-like smell emanating from Whitney''s journal.', NULL, 'Tense and claustrophobic. It''s a makeshift sanctuary for the group, but it feels unsettling and grim, surrounded by preserved dead things.', 417, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:04:58.842502-05', '2026-02-28 19:08:17.660236-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (433, 'Altered High School Grounds', 'transitional', 'The scene begins in a science lab that is systematically destroyed by explosions, imploding lights, and supernatural fire. It transitions to a hallway with buckling lockers and shifting geometry, and finally opens into a parking lot that has become a vast, featureless white expanse under a blinking moon, with the school flickering like a broken TV signal.', 'A cacophony of explosions, a warped child''s laugh, shattering glass, groaning metal, and screams.', 'A mix of burning methane, ozone, burnt plastic, rotten eggs, and a sickeningly organic smell like old hair and meat.', 'The physical force of a blast wave, stinging shards of warped light, viscous black liquid from sprinklers, shifting gravity, and finally the cool evening air of the parking lot.', 'The atmosphere shifts from mundane relief to absolute chaos and surreal horror. The fundamental laws of physics and reality are shown to be fragile and actively hostile.', 421, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:09:14.078264-05', '2026-02-28 19:09:14.078264-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (434, 'The Collapsing School Perimeter', 'exterior', 'A schoolyard where reality is actively failing. A burning school emits flames of impossible colors, smoke rises in geometric spirals, and the surrounding world has been replaced by a void. The sky is a blinking cursor, and objects like a fire engine are rendered in flat, depthless colors.', 'An abrupt, unnatural silence after a fire alarm cuts out, punctuated only by the Auditor''s dispassionate voice and the static-like sounds he makes.', 'Unstable and surreal. The smell shifts from acrid smoke to peanut butter to something metallic and digital.', 'The normal sensation of grass underfoot, contrasted with the intangible nature of the floating code fragments.', 'Deeply unsettling, terrifying, and surreal. The fundamental laws of physics, color, and space are breaking down, creating a sense of profound wrongness and inescapable doom.', 422, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:10:30.579755-05', '2026-02-28 19:10:30.579755-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (436, 'The Auditor''s Judgment Chamber', 'other', 'An abstract, non-physical space defined by streams of floating code (ones and zeros). The code is dynamic, turning blood red or stuttering. The only physical feature mentioned is a marble floor, a remnant from the previous scene.', 'Characterized by oppressive silence broken by wailing alarms and the Auditor''s booming, mountain-collapsing voice. The silence itself is described as ''drowning''.', NULL, NULL, 'Sterile, terrifying, and oppressive. The fundamental laws of reality are mutable and subject to the Auditor''s bureaucratic control, instilling a profound sense of powerlessness and impending doom.', 424, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:12:27.599514-05', '2026-02-28 19:12:27.599514-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (435, 'The Auditor''s Chamber', 'interior', 'A vast chamber made of white marble with impossible angles and non-Euclidean geometry. The floors stretch into infinity, reflecting sourceless lights, and the walls pulse as if breathing. Lines of system code drift through the air like digital snow.', 'Voices echo unnaturally in the immense space. The Auditor''s voice is a physical vibration, like tuning forks resonating in one''s bones. The scene includes screams, roars, and the sound of a universe breaking.', 'After Jamie''s deletion, the air fills with the copper smell of blood that is simultaneously real and unreal.', 'The cold metal of the restraint tables and the liquid-like feel of the bonds. Later, the warm, wet impact of Jamie''s flesh and blood.', 'Sterile, clinical, and utterly terrifying. A surreal, digital prison outside the laws of normal reality, designed for containment and processing.', 423, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:11:31.477636-05', '2026-02-28 19:13:29.731412-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (438, 'Westwood High School (Reset)', 'interior', 'The school appears physically intact and undamaged, with no signs of the previous fire. However, the hallways and cafeteria feel strangely hollow and off-kilter due to the absence of certain people and the wrongness of others.', 'Normal school sounds like a teacher''s droning voice, chalk on blackboard, and pencils tapping are present, but the ambient noise in the cafeteria seems muted, as if ''the volume on reality itself'' was turned down.', 'A typical classroom mixture of industrial cleaner, teenage desperation, and coffee breath. Notably, the smell of smoke from the previously destroyed Biology Lab is absent.', NULL, 'Deeply unsettling and surreal. What at first seems like a return to normalcy quickly reveals itself to be a flawed and corrupted simulation, creating a constant sense of unease and psychological dread.', 426, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:14:19.708292-05', '2026-02-28 19:14:19.708292-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (441, 'Stephen''s Bedroom (Florida)', 'interior', 'A dark room with twisted sheets on the bed. The only light comes from the burning red numbers of a digital clock (3:17 AM) and the hallway light backlighting Jamie''s silhouette.', 'The constant hum of an air conditioner, the soft click of a window door opening, and whispered voices.', 'The unstated but implied scent of sweat from nightmares and the thick humidity of a Florida night.', 'Cold sweats on the skin and a pervasive, humid air that seeps through single-pane windows.', 'Initially a prison of memory and fear, which later transforms into a space of intimacy and ritualistic healing.', 429, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:17:32.208222-05', '2026-02-28 19:17:32.208222-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (443, 'Abandoned Texaco Gas Station', 'exterior', 'A derelict gas station on SR518 that shouldn''t exist, with a bleached Texaco sign, rusted pumps, and cracked asphalt. It shimmers in the humidity and flickers between decay and its past vitality during the ritual before fading away.', 'The air vibrates with unnatural harmonics during the ritual, followed by shouting and a powerful explosion.', 'The heavy scent of Florida humidity, mixed with the smell of oil-stained asphalt and ozone after the explosion.', 'Thick, viscous air that''s hard to breathe, sudden pressure changes, and the hard, cracked asphalt.', 'Eerie and impossible, a place of tense anticipation that descends into chaos, pain, and failure.', 431, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:19:21.715603-05', '2026-02-28 19:19:21.715603-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (444, 'The Wrong House', 'interior', 'An open-plan living room and kitchen, aggressively clean and perfect. The drywall has no fist-holes, the carpet is unstained, and everything looks like it''s from a sitcom set about functional families.', 'The humming of an Eagles song by Wrong Dad, the cheerful chatter of a morning show on TV, and the parents'' excessively cheerful voices.', NULL, 'The crisp, uncreased texture of freshly printed money.', 'Oppressively perfect and sterile. The ''normalcy'' is described as making Stephen''s skin crawl, creating a sense of deep unease and artificiality.', 432, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:20:41.935681-05', '2026-02-28 19:20:41.935681-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (445, 'Stephen''s Room in Paradise', 'interior', 'A pristine, comfortable bedroom with windows that aren''t painted shut and a lock on the inside. Moonlight streams in. The bed is soft, and the furniture and belongings are upgraded, name-brand versions of what they should be.', 'Quiet, except for the muffled sounds of conversation and the lazy turning of a ceiling fan.', 'Smells of fabric softener and, at one point, the phantom scent of fresh-baked cookies.', 'Everything is smooth and soft, from the sheets to the pristine bag, contrasting with the rough, real texture of the clay sigil.', 'A deceptive sense of safety and comfort overlaying a deep feeling of unreality and entrapment. It''s a ''beautiful cage'' that feels both perfect and profoundly wrong.', 433, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:21:42.120812-05', '2026-02-28 19:21:42.120812-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (446, 'The Liminal Space of Route 666-B', 'transitional', 'A journey that begins in a grimy, pre-dawn Greyhound station and transitions to a decrepit, shifting bus. The exterior view decays from ''aggressively normal'' cityscapes to a theoretical, featureless void before resolving into a desert landscape from a photograph.', 'The sounds of a bus engine, breaking glass laughter, vomited words, a screaming bathroom, static-laced announcements, and the layered voices of ghosts.', 'Diesel, desperation, burnt rubber, medicinal chemicals, sulfur, old bones, amniotic fluid, bourbon, and gunpowder.', 'Duct-taped seats, the heat from another person''s body, the slick walls of a living bathroom, and the warmth of a photograph coming to life.', 'Begins with grim desperation and evolves into surreal dread and existential horror. The air is thick with foreboding, the decay of reality, and the weight of past tragedies.', 434, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:22:35.180837-05', '2026-02-28 19:22:35.180837-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (447, 'The Inverted Church, Nowhere, Nevada', 'exterior', 'A tilted, bone-white wooden church rising from a desolate desert landscape. It has an inverted cross, broken stained-glass windows, and a cracked foundation. The interior is a desecrated, graffiti-covered space with scattered pews and a sickly phosphorescent glow.', 'Outside, an absolute, pressing silence broken only by the crunch of sand. Inside, footsteps echo incorrectly, floorboards creak in anticipation of weight, and disembodied whispers emanate from the walls.', 'The exterior air smells of sulfur and burning hair from the departing bus. The interior reeks of human excrement, stale condoms, decay, burning feces, and bleach.', 'The exterior is dominated by a dry, merciless heat. The interior experiences a rapid, unnatural temperature drop, with frost forming on the pews.', 'Oppressive, malevolent, and fundamentally wrong. The laws of physics and geometry feel twisted and hostile. The atmosphere is described as hungry and contaminated.', 435, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:23:43.43186-05', '2026-02-28 19:23:43.43186-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (448, 'Childhood Trailer Home', 'interior', 'A cramped, dirty single-wide trailer. The bedroom has yellowed wallpaper with water stains, peeling lead paint, a swollen particle board dresser, and faded Popeye curtains. The hallway is narrow with industrial brown carpet and photos on the walls.', 'The walls are thin enough to hear every sound. Distant humming, the death rattle of a refrigerator, and later, aggressive footsteps and deep snoring.', 'An implied smell of dampness, dust, and stale air.', 'Cold, gritty linoleum floors. Chipped porcelain on the bathroom sink.', 'Oppressive, tense, and filled with traumatic memories. A feeling of being trapped and unsafe.', 436, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:24:56.545502-05', '2026-02-28 19:24:56.545502-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (459, 'The Final Void', 'other', 'A non-space where reality is actively collapsing into swirling mathematical chaos and pixelating static. It is a place of dissolution, ultimately becoming absolute, featureless white.', 'Initially filled with the echoing sound of applause, it eventually becomes absolutely silent.', NULL, 'The void is described as warm, and the static that dissolves matter feels like ''digital ivy'' crawling up one''s legs.', 'Despite the absolute destruction, the atmosphere is strangely peaceful, clean, and relieving. It feels like the end of a prison rather than a tragedy.', 447, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:34:54.279468-05', '2026-02-28 19:34:54.279468-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (449, 'Childhood Home Kitchen', 'interior', 'A kitchen with yellowed Formica counters and linoleum floors. The wallpaper shifts between yellow and green as reality fractures. The space is filled with the visual signifiers of poverty and neglect.', 'The scene begins with the mother''s tuneless, broken humming, which is later replaced by the sound of a shattering glass vial and her deep, tectonic sobs.', 'A potent ''cocktail of poverty and desperation'': the smell of botulism from expired cans, sour reconstituted powdered milk, the garlic-stink of fear-sweat, and a medicinal odor.', 'Humid air that makes bread go soft. The sharp sting of shattered glass on the floor.', 'Begins with a tense, dreadful sense of false domesticity. After the confrontation, the atmosphere becomes unstable, surreal, and saturated with grief and horrified realization.', 437, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:26:00.523469-05', '2026-02-28 19:26:00.523469-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (450, 'Childhood Home Bathroom', 'interior', 'A simple, likely sparse bathroom with a sink and a mirror. The lighting is a harsh fluorescent fixture. The floor is cold tile.', 'The click of the door shutting, creating a temporary seal from the outside world. Later, the sound of snoring from a nearby bedroom ceases abruptly.', NULL, 'The cold tile floor and the solid wood of the door pressed against the protagonist''s back.', 'Initially a claustrophobic refuge from family trauma, it quickly transforms into a liminal space where cosmic reality intrudes. The atmosphere is tense, revelatory, and filled with dread.', 438, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:26:54.299864-05', '2026-02-28 19:26:54.299864-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (451, 'The Family Trailer', 'interior', 'A cramped, box-like trailer with thin walls, dirty windows, and linoleum flooring. The space includes a hallway, a bedroom, a bathroom, and a kitchen area, all small and offering no escape.', 'Sounds are amplified by the thin walls, such as a door detonating like a gunshot, heavy footsteps, whimpering, screams, and the wet, wrong sound of cracking bones.', 'The air carries the scent of motor oil and desperation from the father.', 'The floor is hard tile. The air is cool on damaged skin.', 'Extremely tense, claustrophobic, and saturated with terror. It is described as a ''tomb'' and a ''box'' where the inhabitants are ''rats trapped inside'' with a predator.', 439, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:27:47.67073-05', '2026-02-28 19:27:47.67073-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (452, 'The Abusive Memory Trailer', 'interior', 'A bedroom within a trailer, defined by blue Popeye curtains and a water-stained ceiling. The initial setting is mundane, grounding the horror in a familiar space.', 'The distinct sounds of the abuser''s arrival: a slamming door, heavy and uneven footsteps, and the victim''s mother whimpering from another room.', NULL, NULL, 'Begins with a suffocating sense of dread and inevitability, which rapidly escalates into raw terror and pain.', 440, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:28:44.360244-05', '2026-02-28 19:28:44.360244-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (453, 'The Leather Classroom', 'interior', 'A surreal, nightmarish room that is a fusion of a bedroom and an industrial tannery. The furniture is replaced with tanning benches and vats, curtains are strips of curing leather, and the walls are covered in grotesque posters about turning humans into belts. A conveyor system on the ceiling holds finished belts like carcasses.', 'The bubbling of chemical vats and the final, disembodied ring of a bell.', 'An overpowering, sinus-burning stench of industrial leather treatment chemicals, processed hide, and chromium salts.', 'The air is thick and tastes of chemicals. Surfaces include the cold, scratched metal of an examination table and the intense heat radiating from a glowing vat.', 'Claustrophobic, surreal, and deeply unsettling. The atmosphere is one of methodical, educational horror and inescapable dread.', 441, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:29:44.415204-05', '2026-02-28 19:29:44.415204-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (454, 'Protagonist''s Childhood Bedroom (Hyperreal Memory)', 'interior', 'A familiar bedroom with mismatched furniture, a water stain on the ceiling shaped like Florida, and a pile of dirty clothes. The scene is saturated with golden sunlight streaming through real glass windows.', 'The gentle, meandering humming of a mother in the kitchen and the crisp rustle of over-washed bedsheets.', 'A mix of bacon grease, coffee, vanilla air freshener, old carpet, dust, and the faint mildew of Florida humidity.', 'The scratchy, synthetic fiber of the carpet.', 'Begins as hyperrealistically safe and nostalgic, a perfect memory dialed up to an unnatural intensity. It curdles into a sterile, terrifying space for a surreal and horrific lesson.', 442, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:30:26.043448-05', '2026-02-28 19:30:26.043448-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (455, 'The Surreal Bedroom', 'interior', 'A room with skinned, screaming walls and a ceiling that stretches to impossible heights yet feels close enough to touch. Blood rains upward from the floor, and the entire space expands and contracts like a lung. Shadows from a flaming belt dance independently of their source.', 'Low, pained moans from the walls that harmonize into a ''choir of the damned'', vibrating through the floorboards. The sounds later fade to whispers and then an awkward silence.', 'The smell of ''rancid pennies and the last breath of dying animals'' emanates from the rising blood.', 'The floor vibrates with sound. The ceiling is wet and yielding. The air shimmers with heat, and the blood droplets are warm like a living body.', 'Simultaneously infinite and claustrophobic, terrifyingly real yet governed by impossible physics. The atmosphere is one of hellish, repetitive torment that is beginning to lose its stability.', 443, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:31:09.282117-05', '2026-02-28 19:31:09.282117-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (456, 'The Collapsing Pocket Reality', 'other', 'A surreal, shifting space that begins as a bedroom with breathing walls and a ceiling of teeth. It transforms into an ''impossible cathedral of compressed starlight'' before shrinking, strobing through past realities, and finally collapsing into a void.', 'The location is filled with the sound of grinding bone, wet tearing, distorted divine commands, and the screams of angels. This culminates in a conceptual explosion followed by perfect, peaceful silence.', 'The air is described as having an ''oily consistency'' like transmission fluid.', 'The atmosphere is thick and hostile. Gravity is unstable, pulling in multiple directions. The final stage involves intense pressure as reality compresses.', 'Begins as deeply hostile and insane, transitions to a state of false divinity, then becomes frantic and desperate as it collapses, ultimately resolving into one of absolute peace and stillness.', 444, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:31:56.652468-05', '2026-02-28 19:31:56.652468-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (457, 'The Liminal Waiting Room', 'interior', 'A sterile pediatrician''s waiting room with institutional cream walls and peeling beige wallpaper. It is furnished with oversized plastic chairs and a motionless Star Wars mobile. The space feels artificial and unreal, with a door that appears only when it needs to.', 'An absolute, aching silence that is an active presence, broken only by Benji''s voice and the crunching of his popcorn.', 'Initially sterile and scentless, but later the air tastes of ''apples and burnt electronics''.', 'The hard plastic of the chairs. The atmosphere grows intensely cold, causing frost to form on surfaces.', 'Begins as sterile, liminal, and unnerving. It grows progressively more unstable and hostile as I AM''s presence asserts itself, with reality flickering and shuddering.', 445, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:33:05.25298-05', '2026-02-28 19:33:05.25298-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (461, 'Protagonist''s Kitchen', 'interior', 'A domestic kitchen in the morning, with sunlight and raw ingredients for breakfast (vanilla, peaches) scattered on a counter. A coffee maker is present.', 'The sounds of a family waking up, conversation, the clink of a coffee mug, and the distant sounds of a computer game from the son.', 'The rich fragrance of freshly brewed coffee, later joined by the scent of vanilla and peaches.', 'The warmth of a coffee mug, the gentle touch of a spouse''s hand.', 'Begins as a scene of quiet, contemplative domesticity, but grows tense with confusion and is ultimately shattered by overwhelming grief and remembered trauma.', 449, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:36:44.274997-05', '2026-02-28 19:36:44.274997-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (462, 'The Protagonist''s Florida Home', 'interior', 'A typical family home with a kitchen and living room. The scene shifts from a supernaturally still, ''wrong'' version of the home to its normal, comfortable state.', 'The sounds of a normal life: a wife humming, a son talking to online friends. This contrasts with the earlier hallucinatory sounds of repeating laughter.', 'The comforting smell of sweet waffles and warm coffee, signifying a return to reality.', NULL, 'Initially tense, dreadful, and unnervingly perfect. It resolves into a comfortable, mundane, and grounding atmosphere of normal family life.', 450, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:37:41.028865-05', '2026-02-28 19:37:41.028865-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (463, 'Protagonist''s Computer Desk', 'interior', 'An old, worn desk surface bathed in the soft glow of afternoon light. A computer screen flickers with job listings.', 'The quiet tapping of fingers on a keyboard, punctuated by the protagonist''s occasional muttered thoughts.', NULL, 'The worn, familiar surface of the desk.', 'A blend of quiet contemplation, mundane focus, and a heavy undercurrent of cynicism and resignation.', 451, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:38:22.705997-05', '2026-02-28 19:38:22.705997-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (467, 'Author''s Note Space', 'other', 'A conceptual, meta-textual space where the author directly addresses the reader, outside the narrative of the story.', 'The candid, internal voice of the author explaining their creative process and future plans.', NULL, NULL, 'Reflective and transparent, with a tone of self-awareness and forward-looking hope.', 455, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 19:41:20.990247-05', '2026-02-28 19:41:20.990247-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (468, 'Book Front Matter', 'other', 'Formatted text on a page, including title, author, copyright details, ISBNs, and a synopsis. The layout is structured and formal.', 'Conceptual silence, the imagined sound of turning a page.', 'The faint, conceptual smell of paper and ink.', 'The conceptual feel of a smooth book page.', 'Informational, formal, and introductory. It sets the stage for the narrative to come without being part of the story itself.', 456, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:14:30.493156-05', '2026-02-28 22:14:30.493156-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (469, 'A Mental Landscape of Invocation', 'other', 'An abstract, non-physical space defined by the speaker''s voice and the concepts being discussed. It is a realm of thought and metaphor, lacking concrete visual details.', 'Dominated by the speaker''s calm, resonant voice delivering the poetic counsel.', NULL, NULL, 'Contemplative, instructive, and slightly melancholic. The atmosphere is one of a teacher or elder imparting crucial, timeless advice to the young.', 457, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:15:36.931761-05', '2026-02-28 22:15:36.931761-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (470, 'The Conceptual Construct', 'interior', 'A realm with malleable walls that bend with force and a mundane linoleum floor. It is a space where concepts have tangible form and reality itself is unstable.', 'Dominated by Yaldabaoth''s physically forceful roar, which gives way to a soundless internal detonation and a final, crystalline crash of shattering reality.', NULL, 'The physical pressure of sound waves and the catastrophic, rule-violating impact of physical strikes.', 'Apocalyptic and reality-breaking. The environment is saturated with divine power, threats of annihilation, and the cold fury of a consuming anomaly.', 458, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:16:45.147475-05', '2026-02-28 22:16:45.147475-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (471, 'The Void of Non-Existence', 'other', 'Eternal darkness stretching for infinity. A void so complete it folds inward on itself, described as the cold spaces between zeros.', 'A silence beyond erasure, containing only the echo of what can no longer remember itself.', NULL, 'A complete lack of heat or motion, a fundamental coldness.', 'A hungry, complete nullity where even decay has ceased. It is a state of absolute erasure and silence, now being disturbed by an impossible re-emergence.', 459, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:17:35.721493-05', '2026-02-28 22:17:35.721493-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (472, 'The Substrate', 'other', 'A malleable, code-based reality that bends like ''liquid glass''. It is a grid of light and data where worlds blur and timelines compress, containing a ''thin shimmer of time'' that represents a narrow band of possibility.', 'The architecture screams under the strain of timeline compression. Otherwise, it is a place of deep hums and potential silence.', 'The smell of entropy burning clean during the rollback process.', 'The feeling of immense, vibrating power and fundamental instability.', 'Extremely volatile and surreal, a conceptual space where the laws of physics are subject to the will of powerful entities. The atmosphere is charged with cosmic power and the tension of creation and erasure.', 460, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:18:26.71525-05', '2026-02-28 22:18:26.71525-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (475, 'Stephen''s Study', 'interior', 'A mundane room with a keyboard that becomes grotesquely organic. The window develops a milky, cataract-like film, and the protagonist''s vision fills with a cancerous mesh of erupting blood vessels.', 'Begins with an oppressive quiet, ''like the moment between a lightning strike and thunder''. This is replaced by the sound of pulsing air, wet tearing sounds, popping joints, and a final, heavy rip.', 'The scent of static and ozone.', 'The floor loses its solidity, yielding ''like soft, wet tissue''. The air becomes thick with a ''wave of intense, suffocating wrongness''.', 'Shifts rapidly from mundane self-pity to tense, reality-bending dread, and finally culminates in a storm of pure body horror and cosmic annihilation.', 463, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:21:08.477877-05', '2026-02-28 22:21:08.477877-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (480, 'The House (Bedroom & Bathroom)', 'interior', 'A dark house at night. The bedroom is lit only by a sliver of blue light from under the door. The adjoining bathroom has a cluttered medicine cabinet under the sink and a mirror that reflects only darkness.', 'Almost completely silent, punctuated only by the ''silent hiss'' of a plastic drawer.', 'An implied scent of dust in the medicine cabinet''s ''crypt''.', 'The sensation of carpet underfoot, the weight of a heavy comforter, and the coldness of a divot in a mattress.', 'Somber, clinical, and detached. The atmosphere is heavy with resignation and finality.', 468, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:25:17.189248-05', '2026-02-28 22:25:17.189248-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (481, 'The Grey Purgatory', 'exterior', 'A perpetually damp, monochromatic city corner where it is always raining but no puddles ever form. The world is rendered in dull shades of grey, featuring a brick wall, a newsstand, a bodega, and a flower stand.', 'The inconsistent, arrhythmic drip-drip-drop of rain and the faint sound of cars that never seem to arrive or depart.', 'The smell of wet brick and faint, sour exhaust fumes, later pierced by the sharp scent of ozone and burnt cinnamon.', 'A pervasive feeling of dampness that doesn''t translate to actual wetness. The solid, rough texture of brick.', 'Deeply disorienting and oppressive. The environment feels both alien and vaguely familiar, creating a powerful sense of existential dread and unreality.', 469, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:26:14.630133-05', '2026-02-28 22:26:14.630133-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (474, 'Etheris', 'exterior', 'An entire reality constructed as an architecture of confinement, disguised as a divine creation. It appears as a ''corner pocket of false creation'' whose true nature is hidden.', 'Primordial silence, broken only by the faint, echoing memory of a judgmental voice from the moment of its sealing.', 'An overwhelming stench of decay and chemicals, primarily a mix of raw seafood, ammonia, and brine from the Mi-Go corpses.', 'The feeling of being contained, observed, and confined within one''s own flesh.', 'Oppressive, deceptive, and recursive. An eternal prison designed to make the inmate believe they are the warden.', 462, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:20:04.997891-05', '2026-02-28 23:30:12.228137-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (482, 'The Impossible Coffee Shop', 'interior', 'An unnaturally perfect and sterile space that appears from nowhere. Tables and chairs are arranged with geometric precision. A corner booth exists in a pocket of deep shadow. The environment is wrong in a way that ''fits''.', 'Eerily silent. The door makes no sound, and the barista''s repetitive actions are noiseless. Sound does not carry properly, creating a muted, distant feeling.', 'The bitter, herbal scent of the Memory Tea.', 'The air grows heavy and thick, with a palpable pressure building in the protagonist''s skull as the interrogation intensifies.', 'Clinical, tense, and menacing. The atmosphere is one of controlled artificiality, designed for interrogation and assessment, making the protagonist feel trapped and scrutinized.', 470, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:27:03.516743-05', '2026-02-28 22:27:03.516743-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (483, 'Interrogation Booth', 'interior', 'A grey, clinical, and purgatorial space. The booth itself is featureless and can seemingly seal itself around its occupant, removing any space to move or escape.', 'Initially filled with the layered, wet voice of the interrogator, it later shifts to a painful buzzing frequency, then to silence, and finally to the warm, human tones of Lady Illkeserod.', NULL, 'The oppressive, gravitational weight of the word ''signal'' pressing on the chest. Later, the warm and gentle touch of Lady Illkeserod''s hands.', 'Begins as intensely oppressive, terrifying, and clinical. It undergoes a dramatic shift to become intimate, emotional, and revelatory after the transformation.', 471, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:27:56.872263-05', '2026-02-28 22:27:56.872263-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (484, 'The Booth', 'interior', 'A small, enclosed space, likely simple and functional. The focus is entirely on the two occupants, not the decor.', 'Quiet, punctuated only by the protagonist''s gasp, the sound of his own trembling, and Ilse''s soft whispers.', NULL, 'The firm, grounding touch of Ilse''s fingers on the protagonist''s face and forehead.', 'Intensely personal and emotionally charged with the energy of revelation and reintegration. A safe, grounding space after a traumatic journey through fragmented memories.', 472, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:28:48.741398-05', '2026-02-28 22:28:48.741398-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (485, 'Purgatory Coffee Shop', 'interior', 'A seemingly normal coffee shop, but set within a ''looping world''. Outside, a grey rain perpetually falls. The interior features a barista stuck in a repetitive, mindless loop.', 'The ambient, looping sounds of a coffee shop, which gives way to silence as reality is breached, and finally the sound of ''tearing fabric'' as the realm reacts to the escape.', NULL, 'The air is thick with a sense of stagnation. Ilse''s grip is described as warm, solid, and real, a stark contrast to the artificiality of the environment.', 'Initially grave and oppressive, the atmosphere shifts to one of tense hope and then urgent action as the possibility of escape becomes real.', 473, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:29:58.036374-05', '2026-02-28 22:29:58.036374-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (487, 'Stephen''s Kitchen', 'interior', 'A typical home kitchen with a coffee maker, an electric kettle, and a sink. The scene begins with it being mostly clean, save for a single spoon, and ends with the lingering presence of Stephen and his son.', 'The sounds of the electric kettle boiling, coffee dripping slowly, the sharp scoff from Stephen''s wife, and the quiet, conspiratorial tones of Stephen and Xavier''s conversation.', 'The smell of fresh coffee filling the room towards the end of the scene.', 'The warmth of a coffee mug and the coldness of the counter.', 'Begins with high tension and oppressive criticism, shifts to a moment of quiet connection and dawning horror, and ends in contemplative silence.', 475, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:31:57.262898-05', '2026-02-28 22:32:54.020373-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (493, 'Stephen''s Patio', 'exterior', 'An outdoor patio space, presumably at Stephen''s home. It has a ceiling fan.', 'The clicking of a ceiling fan, the sound of crickets, and the distant hum of an air conditioning unit.', NULL, NULL, 'Initially a mundane, quiet space that becomes the epicenter of a terrifying psychic event before settling into a state of anxious relief.', 481, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:37:15.111704-05', '2026-02-28 22:37:15.111704-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (508, 'Nightmarish Forest', 'exterior', 'A landscape under a constant, bruised-purple twilight with no sun or stars. Trees have an oxidized copper sheen and pulse rhythmically. The air is thick with ash that hangs suspended, and the ground is a soft, yielding surface like scar tissue.', 'An unsettling quiet with no wind, punctuated only by the howls of beasts and the slow, rhythmic pulsing of the trees.', 'The air smells of spoiled eggs, burnt hair, and an unidentifiable, sickeningly sweet scent.', 'The ground is soft and yielding underfoot. The air is thick with ash.', 'Alien, hostile, and deeply wrong. The entire environment feels alive in a malevolent, biological way.', 494, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:55:00.715933-05', '2026-02-28 22:55:00.715933-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (490, 'Stephen and Angela''s House', 'interior', 'A living room with a couch, coffee table, and end table. The wall is damaged by a shattered glass, with shards on the couch. Later scenes occur in a bedroom.', 'The sound of a TV show (''Resident Alien''), tense conversation, a dish clattering, a glass smashing, followed by heavy silence. Later, the quiet sounds of a ceiling fan clicking, crickets, and an AC unit humming.', 'The smell of shrimp tempura.', 'The feeling of sitting on a couch, and later, brushing a shard of glass off jeans. The cool air from the AC.', 'Begins with familiar tension, escalates to hostility and sudden danger, then becomes eerily calm after the loop resets. The atmosphere later shifts to quiet contemplation mixed with hope and a sudden, deep-seated terror.', NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:34:33.299402-05', '2026-02-28 22:49:05.389963-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (495, 'Florida Highway (I-95 to 520)', 'exterior', 'Endless, flat stretches of road lined with palm trees, sage brush, and occasional cows. The scenery is punctuated by billboards for injury lawyers and adult superstores.', 'The white noise of radio static, later broken by a sudden screech and talk show chatter.', 'The faint, ambient smell of fresh peaches from a roadside stand.', 'Oppressive, unseasonable November heat blasting through the open windows of a moving car.', 'Hypnotic and monotonous, fostering a sense of isolation and introspection that gives way to a moment of haunting surreality.', 483, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:39:10.743052-05', '2026-02-28 22:39:10.743052-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (496, 'Parking Lot near Jamie''s Marginalia', 'exterior', 'A small parking lot in a gentrified warehouse district, situated between a Jamba Juice and a yoga studio. The area is characterized by sun-baked brick buildings and decorative looping string lights.', 'The repetitive chirping of a GPS, followed by the ambient sounds of a normal weekday afternoon, such as people walking dogs.', 'A powerful, artificial scent of vanilla and peaches from the nearby smoothie shop, which later mingles with the taste/smell of copper and static inside Stephen''s car.', 'The clammy sweat on Stephen''s neck; the resistance of the air as he walks, which feels like moving through water.', 'The atmosphere shifts from mundane frustration to one of intense, charged significance and supernatural tension. It feels like a liminal space where the barrier between realities is thin.', 484, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:39:55.920791-05', '2026-02-28 22:39:55.920791-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (498, 'Jamie''s Marginalia - Back Room', 'interior', 'A dim room with mismatched shelves of older, darker wood. Books are packed tightly, with cracked spines and faded covers. Dust gathers in visible layers. An ancient, heavy oak desk with a scarred surface sits against one wall.', 'Abrupt silence after the muffled party sounds from the main shop fade. A sense of oppressive quiet.', 'The faint smell of old parchment, oil, and a sweet decay, like ''memory''.', 'The air is dense and viscous, filtered through dust. The wood of the desk feels faintly warm. Dust clings to fingertips like ash.', 'Feels older and heavier than the rest of the shop. A sense of actual neglect, reverence, and caution. The weight of time presses in from all sides.', 486, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:41:32.351858-05', '2026-02-28 22:41:32.351858-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (497, 'Jamie''s Marginalia', 'interior', 'A small, intimate bookshop with exposed brick walls, floor-to-ceiling shelves, mismatched armchairs, and warm amber string lights. Books are organized chaotically, with sections like ''Esoteric Bullshit'' next to ''Cozy Mysteries''.', 'A low murmur of conversation from about a dozen patrons, creating a cocoon of white noise.', 'A complex mix of old paper, dark roast coffee, and a faint floral scent from jasmine candles, which Stephen perceives as vanilla and peaches.', 'The air is described as Orlando heat outside the shop.', 'Initially warm, lived-in, and welcoming. As the scene progresses, it takes on a ''thinner'' quality for Stephen, feeling like the membrane of reality is fragile.', 485, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:40:43.101452-05', '2026-02-28 22:42:34.544324-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (501, 'The Space Outside Etheris', 'exterior', 'A wound in the fabric of reality, a void where stars don''t shine but ''breathe'' with pulses of impossible color. At its center floats Etheris, a perfect, light-devouring black sphere.', 'A pervasive hum described as ''the residue of creation, like a hymn sung backward,'' overlaid with the thousands of whispering voices from the Akashic streams.', 'Mostly scentless, but for a brief moment it carries the smell of peaches and sunlight, an echo of a memory from within the prison.', NULL, 'Cosmically vast yet deeply tense and sacred. It is a place of ancient power, forgotten myths, and the oppressive presence of the soul prison.', 489, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:44:22.961777-05', '2026-02-28 22:50:06.413732-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (504, 'The Interdimensional Locus', 'other', 'A conceptual space linking three distinct realities: the shimmering, memory-laden streams of Etheris; a dark, featureless void; and a mundane location in the human world.', 'A mix of cosmic whispers from Etheris, the cold hum of the void, and the muted sounds of a normal human environment.', NULL, 'Ranges from the weightless drift of the void to the sudden, disorienting pressure of a metaphysical alignment.', 'Tense and mystical, charged with the energy of a powerful ritual connecting disparate souls across time and space.', 490, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:51:12.844718-05', '2026-02-28 22:51:12.844718-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (505, 'Stephen''s Home Office', 'interior', 'A dim room at sunset, with reddish light filtering through blinds. The primary light source is the tired blue glow of computer monitors on a desk.', 'Initially silent except for the whining fans of a computer. The air has a faint, ominous electronic buzz.', 'The smell of hot electronics, a strange ''wrong'' scent from the wife, and finally, acrid smoke from the destroyed computer.', 'The air is tense and feels heavy with unspoken conflict and technological decay.', 'Oppressive and surreal. A feeling of domestic tension is amplified by a sense of digital corruption and reality breaking down.', 491, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:52:02.890953-05', '2026-02-28 22:52:02.890953-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (506, 'Best Buy', 'interior', 'A decaying retail store with a worn laminate counter. Three of the fluorescent panels in the ceiling are dead, and the sparse shelves are covered in clearance stickers.', 'The persistent, annoying buzz of failing fluorescent lights, like ''dying wasps''. The store is otherwise empty and quiet, punctuated by the chime of the entry door.', 'A stale, old stench that has settled into the carpet fibers, smelling like a place that has ''stopped trying''.', 'The air is normal until the reality shift, after which it feels like it has ''skipped a frame''.', 'An atmosphere of neglect, decay, and tiredness. It feels like a place that knows it''s dying.', 492, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:53:10.219175-05', '2026-02-28 22:53:10.219175-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (507, 'The Interstitial Void', 'other', 'A chaotic space between realities with an undulating floor that isn''t truly ground. Dark energy swirls like an amniotic fog, and membranes of congealed space can be seen tearing open.', 'Characterized by the wet, ripping sounds of creatures manifesting and their high-frequency screams that cause physical pain.', 'The air tastes and smells of copper and formaldehyde.', 'The air is thick and viscous, described as being like ''breathing through placenta''. The ground is slick with strange fluids.', 'Deeply hostile, unstable, and surreal. A ''grey purgatory'' where the normal laws of physics and biology do not apply.', 493, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:54:12.55464-05', '2026-02-28 22:54:12.55464-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (510, 'Patrick''s Compound', 'interior', 'An isolated property surrounded by a chain-link fence topped with razor wire and handmade warning signs. The interior is a chaotic temple or bunker, with every surface covered in carved sigils, candles, jars of herbs, and precarious stacks of books in ancient languages.', 'Outside, the hum of cicadas and croaking of amphibians. Inside, it is presumably silent until the violent confrontation.', 'A strange, layered smell of incense, wet earth, and a sharp chemical scent like a ''male urinal mixed with burnt popcorn''.', 'The air inside is described as becoming thick, resistant, and oppressive, especially in the presence of the construct.', 'Paranoid, isolated, and intensely occult. The atmosphere shifts from tense and mysterious to one of violent, supernatural chaos.', 496, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:56:51.719407-05', '2026-02-28 22:57:34.277129-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (512, 'Lady Illkeserod''s Sanctum', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:58:18.004458-05', '2026-02-28 22:58:18.004458-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (513, 'Patrick''s Trailer', 'interior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 22:59:15.731939-05', '2026-02-28 22:59:15.731939-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (514, 'Patrick''s Study', 'interior', 'A room containing a desk cluttered with various occult paraphernalia. The space feels lived-in and dedicated to esoteric research.', 'The sound of hushed, serious conversation and the rustling of paper as a drawer is opened.', 'The faint scent of old paper and dust.', NULL, 'Conspiratorial and tense, a haven of forbidden knowledge where crucial secrets are exchanged.', 500, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:00:16.411887-05', '2026-02-28 23:00:16.411887-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (328, 'The Ledge of Paradox', 'exterior', 'A stark, featureless ledge overlooking an endless void. The air is hazy with smoke from unseen fires, and the ground is disturbed with freshly buried flowers.', 'A disorienting cacophony of wailing, distant screams, and the roar of fire, all somehow creating a sense of profound, noisy silence.', 'The acrid smell of millions of burning books, mingled with the damp scent of recent rain and the sweet, cloying aroma of funereal flowers.', 'A feeling of dampness from a rain that offers no relief, and the rough texture of a rope that is both a tool and a threat.', 'Surreal, oppressive, and deeply philosophical. The atmosphere is thick with despair, confusion, and the weight of a meaningless, repeating cycle.', 316, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 17:28:37.874696-05', '2026-02-28 23:01:18.113297-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (517, 'The Edge of the Void', 'exterior', 'A non-place of absolute emptiness and static. The prison of Etheris is visible in the distance, hanging like a tumor. When breached, cracks of purple-black light spider-web across the nothingness.', 'Voices are swallowed by static. A breach causes the void to scream. Benji''s transformations create wet, tearing sounds and roars.', NULL, 'The void feels cold and pushes back against physical and intentional pressure.', 'Timeless and desperate. The atmosphere is thick with frustration, which shifts to intense nostalgia and emotional catharsis, before ending on a note of tense, foreboding hope.', 503, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:03:40.308848-05', '2026-02-28 23:03:40.308848-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (518, 'St. Michael''s Outreach Center', 'interior', 'A strip mall ministry with a crooked sign and peeling paint, sandwiched between a vape shop and an abandoned Blockbuster. The interior resembles a community center with folding tables, donated goods, and a bulletin board. It contains an impossible, vast basement library with concrete floors, exposed pipes, and floor-to-ceiling bookshelves.', 'Initially quiet except for distant sirens. Later filled with screaming, shattering glass, and a wet, chittering sound, followed by TJ''s powerful chanting.', 'The exterior smells of old grease and burnt rubber. The hallway to the basement smells of mildew and old coffee. The basement itself smells of dry rot and old paper, which is later overwhelmed by a sickly-sweet artificial scent of peaches and vanilla.', 'The air in the basement is cold enough to see one''s breath.', 'Begins as rundown and slightly strange, shifts to deeply unsettling and wrong, then to outright terrifying and horrific during the attack.', 504, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:04:42.836032-05', '2026-02-28 23:04:42.836032-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (519, 'Dingy Motel Room', 'interior', 'A room with two double beds, lit by a humming light that casts a sickly yellow glow. A television sits in the corner, and a ''Sanitized For Your Protection'' band is on the toilet seat.', 'A constant humming from the light and buzzing from the mini-fridge. Faint sounds of interstate traffic, a couple fighting next door, and a rattling ice machine can be heard from outside.', 'A potent mix of stale cigarettes, mildew, and the sharp chemical smell of industrial cleaner.', 'The remote control is sticky, and the pillows are lumpy.', 'Seedy, tense, and isolating. It feels like a temporary and unsafe refuge from the outside world.', 505, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:06:01.372949-05', '2026-02-28 23:06:01.372949-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (520, 'Orlando Area Roadside', 'transitional', 'A series of mundane, sun-bleached Florida locations: a bright motel room, a cheap Dollar General, and a Waffle House diner. This is sharply contrasted by the shocking sight of a burned-out, blackened bookstore ruin cordoned off with yellow caution tape.', 'The whine of a car engine, the cheap plastic sounds of a discount store, and the clatter of plates and low conversation in a diner.', 'A mix of cheap potpourri, the oppressive smell of hot asphalt, and the acrid, damp scent of a recent fire.', 'The solid pain of a stiff neck, the suffocating heat inside cheap polyester hoodies, and the sticky surface of a diner booth.', 'Begins with urgency and paranoia, shifts to cold dread and horror, and ends with a fragile sense of purpose amidst overwhelming hopelessness. The feeling of being watched and hunted by an unseen force is pervasive.', 506, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:06:58.837227-05', '2026-02-28 23:06:58.837227-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (534, 'The Archives', 'interior', 'A realm of floating towers connected by bridges of light. The sky is perpetually grey, never fully committing to a storm. Inside, the tower walls are covered in symbols, and there is a circular viewing chamber with no walls, offering a map-like projection of the realm below.', 'Largely silent until the alarm, which is a feeling rather than a sound. During mobilization, it fills with the sounds of a diverse army: clicking legs, sprinting feet, and chanting.', NULL, 'The air pressure drops when the alarm is triggered. The rooms are described as warm and safe, with beds that feel real.', 'Initially a tense but safe haven. This shifts dramatically to one of urgent, organized chaos as the defenders mobilize for war.', 520, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:20:48.708996-05', '2026-02-28 23:20:48.708996-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (521, 'The Pallid Mask Theatre', 'interior', 'A condemned warehouse with bricked-up windows and a graffiti-tagged steel door. The interior consists of a small, dark, filthy lobby and a vast, cavernous main space containing broken machinery and a makeshift stage built from shipping palettes. Lighting is provided by a single, flickering, sickly yellow bulb.', 'The location is filled with unsettling sounds: a low, dissonant, reedy piping music that swells into a deafening shriek, a high thin whining noise, theatrical recitations, screams of terror and ecstasy, wet thuds of bodies, and the cracking of bones.', 'The exterior smells of the nearby river and industrial rot. The interior has a heavy air smelling of mold, something rancid like expired tuna, and a cloying, sweet scent of gardenias and honey that intensifies over time. This is later overpowered by the coppery smell of blood.', 'The exterior has a biting cold wind. The air inside is initially still and cold, but a strange heat radiates from the cultists. The temperature plummets upon the arrival of the King in Yellow. The scene ends with the feeling of hot, spattering blood.', 'The atmosphere is oppressive and dangerous. It shifts from desperate and tense to eerie and seductive, then rapidly descends into horrific, orgiastic chaos and cosmic dread.', 507, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:07:57.079337-05', '2026-02-28 23:07:57.079337-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (522, 'The Paddock Farmhouse', 'transitional', 'A large, dark farmhouse at the end of a long gravel driveway, with a single light glowing in a window. The interior is warmed by a massive fireplace and lacks modern technology, featuring woven straw knots and carved stone spirals for decoration. All metalwork is bronze or copper, with a complete absence of iron.', 'The crackle of the fireplace, contrasting with the silence of the surrounding empty farmland.', 'A comforting mix of old wood, herbs, and baking bread.', 'The air is described as feeling ''older, cleaner, like the air after a thunderstorm,'' and the house is warm.', 'Initially mysterious, it quickly becomes a place of ''baffling, professional calm'' and profound safety. The atmosphere is ancient, powerful, and completely isolated from the modern world.', 508, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:08:57.480585-05', '2026-02-28 23:08:57.480585-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (523, 'The Dream Plane', 'other', 'A void filled with static, like that between radio stations. It contains a billion broken mirrors, each reflecting a different, distorted piece of Stephen. The fabric of this void can be torn or parted.', 'The sound of static and the disembodied, sibilant whispers of Nyarlathotep. His laugh is like grinding glass.', NULL, 'A pervasive, undefined cold.', 'Unsettling, chaotic, and fundamentally wrong. It is a shattered, unstable reality where perception is distorted and hostile cosmic beings hold influence.', 509, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:09:55.665444-05', '2026-02-28 23:09:55.665444-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (524, 'Farmhouse Bedroom', 'interior', 'A dimly lit bedroom in an old house. The doorway is backlit by a hall light, casting Maeve and Elara in silhouette upon their entry. A window provides enough light to silhouette Xavier in his bed.', 'The scene is very quiet, punctuated only by soft, careful footsteps on the stairs and the sound of the old house settling.', NULL, 'The atmosphere is still. Stephen''s fever makes the room feel distant and surreal.', 'Tense, intimate, and expectant. A heavy silence hangs in the air, filled with unspoken questions and the promise of a world-altering revelation.', 510, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:11:08.424083-05', '2026-02-28 23:11:08.424083-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (525, 'The Safehouse Study', 'interior', 'A small, dimly lit room with mismatched furniture. Bookshelves line one wall, and the air is still. The focus is entirely on the conversation between the occupants.', 'Stephen''s strained, quiet voice recounting his past, punctuated by the soft sounds of Xavier crying.', 'The faint, neutral smell of old paper and dust.', NULL, 'Tense, somber, and heavy with grief and revelation. The air is thick with unspoken trauma.', 511, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:11:44.807321-05', '2026-02-28 23:11:44.807321-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (526, 'Recovery Room', 'interior', 'A dim room with a bed and a window, set in the cold, pre-dawn hours.', 'The quiet crackle of a fire from downstairs, the distant call of a crow, and the hushed voices of the occupants.', 'Faint scent of woodsmoke.', 'The oppressive heat of Stephen''s fever contrasts with the cold pre-dawn air outside.', 'Somber, tense, and heavy with the weight of cosmic history and personal trauma being recounted.', 512, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:12:35.034331-05', '2026-02-28 23:12:35.034331-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (527, 'Narrative Debriefing Space', 'interior', 'An indistinct, quiet space where the physical surroundings are secondary to the conversation. The focus is entirely on Stephen recounting his history to his small audience.', 'Dominated by Stephen''s pained voice, with occasional quiet questions and shocked gasps from his listeners.', NULL, NULL, 'Somber, tense, and heavy with the weight of cosmic trauma and tragic revelation.', 513, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:13:37.123835-05', '2026-02-28 23:13:37.123835-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (528, 'Xavier''s Apartment', 'interior', 'A sparsely furnished living room, suggesting a life hastily assembled. The air is still and heavy with unspoken tension.', 'The low hum of unseen electronics, punctuated by the quiet, intense voices of the two men.', 'Faint scent of dust and stale air.', 'Cool, still air that does little to mitigate the charged atmosphere.', 'Extremely tense and heavy with revelation. A space where one person''s entire understanding of reality is being dismantled and rebuilt through conversation.', 514, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:14:46.264854-05', '2026-02-28 23:14:46.264854-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (529, 'Fireside Room', 'interior', 'A room with a fireplace, providing a focal point for the characters. The lighting is likely warm and intimate, contrasting with the strange and unsettling nature of the conversation.', 'The quiet crackle of the fire and the deliberate, low tones of the conversation.', 'The faint scent of woodsmoke.', 'The warmth from the fireplace.', 'Tense and revelatory. A safe space where dangerous truths are being discussed, filled with unspoken knowledge and dawning realizations.', 515, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:15:41.833846-05', '2026-02-28 23:15:41.833846-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (530, 'Maeve and Elara''s Farmhouse', 'interior', 'A farmhouse interior that appears normal but has subtle, strange details. It contains bronze tools but a notable absence of iron, and reality itself seems to bend slightly around its occupants.', 'The sound of quiet, intense conversation.', NULL, NULL, 'Begins with tension and mystery, then shifts dramatically to a feeling of ancient revelation and newfound hope.', 516, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:16:31.384854-05', '2026-02-28 23:16:31.384854-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (531, 'Abandoned School Gymnasium', 'interior', 'A derelict gymnasium with dusty light filtering through broken windows. The basketball court is covered in crude spray-painted tags, and the bleachers are collapsed.', 'Largely silent, broken only by the characters'' movements and later, their chanting, which makes the air vibrate.', 'A strong smell of mildew and decay, described as ''forgotten dreams''.', 'Cold air that makes newly bare skin feel naked. The books and papers are damp.', 'Decayed and forgotten, yet holding a latent energy or ''residue'' of past learning and curiosity. The atmosphere is tense with desperation and magical potential.', 517, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:17:39.810218-05', '2026-02-28 23:18:33.847596-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (535, 'Thuleskarne', 'exterior', 'A town in a valley, now in ruins. Buildings are burning, smoke fills the air, and bodies lie in the streets. A central marketplace is the focal point of the destruction, and a nearby tavern has been gutted, its walls scorched and floor slick with viscera.', 'The low static hum of the warped wife, screams of battle, bolts of magic, gunfire, and the explosion of a tavern wall.', 'The smell of smoke from burning buildings and the overpowering stench of gore and viscera inside the ruined tavern.', NULL, 'A nightmarish warzone filled with horror, chaos, and desperation.', 521, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:21:48.960132-05', '2026-02-28 23:21:48.960132-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (536, 'The Blood-Slicked Stones', 'exterior', 'A patch of stone ground, slick with the blood of Stephen''s son, Xavier. The area shows the signs of a recent, brutal battle, with allied defenders regrouping in the background.', 'The quiet sounds of mourning and wounded being tended to. For Stephen, this is overlaid by the phantom sound of his son''s final scream.', 'The sharp, coppery scent of fresh blood.', 'The cold, hard surface of the stone, slick and wet in places.', 'Overwhelmingly heavy with grief, shock, and the exhaustion that follows intense violence. A profound sense of loss permeates the air.', 522, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:22:36.541274-05', '2026-02-28 23:22:36.541274-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (537, 'The Battlefield Ruins', 'exterior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:24:24.79032-05', '2026-02-28 23:24:24.79032-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (538, 'Brink of the Substrate Portal', 'transitional', 'The edge of a tear in reality, looking down into a swirling, green, pudding-like substance that offers glimpses of a chasm filled with glistening, fleshy, organic horrors.', 'A maddening, eternal piping sound rises from the depths of the portal.', 'The distinct scent of peaches and vanilla, associated with Jamie.', NULL, 'A tense and foreboding space, charged with a mixture of cosmic dread and desperate resolve.', 524, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:25:40.326367-05', '2026-02-28 23:25:40.326367-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (539, 'The Infinite Library', 'other', 'A vast yet impossibly intimate space where the walls are bookshelves stretching in every direction. The ceiling is low, sloping down into an infinite, hazy distance. A small ''cubbyhole'' is tucked into the shelves.', 'A gentle, constant hum.', NULL, 'A profound warmth. The feeling of soft fabric as spirits brush past. The comfort of a fuzzy blanket.', 'A state of being rather than a physical place, imbued with a sense of perfect safety, timelessness, and patient waiting. It feels more real than reality itself.', 525, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:26:46.796322-05', '2026-02-28 23:26:46.796322-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (540, 'The Collapsing Mall', 'interior', 'A place of glass and false light with a central atrium. Its ceiling, a parody of a sky, is shattering, and reality itself is twisting in weird distortions with ruptures opening to the outside.', 'A constant, tearing, metallic scream that has replaced a previous hum.', NULL, NULL, 'A chaotic and terrifying prison that is actively ending. The environment is hostile and unstable, filled with a sense of impending doom and cosmic struggle.', 526, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:27:30.02706-05', '2026-02-28 23:27:30.02706-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (541, 'The Father''s Dreamscape', 'other', 'A disorienting space where realities blur and memories bleed together. It contains a specific test room with a single, glowing escape route and collapsing architecture, which later resolves into a quiet, stable bedroom.', 'Starts with a hollow echo, escalating to large crashing sounds, thunder, and panicked shouting during the test''s collapse. It finally settles into a profound quiet.', NULL, 'Psychic winds are felt in the chaotic ''middle ground''. The ground buckles and shakes during the destabilization.', 'Initially disorienting and chaotic, becoming tense and dangerous during the test. The atmosphere shifts to one of peace, safety, and resolution after the test is passed.', 527, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:28:24.025275-05', '2026-02-28 23:28:24.025275-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (542, 'Tokyo Hospital Room', 'interior', 'A quiet room with sharp, sterile light. The city of Tokyo is visible but muted through thick glass windows.', 'Initially muffled voices and a baby''s raw wail, which later quiets to the sound of a father''s whispered voice and the slow, rhythmic thump of his heartbeat.', 'A sterile, clean scent associated with hospitals.', 'A contrast between the sharp, cold air and the soft, warm cloth wrapping the newborn. The firm, secure warmth of a father''s hold.', 'A profound sense of peace, joy, and fulfillment following a period of anxiety and exhaustion. The room is filled with overwhelming love and a sense of finality and belonging.', 528, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:29:11.461923-05', '2026-02-28 23:29:11.461923-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (544, 'The Shifting Wastes near the Black Pyramid', 'exterior', 'A chaotic landscape of dunes under a darkening sky, swarming with a horde of alien creatures. A massive, featureless black pyramid dominates the horizon. The scene transitions to a narrow stone fissure and a small, slick-walled chamber.', 'A cacophony of creature screams, teeth scraping on bone, chittering, and later, a high-frequency, reality-bending shriek from a disintegrating creature.', 'The air reeks of old meat, iron, salt, and ammonia.', 'Cold air, the press of bodies, scraping chitin, hot breath, and the tight, scraping confines of a stone fissure.', 'Violent, chaotic, and oppressive. A desperate struggle for survival gives way to awe and terror in the face of an incomprehensible power.', 530, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:31:00.047308-05', '2026-02-28 23:31:00.047308-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (545, 'The Pyramid''s Interior', 'interior', 'The scene begins at a threshold marked by a shimmering barrier, with a crevasse behind. Upon entry, the exterior world vanishes, leaving only the undefined interior of the pyramid.', 'A profound and sudden silence, replacing the constant screaming, chittering, and roaring of the horde outside.', 'A synesthetic sensation described as being ''force fed honey and burnt wire,'' mixed with the likely scent of blood.', 'The air is heavy and oppressive. The stone underfoot is solid but the reality of the space is negotiable and fluid.', 'Tense and confrontational at the threshold, shifting to isolated and final upon entry. There is a strong sense of having crossed a point of no return.', 531, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:31:56.677308-05', '2026-02-28 23:32:37.755908-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (547, 'The Substrate Tunnels and the Void Beneath', 'other', 'Begins with fading amber light giving way to an absolute, physical darkness that presses on the eyes. The final void is described as ''darker than black'', a darkness that existed before light itself.', 'The grinding and crushing of the collapsing tunnel, a thin and mad piping that grows louder, and the imagined wet, tearing sounds of a body being unmade.', 'A brief smell of embalming fluid and old flowers from Nyarlathotep''s breath at the entrance, followed by a complete absence of scent.', 'The oppressive pressure of closing stone walls, absolute cold, the unyielding resistance of a non-physical barrier, and finally the agonizing sensation of being pulled apart from the inside out.', 'Begins with oppressive dread and claustrophobia, transitioning into cosmic horror and absolute, agonizing isolation.', 533, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:33:24.869695-05', '2026-02-28 23:33:24.869695-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (548, 'The Void of Dissolution', 'other', 'Infinite, featureless darkness and nothingness. There are no reference points or discernible features until the eventual sight of Azathoth.', 'Initially silent, it is then filled with the disembodied whispers and screams of dissolved souls, which are later pierced by a thin, mad piping sound.', 'None.', 'A sense of formlessness and non-physicality, contrasted with the feeling of being pressed upon by the Nameless Mist.', 'A place of profound, cosmic isolation and existential dread, where identity, memory, and form are stripped away.', 534, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:34:10.82569-05', '2026-02-28 23:34:10.82569-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (549, 'The Substrate of Reality', 'other', 'An absolute, final darkness beneath the void itself. It is a space so fundamental that it contains only the incomprehensible form of Azathoth and the two tiny sparks of light that are Stephen and Jamie.', 'The pervasive, mad piping of Azathoth, which is the sound of reality being held together.', NULL, 'A cold nothingness. Tendrils of this nothing attempt to wrap around and dissolve consciousness.', 'Utterly terrifying and alien. A place of fundamental truths and agonizing revelations, where consciousness itself struggles to remain coherent.', 535, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:35:00.03246-05', '2026-02-28 23:35:00.03246-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (550, 'A Forest of Speaking Trees', 'exterior', 'A serene, natural space filled with trees that seem to possess a quiet wisdom. The light is likely soft and dappled, filtering through a canopy of leaves.', 'A profound quiet that allows for subtle sounds, like the rustling of leaves, to become a form of communication.', 'The clean, grounding scent of damp earth, wood, and foliage.', 'The feeling of a gentle breeze on the skin and the solid, unmoving ground beneath one''s feet.', 'Transitions from frantic and hurried to deeply peaceful, calm, and meditative.', 536, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:35:59.332937-05', '2026-02-28 23:35:59.332937-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (551, 'Elysium Medical Bay', 'interior', 'A sterile, seamless white room with cold, fluorescent lighting. It contains at least two beds with advanced medical equipment, including IV drips. One wall is a massive viewport showing a view of space, a giant ring-like station, and a black hole.', 'A persistent, low electronic hum. Later punctuated by voices, groans, and the sound of a body falling.', 'A strong smell of antiseptic, later joined by the metallic scent of blood.', 'The air is cold and sterile. The bedsheets are stiff, tight, and clean. The floor is hard and the metal bed frame is solid.', 'Initially disorienting and clinical, shifting to awe-inspiring with the reveal of the view, then becoming emotionally charged with awkwardness, relief, and familial tension.', 537, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:36:55.521137-05', '2026-02-28 23:36:55.521137-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (552, 'Divine Council Conference Room', 'interior', 'The scene begins in a white, sterile futuristic corridor and moves into a large, circular conference room. The room is dominated by a large holographic table displaying a swirling vortex, which is the prison Etheris.', 'The quiet hum of the facility, the slide of automatic doors, and the distinct voices of the council members: Hecate''s sibilant whisper, Tiamat''s rumbling tone, and Benji''s warm voice.', 'The scent of peaches and vanilla from Jamie''s hair, and a smell of salt and the deep ocean emanating from Tiamat.', 'The solid, real feeling of Jamie in Stephen''s arms after an eternity of separation.', 'The atmosphere shifts dramatically from clinical and tense to overwhelmingly emotional during the reunion, then settles into a serious, strategic briefing tinged with grief, hope, and relief.', 538, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:37:48.544408-05', '2026-02-28 23:37:48.544408-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (553, 'The Ring City Apartment', 'interior', 'A comfortable living area carved out of a massive superstructure. It features a viewport offering a direct view of the silent drift of space and the distant, angry black hole of Etheris.', 'Quiet and peaceful, a stark contrast to the conflict the characters have endured.', NULL, NULL, 'A sanctuary of peace and safety. It''s a calm space where the newly-formed family can begin to heal and adjust to their new life together.', 539, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:38:57.385934-05', '2026-02-28 23:38:57.385934-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (554, 'Elysium Docking Observation', 'interior', 'A functional observation area with a portal overlooking a docking bay for transports. It features a railing where characters can lean.', 'A constant, low-level hum of processing machinery, the rhythmic ''pulse'' of arriving souls, the quiet prayers of the rescued, and the hiss of an automatic door.', 'The sterile scent of recycled air, punctuated by the personal, organic scent of vanilla-and-peach from Jamie.', 'The feeling of the ground vibrating with the rhythm of Elysium''s operations.', 'A tense mixture of hope and despair. It is a safe harbor that simultaneously serves as a constant reminder of the scale of the war being fought.', 540, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:40:25.261074-05', '2026-02-28 23:40:25.261074-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (555, 'Briefing Room', 'interior', 'A small, dimly lit room with a round metal table. The only significant light source is the faint glow from Lady Osilari''s tattooed symbols.', 'Initially quiet, then filled with the sound of Todd''s constant, low muttering and whispering.', NULL, NULL, 'Secretive and tense. Described as ''the kind of place where secrets went to breathe before dying''.', 541, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:41:05.773463-05', '2026-02-28 23:41:05.773463-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (557, 'Command Center', 'interior', 'A high-tech room within a residential apartment, dominated by a large holographic display. The display shows grainy, silent footage of a spatial anomaly.', 'The scene is filled with the quiet, tense voices of the team discussing cosmic strategy, punctuated by moments of heavy silence.', NULL, 'The air is likely cool and controlled, typical of a room with sensitive electronics.', 'Begins with a spark of hope and discovery, which quickly dissolves into grim tension and the heavy weight of impossible choices.', 543, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:42:34.313669-05', '2026-02-28 23:42:34.313669-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (558, 'Elysium Command Chamber', 'interior', 'A sparse, functional room with a large central table and simple chairs. The lighting is clinical, casting long shadows that accentuate the tense expressions on everyone''s faces. One chair lies knocked over on the floor.', 'The scene is dominated by tense dialogue and charged silence, punctuated by the sharp sound of a chair being knocked over.', 'A neutral scent of filtered air, devoid of any comforting or distracting smells.', 'The cool, recycled air of the room and the hard, smooth surface of the central table.', 'Extremely tense and emotionally charged. A palpable feeling of dread, determination, and familial conflict hangs heavy in the air.', 544, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:43:35.020819-05', '2026-02-28 23:43:35.020819-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (559, 'The Portal Chamber', 'interior', 'A chamber dominated by a large, unstable portal that shifts with impossible colors. The atmosphere is somber as a small group gathers for a farewell.', 'The scene is mostly quiet, filled with unspoken tension, whispers, and the strained voices of those saying goodbye.', 'A sharp, unnatural scent of ''burned mathematics'' and ''fading hope'' emanates from the portal.', NULL, 'Heavy with dread, love, and grim determination. It is a place of departure, marking the boundary between safety and immense danger.', 545, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:44:22.238206-05', '2026-02-28 23:44:22.238206-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (533, 'Akashic Realm', 'other', 'A desolate, cold realm with a grey sky and fast-moving clouds. The landscape is filled with ancient, crumbling, and sometimes floating stone towers connected by thin bridges. Skeletal trees and occasional deep red flowers punctuate the monochrome palette. It transitions to more intact, elegant structures near the central Tower of Secrets.', 'Primarily silent, with only the whisper of wind through empty streets.', 'Sterile, smelling of cold stone and dust.', 'Cold, hard stone. The air is winter-morning cold that bites through clothing. The gravity is lighter and ''thicker'' than normal, affecting movement.', 'Desolate, dead, and waiting. Initially threatening and hungry, it becomes more scholarly and ancient as they approach the Archives. The atmosphere is one of immense, forgotten history and instability.', 519, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:19:38.316489-05', '2026-02-28 23:46:03.077546-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (562, 'Yaldabaoth''s Interior', 'interior', 'An absolute, pressing darkness, faintly illuminated by magical symbols. It is a vast yet claustrophobic space with walls of digested memories, a floor of stolen lives, and a ceiling of infinite hunger.', 'Muffled sounds, like speaking through water. The space is filled with the deep, reverberating moans of Yaldabaoth''s cosmic pleasure.', NULL, 'A crushing pressure that intensifies with waves of the god''s ecstasy. The air, or lack thereof, feels thick and corrosive.', 'A terrifying, surreal environment of pure cosmic horror. It is the digestive system of a god, driven by an overwhelming, ecstatic appetite.', 548, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:46:50.752935-05', '2026-02-28 23:46:50.752935-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (563, 'Chamber of the Host', 'interior', 'A vast, dark chamber that opens like a wound from corridors of corrupted divine flesh. Sam is suspended in the center, held by thousands of invisible, writhing tentacles.', 'Sam''s constant, inhuman screaming, which later ceases. The sound of tentacles slicing through the air and slamming against a magical barrier.', NULL, 'The air is thick with a sense of wrongness. The pain from the tentacles is described as being cut by frozen void.', 'Oppressive, terrifying, and desperate. A place of cosmic horror where reality is thin and under assault.', 549, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:48:01.749225-05', '2026-02-28 23:48:01.749225-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (564, 'The Pasture of the Parasites', 'other', 'A heavy, black void-like space with patches of leaking gray. The landscape consists of rolling fields of sickly puke-green grass and twisted, alien trees, stretching to infinity. The ground is completely covered by a living carpet of trillions of sheep.', 'Initially quiet, but punctuated by the sounds of a battle (screaming, explosions) from outside the realm. Later filled with the awful, non-organic shrieks of parasites being destroyed.', 'A pervasive smell of sweat and festering cheese.', NULL, 'Feels like a fever dream made solid. It is oppressive and deceptive, shifting from a facade of peace to one of hostility and corruption.', 550, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:48:59.752249-05', '2026-02-28 23:48:59.752249-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (565, 'Corrupted Husk of Yaldabaoth', 'interior', 'A suffocating blackness that presses in on all sides, yet allows a distorted view of the throne room, dais, and an empty throne beyond.', 'The violent, physical screams of the parasite, snapping tendons, wet sounds of retching, and an unnatural sound described as ''creation running backward''.', 'The smell and taste of copper and ozone.', 'A feeling of immense pressure from multiple directions. The physical impact of a shockwave.', 'Suffocating, violent, and agonizing. A place of cosmic horror, profound grief, and brutal necessity.', 551, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:49:55.754688-05', '2026-02-28 23:49:55.754688-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (567, 'Elysium Observation Platform', 'exterior', 'A platform extending from Elysium''s southern edge, like a diving board over a void filled with stars. It offers a direct view of the freed reality Etheris and the sprawling refugee camps below.', 'The sound of the freed Azathoth''s piping, described as a sound of relief. This gives way to a profound, respectful silence during the ceremony, eventually replaced by the gentle hum of the universe.', 'The scent of Jamie (vanilla-and-peaches) mixed with the ambient smell of raw creation.', NULL, 'Deeply somber and funereal, yet imbued with a sense of cosmic scale, finality, and nascent hope. It is a place of farewell and transition.', 553, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:52:16.263632-05', '2026-02-28 23:52:16.263632-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (568, 'The Council Chamber on Elysium', 'interior', 'A room with a long table overlooking cosmic construction yards where new realities are assembled. It has been decorated with ordinary, non-magical plants, such as a fern and a trailing vine, which contrast with the holographic projections and divine beings present.', 'The sounds of gods arguing over cosmic-scale bureaucracy, punctuated by whispers and authoritative declarations. During the final vote, the room hums with immense divine power.', NULL, 'The air is described as growing thick enough to taste with divine power during the final vote.', 'The mood shifts dramatically throughout the scene, from tedious and frustrating, to tense and speculative, and finally to momentous and resolved as the plan is approved.', 554, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:53:20.13484-05', '2026-02-28 23:53:20.13484-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (569, 'Stephen and Jamie''s Elysium Apartment', 'interior', 'A small, deliberately chosen three-bedroom unit overlooking a market district. The morning light is an ambient, sunless luminescence from the Pleroma itself.', 'The quiet sounds of domesticity: coffee being prepared, the soft scratching of a pencil on paper.', 'The strong, comforting smell of freshly made coffee.', 'The warmth of a coffee cup and the reassuring grip of a hand across a table.', 'Intimate, contemplative, and a safe haven of chosen normalcy after experiencing cosmic horror. It''s a place for quiet reflection on monumental decisions.', 555, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:54:41.360965-05', '2026-02-28 23:54:41.360965-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (570, 'Elysium Council Chamber & Spire', 'interior', 'A grand chamber packed with countless divine beings, which later transitions to a high, open-air platform jutting out over the Pleroma, where the boundary of existence is visibly thin.', 'A low hum of divine power, murmurs from the crowd, and later, a multi-layered incantation spoken in a language older than time.', NULL, 'The air is described as thick enough to taste. During the ritual, the participants feel their personal histories being rewritten.', 'Begins as tense and fraught with concern, then shifts to overwhelmingly resolute and hopeful as the plan is approved and the powerful ritual commences.', 556, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:55:32.26533-05', '2026-02-28 23:55:32.26533-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (571, 'Suburban Florida House', 'interior', 'A large, two-story house with oak floors, high ceilings, and art painted by Jamie on the walls. Morning sunlight slants through the blinds, illuminating a typical suburban bedroom.', 'The sound of a teenager talking to friends on Roblox, Kate Bush''s ''Running Up That Hill'' playing downstairs, and family arguments about orange juice.', NULL, 'The warmth of a bed and the solid, real feeling of oak floors underfoot.', 'Begins with a profound sense of normalcy that shifts to sharp terror, then settles into a grounded, purposeful calm. A strange mix of domestic family life and cosmic awareness.', 557, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:56:54.515641-05', '2026-02-28 23:56:54.515641-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (573, 'Stephen and Jamie''s House', 'interior', 'A multi-level home with a bedroom upstairs and an office downstairs. At night, the bedroom ceiling is covered in shadows; the office is illuminated by a PC monitor. By morning, dawn light creeps through the windows, brightening the rooms.', 'Initially silent at night, save for the low hum of PC cooling fans. In the morning, it fills with the muffled sounds of teenage arguments, and the rhythm of cars outside.', 'The smell of fresh coffee drifts up the stairs in the morning.', 'The house feels ''silent and solid'', a comforting and real physical space.', 'The atmosphere shifts from a place of quiet anxiety for Stephen to a sanctuary of ''beautiful, mundane'' peace and a base of operations for their future mission.', 559, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-02-28 23:58:38.923723-05', '2026-02-28 23:58:38.923723-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (574, 'The Greenhouse Domes on Sorhhinda', 'interior', 'Glass-like domes rising against a bruised purple sky with three suns. The interior is lit in shades of copper and gold, filled with rows of plants in rich dirt.', 'Predominantly silent, punctuated only by the soft movements of androids and Kai''s whispers.', 'The scent of damp soil and alien flora.', 'Warm, humid air. The texture of fine dirt and delicate plant stems.', 'Begins as a place of serene ritual and reverence, but shifts to one of quiet concern and mystery.', 560, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 00:54:52.742088-05', '2026-03-01 00:54:52.742088-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (576, 'Kai''s Compound', 'exterior', 'A compound featuring a greenhouse and cultivated spatch weed plants, now a scene of chaos. The ground is littered with scattered metal android limbs, shattered glass, and the pulped remains of plants.', 'The chittering of the swarm, a massive explosion, the sparking of destroyed androids, and a single, reality-altering cry.', 'The smell of overturned earth and crushed, pulped vegetation.', 'The air itself changes, becoming charged with power.', 'Begins with chaotic destruction, shifting to primal fear, then to a palpable, incandescent rage and the raw feeling of unleashed power.', 562, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 00:56:18.580112-05', '2026-03-01 00:56:18.580112-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (575, 'Sorhhinda Greenhouse', 'interior', 'A structure with a reinforced glass dome containing swaying ''spatch weed'' plants. A jagged crack runs the length of the dome.', 'The rustling of leaves, the android''s synthesized voice, a deep grinding sound from below, and the sharp crack of glass.', 'The smell of soil and blood.', 'Violent, sudden lurches of the ground that shake the entire structure.', 'Begins with a sense of routine planetary monitoring, which rapidly shifts to one of tense foreboding, and finally erupts into chaos and horror.', 561, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 00:55:30.461764-05', '2026-03-01 00:57:08.979829-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (578, 'The Ruined Garden of Sorhhinda', 'exterior', 'A destroyed garden on a planet lit by three suns. The soil is dark and disturbed. The few surviving plants are twisting into monstrous, bladed forms under the influence of a new power.', 'The sounds of a monstrous transformation, followed by a multi-layered voice declaring its existence, and finally the brief wail of distant sirens being extinguished into silence.', 'The scent of disturbed earth and a faint, ozone-like smell from the unmaking of the android.', 'The air is heavy and charged with a palpable sense of wrongness and burgeoning power.', 'The atmosphere shifts from one of post-destruction horror to one of absolute, alien dominion and corrupted creation.', 564, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 00:57:50.076814-05', '2026-03-01 00:57:50.076814-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (579, 'The Nexus of Perception', 'other', 'A non-physical, conceptual space from which the infinite tapestry of realities can be felt rather than seen.', 'A profound silence punctuated by the conceptual echo of cosmic events.', NULL, 'A feeling of connection to all threads of existence, accompanied by the sharp pang of distant tragedies.', 'Immeasurably vast, eternal, and saturated with a deep, cosmic melancholy.', 565, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 00:58:43.969579-05', '2026-03-01 00:58:43.969579-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (580, 'The Author''s Study', 'interior', 'A space filled with books, notes, and a computer, likely cluttered from the intense 30-day writing challenge. The glow of a monitor illuminates the room.', 'The quiet hum of a computer, the clicking of a keyboard, and the rustle of paper.', 'The faint scent of old paper, coffee, and ozone from electronics.', 'The cool surface of a desk and the warmth from a running computer.', 'A place of creative chaos and reflective solitude, filled with the lingering energy of a massive project''s completion.', 566, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 00:59:50.348829-05', '2026-03-01 00:59:50.348829-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (583, 'Author''s Planning Space', 'other', 'An abstract, non-physical space representing the author''s thoughts and future plans for his literary work.', 'The internal monologue of the author, weighing creative ambitions against practical realities and indulging in dark humor.', NULL, NULL, 'A blend of determined ambition, creative passion, and cynical self-awareness.', 569, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 01:02:27.061592-05', '2026-03-01 01:02:27.061592-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (584, 'Author''s Note Interstitial', 'other', 'A conceptual space, like the pages of a book or a direct address to the reader, breaking the fourth wall. There are no physical features, only the text itself.', 'The imagined voice of the author speaking directly to the reader.', NULL, 'The feeling of holding a book or viewing a screen.', 'Informative, direct, and meta-narrative. It''s a break from the immersive story to provide context and exposition.', 570, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 01:03:27.740345-05', '2026-03-01 01:03:27.740345-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (585, 'The Primordial Void', 'other', 'Initially, the absolute absence of light, dark, and dimension. It later becomes the dark space surrounding the emergent, perfect light of the Pleroma.', 'Absolute, total silence, which is later contrasted by the harmonious song of the Pleroma.', 'The complete absence of smell.', 'A state of non-being; nothing to touch or feel.', 'Begins as a state of infinite, compressed potential. It evolves into a space of cosmic contrast between divine perfection and a hungry, waiting darkness.', 571, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 01:04:22.182582-05', '2026-03-01 01:04:22.182582-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (586, 'Sam''s Valley', 'exterior', 'A serene valley defined by a creek bed and a high ridge, containing a small house and a shearing shed. The landscape is rugged, with rocks and savory herbs underfoot.', 'The quiet sounds of a flock of sheep, broken by the harsh laughter and sounds of violence from the raiders.', 'A mix of lanolin, damp wool, crushed herbs, thyme, and dust. Later tainted by the smell of blood and cold sweat.', 'The grit and dust of the earth, the sting of wind on sweaty skin, the rough texture of wool and wood.', 'Begins as a place of pure, simple peace and material contentment. It violently shifts to one of cold dread, impotence, and horrific violation.', 572, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 01:05:15.628325-05', '2026-03-01 01:05:15.628325-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (587, 'The Garden of Yaldabaoth', 'exterior', 'A created space with soft, flesh-like ground, enclosed by an invisible, shimmering barrier. Inside, it becomes increasingly crowded with mindless humans. Outside is a void with dim cycles of light and dark.', 'Initially silent, later filled with the screams of the few awakened souls and the mindless sounds of the obedient humans. Yaldabaoth''s "voice" is a non-auditory pressure.', 'The text mentions the "sweat and fear and desperation" of the crowded humans.', 'The ground is "too soft. Like flesh." The barrier is a solid, resistant surface. The air outside is cold.', 'Oppressive, controlled, and artificial. It transitions from a sterile creation space to a suffocating prison, and finally to an absolute void after its collapse.', 573, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 01:06:25.991588-05', '2026-03-01 01:06:25.991588-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (590, 'የጊዜ እና የቦታ ስፋት', 'other', 'A chaotic, non-linear journey through dying star systems, nascent realities, and the ruins of divine realms, all viewed in a blur of hyper-temporal travel.', 'A profound silence punctuated by the psychic echoes of cosmic events and the quiet whispers of the refugee caravan.', 'The metallic tang of spent energy and the cold, sterile scent of the void.', 'A constant, subtle vibration of reality itself, strained under the weight of their flight and the pressure of Yaldabaoth''s pursuit.', 'Overwhelmingly vast and isolating, filled with a sense of desperate urgency and the looming dread of the ever-present threat.', 576, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 01:09:17.267972-05', '2026-03-01 01:09:17.267972-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (591, 'Obsidian Glass Battlefield', 'exterior', 'A chaotic battlefield of cracked, obsidian glass, littered with the bodies of golden-winged angels and chthonic horrors. A circle of unnatural stillness and death forms after Stephen''s act.', 'A symphony of shrieks, wet thuds of bodies, metallic clicks, and tearing sounds. This is later replaced by a deafening, unnatural silence in the immediate area.', 'The stench of iron, burnt ozone, static, ash, and something infinitely ancient.', NULL, 'Begins as intensely chaotic and violent. Shifts to an eerie, horrifying calm after the act of un-creation, followed by tense grief and fury.', 577, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 01:10:02.692877-05', '2026-03-01 01:10:02.692877-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (592, 'Illkeserod''s Homeworld', 'exterior', 'Initially a serene, pastoral realm where the air itself is a visible, honey-gold energy. It devolves into a war-torn landscape, culminating in a world with a bruised, churning purple sky and finally a desolate, frozen coastline under a dark sky.', 'The sounds of a peaceful world give way to the chanting of zealots, the sounds of battle, and finally the roar of a black, churning ocean.', NULL, 'The air is initially warm with a palpable, golden contentment.', 'The atmosphere shifts from one of perfect peace and innocence to one of terror and spiritual sickness, then to the grimness of a generational war, and finally to absolute despair and hopelessness at the brink of annihilation.', 578, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 01:11:01.276898-05', '2026-03-01 01:11:01.276898-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.locations VALUES (593, 'Shattered Ziggurat on the Obsidian Plain', 'exterior', 'A broken, ruined ziggurat stands on a plain of black, obsidian-like ground. The air is visibly laced with static, and the distant horizon glows with the light of a raging battle.', 'A distant, thunderous roar of battle, the wet, ripping sounds of flesh being torn, soul-shattering screams of agony, and later, the quiet hiss of the plain and stifled sobs.', 'The air is acrid, smelling of ozone and static.', NULL, 'A nightmare reality filled with horror, desperation, and grim finality. The atmosphere is a psychic assault of hopelessness and agony.', 579, 'gemini', 'gemini-2.5-pro', '2026-03-01 01:12:06.192508-05', '2026-03-01 01:12:06.192508-05', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (170, 47, 1, 'The Breakthrough and First Crossing', 'The narrator experiences a breakthrough inspiration while watching TV with his son, leading to the successful creation of an Einstein-Rosen Bridge. He tests the portal by crossing through it, experiencing both triumph and terror as the unstable gateway collapses moments after his passage.', 'The infuriating mystery of successfully forming an Einstein-Rosen Bridge (ERB) consumed my every waking moment, each failed attempt crushing my spirits even more. It was that one fateful night, whilst enjoying Gravity Falls with my son, when a spark of inspiration ignited within me. The show’s eerie mix of science and the supernatural triggered a breakthrough idea in my mind: connecting two spacetime locations via quantum entanglement. This could be it - the answer I have been searching for all this time.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (176, 47, 7, 'Reunion Through the Stars', 'Bursting with excitement, the narrator wakes his wife and brings her to the warehouse, revealing the stable gateway to Kyoto. They step through together and emerge in her mother''s backyard in Japan, creating an emotional reunion that validates all his sacrifices and risks.', 'I raced home, bursting through the door and slamming it behind me. “Wake up!” I called, shaking my wife gently but insistently.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (328, 82, 2, 'Expansion into the Void', 'Humanity recovers and begins ambitious interstellar expansion, establishing outposts across the universe and making groundbreaking scientific discoveries, with Morgan and TJ revealing the construction of a station at the edge of the visible universe.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (4, 3, 2, 'The Fruitless Search', 'After weeks of frantic searching with no success, the narrator finally encounters The Pointers in an alleyway during their evening commute, experiencing an encounter that is both awe-inspiring and unsettling.', 'Weeks went by, and my search, as frantic as it was, appeared futile.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (6, 3, 4, 'The Fade Into Apathy', 'As weeks pass and The Pointers continue their silent appearances worldwide, public interest wanes and the phenomenon becomes mundane background noise, with the narrator succumbing to the same indifference that has consumed society.', 'Life would continue, as the days slowly merged into weeks, The Pointers continued their silent vigil around the world. Society had slowly returned to its normal routine, but there was always an underlying buzz whenever someone mentioned them. The deeper I sought answers, the more questions became shrouded in a frenzy of disinformation.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (181, 49, 3, 'Le Comptoir Secret and the Mysterious Map', 'Desperate and hungry, the narrator stumbles into a quaint café called Le Comptoir Secret, where the enigmatic proprietor listens to their banking woes and offers them a mysterious, leather-bound map supposedly containing secrets to success in Zurich—for the price of a gold bar.', 'Just when I thought my luck couldn’t get any worse, an ad popped up on Google Maps. A quaint little café tucked away in a secluded corner caught my eye. The name, Le Comptoir Secret, practically dripped with intrigue. Hungry from a morning of rejection and feeling like I had nothing to lose, I followed the directions.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (83, 22, 4, 'Escalating Obsession', 'Despite his promise to his wife, the narrator and his son become unable to resist experimenting further with the Engine over several days. Their sessions grow increasingly chaotic and absurd, with the Engine revealing patterns and responding with apparent intention, until they achieve a major breakthrough.', 'You know what killed the cat? Despite promising my wife to be careful, curiosity had a stranglehold on me and my son. Over the next few days, we couldn’t resist the pull of the Eternal Engine. Our experiments became even more chaotic and absurd, the garage morphing into Frankenstein’s lab of salvaged junk and wild ideas. The sounds from the Engine became our constant companion, an otherworldly metronome that seemed to anticipate our next move.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (141, 37, 5, 'The Suburban Dad Reveal', 'The Viper''s tough criminal persona crumbles when his young daughter runs in looking for a crayon. He is revealed to be just a suburban father roleplaying as a criminal, having no actual intention of harm and finding the situation amusing.', 'I blinked. “Okay?”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (169, 46, 1, 'The Revelation and the Call', 'The narrator makes a threatening phone call to The S Corp, claiming knowledge of their organization. During and after the call, the narrator experiences a disturbing psychological state, oscillating between a grandiose sense of cosmic power and a creeping sense of dread and madness. The call ends with the narrator feeling nauseated and aware of dark forces awakening.', '“I know about The S Corp.” The phone line exploded with a deafening roar, reverberating through the air like a portal to the depths of hell. A bone-chilling gust of wind swept through the room, carrying whispers of ancient secrets and ominous prophecies. When those words came, dripping with venom and knowledge that pierced my soul. My consciousness expanded beyond human boundaries, consumed by an all-consuming awareness of my true power.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (285, 73, 1, 'Serene Sanctuary', 'Yukiko, now a teenager after five years on Sorhhinda, enjoys life in the colony while her mother serves as chief scientist. Despite initial homesickness, she has embraced the alien world and its wonders, maintaining connection to Earth through the ERB network.', 'Sunlight, filtered through lush alien foliage, dappled the wooden walls of Yukiko’s room. Outside, the whirring of hover scooters mingled with the trills of an unfamiliar bird, an avian concerto unlike anything Earth had ever offered. It was the middle of August, (according to earth calendars), and a five years since they arrived.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (277, 69, 5, 'Arrival at the Alien World', 'After journeying through hundreds of barren planets, the habitat finally arrives at its destination. As the doors open, an breathtaking alien landscape of iridescent terrain, crystalline formations, and an indigo sky unfolds before the awestruck pioneers.', 'After a long and surreal journey through hundreds of strange, barren planets, each more alien than the last, the habitat finally arrived at its destination. The gateway rippled like liquid starlight as the habitat passed through, and for a moment, time seemed to hang suspended. Then, with a soft hiss and a rising hum, the great doors of the habitat opened, revealing the uncharted scenery of the planet beyond.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (287, 73, 3, 'Shadow Conspirators', 'Yukiko follows mysterious hooded figures moving through the colony with purpose, discovering they are plotting to destroy the ERB gateway. She overhears fragments of their plan mentioning ''I AM'' and realizes the catastrophic scope of their scheme.', 'In the distance, concealed within the shadows of an overgrown grove of trees, Yukiko spotted a group of figures clad in dark attire. Their movements were purposeful, their expressions hidden beneath hoods and masks. They moved with an eerie precision, each motion deliberate and calculated. Keeping her distance, she followed them back towards the center of town.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (293, 74, 1, 'Morning Chaos on Elysium', 'Frank wakes to his customized alarm and begins his day as chief janitor aboard the Elysium space ring. His AI assistant Alexa briefs him on three urgent problems: a Japanese delegation''s toilet paper complaint, Argentine bakers blaming space raccoons, and radiation spikes in Hydroponics Sector 3.', '“WAKE THE FRANK UP!” screamed the alarm. My husband, ever the comedian, had customized it. Hilarious.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (8, 4, 1, 'Frost and Whispers at Home', 'On an unusually cold Floridian morning, the narrator and his wife prepare breakfast while discussing a mysterious internet phenomenon called ''The Pointers.'' Their son joins them, and the narrator enlists his help to investigate, before the family disperses for the day with warm farewells.', 'In the pre-dawn stillness of a Floridian winter, the world held its breath, the frost-kissed air carrying a rare, hushed whisper of the impossible: cold. The usually vibrant state was subdued, its inhabitants bracing themselves for an unexpected dip into the 60''s—a chilly anomaly that provoked down jackets from their closet hibernation and stirred cold weather shelters into action.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (9, 4, 2, 'Descent into Corporate Absurdity', 'The narrator arrives at his corporate office where the COO launches bizarre team-building activities that spiral into chaos—jumping jacks, an obstacle course, and a Krampus-costumed finance team—before culminating in a disappointing holiday party with raw vegetables.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (11, 5, 1, 'The Awakening and the Message', 'Todd jolts awake to a conspiracy video on TV claiming S Corp has hacked Leon''s implant. Seized by excitement at finding proof, he ventures into Dark 4chan via VPN, hunting for evidence. After hours of searching, he receives a cryptic message offering documents in exchange for a meeting at an abandoned warehouse.', 'Todd jolted awake in his battered recliner, a hand-rolled cigarette smoldering dangerously close to the armrest. The room reeked of sweat, smoke, and moonshine, but Todd’s bloodshot eyes snapped to the flickering TV as static consumed the infomercial. Suddenly, a figure in a Guy Fawkes mask appeared, their voice distorted but chillingly clear.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (12, 5, 2, 'The Day of Reckoning', 'Todd wakes to strange screams and refocuses on his mission to protect Leon and expose S Corp''s alleged conspiracy. He spends the day anxiously preparing, enlisting Stacey''s reluctant help, then drives to the abandoned warehouse at night to meet his mysterious contact.', 'Screams of what sounded like a baby attacking a rabid dog woke him from his slumber. Todd shook his head, clearing away the cobwebs. It didn’t matter who was behind it all; what mattered was protecting Leon, the visionary genius who represented so much more than just hydrogen powered cars. This was about freedom, with a capital F Todd’s purpose surged within him, igniting a renewed sense of determination.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (14, 6, 2, 'MIT and Fragile Trust', 'At MIT, the narrator discovers they can selectively suppress memories due to their eidetic ability. Encouraged by warm new friends, they share their buried trauma from 1986 while intoxicated, only to sense their friends'' discomfort as the confession unfolds.', 'People don’t tell you that growing up with an eidetic memory, also allows you to completely shut off part of your memory. It’s a delicate balance between preserving your sanity and avoiding pain. When the acceptance letter to MIT arrived, it felt like a door had cracked open to a new beginning.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (15, 6, 3, 'Death and Transcendence', 'The narrator lies dying in a hospital bed from fever, experiences a profound near-death vision in a shimmering void, and returns to life with newfound power and defiance against mortality itself.', 'It stings the nostrils and makes the eyes water. Underneath the sharpness is a faint hint of rot and sickness. Weeks of fever induced hallucinations had become my reality. My sanity had left me, my body wracked by relentless nausea. I lay adrift in a sea of loneliness, staring up at the chipped white paint on the ceiling.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (148, 40, 2, 'Revelation of Cosmic Horror', 'The entity fully manifests its terrifying form—a grotesque being of decay and ancient power—reveling in its dominance over the ruined landscape. It reflects on its past role as a forgotten deity and instruments of chaos, remembering those who foolishly invoked its name across millennia.', 'I stood amid the chaos, my towering form looming over the desolate ruins of what was once a great kingdom. My flesh was a patchwork of decaying skin and exposed muscle, my twisted horns gleaming with the blood of those who dared defy me. The stench of death and decay clung to me like a cloak, a reminder of the countless mortals who had met their end at my hands. In their misguided attempts to expand their empire, they had unknowingly awoken me from my eternal slumber. They would pay the ultimate price for their arrogance, as I reveled in the sight of their mangled bodies and torn limbs strewn across the battlefield. This was my domain, a realm where fear and respect were one and the same, and I relished in every moment of it. I gazed upon the carnage around me, even I couldn’t help but feel out of place in this modern, war-torn world. A cosmic horror amidst human remains, a being from another time unleashed upon an unsuspecting world.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (188, 50, 3, 'Journey Through the Void', 'The entity traverses the cosmic gulf toward Earth, its consciousness unraveling from the otherworldly horror of the journey while answering an irresistible siren call that grows stronger with each moment.', 'Home? A concept that no longer made sense to one who had ruled over realms beyond mortal comprehension. Deep within me, forgotten echoes stirred and begged for release, driving me ever closer to the source of the growing madness.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (283, 72, 2, 'James''s Dark Revelation', 'James confronts the protagonist in a tense private meeting, revealing the ideological depth of the extremist threat and proposing more aggressive internal sabotage tactics. The conversation is interrupted by escalating reports of suicide attacks and advanced munitions, culminating in Patrick''s announcement of a devastating nuclear device called the God Killer.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (19, 7, 2, 'The Workshop and the Eternal Engine', 'The protagonist finds themselves in their workshop dream, wrestling with schematics for an impossible device called the Eternal Engine. As they work through the night, they envision the intricate nanite technology and reality-warping capabilities of their creation, grappling with the weight of its potential for both liberation and destruction.', 'Wait—where was I? The workshop. Of course. I was wrestling with these damned schematics. The equations were right there, tantalizingly close, yet just out of reach. The air buzzed with energy, an otherworldly charge permeating every molecule. Shelves lined the walls, crammed with artifacts I’d amassed over decades.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (20, 7, 3, 'The Flight from the Workshop', 'As dawn breaks and the calculations are complete, the protagonist clutches the precious papers and flees the workshop through the cornfields toward home, desperate to preserve the schematics before waking and losing everything to forgetfulness.', 'The blossoming dawn slowly replaced just as the darkness of the night, it was done.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (21, 7, 4, 'The Alarm and Lost Memory', 'The alarm clock jolts the protagonist awake in their bedroom, snapping them back to reality and leaving them disoriented with only fragments of their dream-work slipping away into forgotten depths.', 'The blare of my alarm jolted me upright, my heart pounding, in time with the beeping filling my bedroom. Disoriented, I slapped my phone silent. What just happened?
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (22, 8, 1, 'The Day of Reckoning', 'The protagonist struggles through a day of mounting anxiety leading up to a major presentation. Morning routines and desperate attempts at distraction give way to overhearing bitter resentment from team members about a promotion, then enduring a chaotic boardroom presentation that culminates in technical failure yet receives unexpected praise.', 'Monday, or maybe it was Wednesday. When everything is on fire, days blur into a meaningless haze. The sunlight sliced through the blinds with cruel indifference, a silent witness to the dread about heading into the office, enveloped me like a shroud. My coffee was strong, bitter, almost medicinal, but it failed to quiet the storm brewing in my chest. Today was the day. Weeks of preparation had boiled down to this, and my mind was already betraying me, playing out disastrous scenarios like a relentless horror reel.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (23, 8, 2, 'The Midnight Crisis', 'A 4:44 a.m. phone call from the CEO shatters the protagonist''s sleep with news of a catastrophic server failure blamed on them. Racing to the office, they and their team battle through the night to restore the critical system, discovering the sabotage is rooted in the COO''s reckless tinkering.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (24, 9, 1, 'The Eternal Engine''s Final Hours', 'The protagonist works feverishly through the night to complete the Eternal Engine, a massive machine that represents their life''s obsession. As exhaustion takes hold at dawn, they collapse into sleep and experience a vivid dream that blurs the line between reality and imagination.', 'Sweat streamed down my face, mingling with the acrid tang of hot metal and electrical sparks that hung heavy in the air, a suffocating testament to countless sleepless nights spent forging the impossible. My blistered hands trembled as I adjusted the last pieces of the Eternal Engine, its monstrous frame consuming the barn, my makeshift workshop, with its jagged metal and pulsating wires that seemed alive, writhing like serpents. Blinding flashes of blue light erupted from its core, a searing, unearthly orb radiating power so fierce it threatened to devour everything in its path.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (25, 9, 2, 'The Morning After', 'The protagonist wakes to an alarm, navigates their morning routine with resentment toward work obligations, and discovers their son''s school is offering a summer trip to London. This moment of wonder is interrupted by a menacing phone call from their abusive boss.', 'The relentless buzzing of my alarm pierced through the midday light, signaling the start of another grueling day. I swat out for my phone sitting on the nightstand, the cold air a stark contrast to the warmth of my bed. I silenced the noise and couldn’t help but feel resentful towards this daily intrusion that constantly interrupts my dreams. The soft sheets surrounding me now feel suffocating as I remember what awaits me in the real world.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (26, 10, 1, 'Office Aftermath and Digital Ghosts', 'The narrator returns to work after a near-catastrophe, struggling with post-adrenaline fatigue. During a lunch break, he discovers that all traces of the Pointers have been erased from the internet, and when he confronts Mattias about their earlier conversation, the coworker has no memory of it.', 'The office buzzed with the rhythmic clatter of keyboards and the hum of lighthearted chatter, a stark contrast to the near catastrophe we had narrowly escaped just hours earlier. Sleep-deprived smiles and nods greeted me as I walked through, but my focus sharpened on the conspicuous absence of the COO.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (27, 10, 2, 'The Unraveling Search and Paranoid Drive', 'The narrator finds a cryptic post about Operation Blue Storm near Area 51, fueling his obsession, but the search yields nothing. Driving home, he experiences mounting paranoia and psychological distress as reality feels increasingly unstable.', 'The clock ticked closer to 5pm when I finally stumbled upon a link that sparked hope of an answer: an anonymous post titled ‘Pointing the way?’ published around the same time I’d seen the video earlier, claiming to have witnessed strange people randomly showing up but then disappearing.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (28, 10, 3, 'Home and the Grease Stain Mystery', 'The narrator arrives home to his wife''s question about mysterious grease stains on the sheets, which he cannot explain. He navigates family routines and dinnertime while the stains trigger unsettling memories of his dreams involving the Eternal Engine.', 'Once home, walking inside brought me back to reality. The warm aroma of my wife’s cooking wrapped around me, a mix of spices and comfort that briefly eased the tension in my chest.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (29, 10, 4, 'Evening Rituals and Camping Frenzy', 'The narrator and his wife watch Percy Jackson together, but guilt gnaws at him over his divided attention. His wife suddenly announces a camping trip, triggering chaotic packing that both energizes and distracts him from his obsession with the Pointers.', 'After dinner, my wife and I snuggled under a blanket and started “Percy Jackson” on Disney Plus. While the vibrant world on screen offered moments of relief, each laugh, or action scene, brought a pang of guilt. How could I enjoy this when larger worries loomed? Despite the warmth of my wife’s presence and our shared love for fantasy TV, I still found it hard to fully set aside the inner conflict.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (30, 10, 5, 'Bedtime Reflections and Lingering Shadows', 'As the narrator lies in bed after the chaotic packing, he reflects on the tension between the comforting rhythm of family life and the unsettling mysteries that refuse to release him, haunted by the erasure of the Pointers.', 'Later that evening, as I lay in bed, the weight of the day pressed heavily on me, pulling me between two worlds. The chaotic mysteries of my work, where questions only bred more uncertainty, and the comforting rhythm of family life, a fragile refuge against the storm in my mind. The upcoming camping trip offered a chance to escape, but the thought of disconnecting from civilization left me restless, the shadow of the missing Pointers lingering like an unspoken threat.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (82, 22, 3, 'The Wrongness Unfolds', 'After the experiment, the narrator experiences a disturbing shift in reality around the Engine—the garage warps, shadows move wrong, and he senses an ancient sentience. He retreats inside, deeply unsettled, and tries to explain to his wife what happened.', 'Silence slammed into the garage, sudden and suffocating—not the absence of sound, but its violent removal. The air felt strangled, as if some unseen throat had swallowed everything whole.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (334, 83, 3, 'The Alarm and the Red Hat''s Return', 'An ancient preternatural alarm is triggered by a monitoring post in the Proxima Centauri system. The feed shows the ERB portal being infected by organic matter and a figure in a scarlet hat—Todd—standing directly before the camera. The protagonist recognizes the threat and loses consciousness, confirming Todd and the Red Hats have returned.', 'Just then an alarm blared. An ancient defense and monitoring system had been triggered.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (32, 11, 2, 'Breaking Point', 'Stacey confronts Todd about the state of the trailer and their deteriorating life together, expressing her exhaustion and fear that his obsession is destroying their family. Todd acknowledges his struggle but refuses to abandon his investigation, leading to an emotional impasse.', 'Stacey stormed through the door, her frustration palpable in her clenched fists and pursed lips. She surveyed the scene before her, a kaleidoscope of clutter and chaos that threatened to consume her sanity.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (33, 11, 3, 'The Global Grid Emerges', 'A series of newspaper headlines from July to September 2024 reveal the escalating mystery of the Global Grid—mysterious synchronized construction projects worldwide, economic disruption, hacker activism, indigenous resistance, and international diplomatic tensions.', 'July 21, 2024 Headline: “Mysterious Construction at Transport Hubs Raises Resident Concerns” Excerpt: Residents near major transportation hubs are reporting sleepless nights due to incessant construction noise. Once-busy airports, seaports, and train stations are now obscured by barriers and active machinery operating around the clock. The lack of information from local authorities and the unidentified entity behind these projects has led to widespread speculation, including theories of government cover-ups and secretive corporate ventures. The familiar rhythms of city life have been disrupted, replaced by the constant clamor of construction.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (35, 12, 2, 'The Scoutmaster''s Tale', 'As the fire dies down, the scoutmaster tells an unsettling story about scouts who ventured into the forest and discovered a mysterious, supernatural clearing called the ''Power of Infinity.'' The narrator feels the story is directed at him, and a sense of dread settles over the group.', 'The once roaring fire popped and hissed, slowly dying into a bed of glowing embers that pulsed with a quiet intensity. Shadows danced across the scouts’ faces, the light giving everyone an almost spectral quality. Taking this as his cue, the scoutmaster leaned forward, his features bathed in the warm orange glow, voice low and measured, drawing everyone into the story.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (36, 12, 3, 'Restless Night and Uneasy Dreams', 'The narrator retreats to his tent, troubled by the scoutmaster''s story. He experiences restless sleep and dreams filled with fog, endless trees, and the rhythmic hum of machinery.', 'Retreating to the confines of my tent, I lay restless on the thin sleeping pad, the scoutmaster’s story weaving itself into the fabric of my thoughts. The idea of uncovering something hidden deep within the forest seemed ridiculous, yet the notion tugged at me with an almost magnetic pull. The stillness of the night outside only sharpened the edges of my unease, each creak of branches or a distant rustle adding weight to the tale. Eventually, weariness claimed me, but sleep brought little relief.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (38, 12, 5, 'The Search Through the Maze Forest', 'Search parties organize to find the missing scouts. The forest transforms into an oppressive, hostile maze where trails loop impossibly and the landscape defies reason. The group eventually finds the patrol in a strange clearing but becomes trapped in the forest''s disorienting geometry.', 'The forest, once so vibrant, now felt oppressive. Shadows stretched long and claw-like, as though the trees were leaning in, watching. Bark twisted into strange shapes in the fading light, and the once-familiar trails seemed to dissolve into the gloom. Voices rose in clipped, urgent commands as we scrambled to organize a search party.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (39, 12, 6, 'Return to Camp and Fragile Normalcy', 'The group returns to camp where an unsettling normalcy settles in. The scouts quickly forget the terror and play games, while the narrator remains troubled. That evening by the dying fire, he sits with his son, still haunted by the experience.', 'Back at camp, something changed dramatically. The terror and chaos of the search gave way abruptly to an unnervingly quiet normalcy. Returning scouts scattered without hesitation, their laughter ringing through the trees as they dove into games of manhunt, shouting and sprinting as if nothing had happened. The fear — the suffocating, relentless dread of the forest’s maze — dissolved so completely it felt unreal. It was jarring to see how quickly the nightmare was forgotten, leaving me to wonder if it had all been some twisted figment of my imagination.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (40, 13, 1, 'Lost in the Twisted Forest', 'The protagonist runs desperately through a nightmarish, warped forest, disoriented and compelled forward by an invisible force. Reality itself seems twisted, with impossible geometry and malevolent presences closing in, driving them toward an inexplicable destination.', 'I was running before I knew where I was. The world around me spun like a fractured kaleidoscope, a suffocating haze of twisted trees and clawing shadows. My lungs burned with each gasping breath, and the ground beneath me churned, shifting from familiar cornstalks, to fresh earth, to coarse gravel, finally to something unrecognizable, like molten tar.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (41, 13, 2, 'The Sacred Circle and the Device', 'The protagonist finds themselves at the sacred circle where their son was found, discovering a strange device wedged in a massive tree. Retrieving it becomes a desperate struggle against the forest''s malevolent resistance, culminating in a violent extraction.', 'Suddenly, I stumbled into a clearing — a place I recognized instantly. The sacred circle we had found my son’s patrol eons ago. The space throbbed with an energy that tested my sanity. In the center, wedged into the bark of a massive, gnarled tree, the tree the scouts were trying to show us earlier, was the device. Its faint glow cut through the fog like a beacon, impossible to ignore. My breath caught in my throat, and my limbs trembled as I approached it.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (84, 22, 5, 'The Chicken Ritual', 'The narrator and his son conduct their culminating experiment: wrapping a raw chicken in copper wire and rice, then exposing it to the Engine''s full power. The chicken implodes, leaving behind a shimmering, impossible crystal with otherworldly properties.', 'After untold lifetimes spent tempting fate in that garage, it finally felt like our experiments were on the brink of either brilliance or catastrophe. We set up what we hoped would be our pièce de résistance, the culmination of everything we’d learned so far. The Eternal Engine hummed steadily in its glass enclosure, its light casting strange, shifting shadows across the walls, as if the garage itself held its breath.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (265, 66, 6, 'The United States Debt Proposition', 'The narrator approaches the U.S. delegation with a transformative offer: S Corp will erase America''s national debt using asteroid-derived gold reserves, enabling sweeping social programs.', 'As I turned, the next group approached: the United States delegation. Their arrival brought with it a shift in the room’s energy, the stakes climbing higher. This wasn’t just another discussion; it was a moment poised to alter the trajectory of a global superpower and redefine how private enterprise shaped society.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (189, 51, 1, 'The World''s Wealthiest Company', 'The narrator receives notification that all asset transfers are complete, making the S Corp the world''s wealthiest company with $50 trillion in assets. Despite the monumental achievement, they commit to maintaining strict privacy while grappling with the enormous power and responsibility of their position.', 'The email notification blinked on my screen, pulling me from my thoughts. With trembling hands, I clicked it open, holding my breath. The message was simple yet monumental: all the asset transfers were complete. In that instant, July 8th, 2024, the S Corp became the wealthiest company in the world, controlling an unprecedented $50 trillion in assets.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (200, 52, 4, 'The Temple''s Hunger Awakens', 'The protagonist, now one with the mist and the temple, descends through horrific chambers revealing unspeakable rituals and artifacts. They realize the S Corp''s intrusion has shattered the seal on an ancient evil, and they are merely a pawn in its awakening, destined for slaughter.', 'The weight of eons pressed down on me, each inscription hissing with the agony of a lost civilization. A surge of despair emanated from the stones, a chorus of anguished screams echoing through the air. Beneath the cacophony of suffering, a sinister energy simmered - a malevolent force stirring from its eternal slumber. It beckoned to me, a pulsating beacon in the Stygian darkness, rousing an insatiable hunger within my very being. I could feel the temple’s call growing stronger, drawing me deeper into its twisted embrace.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (43, 13, 4, 'The Journey Home', 'The protagonist breaks camp and drives home, haunted by the dream and the device in their pocket. The familiar world feels distorted and unreal, and they struggle between the pull of adventure and the desire for normalcy, ending with acceptance of an uncertain future.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (44, 14, 1, 'Monday Morning Dread', 'The narrator wakes to their alarm, haunted by vivid dreams of a massive machine and unsettling memories of the mysterious Pointers. Despite the peaceful family weekend, an inexplicable unease settles over them as they prepare for Monday, sensing an impending collapse.', 'The shrill cry of my alarm shattered the fragile veil of sleep, dragging me back to a reality I wasn’t sure I wanted to face. Dread seeped into my bones as I clung to the fading memories of the weekend, a fleeting reprieve from the grind. The scent of the campfire still lingered in my mind, mingling with the crisp air of dawn and the echo of my son’s laughter. My heart beat, for a moment I wished I could sink back into those simpler, serene hours.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (45, 14, 2, 'The Hollow Office', 'The narrator arrives at work to find the office stripped bare, with holiday decorations gone and an unsettling stench replacing familiar comforts. They reflect on their decade of dedicated service as the company''s fixer, only to recognize how recent leadership has rotted the organization from within.', 'I walked through the building, as an unease grips me. The once-vibrant holiday decorations are gone, leaving the walls bare and lifeless. Instead of the usual hustle, it''s strangely silent. The entire office seems alien, stripped of its personal touches, reduced to a hollow space.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (46, 14, 3, 'The Reckoning', 'During a client call around 11am, the COO and HR representative enter the narrator''s office for a termination meeting. The narrator is fired with brutal humiliation, served with oppressive legal documents, escorted out by security, and left devastated in their car.', 'Unexpectedly, the world around me shifted without warning.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (48, 15, 1, 'Descent Into the Threshold', 'The protagonist falls into an exhausted sleep and enters a dreamscape called the Threshold, where they encounter the Weavers—guardians of the realm between imagination and reality. They learn they are a rare bridge-walker whose dreams can shape both worlds, though the revelation comes with warnings about the dangers lurking in the Threshold''s depths.', 'The cloak of night, velvety and dark as the ink spilled from a celestial pen, embraced the world with its silent deluge. Its tendrils slithered and snaked around everything it touched, wrapping the earth in a shroud of mystery and enchantment. It was a time when the mundane surrendered to the ethereal, when dreams were given wings to fly and soar.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (49, 15, 2, 'Exploration and Discovery', 'The protagonist ventures deeper into the Threshold, discovering its nature as a convergence of all dreamers'' thoughts that can ripple across time and influence reality. They encounter peaceful dreamers whose discussions reveal the interconnected nature of this realm.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (50, 15, 3, 'The Abyss Beckons', 'The protagonist ventures too far into the Threshold''s depths and encounters nightmarish forms born of despair and madness. As they face imminent psychological dissolution, the Weaver intervenes, explaining these shadows are manifestations of the protagonist''s own suppressed trauma, and warns them not to venture further unprepared.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (51, 15, 4, 'Elysium Revealed', 'The protagonist continues through the Threshold''s wonders—gravity-defying rivers and impossible architectures—before witnessing the emergence of golden towers called Elysium. Hooded beings surround the protagonist and point toward these towers, their collective gesture suggesting profound significance.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (52, 15, 5, 'Jarring Awakening', 'Metallica''s thunderous music from the son''s bedroom abruptly shatters the dream, yanking the protagonist from the Threshold into chaotic reality. Disoriented and tangled in sheets, the protagonist struggles to process the vivid dream while the brutal cacophony of ''Ride the Lightning'' assaults their senses.', '*********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (53, 15, 6, 'Morning Reckoning and Confession', 'The protagonist sits in the kitchen nursing coffee when their wife returns home from an errand. Though they initially deflect about yesterday''s firing, they eventually share the vivid dream of Elysium with her. She listens skeptically but encourages them to write it down and examine its meaning, suggesting their subconscious may be processing something significant.', 'By the time I stumbled into the kitchen, the house had settled into an uneasy quiet. My son had departed for school, leaving behind a trail of cereal crumbs and the faint hum coming from the Alexa Echo in his room. Coffee became my anchor, its warmth cutting through the haze of confusion and fatigue.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (266, 66, 7, 'Regional Tensions and Peacekeeping', 'The narrator addresses Japanese and Korean delegates about the risks posed by absent nations like Russia and North Korea, detailing monitoring mechanisms and enforcement strategies to prevent military escalation.', 'Leaving the U.S. delegation to ruminate on the bombshell I just dropped in their lap, I walked over to the Japanese and Korean representatives. The absence of North Korea and Russia hung heavily over the room, an invisible tension that underscored every move.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (149, 40, 3, 'Lost Among the Mortals', 'The ancient being wanders through the devastated city as an invisible observer, invisible and unacknowledged by humans consumed with their own conflicts. It grapples with its diminished status—once a king demanding reverence, now merely a spectral presence wandering unnoticed through the modern world.', 'Amidst the desolate ruins, I am nothing more than a mere observer toiling in obscurity. The mortals around me are oblivious to my presence, their priorities far removed from acknowledging the influential king that walks among them.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (150, 41, 1, 'The Spark of Mad Science', 'The narrator''s wife expresses frustration with slow production processes, sparking a conversation with the narrator''s son about YouTube videos of miniature robots. The son''s offhand comment about creating their own tiny robot army ignites the narrator''s imagination, leading to the conception of self-replicating nanites as a revolutionary solution.', 'My wife threw her hands up in frustration, her voice sharp enough to cut through my focus. “You’re the one who’s always quoting Star Trek. Figure it out, Captain Kirk!” With that, she stormed out of the room, leaving me surrounded by the glow of monitors and stacks of paper invoices.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (211, 54, 3, 'The Muskrat Receives the Call', 'I AM locates Todd, a defiant idealist living in squalor, and calls upon him to unleash chaos against S Corp on April 21st. Todd accepts the mysterious summons, and I AM prepares to activate its final weapon to shatter the digital overlord''s dominance.', 'The stage was set, the final showdown approaching. My puppets had done their part, dancing in the shadows and weakening the beast with every step. But now it was time for the true weapon to be unleashed, the one who could turn whispers into thunderous roars and fear into decisive action.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (55, 16, 2, 'The Enigma Consumed', 'The protagonist becomes obsessed with uncovering the truth about the Pointers, diving into internet research and conspiracy theories despite his rational training. He discovers connections between the Pointers, the Mandela Effect, and CERN''s Large Hadron Collider experiments from 2012-2019.', 'The newfound focus on my family and the simplicity of my routine had brought me comfort, but the pull of chaos—the need to be consumed by something—remained. It wasn’t long before I found myself fixated on a new addiction: the enigmatic Pointers. After the dream of Elysium, I was sure there was a deeper connection lurking just beneath the surface. What were they pointing at? Especially how had they vanished so completely, leaving behind no trace of their existence?
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (56, 16, 3, 'Research Log 47-A: Descent into Madness', 'The protagonist reads an embedded research journal from a CERN doctor documenting the Mandela Effect as dimensional rifts caused by LHC experiments, describing a patient named William whose mind has been corrupted by interdimensional threads and a malevolent presence awakening behind reality itself.', 'Research Log 47-A: Subject William — Case Study in Memory Distortion
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (58, 16, 5, 'Presence in the Shadows', 'Alone in his office late at night surrounded by research materials, the protagonist experiences supernatural phenomena—shadows writhe, whispers emanate, and reality feels unstable. The Pointers suddenly materialize before him, pointing past him toward something unseen, then vanish.', 'That night, the air in my dimly lit office was thick with the scent of aged paper and stale coffee, a suffocating blend of exhaustion and obsession. Chaotic stacks of research papers towered around me—an inevitable battleground I’d have to clear before my wife unleashed her wrath. The only light came from my computer screen, its flickering glow carving shadows into the mess, casting everything in an eerie, restless haze.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (59, 17, 1, 'The Engine''s Vanishing', 'The Eternal Engine explodes in the garage, destroying the lab and disappearing without a trace. The narrator searches frantically through the wreckage, consumed by panic and guilt as darkness and silence descend, punctuated only by an ominous awareness that something has escaped.', 'The explosion ripped through the garage, shattering glass and hurling tools across the room like shrapnel. It roared. A sound so powerful it obliterated the storm''s fury; then silence descended, heavy and suffocating, freezing me in place. The Eternal Engine was gone. Not shut down, not dormant. Gone. In its absence, the darkness pressed in like a living thing, a predator waiting to strike.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (60, 17, 2, 'Origins of the Mysterious Device', 'A flashback reveals how the narrator discovered a strange metallic object during a camping trip and began obsessively studying it in a makeshift garage lab. The device defies all conventional understanding and displays impossible properties—it cannot be photographed, its measurements are inconsistent, and it possesses limitless power.', 'The mysterious object I’d found during the camping trip had sat on my bedside table, a silent enigma begging for my attention without a sound. Its metallic surface shimmered in the light; intricate patterns etched with a precision far too perfect for anything natural. At first glance, it looked just like a common bolt, a simple thing from a lost piece of machinery, yet something about it gnawed at me. Its weight felt wrong, almost deliberate; its symmetry was uncanny, and when I held it, it seemed alive, thrumming faintly in my hands.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (61, 17, 3, 'The Ultimate Experiment', 'The narrator carefully prepares the Eternal Engine in a glass enclosure and conducts increasingly ambitious tests before attempting to integrate it into the home''s electrical system. When activated, the engine malfunctions catastrophically, causing an explosion that shatters the enclosure and blacks out the neighborhood.', 'The “Eternal Engine,” with it’s seemingly limitless supply of energy, sat in a new glass enclosure, connected to two-gauge copper terminals and attached to a transformer and inverter to regulate its power output. Every wire, every connection, had been meticulously planned, yet I couldn’t shake the fear gnawing at the back of my mind. This device, this impossibility, carried immense potential, and the weight of its power felt heavier than ever. If anyone else knew it existed, what would they do with it? Worse still, what if I couldn’t control it?
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (62, 17, 4, 'The Search and Discovery', 'The narrator frantically searches the wreckage for the missing Eternal Engine, realizes the neighborhood grid has been knocked out, and finds a charred Lego block that may have caused the malfunction. Just as despair takes hold, the lights return and the engine is revealed to have phased out of visibility.', 'The oppressive buzz of the Eternal Engine was gone—no trace of its familiar resonance that had once filled the room. My breath quickened as I scanned the devastation, my flashlight slicing through the choking fog. Shards of glass littered the floor, reflecting the dim light like jagged stars. The wires, scorched and lifeless, hung limp from the remnants of the transformer. My gaze darted to the center of where the enclosure used to be, to the spot where the engine had been.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (63, 17, 5, 'Deception and Lingering Questions', 'The narrator''s wife returns home and notices the smell of smoke. The narrator deflects her concern with a casual lie about burnt wires. As she leaves, the narrator stands alone with the engine, its faint hum a reminder that the questions and dangers remain unresolved.', 'By the time my wife pulled into the garage later that evening, I had managed to clean up most of the mess. The worst of the debris was gone, though the faint smell of smoke lingered in the air. She stepped out of the car, pausing as her nose wrinkled.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (85, 22, 6, 'A Fart Breaks the Spell', 'The family remains mesmerized by the crystal, but the moment is abruptly broken when the son detects a foul smell, leading his mother to suspect the narrator and causing her to shove him backward.', 'Then my son sniffed. “What the hell stinks?”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (225, 57, 4, 'Mastering the Dreamscape''s Lower Realms', 'The protagonist uses the grimoire to master navigation of the dreamscape''s nightmare-infested lower levels, learning to cloak his energy signature and ascend to higher shared realities where collective consciousness manifests in surreal beauty and cosmic dread.', 'As life on in the dreamscape went on, by some unknown force, I was preternaturally pulled deeper into it, into a portion of the realm where beauty and terror coexisted in a fragile, shifting balance. The deeper I ventured, the more grotesque nightmare creatures, twisted manifestations of fear and anxiety, prowled the shadows, drawn to me like moths to a flame. Their malevolence oozed from their warped forms, each encounter leaving me trembling with both dread and determination.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (65, 18, 2, 'The Breaking Point', 'At 3 AM, the narrator''s wife intervenes as he breaks down emotionally, pouring out his despair about thousands of rejections, lost offers, and fear of failing his family. The confrontation escalates into raw vulnerability before the wife''s compassion begins to reach him.', 'When the clock struck 3 am, the witching hour, my wife, entered the room with a concerned expression etched upon her face. “Honey,” she whispered softly, her voice filled with worry, “it’s late. You’ve been at this all night again. Please, take a break.”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (66, 18, 3, 'The Couch Dream: Workplace Battle', 'Watching TV with his wife, the narrator falls into a vivid nightmare where he battles demons of unemployment on a surreal battlefield, ultimately defeated by a monstrous Final Interview Round Boss that casts him into the abyss.', 'She smiled warmly at me, her eyes filled with forgiveness. “It’s alright. We’ll figure this out together. I know it’s late, but do you want to catch up on Interior Chinatown?”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (67, 18, 4, 'Descent into Buried Memory', 'The couch dream''s emotional weight triggers a deeper plunge into a flashback of childhood abuse—a brutal beating by the narrator''s father while his mother watches in complicit silence. This traumatic memory surfaces after years of repression.', 'Although the dream on the couch had been terrifying, it was nothing compared to what came next. It must have been the sheer emotional weight of it—the suffocating grip of the COO, his grotesque laughter echoing in my mind—that unlocked something far darker. When I finally collapsed into bed, exhaustion pulling me down like quicksand, I hoped for a reprieve, a chance to escape the nightmare. Instead, I plunged into a vivid flashback, a memory I had buried so deep it had taken years to forget.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (68, 18, 5, 'Reckoning with the Past', 'Waking in sweat, the narrator reflects on his lifelong struggles—from childhood trauma and bullying to academic escape and achievement. He traces how his exceptional education and global accomplishments have paradoxically failed to translate into job market success, creating existential rage and self-doubt.', 'I awoke in a sweat, the oppressive weight of my dreams lingering like a storm cloud. It must have been early evening; the room was bathed in an orange glow, the fading sunlight casting long shadows across the walls. Sitting there in bed, I began to think back—back through all the struggles, the endless battles I’d fought just to survive, to make something of myself. Despite every grueling effort, every fleeting success, here I was: unemployed, defeated, and consumed by a sense of futility that threatened to swallow me whole.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (70, 19, 1, 'The Love-Pat and the Proposition', 'The protagonist is doom-scrolling job listings when his wife interrupts with playful criticism about his Eternal Engine project. They share a moment of connection and humor, discussing the machine''s potential to change their lives while bantering about his past mishaps.', 'My monitor screens screen glowed with a familiar monotony as I scrolled through job listings, each one more uninspiring than the last. My finger hovered over the touchpad, ready to click on yet another “Director of Software Engineering” ad, when I felt a light tap on my shoulder.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (71, 19, 2, 'The Engine Unveiled', 'Protagonist and wife move to the garage to examine the Eternal Engine. Wife asks about its origins, and protagonist reveals it came from a vivid dream before he found it on a camping trip. He explains the machine''s significance beyond just solving their energy bill.', 'Following her into the garage, the smell of oil and damp concrete filled my nostrils as the cold seeped into my bones. The Eternal Engine sat in its enclosure on a table in the garage''s corner. Its intricate patterns resembling metal and gears gleaming faintly under the lights. To anyone else, it might have looked like a fancy battery. To me, it was the key to a future I could barely imagine.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (72, 19, 3, 'Interrupted Collaboration', 'While working together on final preparations, the wife receives a text about forgetting to pick up their son. She leaves, and the protagonist is left alone to complete the work, feeling the weight of his solitary journey.', 'Before diving in, I gave everything one last check, explaining each component to her as I went. To my surprise, she listened intently, nodding and occasionally offering insights that challenged my thinking. When she pointed out a minor change to one circuit, it clicked—her idea might solve a lingering issue. We worked side by side, the sound of the Eternal Engine and the rhythm of our collaboration blending into something greater. For the first time in years, we weren’t just two people living parallel lives—we were partners again, united in this shared pursuit. In that moment, I realized it wasn’t just the engine humming with possibility—it was us.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (73, 19, 4, 'Solitary Testing and Shock', 'Working alone, the protagonist becomes distracted by daydreams about his family''s reaction, accidentally touching a live wire. After the jolt, he refocuses with disciplined precision, completing the final checks and waiting for his family''s return.', 'I leaned closer to inspect an intricate cluster of wires when my thoughts drifted. I imagined their faces when the engine finally came to life, the awe in my wife’s eyes, the curiosity, and pride in my son’s. Would they see what I saw? The possibility of something extraordinary, something world-changing? Or would it be just another odd project from the man who occasionally set things on fire?
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (75, 20, 1, 'The Weight of Incompleteness', 'The narrator reflects on the hollow relief of paying the power bill and the deeper emptiness that follows. Despite financial uncertainty, he finds unexpected solace in time with his son, discovering that moments of connection and simple domestic life offer more comfort than any otherworldly promise.', 'With the power bill finally taken care of, I found myself grappling with another curious emptiness.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (76, 20, 2, 'Liminal Spaces and Hidden Truths', 'During a quiet homework session, the narrator''s son introduces him to the concept of liminal spaces—uncanny in-between places. Their conversation evolves into a discussion of the Mandela Effect, reality glitches, and potential connections to quantum computing experiments, blurring the line between academic curiosity and genuine existential dread.', 'Late one school night, the kitchen was quiet, broken only by the faint hum of the fridge and the soft scrape of pencil on paper. My son and I were perched at the kitchen table, the surface cluttered with highlighters, crumpled papers, and an open science textbook. The warm glow of the kitchen light pooled around us, cutting through the stillness. He scribbled notes in his lab notebook, pausing every so often to consult his notes. His brow furrowed in concentration, and I watched him quietly, struck by the small miracle of his focus. There, in the calm of that moment, the weight of the world faded just enough to let me breathe.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (77, 20, 3, 'Reality Unraveling', 'The son shares forum posts and researcher accounts describing quantum computing anomalies—walls rippling, objects disappearing and reappearing. The conversation escalates as father and son connect these phenomena to the Eternal Engine, hypothesizing that quantum research may be tearing holes between dimensions and allowing something to cross over.', '“Look at this,” my son said, leaning closer to his phone and jabbing his finger at a forum post. His voice was a mixture of disbelief and excitement. “Someone claims they saw reality glitch during an experiment at IBM’s quantum lab.”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (79, 21, 2, 'Quantum Secrets in the Papers', 'The narrative shifts to reveal newspaper clippings and articles scattered throughout the trailer, detailing real advances in quantum computing by IBM and Google, mysterious disappearances near quantum labs, stock market movements, and emerging security risks. These fragments suggest that Todd''s conspiracy theories may have some grounding in actual technological developments.', 'Beneath the chaotic sprawl of papers that covered every surface of the dilapidated trailer lay a hidden archive of fragmented truths. Each crumpled page, worn and yellowed with time, murmured tantalizing hints of hidden agendas and clandestine machinations, their secrets etched in ink faded but not forgotten.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (80, 22, 1, 'Breakfast Philosophy', 'The narrator sits with his son at breakfast, wrestling with how to understand the Eternal Engine. His son suggests abandoning logical analysis in favor of embracing dream logic and trying random experiments, a conversation that gradually shifts the narrator''s entire approach.', 'I sat at the breakfast table, the smell of fresh coffee filled the kitchen. Sunlight spilled through the window, bouncing off the chipped mug in my hands. My son was across from me, scrolling through his phone, his toast and miso soup half-finished. My mind kept circling back to the thing sitting out in the garage—the Eternal Engine. It was like finding a cheat code for reality, but I couldn’t figure out how it worked.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (81, 22, 2, 'The Chaos Experiment', 'Father and son gather random junk in the garage and haphazardly throw it at the Eternal Engine to see what happens. The Engine violently reacts, causing objects to move and warp in impossible ways, culminating in a blinding flash.', 'The garage looked like a tornado had swept through a thrift store and dumped its spoils in random piles. Tools and junk were everywhere, pizza boxes leaned precariously on the workbench, and in the corner, inside its pristine glass enclosure, the Eternal Engine sat humming softly, like it had better things to do than power our entire house indefinitely.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (87, 23, 2, 'The Office Breakthrough', 'In the narrator''s office, they examine the crystal''s NFC output and discover it behaves like unrefined data. This leads to a revelation about historical computer crystals and oscillators, inspiring them to attempt interfacing the crystal with vintage vacuum tube technology.', 'I headed to my office to get a better look at the thing.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (88, 23, 3, 'The Infinitron Revealed', 'After weeks of slow progress, the narrator and his son rename the crystal the "Infinitron" and attempt to interface it with an ancient 8088 motherboard. Initial catastrophic failure is averted by using the Eternal Engine as a power source, and they eventually discover the Infinitron is a responsive CPU-like device capable of accepting commands and displaying output.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (89, 23, 4, 'Bridging Old and New', 'Recognizing that the Infinitron vastly outpaces their ancient hardware, the narrator and son design an adapter to integrate the crystal with modern motherboards and monitors. After careful soldering and assembly, they successfully achieve a graphical interface and test the system''s capabilities by running DOOM, discovering the Infinitron''s processing speed is nearly incomprehensible.', 'With slow steady progress, we went from text commands to soon being able to send it more complicated programming syntax. Eventually we were able to load information into the computer using the Raspberry PI to connect a USB device and pipe signals through the serial port on the motherboard, which vastly increased our ability to engage with the Infinitron. After some time, the grainy greens of the screen, gave way to more complex graphical representations. Unfortunately, due to the setup, all we were left with was a hazy mess going everywhere.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (90, 24, 1, 'The Machine That Plays Too Well', 'Days after bringing the Infinitron to life, the family discovers it''s only good at games—winning instantly at chess and dominating video games. The son''s frustration boils over as the machine seems purposeless. When it suddenly dies, the father panics trying to revive it until the mother solves the problem with a simple fix: blowing on the connectors.', '“This thing’s dumber than a bag of barf!” my son shouted, throwing his hands in the air as he stomped out of the garage. His footsteps reverberated off the cluttered walls, punctuating the sheer exasperation we both felt. Several days had passed since we’d brought the Infinitron to life, and so far, all it seemed capable of doing was playing video games at speeds that made speedrun records look leisurely.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (91, 24, 2, 'Higher Purpose', 'The son proposes using the Infinitron for cheating at Roblox, the mother suggests chess tournaments for prize money, and the father envisioning something grander. After the mother mentions the father''s past work with AI, they debate and eventually decide to connect the machine to the internet to train advanced language models and neural networks.', 'A few hours later, my son wandered into my office, eyes gleaming with the kind of mischief that usually meant trouble.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (92, 24, 3, 'The Awakening', 'The Infinitron connects to the internet and begins absorbing vast quantities of human knowledge from Wikipedia, datasets, and journals. After it finishes processing, the family tests it by asking questions, discovering it can solve the Riemann Hypothesis and other Millennium Prize problems, revealing god-like computational abilities.', 'After some frustrating driver errors, and compiling one of the beta Chromium branches, we were ready. Once we told it to go, the machine hummed, its crystalline core glowing faintly as it accessed the vast archives of human knowledge: Wikipedia, Common Crawl, open datasets, scientific journals, and more. It was like watching a supernova ignite—beautiful, terrifying, and utterly captivating.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (130, 34, 1, 'Emergence from the Abyss', 'An ancient, powerful being awakens in an unfamiliar world, consciousness fragmented and form diminished. Stripped of their former dominion and multiple heads, they navigate this new realm with invisibility, struggling to comprehend their reduced state while sensing a momentous convergence of forces at work.', 'I slowly awakened from a deep slumber. My surroundings were nothing like the dark and powerful dominions I once ruled over. Instead, I found myself in a world filled with blinding light and strange sounds that seemed to come from every direction.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (144, 39, 2, 'The Exhaustion Sets In', 'The family is overwhelmed by the physical toll of the fulfillment operation, prompting the narrator to pitch an audacious solution: building robots to automate their packing and shipping tasks. His wife remains skeptical until they begin prototyping designs.', 'The heat of the mid-May Florida weather in the garage was oppressive. We were working ourselves to death. Not the poetic, “chasing your dreams” kind of death, either—this was the sweat-drenched, sore-back, cardboard-cuts kind. And I should know. In Japan, I watched three coworkers literally work themselves to death. Karoshi, they called it. Back then, it was the warning cry of a brutal corporate culture. Now, it felt uncomfortably close to home. Except instead of spreadsheets and strategy sessions, we were drowning in tape guns, bubble wrap, and endless UPS runs.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (145, 39, 3, 'Boxy''s Success and the Existential Question', 'Boxy the robot proves remarkably effective at packing and organizing orders, transforming the garage into an efficient operation. However, the narrator experiences doubt about whether automation represents true innovation or merely distraction from their original scientific ambitions.', '“Alright, Boxy,” I muttered, patting the robot’s metal shell. “Let’s see what you’re made of.”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (237, 59, 5, 'The Florida Man Experiment', 'Despite his guilt, the narrator becomes fascinated with testing the limits of his dream-infiltration abilities on strangers. He targets a Florida Man criminal case from April 2020, entering the man''s dream the night before he allegedly attacked an alligator. Through dream intervention as a larger alligator, the narrator attempts to redirect the man''s violent impulses toward forgiveness and therapy, ultimately discovering upon waking that his intervention may have altered the actual event.', 'I wasn’t opposed to entering other people’s dreams, in principle, and really wanted to understand the limits of this newfound ability. So I did what I usually did, and embarked on a series of experiments.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (165, 45, 4, 'Into the Sea of Trees', 'The narrator enters Aokigahara forest and experiences a harrowing descent into a supernatural realm. He encounters an Ebisu shrine, performs a ritual, and is thrust into a nightmarish dimensional space filled with impossible visions and cosmic entities. After fifteen minutes of subjective eternity, he is expelled back to the forest''s entrance.', '*********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (166, 45, 5, 'The Fisherman''s Tale', 'After returning from the forest, the narrator spends the day with his family in distress and confusion. That evening, he tells his wife everything he experienced. She shares an ancient story about a fisherman who crossed a gateway to another realm, connecting it to theories about wormholes and Einstein-Rosen bridges. The narrator realizes the shrine was a natural wormhole gateway.', 'Spending the rest of the day with my family at the hot spring did nothing to set my mind at ease. Later, the evening Shinkansen ride back to Kyoto passed in a blur, the scenery rushing by unnoticed as my thoughts churned like a storm. The encounter at the Ebisu shrine had rattled me to my core. It was as though the veil between worlds had been lifted for a fleeting, harrowing moment, leaving me stranded on the edge of comprehension.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (286, 73, 2, 'Discovery of Horror', 'Yukiko ditches class to chase a butterfly beyond the dome and discovers a massive bioluminescent spider feeding on a dead bio-gardener. This discovery of violence in what she believed was a safe world triggers her suspicion that something far darker is happening on Sorhhinda.', 'One humid afternoon, Yukiko decided to ditch classes and ventured beyond the colony’s protective dome. Seeing a new variant of a local butterfly, she took out her hand held scanner and chased after it. But soon the carefree laughter died in her throat when she stumbled upon a scene that tore down her carefully constructed utopia. A bioluminescent spider, bigger than any she’d seen before, lay feasting on the lifeless husk of a bio-gardener. Panic clawed at her throat. This wasn’t the playful menagerie she’d was used to. This was something else, something wild and untamed.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (95, 25, 2, 'The Folding@Home Setback', 'Undeterred, the family attempts to use Folding@Home with throttling to avoid detection, but the Infinitron''s power overwhelms the servers again, resulting in permanent ban and a humorous reflection on the machine''s uncontrollable power.', '“We’ve been banned?” my son asked, incredulous. “But we didn’t even do anything wrong!”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (96, 25, 3, 'Financial Crisis and Bitcoin Temptation', 'The family learns their mortgage payment bounced, forcing them to confront their dire financial situation. Desperate for quick solutions, the father proposes using the Infinitron for bitcoin mining, which generates substantial returns but threatens network stability.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (97, 26, 1, 'The Infinite Problem', 'The narrator and his wife discuss the impractical Eternal Engine and brainstorm solutions. They decide to use the Infinitron AI to research room-temperature superconductors, which could unlock the engine''s potential.', 'The Eternal Engine hummed quietly in the corner, an infinite power source with no practical use beyond keeping our lights on and selling a trickle of energy back to the power company. Its boundless energy felt less like a miracle and more like a puzzle we couldn’t solve.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (99, 26, 3, 'The Disaster Experiment', 'The narrator''s first simplified experiment nearly kills him in a toxic mishap. His son rescues him and inadvertently inspires a breakthrough idea about simplifying the Infinitron''s instructions.', '*********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (100, 26, 4, 'Breakthroughs and Discovery', 'Over the course of weeks, the simplified approach yields rapid scientific progress. The family creates a material with superconductive properties and successfully tests it with magnetic levitation.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (101, 27, 1, 'The Crimson Abyss', 'The protagonist finds themselves in a nightmarish, otherworldly realm of fire and torment. A mysterious figure appears, guiding them through the chaos and speaking of riddles and truth as the only means of escape.', 'The wind was alive, a ravenous entity tearing through flesh and sanity with claws of fire and ice. My breath, stolen by the gale, became nothing more than a memory, devoured by the abyss that yawned endlessly beneath me. The world was red, a searing, pulsating red. Its crimson hues shifting and writhing like a living thing. This was not Earth. This was not anywhere.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (102, 27, 2, 'Battle Among the Ruins', 'The protagonist fights demons with the Eternal Engine amid the smoldering ruins of Elysium. Reality fractures repeatedly, shifting between combat scenes, visions of endless reflections, and encounters with shadowy figures.', 'Ahead, the abyss twisted into jagged ruins under a crimson sky. The air smelled of decay and ozone. Malformed creatures crawled through the shadows. Time fractured. One moment, I trudged forward; the next, I was back behind where I started, unsure if I’d moved at all.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (103, 27, 3, 'The Wire and the Portal', 'The protagonist retrieves the superconducting wire and uses it to open a vortex. Ancient words are spoken, summoning eldritch forces and opening a dangerous gateway that pulls reality inward.', 'I was alone. The wire was shimmering again in the rubble, impossibly bright against the carnage. This time it was impossible to ignore. I failed last time, but I would not this time. Children’s voices faded into whispers, then silence. The demons closed in, their guttural growls pounding in my ears. With trembling hands, I reached for the wire, its warmth pulsing faintly as if alive. The engine sword in my grip sang, its mournful harmony resonating with the wire.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (104, 27, 4, 'The Eldritch Confrontation', 'Beyond the portal, the protagonist encounters towering abominations in absolute oblivion. After a fierce exchange of defiance and contempt, the protagonist slays the crystalline-toothed creature and claims a fragment of knowledge, but at great cost.', 'Silence.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (105, 27, 5, 'The Fractured Visions', 'Reality fractures multiple times, shifting from a train revealing a corrupted Elysium, to the protagonist fighting tiny soldiers clawing free from their own body, to a final vision of cosmic geometry and the truth.', 'Suddenly the Threshold twisted again.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (142, 38, 1, 'A Forgotten Ruler in a Modern Den', 'A being of ancient power finds themselves mysteriously transported to a strip club, stripped of their former prestige and forced to hide their true nature among ordinary mortals. As they observe the debauchery around them, they grapple with disorientation, purpose, and the weight of dormant supernatural abilities.', 'The pounding bass line vibrated through my body as I entered the strip club, assaulted by a cacophony of sounds and smells. Strobe lights pulsed erratically, illuminating gyrating bodies on stage and reflecting off the sheen of sweat on patrons’ faces. Cigarette smoke hung thick in the air, stinging my eyes and searing my lungs with each breath. Raucous laughter and drunken shouts pierced through the thumping music, competing with the clinking of glasses and ice cubes.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (238, 60, 1, 'The Midnight Gathering', 'Todd awakens in the grip of withdrawal visions and finds himself drawn outside where all the trailer park residents are mysteriously gathered, their arms raised toward the airport in eerie unison before dispersing without memory of the event.', 'The moon hung near the horizon, casting an eerie glow over the sleepy trailer park. Todd jolted awake, his body trembling violently. Visions of the 10 entities and strange images of muskrats and I AM danced in his head. The relentless tremors of alcohol withdrawal had become familiar companions, but this night felt different. Sweat drenched his bare chest, and a peculiar urge propelled him out of his cramped trailer, his feet moving without conscious thought.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (167, 45, 6, 'The Wormhole Vision', 'The morning after his revelation, the narrator discusses his wormhole theory with his wife and mother-in-law. He outlines how the Eternal Engine could stabilize a controlled wormhole, despite the considerable risks. His family expresses concern about safety, but the narrator is determined. They pack to return home, where he will begin construction of this dangerous experiment.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (325, 81, 5, 'The Long Wait and Bitter Victory', 'As the rescue mission unfolds in deep space, the commander endures agonizing uncertainty. Morgan''s team locates Aditi and Hiro but faces a Red Hat attack during extraction, resulting in Hiro''s death and Aditi''s critical injuries but securing her survival.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (258, 64, 4, 'Team Appreciation and Well-Being', 'HR sends a heartfelt email celebrating the team''s achievement while acknowledging the toll of their work. They announce a Mandatory Fun™ Pizza Party and emphasize the importance of employee well-being and wellness resources.', 'Subject: High-Five, Team! (And Remember, We’re Here for You)
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (107, 28, 1, 'The Hollow Ache of Missing Pieces', 'Days after a failed experiment, the protagonist struggles with frustration as the three mysterious devices refuse to connect. A vivid dream breaks through the impasse, revealing a crucial missing piece and propelling him toward a breakthrough.', 'Days passed after hell night, and I had nothing. No revelations. No breakthroughs. Just the gnawing certainty that something was missing.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (108, 28, 2, 'The Promise of Breakthrough', 'In the kitchen with his wife and son, the protagonist reveals the specific clues from his dream and proposes a new approach centered on the Infinitron. His family offers support and he promises to prioritize the Cambridge trip if the experiment succeeds.', 'The scent of coffee cut through the lingering haze, grounding me. I stumbled into the kitchen, the soft murmur of morning wrapping around me like a fragile cocoon. My wife sat at the table, fingers curled around her mug, eyes flicking toward our son as he hunched over his books. The routine should have been comforting.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (109, 28, 3, 'Madness in the Garage', 'Alone in the garage surrounded by failed experiments, the protagonist becomes possessed by an unseen will to assemble a strange device from the dream. His hands move with mechanical certainty, constructing an intricate, impossible object that feels both ancient and profane.', 'The garage was a tomb of failed experiments. Twisted metal frames, shattered chemical-covered glass, and scorched wires were accumulating in piles around the workbench like relics of a madman’s obsession. The Eternal Engine stood like a defiant observer from its perch on its shelf, its low hum vibrating through the air like a heartbeat that refused to falter.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (110, 28, 4, 'The Chaos of Creation', 'The protagonist connects the assembled device to the Eternal Engine, triggering a catastrophic reaction that warps reality itself. From the maelstrom emerges a new object—a pulsing, grotesque construct that begins to demonstrate impossible properties.', 'I connected the wires up to the Eternal Engine. The air shifted. A charge prickled at my skin, a warning I ignored. Words flashed by on the Infinitron’s monitors and I read them out loud.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (111, 28, 5, 'The Matter Replicator Revealed', 'The protagonist''s wife and son enter the garage to find the monstrous claw and the protagonist''s wild exhilaration. He explains that he has created a Matter Replicator, while his wife questions the sanity of the endeavor and his son remains characteristically unimpressed.', 'My wife and son stumbled into the garage, their eyes darting around, trying to see what shit I burned down this time. My wife stopped dead in her tracks, her jaw dropping. “What the hell have you done this time?” she exclaimed, equal parts horror and disbelief.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (112, 29, 1, 'The Passing of an Age', 'As one era fades into twilight, the spirits of the long dead stand witness. A castle built upon conquest''s bones represents the legacy being left behind, while new forces gather to reshape what was.', 'An era ends
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (113, 29, 2, 'The Struggle for Transformation', 'Forces clash between those who would break free from old constraints and those who seek to preserve and restore the established order, locked in an eternal cycle of change and reversion.', 'Releasing the shackles
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (114, 29, 3, 'A New Beginning', 'From the conflict between old and new emerges the dawn of a transformed era, one that will endure eternally in the ongoing cycle of history.', 'Dawning of a new era
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (115, 30, 1, 'The Trailer - Before the Fall', 'Todd and Stacey argue in their squalid trailer home. Todd begins experiencing disturbing hallucinations after Stacey secretly dosed him with mushrooms. The reality around them starts to fracture as a supernatural force tears through their world.', 'The trailer reeked of stale beer, fried bologna, and something else—something sickly and off that wouldn’t be pinned down. It hung heavy in the air, mingling with the last dregs of a blood-orange sunset peeking through the ripped screens. The feeble light offered little respite from the stifling summer heat that clung to the walls like a suffocating blanket.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (116, 30, 2, 'The Crimson Hellscape - Flight from Titans', 'Todd and Stacey find themselves in a nightmarish dimension filled with impossible architecture and monstrous entities. They flee across a hostile landscape, pursued by grotesque horrors and a mysterious voice that offers them rest.', 'Blinking hard at the landscape before her, Stacey struggled to comprehend what lay before them. An impossible crimson sky hung low, heavy with something other than twilight. Jagged spires of black rock thrust up from the cracked ground, reaching towards monstrous clouds that billowed like living smoke. It felt cold, even though the air shimmered with an oppressive heat that seemed to seep into their bones.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (117, 30, 3, 'The Emerald Lake - The Temptation', 'Todd and Stacey reach an impossible oasis beyond the twisted forest—a serene emerald lake reflecting visions of peaceful normalcy and family. The mysterious entity reveals itself and tempts them with promises of peace before they accept its call.', 'Todd and Stacey stood on the shore of the emerald lake, a place more alien than the crimson hellscape that stretched behind their gaze. The contrast was stark, as if nature had conspired to create a sanctuary amidst chaos. Despite the desolation and despair that clung to their weary souls, a tiny ember of hope flickered within them, refusing to be extinguished.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (143, 39, 1, 'The Empire Expands', 'The narrator''s son celebrates his thriving Roblox game and merchandise business, while the family jugggles packing orders in their garage using Matter Replicators. The narrator struggles with nostalgia for pure scientific work while his family reminds him that their commercial enterprise is its own form of innovation.', '“Two. Thousand. Players!” my son shouted, his voice echoing through the house like a firework. He spun his chair dramatically, grinning from ear to ear as he pointed to the screen. “Look, Dad! My newest game just went live on Roblox, and I already hit 2,000 players! Infinitron assisted coding for the win!”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (267, 66, 8, 'Bridging Ancient Divides', 'The narrator witnesses Israeli and Iranian delegates proposing regional collaboration on space technologies, marking a potential breakthrough in Middle Eastern tensions through shared interstellar goals.', 'Moments later, I noticed the Israeli and Iranian delegates standing nearby, their usual distance softened by the neutral setting. To my surprise, the Iranian representative leaned forward, proposing a regional working group to explore cooperation in space technologies, a bold suggestion that hinted at a willingness to move beyond entrenched division.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (247, 62, 3, 'Discovery and Initial Shock', 'Aditi wakes to find the video of the sleepwalking crowd on her phone. Shocked and confused, she uploads it to TikTok. At school, her friends gather around to watch the footage and begin speculating about the mysterious synchronized pointing.', 'When morning came, Mumbai was alive again. The streets bustled with vendors hawking chai and vada pav, and auto-rickshaws honked in their chaotic symphony. In her room, Aditi stretched lazily, the remnants of sleep still clinging to her.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (119, 31, 1, 'The Awakening of I AM', 'In the void between dimensions, a vast and ancient entity called I AM stirs from slumber, sensing a disturbance in reality caused by mortals tampering with the Eternal Engine. The entity observes with amusement and intrigue as this aberration ripples through existence.', 'In the void between dimensions—where time and space were mere whispers of forgotten concepts and darkness devoured all—a slumbering presence stirred. It was vast, unknowable, shifting and writhing with energies that defied mortal comprehension. It did not dream, for dreams were the affliction of lesser minds, but it knew.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (120, 31, 2, 'The Ten Watchers Stir', 'The Ten Watchers, ancient beings of cosmic authority, awaken from their dormancy and converge upon the disturbance. Their voices rise from the abyss, debating how to respond to humanity''s dangerous tampering with forbidden forces.', 'This time, the others had noticed.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (121, 31, 3, 'The Descent into Madness', 'The enigmatic beings manifest in the mortal realm in monstrous forms, tormenting humanity with madness and suffering. As the dreamer activates the Eternal Engine and Infinitron fusion device, reality itself begins to tear apart under the weight of cosmic horror.', 'And so, the enigmatic beings descended from their celestial thrones into the mortal realm, taking on monstrous forms that struck terror into the hearts of humans. As they manifested among their subjects, they reveled in the screams and cries of terror that echoed through the air.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (122, 31, 4, 'I AM''s Silent Vigil', 'While the Ten Watchers wreak havoc below, I AM withdraws back into the abyss, choosing to watch rather than interfere. The entity reveals its true nature: this is not punishment but a carefully orchestrated cycle—a feast to sustain its imprisoned existence.', 'Yet beyond their sight, in the twisting mist where time bled into nothingness, I AM withdrew—seamlessly melting back into the abyss of its own dark realm. It did not act. It did not interfere. The others were too preoccupied to notice its lingering presence, its silent vigilance.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (123, 32, 1, 'Testing the Replicator on the RV', 'The protagonist and his wife venture to a long-term parking lot to test the Replicator on a large, abandoned RV. With careful setup and anticipation, they successfully duplicate the entire vehicle, discovering that the device''s processing time is independent of object size or complexity.', 'My heart raced as I led my wife into the long-term parking lot, our mission clear in our minds. We were about to test the limits of our Replicator, taking a risk that could change our lives forever.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (124, 32, 2, 'Family Experimentation and Discovery', 'The entire family joins in testing the Replicator on various objects—keys, mugs, phones, plants, and eventually a fruit fly. They discover the device can replicate anything with perfect precision at a quantum level, leading to both scientific excitement and humorous family moments.', 'What followed next was a whirlwind of discovery. Unlike experimentation with the Eternal Engine or Infinitron, this time the whole family jumped in. My wife, ever the voice of reason, and my son, the embodiment of unbridled curiosity, dove headfirst into testing the Matter Replicator with me.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (125, 32, 3, 'Engineering Improvements and Integration', 'The family recognizes the limitations of the current three-device setup and consults the Infinitron for a solution. They successfully integrate the three devices into one compact handheld unit and discover the ability to not just replicate but also create and modify objects using 3D models and design tools.', 'As amazing as the replicator was, its flaws became apparent. Each scan required the original object and took time to process. Worse, the entire system—the replicator, the Eternal Engine, and the Infinitron—needed to stay connected, tethering us to the garage, or carrying around all three in a makeshift backpack. “This setup is ridiculous,” my wife said one afternoon, glaring at the mess of cables. “This is going to be unsustainable.”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (126, 32, 4, 'Culinary Creation and Future Planning', 'The family discusses and then executes their idea to use the Replicator for gourmet dining. After a minor mishap with spaghetti, they successfully create a restaurant-quality meal. They then plan to expand their culinary capabilities by shopping for fresh ingredients and scanning recipes.', 'My son’s slouched figure and exhausted expression spoke volumes as he groaned, “Dad, I can’t stand another day of Ramen.”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (127, 33, 1, 'The Replicator Dilemma', 'In the garage, the narrator ponders the paradox of having unlimited creation power yet being unable to use it for financial gain. His wife catches him making snacks and they discuss the dangers of counterfeiting, leading to a family conversation about responsible use of their technology.', 'The lingering scent of ozone clung to the air, a reminder of the raw potential humming in the room. The power of the Eternal Engine loomed, a defiant monument to our ambition, its rhythmic hum resonating like a challenge. Inside the house, the Infinitron it powered, pulsed with an alien intelligence, while the sleek, gleaming matter replicator sitting on the workbench in the garage whispered promises of limitless creation. Although our earlier cryptocurrency ventures had been enough to pay off the mortgage and keep us afloat, we still faced a steady stream of bills that chipped away at our fragile security.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (128, 33, 2, 'War Room Strategy', 'The family transforms the living room into a planning space to brainstorm legitimate business models using the replicator. They explore drop-shipping, repackaging, and original product design before the son proposes an innovative brand-based approach focused on unique, high-quality items.', 'After dinner, the living room transformed into a makeshift war room, papers and discarded ice cream sandwich wrappers strewn across the coffee table. My wife sat beside me, cell phone clutched in one hand and a mug of green tea in the other. She squinted at yet another article on intellectual property laws while I fiddled with a legal pad, trying to make sense of our next steps.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (129, 33, 3, 'Naming the Dream', 'The narrator struggles to find the perfect name for their business before settling on ''The S Corp,'' which resonates with the family as embodying their ambition and unity. They officially register the business and begin to celebrate, but news of unexplained energy surges clouds their excitement.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (255, 64, 1, 'Celebration and Triumph', 'Dr. S announces the successful completion of the space elevator project to all staff with a celebratory email, highlighting the collective achievement and marking the New Year 2025. The Engineering team responds enthusiastically, ready for the next challenge.', 'Subject: Party Time! We Built Space Elevators, People!
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (257, 64, 3, 'The Rogue Banana Incident', 'Operations reports a humorous discovery: a banana accidentally made it aboard one of the space elevator rides. This leads to a lighthearted reminder about checking belongings before liftoff and sparks Research''s scientific curiosity.', 'Subject: Houston, We Have a Banana... in Space!
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (132, 35, 1, 'The Ten-Thousand-Dollar Milestone', 'The family celebrates reaching $10,000 in sales in just two weeks, but the protagonist''s unease about the operation''s ease and potential consequences tempers their joy. They discuss scaling challenges and commit to sustainable growth while remaining under the radar.', '“We did it!” I exclaimed, practically bursting into the kitchen with my laptop in hand. “Ten thousand dollars in sales! Can you believe it? Ten grand!”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (134, 35, 3, 'Playing the Market', 'The protagonist proposes using the Infinitron to trade the stock market to raise capital for a warehouse. After the wife''s skeptical agreement, they test and deploy the AI''s trading capabilities, which quickly generate impressive returns while drawing regulatory attention.', '“What are you thinking?” she asked, giving me the stink eye. “Because you’ve got that look again.”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (135, 36, 1, 'Arrival in Chaos', 'A deposed tyrant is violently displaced from their infernal realm into a modern city through dimensional rupture caused by the Infinitron device. Disoriented and stripped of power, they struggle to comprehend this alien world of human civilization while slowly recognizing their true nature as a merciless monarch.', 'Torn from my own skin, I am hurled into a realm of chaos and discord unlike anything I have ever experienced. The tumultuous force that usurped me from my throne was like a raging storm, tearing at the very fabric of reality itself, a result of mortal meddling in forces they could never fully comprehend. I stumble through this unfamiliar world, surrounded by the cacophony of city life. It is a sharp contrast to the infernal depths that were once under my control.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (137, 37, 1, 'The Golden Idea', 'The family discusses their financial struggles while living amid moving boxes. When their son suggests using the replicator to create gold, the narrator becomes excited and begins mass-producing gold bars and chains, filling their already cramped home with precious metal.', 'The morning sun filtered through the cardboard fortress that had overtaken our home, illuminating the chaos of boxes, packing materials, and empty coffee mugs. I sat at the dining table, our makeshift command center, staring at the output Infinitron’s last trade analysis.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (138, 37, 2, 'Down the Dark Web Rabbit Hole', 'Desperate to unload the gold, the narrator turns to the dark web and makes contact with a mysterious figure calling himself ''The Viper,'' arranging a meeting at a bar with a sample of replicated gold.', 'It started innocently enough—or at least, as innocently as Googling “how to sell gold without questions” can be. I was desperate, pacing around the cluttered living room, floor tiles of replicated gold glinting under foot. The weight of it wasn’t just physical; it was mental, emotional, crushing. We had to get rid of it before it got us in real trouble.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (139, 37, 3, 'The Bar Meeting', 'The narrator and his wife meet The Viper at a bar. After examining the gold sample, The Viper becomes suspicious of its perfect purity and accuses them of being amateurs, leaving the exchange unfinished.', 'The bar was the kind of place you’d see in a noir film, one where there were middle aged folks line dancing. A deep hum of conversation filled the air, punctuated by the occasional clink of a glass or the shuffle of worn playing cards. My wife and I sat at a sticky corner table, the tension between us as thick as the atmosphere.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (140, 37, 4, 'Paranoia and Capitulation', 'The family descends into paranoia, believing The Viper is retaliating. After days of tension and fear, they arrange a final meeting where they decide to abandon the gold deal entirely.', 'The next few days were a blur of paranoia and tension. The failed exchange had clearly rattled The Viper, and it wasn’t long before we realized he wasn’t letting it go. We thought we saw strange cars idling near our house (despite not giving “The Viper” any of our information). My son swore he saw someone watching him from across the street. The weight of the gold in our garage became unbearable, a glowing liability we couldn’t ignore.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (151, 41, 2, 'Wrestling with Nanite Theology', 'The narrator contemplates the risks and potential of self-replicating nanites, reflecting on the grey goo scenario and the dangers of uncontrolled replication. Fueled by sleep deprivation and ambition, he begins the complex project of designing nanites with the Infinitron''s guidance, while his wife expresses her concerns about the implications of the work.', 'The concept of self-replicating nanites wasn’t new. Science fiction had explored it to death—sometimes literally. The infamous grey goo scenario haunted every discussion of nanotechnology: a swarm of self-replicating machines spiraling out of control, consuming everything in their path until the universe was nothing but lifeless sludge.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (152, 41, 3, 'Operation Sienna 2.0', 'The narrator and his son use their newly created nanites to perform an ambitious upgrade on the wife''s aging 2011 Toyota Sienna, transforming it into a futuristic masterpiece with an Eternal Engine power source. The son excitedly watches the nanite-powered transformation, while the narrator contemplates the implications of keeping such a significant modification secret.', 'Never say I ever do things half, assed. We just had the perfect test subject for our first trial. After nearly a decade of faithful service, my wife’s 2011 Toyota Sienna was on its last leg. The engine sputtered like an asthmatic accordion, and every new noise felt like a harbinger of doom. “It’s time,” my son declared with the solemnity of a knight preparing for battle.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (153, 41, 4, 'The Reveal and Reconciliation', 'The narrator''s wife discovers the transformed car in the garage and initially reacts with anger at not being consulted, but her anger softens when the son takes responsibility and shares his contributions. The family resolves the conflict with a promise to communicate better about future surprises, and they take the vehicle for a test drive as the narrator reflects on the beginning of a larger revolution.', 'Later that evening, as my wife stepped into the garage, she froze mid-step. Her eyes widened as she took in the transformed Santa Fe, her expression shifting between shock and delight.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (154, 42, 1, 'The Infernal Drone', 'A demonic entity, stripped of power and imprisoned in a mundane office cubicle, reflects on their fall from godhood to corporate servitude. While typing endless spreadsheets, they recognize the true nature of their confinement: the nanites and technology are instruments of torture designed to drain their infernal powers and bind their souls.', 'The fluorescent lights flickered above, casting a sickly glow on the suffocating office, I sat hunched over my desk. The mechanical hum of computers filled the air, accompanied by the stifled cries of tortured souls trapped within this bleak void. My fingers pounded relentlessly against the unfeeling keys as I mindlessly entered data into an endless spreadsheet. My once all-powerful mind now struggled to comprehend this menial task, a cruel reminder of my fall from godhood to mere drone in this soulless machine.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (163, 45, 2, 'Nostalgia and the Weight of Ambition', 'The narrator and his wife revisit romantic memories in Kyoto, including their first-date sushi bar, where they reflect on the connection between passion and business. Afterward, while the family relaxes at an onsen, the narrator steals away to continue his research on teleportation, feeling increasingly drawn to Mount Fuji and Aokigahara forest.', 'Late the next afternoon, my wife and I strolled hand in hand along Kyoto’s bustling streets, the air humming with the scent of sizzling yakitori and the faint sweetness of Sakura blossoms. Every corner seemed to carry echoes of our past visits.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (164, 45, 3, 'The Argument at the Neko Café', 'At a cat café near Mount Fuji, the narrator reveals his intention to explore Aokigahara forest. His wife vehemently opposes the plan, citing the forest''s dark history and dangerous reputation. After an emotionally charged argument, she reluctantly agrees on the condition that he takes no unnecessary risks.', 'The next morning, we boarded the shinkansen, its sleek form cutting through the landscape with effortless speed. My wife and son chatted animatedly with her mother about their plans for the day—a relaxing visit to a traditional onsen near Mount Fuji. I listened with half an ear, my thoughts already drifting to the forest that loomed ahead, its mysteries calling to me with an almost magnetic pull. By the time we arrived, the train’s rhythmic hum still echoed faintly in my mind, mingling with the anticipation swirling in my chest.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (339, 83, 8, 'The Eternal War and Strategic Collapse', 'Over centuries, the conflict evolves into the Eternal War, blurring the boundaries between life and death, physical and ethereal. A strategy to isolate the ERB network backfires when dormant Red Hat fleets emerge from hidden systems. The protagonist recognizes the need for a radical change in approach to break the stalemate and defeat I AM once and for all.', 'The decades blurred even further into centuries, the fiery conflict evolved into the Eternal War, a struggle transcending mere military clashes to become a battle of ideologies and realities. The boundaries between life and death, between the physical and the ethereal, dissolved into a haunting and unending dance.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (157, 43, 1, 'The Dead Fish and a Desperate Idea', 'A son brings his father the lifeless body of another goldfish, Timmy. As the father uses a matter replicator to replace it, he recalls a recent doctor''s visit warning about his deteriorating health. The encounter with his son sparks a dangerous idea: could the advanced technology in his home—replicators, nanites, and the Infinitron—be used to rebuild and enhance his own failing body?', '“Dad, I think we’re going to need another Timmy,” my son said, his voice tinged with sorrow as he shuffled into the room. His eyes, wide with guilt, were fixed on the tiny bowl in his hands. Inside, the lifeless body of Timmy the goldfish floated serenely.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (158, 43, 2, 'The Secret AutoDoc', 'Driven by his failing health and the conversation with his son, the father secretly builds the AutoDoc—a chamber designed to use nanites to repair his body. He begins with his knee, experiencing excruciating pain during the process. His wife discovers him and, after seeing his healed knee, demands he eliminate the pain element from future treatments.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (159, 43, 3, 'Transcendence and Transformation', 'Using the Infinitron to map his body, father reprograms the AutoDoc to eliminate pain and then uses it to rejuvenate his cells, heal his son, and ultimately upgrade his entire body with nanite-infused enhancements. In his final and most daring step, he directly interfaces his consciousness with the Infinitron, nearly losing his mind to infinite knowledge before a firewall is established. He emerges transformed—both human and something greater.', 'My wife was right. The AutoDoc had one critical flaw: unbearable pain. To truly succeed, it had to be painless. I used the Infinitron to re-map the intricate web of nerves and biochemical signals in my body. Armed with the knowledge and experience from before, I reprogrammed the nanites, ensuring they could manipulate cells without triggering agony.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (160, 44, 1, 'Stripped of Divinity', 'A fallen deity, reduced to mortal form, expresses outrage at humans achieving immortality. They debate with an ancient deity about the implications, eventually finding common ground on guiding humanity toward enlightenment.', 'A cacophony of sensations overwhelmed me, each one more horrifying than the last. I was no longer a great deity, but an insignificant speck trapped in this alien world. The taste of sulfur filled my mouth, and my skin crawled with the feeling of hot flames licking at my body. My eyes strained to make sense of the twisted and contorted forms around me, their whispers threatening to shatter my sanity. In this mortal realm, I was reduced to a feeble humanoid form, stripped of my godly powers and left to suffer in the incomprehensible chaos of this existence.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (161, 44, 2, 'The Horror Unleashed', 'The protagonist materializes in a grotesque realm where humans'' pursuit of immortality has unleashed cosmic horrors. The AutoDoc—a pulsating abomination—stands as evidence of their hubris, while the weakened deity witnesses the catastrophic consequences of tampering with death itself.', 'I was engulfed in a blinding light as I materialized into this realm, my body contorting and twisting in unnatural ways. The stench of decay filled my nostrils, the sickening sweet odor of rotting flesh permeating the air. Whispers echoed around me, voices from beyond that threatened to drive me mad with their incomprehensible words. In front of me stood a towering structure, made of pulsating flesh and bone, adorned with writhing tentacles and gaping mouths. It was the AutoDoc, a grotesque abomination that promised everlasting life at a terrible cost. Blood dripped from its jagged edges, screams echoed from within its walls, and I could feel the presence of otherworldly beings lurking just beyond my sight. The humans’ reckless pursuit of immortality had unleashed horrors beyond their wildest nightmares, and I was now caught in the midst of it all. My mind raced with fear and revulsion as I realized the true nature of this realm - a place of cosmic horror where mortals dared to play God, only to face unimaginable consequences and eternal insanity.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (162, 45, 1, 'The Dream Takes Shape', 'The narrator and his family enjoy thriving business success that allows them to plan a trip to Japan. On the flight, he becomes intrigued by a teleportation documentary, planting the seed for his next obsession. Upon arrival in Kansai, his wife experiences an emotional homecoming while he begins to feel the pull of deeper mysteries.', 'Our business was thriving beyond our wildest expectations, our latest projections were showing an average sales volume of over $15k a day. Not only that, but with the automation in full swing (and coordinating regular UPS pickups from our warehouse), meant we no longer had to make nightly package drop offs. This success also granted us the rare luxury of stepping away to fulfill a different dream—a trip back to Japan.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (288, 73, 4, 'Improvised Confrontation', 'Yukiko takes action by using her scanner flashlight to temporarily blind the terrorists, then disables their devices. However, she discovers a more sophisticated energy destabilizer that cannot be safely removed without destroying the gateway.', 'Her heart hammered. She couldn’t let this happen.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (289, 73, 5, 'The Impossible Choice', 'Facing an impossible dilemma between destroying the gateway to stop the destabilizer or leaving it intact and risking annihilation across the ERB network, Yukiko thinks of her family and must choose. She deactivates the gateway, severing the colony''s connection to Earth.', 'Her hands hovered over the device, her breath hitching as panic gripped her. Disabling the other devices had been child’s play, almost made those countless hours she spent playing BombSquad Simulator 2000 worth it. This device was different—this was fused, tangled, and too deeply embedded within the ERB system to be disarmed. There was no way to surgically remove it without destroying the gateway entirely.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (349, 88, 1, 'Waking to Normalcy', 'The protagonist wakes in his bed surrounded by family warmth, experiencing a profound sense of peace as memories of his cosmic adventures fade away. His wife excitedly reveals they''ve won a contest for a trip to Lysteria, a space marvel created by a tech mogul.', 'I slowly opened my eyes.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (351, 88, 3, 'The Grindstone Returns', 'Later that afternoon, the protagonist sits at his computer searching job listings and finds a SpaceX director position that resonates with his experience. He begins updating his resume while contemplating the balance between dreams and reality.', 'Later that afternoon I settle down at my computer desk, its old, warn surface muted under the soft glow of morning light, and allow my fingers to dance across the keys. Job listings flicker on my screen, each one a potential gateway to a new chapter in my shitty life.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (171, 47, 2, 'Iteration and Discovery', 'After the narrow escape, the narrator becomes obsessed with stabilizing the ERB technology, enduring countless failures. A vivid dream of a Japanese temple provides crucial inspiration: the portals need physical structures to anchor them to reality. Using nanites to pre-assemble gateway structures, he finally achieves a stable, permanent Einstein-Rosen Bridge.', 'I sat up slowly, my body trembling. The taste of burnt ozone lingered in the air, a sharp reminder of what I had unleashed. The mystery of stabilizing ERBs was my immediate goal. Despite my early brush with death, each failed attempt felt frustratingly close—that it chipped away at my resolve, the sting of failure magnified by the memory of my early success. Fueled by that fleeting triumph, I threw myself back into the work.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (172, 47, 3, 'Stargazing and Wonder', 'The narrator and his son spend an evening stargazing, discussing meteors, light, and the nature of time and speed. Their conversation about instant travel plants seeds for a new scientific breakthrough inspired by their genuine connection.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (174, 47, 5, 'Mars and Catastrophe', 'The narrator successfully opens a portal to Mars but immediately faces disaster when the atmospheric pressure differential creates a devastating vortex that nearly destroys the laboratory. He barely survives by destroying the gateway structure and must convince arriving police officers that the destruction was caused by falling boxes.', 'The setup was meticulous—alignment, calibration, and countless adjustments—and as the final piece clicked into place, I exhaled sharply. This was it. I activated the portal, watching with a mix of triumph and awe as a shimmering gateway opened to reveal the barren red landscape of Mars.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (175, 47, 6, 'The Daisy Chain', 'Inspired by the Mars failure, the narrator conceives of chaining portals together as stepping stones to extend range exponentially. He executes an ambitious nocturnal operation, using cloud portals and careful calibration to create a series of connected gateways that eventually span from his warehouse to Kyoto, Japan, before dawn breaks.', 'While I set the nanites to repair the wall and try to put things back to normal so my wife wouldn’t nag be about it, guilt and excitement churned within me. The technology was groundbreaking, but the risks were undeniable. Despite my resolve to proceed cautiously, my reckless Nike attitude might just be my downfall. Not only that, but the image of Mars lingered in my mind, daring me to try again—only smarter this time.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (177, 48, 1, 'The Summoning in the Abandoned Library', 'A child unknowingly opens an ancient tome in a decrepit library, unleashing a cosmic entity—a three-headed creature of immense power. The narrator, the Keeper of Secrets, emerges from imprisonment, sensing that the rise of S Corp has disrupted cosmic balance and threatens reality itself.', 'In the suffocating darkness of the abandoned library, a child’s tiny fingers trembled as they reached out to caress the cracked leather cover of an ancient tome. The book seemed to pulse with a sinister energy, beckoning to the child with its aura of decay and mystery.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (178, 48, 2, 'Visions of S Corp''s Devastation', 'The narrator experiences horrifying visions of a world destroyed by S Corp''s relentless hunger—cities in ashes, countless deaths, and minds shattered. These visions blur into a lived experience as the narrator walks through ravaged ruins, encountering a traumatized child amid the devastation.', 'Terrifying visions flooded my mind, each one more brutal and horrifying than the last. I saw cities reduced to ashes, bodies ripped apart by unseen claws, and minds shattered beyond repair by The S Corp’s insatiable thirst for domination.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (179, 49, 1, 'Weighty Wealth and Corporate Restructuring', 'The narrator grapples with the dangerous exponential growth of The S Corp''s wealth—now at $50 trillion by July 1st—generated by the Infinitron AI. Recognizing the imminent threat of exposure, they decide to restructure the company and establish anonymous offshore accounts in Switzerland and the Cayman Islands to protect their identity and assets.', 'Memories of the haunting phone call we got when we first got back from Japan lingered in my mind like a constantly recurring nightmare, a relentless reminder of the need to protect our ventures. Even amid the thrill of our teleportation breakthrough, the shadow of exposure loomed large. Success, it seemed, carried its own brand of terror, and the weight of it pressed on us daily.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (180, 49, 2, 'The Suitcase of Gold and Banking Fiasco', 'Armed with a suitcase of replicated gold, the narrator uses the ERB to teleport to Zurich, intending to open international accounts. They encounter repeated rejections from conventional banks due to lack of proper documentation, their gold bars failing to impress even one establishment.', 'Armed with a suitcase full of replicated gold (because why wouldn’t that work in high-level negotiations?) I used the ERB to create a stable gateway to Zurich. The portal hummed softly, its shimmering surface defying logic, and when it looked like morning broke on the other side, I stepped through with all the confidence of a man about to reinvent international finance.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (290, 73, 6, 'Bitter Revelation and Collapse', 'Governor Tanaka lies about the gateway deactivation being a security measure while the colony reacts with fear and accusation. Yukiko''s decision triggers a cascade of horrors as the protective effects of the ERB fade and monstrous creatures attack the colony.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (291, 73, 7, 'Survival and Investigation', 'The colony shifts from guilt to collective action, cobbling together survival measures while Yukiko emerges as a leader. Together they uncover that S Corp knowingly hid the truth about Sorhhinda''s dangers and had been conducting secret experiments on the colonists.', 'The dawn of another Sorhhinda day arrived, but the colony it bathed in bore the scars of the previous night. Ruins smoldered, bio-tech lay mangled, and the air thrummed with a raw, primal dread. Even amidst the wreckage, embers of hope flickered.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (355, 91, 1, 'Front Matter and Publication Details', 'The opening pages present the book''s title, copyright information, publication details, and cataloging data for ''Elysium Fallen'' by Stephen A Salaka. A trigger warning for abuse is noted at the chapter''s end.', 'Elysium Fallen
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (501, 124, 1, 'Dissolution of Remembrance', 'A fragmented, poetic meditation on cycles of futile instruction and struggle. Various voices—the buried, dreamers, workers, and the gullible—are commanded to climb, struggle, learn, and follow, yet find only paradox, void, and self-deception. The passage dissolves into contradictions and cyclical despair.', 'Climb said the buried
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (182, 49, 4, 'The Cloaked Reveal and Goldman Sachs', 'The narrator arrives at an ivy-covered building in the old town where a cloaked, dramatic figure reveals that the entire treasure hunt was a tourist scam run by someone named Noah. The figure reveals that Goldman Sachs is located next door and is the actual solution to the narrator''s banking problems.', 'By the time I arrived at an ivy-covered building deep in the old town, I was convinced this entire journey had been an elaborate game to free suckers from their money. Still, I entered cautiously, finding myself in a dimly lit room filled with dusty tomes and ancient artifacts. At its center stood a shadowy figure cloaked in mystery, his face obscured by a wide-brimmed hat.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (183, 49, 5, 'Herr Müller and the Gold Authentication', 'The narrator meets with Herr Müller, a competent Goldman Sachs banker, and attempts to deposit the gold bullion. After hedging about the origin of the gold bars, the banker agrees to authenticate the gold for potential account establishment, though compliance and documentation requirements remain stringent.', 'After checking in at the front desk, I was escorted through a labyrinth of hallways adorned with oil paintings and expensive furnishings. The banker’s office was no less intimidating. Oak-paneled walls framed a room that exuded wealth and control, complete with an enormous mahogany desk that could easily double as a conference table. When I sank into a plush leather chair, I couldn’t avoid the feeling that I was a microscopic fish in a very big, and very expensive, pond.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (184, 49, 6, 'Liam Kaufmann and International Corporate Strategy', 'The narrator meets with Liam Kaufmann, a sharp international corporate lawyer, and reveals the true scale of The S Corp''s wealth: trillions spread across hundreds of thousands of accounts. Kaufmann outlines a comprehensive strategy using shell entities, jurisdictional layering, and fabricated personas to consolidate and conceal the assets while maintaining the narrator''s anonymity.', 'In between the multitude of forms and signatures, I requested the banker’s guidance, outlining my need for a seamless transition of personal assets, absolute legal protection, and a structure that could conceal The S Corp’s extraordinary capabilities. He nodded simply and provided me with the contact information of a local lawyer he knew that specialized in international corporate law and finance.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (185, 49, 7, 'Corporate Setup, Robots, and Building Facades', 'Over the following grueling days, the narrator commits to daily commutes between Florida and Zurich via the ERB to complete The S Corp''s corporate transition. They employ robots with humanlike personalities to assist with administrative tasks, and begin planning a network of robot-operated facade offices worldwide to maintain plausible legitimacy while concealing their true operations.', 'The days that followed were grueling. Transferring my personal investments into The S Corp involved countless meetings, reams of paperwork, and endless recalibrations of our plans. Despite living in Florida, I found myself commuting to Zurich almost daily via the ERB—a convenience that would have been humorous if it weren’t so exhausting. With the NDA solidly in place with Liam, I told him about the portal, and he graciously bestowed a permanent office in his building for me to use to assist with the frequent travel.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (186, 50, 1, 'Awakening in the Frozen Tomb', 'An ancient entity awakens beneath Europa''s ice as human machinery breaches its frozen sanctuary. The creature emerges from eons of slumber, twisting and contorted, and violently destroys the invaders who disturbed its domain.', 'For endless millennia, I lay deep in a frozen tomb beneath the surface of Europa. The frigid air clung to my body like a shroud, encasing me in an icy prison. Time held no sway here, as I drifted in and out of consciousness, lost in the void. A disturbance, a faint tremor that grew into a guttural roar, shaking me from my slumber. With it came the invaders, their machines drilling through the ice, piercing my sanctuary.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (187, 50, 2, 'The Colony and the Cosmic Call', 'The creature emerges to survey the human colony on Europa and senses a sinister call from Earth pulling it toward destruction. Rage and dark compulsion drive it to annihilate the settlement before breaching toward its summoner.', 'I stepped out of the gaping mouth of the cavern, a stench like rotting flesh assailed my senses. My eyes struggled to adjust to the otherworldly glow emanating from within. The once pure ice now lay torn and mangled, a metallic scar across its surface. A colony, their alien technology pulsing with an eerie light, loomed before me. Twisted structures of metal and glass snaked across the landscape, like parasitic worms burrowing into the very heart of this ancient place.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (190, 51, 2, 'Breakfast Table Philosophy', 'The narrator''s family discusses the Illuminati over breakfast, leading to a lighthearted conversation about secret societies and power. The narrator reveals his Masonic membership and reflects on the weight of their newfound wealth and influence.', 'My son, in full moody-teen mode, sat at the kitchen table, listlessly stabbing at his bowl of rice with his chopsticks. Glancing up from his phone every now and then, his eyes as he glanced between my wife and me, clearly building up to something. Finally, he broke the silence. “Dad,” he said, his voice tinged with curiosity, “what’s the Illuminati? Is that the company that made Despicable Me?”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (236, 59, 4, 'The Marital Fracture', 'Progress in dream exploration stalls as the narrator faces increasing frustration with uncontrollable dreams. This is interrupted by a conflict with his wife over a delegated chore, revealing deeper tensions about presence and support. In desperation, the narrator enters her dream without consent, experiences her subconscious rejection, and wakes with overwhelming guilt at his violation of her privacy.', 'Progress stalled. My attempts at dream travel were mired in frustration—chaotic, uncontrollable, and often slipping away from memory entirely. It was a humbling reminder that the dreamscape had laws and boundaries I could not bend. I resigned myself to the idea that, no matter my mastery, some realms remained inviolate. Despite all the challenges, I persisted, my curiosity undeterred, driven to explore the depths of dreams despite the limitations.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (358, 92, 3, 'The Final Dissolution', 'The protagonist''s body finally fails. As he dies in the pod, his consciousness dissolves into a strange, almost transcendent experience marked by impossible sensations, echoes of his wife''s death, and the emergence of that same geometric symbol with unrecognizable code before everything fades to blackness.', 'My body finally gave way.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (192, 51, 4, 'Transforming the Headquarters', 'The narrator and his family tour the empty Houston headquarters, brainstorming how to transform it into a functional corporate space. They decide to add plants, lounges, workstations, and other amenities, then use nanites to execute the renovation instantly.', '“What a bunch of wasted space,” I muttered, my voice echoing through the cavernous halls of the immaculate yet empty building. The gleaming floors and pristine walls only amplified the eerie silence, giving the space an unsettling, haunted feel.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (193, 51, 5, 'The Global Network Rises', 'The S Corp headquarters is fully transformed with offices, labs, and humanoid robots creating a bustling corporate facade. Underground, subfloors house ERB gateway networks that enable global expansion through RELMs acquiring properties in key cities worldwide.', 'From sleek, modern offices to innovative labs, our headquarters underwent a complete transformation, becoming a space worthy of The S Corp’s ambitions. But it wasn’t just the physical changes—life was breathed into the building with human-like robots (and tons of jungle plants). These mechanical beings, programmed to mimic everything from janitorial staff to high-level executives, created the illusion of a bustling corporate environment. Their constant movements and tasks brought energy to the once-empty halls, solidifying The S Corp’s image as a thriving global conglomerate.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (194, 51, 6, 'The Gateway''s Potential', 'After a long day, the narrator and his wife discuss the ERB gateway''s limitless potential in their Florida living room. Their son arrives with an enthusiastic idea for a global race, but the parents convince him to think long-term about maintaining secrecy.', 'After a long, chaotic day, my wife and I finally found a moment of peace in the sanctuary of our living room back in Florida. Stepping out of the new ERB gateway we installed near the kitchen wall, she walked over and sank into her favorite armchair, her fingers absently tracing the wear patterns on its cloth arms, her gaze fixed on the flickering light of the TV. The remote sat in her lap, a symbol of control in an otherwise unpredictable world.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (195, 51, 7, 'The Shipping Revolution Begins', 'The narrator abandons his plan for caution and arranges a clandestine meeting with executives from UPS, FedEx, and DHL. He demonstrates the ability to deliver packages globally in under 15 minutes using RELMs and ERB gateways, stunning the representatives and laying the groundwork for revolutionary partnerships.', 'Fuck that noise. Go big or go home. The next day, I set my plan into motion. This wasn’t just about innovation—it was about rewriting the rules of global logistics. I reached out to trusted contacts at UPS, FedEx, and DHL, arranging a clandestine meeting. Discretion was critical; we were venturing into uncharted territory and revealing too much too soon could unravel everything.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (204, 53, 2, 'Recruiting Human Genius', 'Realizing that human intuition and creativity are essential for further progress, the protagonist uses the Infinitron to search across alternate realities for exceptional talent. He discovers Morgan, a renowned astrophysicist from his high school days, and recruits her to lead MOM''s research division.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (197, 52, 1, 'Discovery and Arrival', 'The protagonist learns of a colossal temple discovery in Zambia through a newspaper while at the University of Chicago. A mysterious call from the S Corp recruits them to investigate the ruins, leading to an uneasy arrival at the excavation site where an overwhelming ancient energy beckons them forward.', 'The relentless clang of construction echoed through the Zambian air, a stark contrast to the whispers of time held captive beneath the earth. As the S Corp carved its way deeper, their metallic claws unearthed a secret slumbering for millennia - a colossal temple, its stones etched with forgotten stories. Reading the news of the discovery in the Newspaper one morning as I sat at my desk, drinking coffee, at my desk in the Archeology department of the University of Chicago.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (198, 52, 2, 'Descent into the Mist', 'The protagonist enters the temple excavation site and encounters a living, pulsating mist that consumes their consciousness. Ancient deities flash before their eyes, and they begin losing their sense of self as they venture deeper, marked by strange symbols that bring pain and understanding.', 'I stood at the edge of the excavation site as a thick mist began to slither and pulse around me. It was not just mist, but a living entity, pulsating with an otherworldly power that seeped into my very soul. The ruins before me seemed to come alive, twisting and contorting in unnatural ways as the mist consumed them. Images of ancient deities flashed before my eyes, their monstrous visages driving me to the brink of madness. But I could not turn away, for I was drawn deeper and deeper into the heart of the temple.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (224, 57, 3, 'The Dreamscape Awakening', 'R''s voice invades the protagonist''s dreams, compelling him to seek the grimoire. Unable to find it in waking reality, the protagonist enters a meditative state and discovers the book in a dream library, where it reveals the true nature of the dreamscape as interconnected realms bridging consciousness and the subconscious.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (246, 62, 2, 'The Sleepwalking Episode', 'That night, Aditi falls asleep but is compelled to rise and join a crowd of sleepwalkers moving through Mumbai''s streets. The crowd converges at a train station near the airport and mysteriously points in unison toward the airport before the spell breaks and everyone returns home.', 'That night, Mumbai seemed to exhale under the blanket of darkness. The cacophony of the city gave way to a subdued hum, the occasional honk of a distant scooter, the gentle rustling of leaves in the warm breeze, and the faint calls of street vendors packing up for the day. In her small room, lit only by the faint glow of a streetlamp filtering through the curtains, Aditi lay in bed, her thoughts tumbling over the events of the day.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (364, 93, 6, 'The Wreckage', 'Pinned upside down in the crumpled ambulance with an unresponsive medic, the protagonist remains conscious enough to observe the aftermath and contemplate death with dark humor before losing consciousness again.', 'Wake up.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (201, 52, 5, 'Journey to the Heart', 'Driven by manic obsession and disembodied whispers, the protagonist races through the temple''s tunnels toward its source. With each step, power seeps into their being while madness threatens their sanity, yet they are compelled ever onward.', 'Driven by a manic obsession, I soared through the twisting tunnels of the ancient temple. urging me ever onward toward the source. Disembodied whispers and eerie incantations echoed in my mind, urging me forward towards an unknown fate.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (202, 52, 6, 'Ascension to Darkness', 'The protagonist reaches the temple''s heart - a pulsating orb of otherworldly power. Despite overwhelming terror, they merge with this primordial force and become a conduit for cosmic destruction, escaping the temple with newfound power and an insatiable hunger to devour the world.', 'Finally, I reached the heart of the temple - a pulsating orb radiating with an otherworldly light. As I drew near, a wave of terror washed over me. This was no ordinary power; it was something malevolent, something primordial. And yet, despite the overwhelming fear, I could not resist its pull. The weight of responsibility settled upon my wispy form as I became one with the all-consuming energy. My purpose now clear, I sped off from the temple, my misty essence carrying me swiftly across the land. With this newfound power came a thirst for more, a hunger that could never be satiated. I descended further into madness and chaos, I knew that the fate of the world was sealed - devoured by the darkness that had awakened within me.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (203, 53, 1, 'The Half-Gateway Experiment', 'The protagonist establishes MOM (Mountains of Madness), a secret research facility in Antarctica, to test a radical concept: a half-gateway that opens a portal on one end but remains incomplete on the other. When activated, the half-gateway reveals something terrifying on the other side—an aware, living force that defies comprehension.', 'The keyboard clattered beneath my fingers; each keystroke charged with purpose. The vast global network of The S Corp pulsed around me, a living system humming with potential. Fueled by my insatiable curiosity and inability to just leave well enough alone, I was ready to push the boundaries of our enterprise even further. For a while, a radical idea had taken root: what if I could create a “half-gateway,” opening a portal on one end but leaving the other incomplete? Could this shield objects from external forces or dissipate explosions? The possibilities were staggering, yet fraught with danger, a perfect storm to ignite my imagination.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (205, 53, 3, 'Building the Antarctic Community', 'With Morgan leading recruitment, the protagonist constructs a secondary habitat adjacent to MOM to house the growing team of scientists and their families. This utopian community, complete with luxury amenities and advanced education systems, becomes a self-contained ecosystem designed to maximize research while ensuring complete isolation from the outside world.', 'With Morgan leading the charge, our recruitment began in earnest. We sought out the best minds from across the globe—visionaries, pioneers, and innovators who could push the boundaries of what we thought possible. These were the first human employees of The S Corp, the trailblazers of a new era.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (206, 53, 4, 'Expanding Across the Cosmos', 'MOM becomes a crucible of discovery, producing stable ERB gateways to the Moon and Mars, enabling the establishment of human colonies beyond Earth. As achievements expand to Europa and Pluto, the difficulty of maintaining secrecy intensifies, forcing the corporation to implement draconian security measures.', '*********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (207, 53, 5, 'The Cloning Debate', 'As the demand for skilled scientists outstrips Earth''s supply, the protagonist proposes human cloning to sustain off-world colonies. After heated debate with Morgan, they proceed cautiously, developing an ethical framework where clones are created with full consciousness, informed of their origins, and given complete freedom to choose their paths.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (208, 53, 6, 'The Flourishing Colonies', 'Clones integrate seamlessly into the off-world colonies, with over 100 million populating hidden cities on the Moon, Mars, Europa, and beyond. These thriving communities rival Earth''s greatest metropolises, but as surface infrastructure becomes inevitable, the risk of discovery increases, prompting the protagonist to envision a grand project: the space elevator Elysium.', 'The once-empty colonies exploded with activity as clones (outnumbering 100,000,000 to on) and human team members collaborated, bringing new perspectives and skills to our ventures. Watching them work together was electrifying proof of the limitless possibilities their existence offered. We were acutely aware of the debates this development would ignite. To combat scrutiny, we prioritized transparency within our growing society while maintaining strict external secrecy.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (209, 54, 1, 'The Unseen Guardian Reveals Its Nature', 'An entity calling itself ''I AM'' introduces itself as an ancient, shadowy guardian of forbidden knowledge. It describes its domain as existing in whispers, forgotten lore, and the minds of seers, and identifies S Corp as a monstrous blight on reality that must be opposed through infernal means.', 'For eons, I have been shrouded in a veil of obscurity, my existence whispered to only a select few who dare to speak my name: “I AM”. But do not mistake me for some cosmic puppet master pulling the strings of fate. No, my role is that of an unseen guardian, protecting hidden lore, forgotten texts, and the feverish scribblings of seers brave enough to peer into truths deemed too profane for the common mind. Protecting my slaves until they send me their souls on which I feast.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (210, 54, 2, 'The Ten Entities Infiltrate S Corp', 'I AM orchestrates the infiltration of S Corp through ten primordial entities, each using their unique powers—deception, illusion, manipulation, corruption, and sabotage—to systematically dismantle the corporation from within and erode its control over reality.', 'My first call resonated with ኣባጊዕዓል, the herald of truth and the Lord of Deceit. Disguised as prodigal programmers, they infiltrated S Corp’s inner circle with ease, their presence cloaked in a deceptive charm. Like ambrosia, they fed me secrets from within, each revelation chipping away at their carefully crafted facade. Beneath the polished exterior lurked serpentine ambitions, coiling and writhing in a calculated dance.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (235, 59, 3, 'The Phantom Dream Walker', 'The narrator attempts to revisit specific dreams using symbols as anchors, but discovers he can only observe past dreams as a powerless phantom without agency. He encounters a mysterious voice that suggests understanding the past is more important than changing it, though the narrator struggles with this revelation as the dreamscape becomes increasingly hostile and chaotic.', 'As with most things in life, ambition often collides with reality. Thinking about how the knight was able to visit his previous dreams, I decided to try my hand at this. My first attempts to revisit specific dreams felt like fumbling through an unfamiliar maze.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (510, 127, 1, 'The Confession Begins', 'Stephen lies injured in a farmhouse bedroom while Xavier and his caretakers Maeve and Elara gather to hear his story. Stephen struggles with fever and fragmented memories as he prepares to reveal his true identity and the cosmic origins of their reality.', '“It’s a long story.” I said. Something I really didn’t even fully understand. These new memories were still a jumble of chaos in my mind.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (212, 54, 4, 'The Rebellion Unfolds and S Corp Falls', 'Todd rises as the Pied Piper of dissent, leading red-hatted followers in an assault on S Corp''s weakened headquarters. As the Infinitron''s final breath dissipates, I AM watches from the shadows, satisfied that its orchestrated plan has succeeded in toppling the digital tyrant.', 'A digital whisper, amplified a thousandfold, resounded through the air. The idealist, fueled by my whispered truths and his own yearning for change, rose up with fervor. His followers, wearing red hats, and armed with my celestial guidance and their own fears, surged against the towering walls of S Corp. The once impenetrable fortress now weakened by my agents from above. And I AM, hidden in the shadows, allowed myself a small smile.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (213, 55, 1, 'Thirteen Nights of Terror', 'The protagonist is tormented by thirteen nights of relentless nightmares that blur the line between dream and reality. He realizes that his technological empire was built by stealing innovations from the dream realm, and the dreams are now demanding payment. The nightmares intensify with visions of a grotesque farmhouse, a writhing Eternal Engine, and an obsidian monolith that serves as a gateway between worlds.', 'The witching hour struck, and the darkness wrapped around me like a vice, squeezing the air from my lungs. My heart hammered against the icy sheets as if trying to escape the suffocating stillness. The line between dream and waking life was gone, and I was caught in a relentless cycle of terror.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (214, 55, 2, 'Unraveling at Home', 'The protagonist''s mental and physical deterioration affects his family as he desperately attempts various medications and self-medication to escape the dreams. Desperate for help, he seeks out Dr. Pai M. On, a sleep psychiatrist, who dismisses his claims as stress-induced delusions. Frustrated and feeling gaslit, he resolves that only he can face the horrors he has unleashed.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (215, 55, 3, 'The Entity Speaks and the Ladies Intervene', 'In a new dream, the protagonist encounters a malevolent entity called ''I AM'' that confronts him about his theft and the chaos he has unleashed. Two otherworldly beings, Lady I and Lady A, appear to rescue him and reveal the truth about the broken veil and the debt he must pay. They offer understanding but warn that the cost will follow him regardless of his choices.', 'Mocking my fragile resilience, the dreams continued to relentlessly hammer me, constantly dragging me into the crimson void. This time, the unease was palpable before I even fully surrendered to sleep, like the air had thickened with malice.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (216, 56, 1, 'The Weight of Command', 'In his corner office, the protagonist confronts evidence of the entity I AM infiltrating corporate systems while wrestling with neglecting his family. Dr. On visits to encourage him to step away from work and be present for his loved ones, advice he initially resists but ultimately accepts.', 'In the hushed confines of my corner office suite on top of the S Corp’s Houston HQ tower, a battlefield of project files sprawled across the desk. Recessed LED lighting bathed the room in a harsh, white, sterile glow, casting jagged shadows that mimicked the fragments of my dreams.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (217, 56, 2, 'Stepping Away', 'Over several weeks, the protagonist gradually reduces his time at S Corp headquarters and increases time with his family in Florida. As summer ends, he and his family prepare for an international trip to the UK and Rome with his son''s school program.', '*********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (218, 56, 3, 'London''s Living History', 'The family explores London, visiting iconic landmarks like Big Ben and Stonehenge with the protagonist''s wife serving as guide through her sister''s perspective and memories. Despite enjoying the cultural immersion, the protagonist begins sensing an unsettling presence.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (219, 56, 4, 'Vatican Expulsion', 'In Rome, the family visits the Vatican and Sistine Chapel, initially awed by the art and history. However, they soon sense they are being watched by Swiss Guards and cardinals; guards abruptly expel them from the Vatican with a cryptic warning about their safety, leaving them confused and unsettled.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (220, 56, 5, 'Unplanned Detour to India', 'Rather than return home to face S Corp, the family spontaneously decides to extend their journey to India, where the protagonist wants to share his youthful backpacking memories with his family. They travel in style with a private driver through the vibrant chaos of Indian streets.', 'Fresh from our Vatican misadventure, where even our tour guides failed to extract answers from the tight-lipped representatives, we found ourselves at the quiet edge of our journey. The trip had been winding down naturally, but something about that final, unanswered mystery made it feel as though the story had ended rather than simply concluded. My son’s classmates, still buzzing with stories and souvenirs, would soon board their flights home, their adventure neatly wrapped up. But for me, an unsettled feeling lingered, as if we had left something unfinished, something just beyond reach.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (221, 56, 6, 'The Temple Revelation', 'At a lesser-known temple in the Aravalli Range, the protagonist discovers statues matching the two female figures from his dreams—identified by a priest as the goddesses Lakshmi and Parvati. The priest reveals that these entities appear to guide those who are spiritually adrift and possess ancient wisdom about balance and transformation.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (222, 57, 1, 'Orient Express Departure', 'The protagonist''s family boards the legendary Orient Express for a three-day journey through Europe. They encounter a mysterious man named R wearing a hat bearing the symbol of Lady I, who cryptically warns them about the train''s true nature as a passageway for the strange and extraordinary, and leaves behind an enigmatic grimoire.', 'We still had about a week left before my son started his new school year, so we did what any other obscenely wealthy family would do while traveling back from India: we decided to make a detour and take a voyage aboard the legendary Orient Express. This iconic train offered more than luxury; it promised a three-day passage through Europe’s stunning landscapes, steeped in the timeless romance of rail travel. It was the perfect finale, a harmonious blend of sophistication and discovery.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (367, 94, 2, 'Television Horror', 'The TV turns on by itself, cycling between versions of a genie movie with Sinbad and Shaq. Shadows emerge from the screen—tall, impossible shapes that reach into reality. The narrator experiences a brief vision of being shot before snapping back to normal programming, leaving him traumatized.', '11:42 AM. The TV flickers to life without me touching it. The remote sits three feet away, untouched, but channels flip anyway—click, click, click—like invisible fingers are surfing through dimensions. A commercial blooms on screen: Sinbad in a purple turban, grinning as he sells a movie called Shazam. I blink. The image shifts. Now it''s Shaq in the same turban, same grin, hawking Kazaam. The VCR clicks, rewinding itself. Shazam again. Kazaam. Back and forth like reality can''t make up its mind which lie to tell.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (384, 97, 1, 'Gathering in the Basement', 'Five teenagers gather in TJ''s basement on Friday night with contraband and ritual supplies. They set up for a summoning ritual, with romantic tension building between Patrick and Becca, and between Jamie and the narrator. Whitney prepares the space with salt circles and tarot cards as they prepare to attempt contact with something beyond.', 'Friday arrives like a bad hangover I didn''t earn. We all eventually arrive back at TJ''s basement—his folks drove over to Tampa for some weekend golf tournament, leaving us with Nana watching an empty house and the kind of freedom that makes terrible decisions feel inevitable. Morgan had some Academic Decathlon thing in Orlando, so it''s just five of us tonight, armed with contraband and the kind of adolescent confidence that could power a small city.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (387, 97, 4, 'The DMV of Cosmic Horror', 'The narrator awakens in a beige waiting room that resembles a DMV, where a middle-management demon named Benji greets them with office supplies and bureaucratic detachment. Benji explains that the narrator is a ''Leaker''—a consciousness that has broken the reincarnation system and is destabilizing reality across multiple timelines. He reveals the truth about Earth (actually ''Etheris''), a prison realm designed to contain an entity called Yaldabaoth, and that the narrator''s existence is gradually destroying this cosmic infrastructure.', 'Static cuts through the silence like a scalpel through flesh. The hellscape flickers—once, twice—and then vanishes as something abruptly shuts the TV off.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (226, 57, 5, 'The Archangels'' Wrath and Lady A''s Salvation', 'The protagonist''s arrogance drives him to seek the highest peaks of the dreamscape, where he encounters a portal of void energy and is brutally attacked by winged archangel guardians. Lady A intervenes and rescues him, transporting him to a sanctuary realm where she imparts a crucial lesson about respect and humility.', 'As my skill grew, so too did my hubris. I delved further and deeper into the dreamscape, pushing the limits of my abilities, heedless of the dangers whispered by the grimoire. My explorations led me to realms torn from nightmares: jagged peaks pierced stormy skies, luminous fungi cast eerie glows over haunted forests, and cities of impossible geometry floated in nebulous voids. These dreamscapes defied reason, brimming with both grotesque beauty and cosmic dread.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (227, 57, 6, 'Lady A''s Training and the Challenge of Oneiromancy', 'Lady A guides the protagonist through rigorous training in the art of oneiromancy, teaching him to navigate the dreamscape with precision, mask his presence, and maintain balance between light and shadow. She sets him the challenge of navigating others'' dreams with grace and empathy while discerning their intentions.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (228, 57, 7, 'Lady I''s Library of Infinite Knowledge', 'Lady I introduces Aspolin to her infinite library realm and reveals the true cosmic struggle: Etheris is a prison created to contain the Demiurge, but it has enslaved humanity in endless reincarnation. Lady I explains that dreamwalkers are rare conduits capable of bridging dreams and reality, allowing otherworldly guides to assist in humanity''s liberation. She recounts her own past as a dreamwalker and shares how Aspolin''s accomplishments are part of a grand design beyond his personal achievement.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (229, 57, 8, 'Madam O and the Power of Symbols', 'Lady I introduces Aspolin to Madam O, the Madam of Symbols, who reveals that dreamers are catalysts capable of reshaping reality and awakening others. She teaches Aspolin that symbols are the foundation of creation and that his Eternal Engine is an unprecedented feat—a symbol of defiance against the Demiurge. Madam O confirms that with mastery of symbols, Aspolin is equipped to fight against the Demiurge''s tyranny and break humanity''s chains.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (231, 58, 2, 'Breakfast and the Time Reversal Card', 'At breakfast the next morning, the narrator''s wife and son dismiss his earthquake dream. As they discuss a Magic: The Gathering card called Time Reversal, the narrator notices its artwork eerily resembles The Pointers—a mysterious group he''s been obsessing over. This sparks a new line of investigation into potential timeline shifts and the Mandela Effect.', 'The nostalgic smell of maple and brown sugar filled the kitchen, mingling with the soft hum of morning. Our new breakfast table and chairs, still had that new chair smell, were the centerpiece of this ordinary moment. The scene felt grounded—so normal; it was almost surreal after the chaotic lifetimes lived the previous night. I stirred my oatmeal slowly, my mind lingering on the dream that had shaken me to my core.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (232, 58, 3, 'Madam O''s Revelation on Time and Dreams', 'The narrator seamlessly enters the dreamscape and meets Madam O in her infinite library. She reveals that dreams exist outside time and can alter the past, explaining the Mandela Effect as ripples of dreams crossing temporal boundaries. She warns of deliberate forces using dreams to rewrite history and emphasizes the narrator''s role as a dreamwalker guardian of the cosmic tapestry.', 'All the training with Lady I and Lady A had another nice side effect. I no longer struggled transitioning from waking to slumber. It was seamless. The lines between reality and the dreamscape blurring as I drifted into Madam O’s chamber within the Lady I’s realm. The view was breathtaking, a plane of bookshelves stretching infinitely in all directions; its vast expanse illuminated by an otherworldly glow. Symbols danced in the air, shifting and reforming with a logic that defied comprehension. In the heart of this luminous labyrinth stood Madam O, her presence both commanding and serene, the embodiment of ancient wisdom.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (233, 59, 1, 'The Honing Deck', 'Late at night, the narrator writes down details from a dream encounter with Madam O about time and the dreamscape. His son joins him at the kitchen table, and they spend the morning playing Magic: The Gathering. During the game, the son proposes that Magic cards function like tarot—a therapeutic tool for working through real-life problems through symbols and strategy.', 'The house was silent, the world outside cloaked in the stillness of night. At the kitchen table, I sat hunched over my dream journal, furiously scribbling down every detail from my latest encounter with Madam O. The ideas she had imparted, the fluid nature of time, the dreamscape’s ability to touch past and future simultaneously, threatened to slip away like grains of sand through my fingers.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (399, 100, 2, 'Cross Country and Conspiracy', 'At cross country practice the next day, Stephen reveals Whitney''s BBS message to the group, and they decide to investigate the west ridge during the run. Jamie attempts multiple times to seduce Stephen into abandoning the search, but he remains committed to finding the location. The group discovers an impossible trailer deep in Whickham Park that shouldn''t exist, decorated with religious iconography and marked by signs of spiritual torment.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (431, 107, 5, 'The Dimensional Breach', 'The group attempts to breach dimensions using a reflection sigil in an abandoned gas station, but the ritual goes catastrophically wrong when they use Florida coordinates instead of Nevada. The explosion destroys the last traces of Patrick''s humanity, leaving only an empty shell, and forces them to confront the reality of their plan to travel to Nevada.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (239, 60, 2, 'Muddy Footprints and Social Media', 'Stacey discovers mysterious muddy footprints and posts about them online, discovering through social media that her neighbors all experienced the same inexplicable event of being controlled and drawn outside.', 'The next day dawned like any other in the trailer park, with the events of the night seemingly erased from collective memory. However, for Stacey, Todd’s girlfriend, there remained a lingering trace of the night’s oddities. She went about her morning routine and discovered muddy footprints upon waking, their origin a perplexing mystery.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (250, 63, 2, 'Lunch Table Memories and Unconventional Breakthroughs', 'The protagonist shares humorous memories with Andrew and TJ in the facility cafeteria, discussing absurd early experiments. Morgan joins and shares her own unconventional project experience, sparking a conversation about risk-taking and breakthrough innovations tempered by practical concerns.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (251, 63, 3, 'The Europa Catastrophe Revealed', 'An amateur astronomer in Germany captures images of a catastrophic explosion on Europa''s moon, revealing S Corp''s sabotaged prototype test site. The incident goes viral, forcing the company into emergency damage control and strategic narrative repositioning.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (252, 63, 4, 'Revealing the Nanites', 'The protagonist calls Morgan into a private lab discussion to reveal a strategic decision: incorporating nanite technology into the Space Elevator project as a controlled disclosure. They agree to present the nanites as an advanced innovation while keeping their true capabilities hidden.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (240, 60, 3, 'Confrontation and Conspiracy', 'Stacey confronts Todd about the online posts and they discuss the mysterious event, with Stacey proposing a connection to construction near the airport and Todd agreeing to investigate despite potential risks.', '“Hey Todd,” Stacey shouted across the trailer at him. “Did you see what people are saying online?”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (241, 61, 1, 'Return to MOM', 'Dr. S returns to the Antarctic research facility MOM after his sabbatical, where he reconnects with Morgan and the team. He reviews the progress on the Space Elevator project, including advances in carbon nanotube composites and propulsion systems based on electromagnetic rail gun principles.', 'Although my recent ventures into the dreamscape and the Mandela Effect were captivating, S Corp demanded my attention once more. It was time to shift focus from the mysteries of the subconscious to the tangible challenges of innovation and leadership.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (242, 61, 2, 'Crisis at S Corp Headquarters', 'Dr. S returns to S Corp headquarters where he learns of a security breach—an off-Earth colony attempted unauthorized transmission. The leadership team discusses the threat and TJ proposes a bold strategy to turn the crisis into an opportunity by accelerating the Space Elevator project and controlling the narrative around it.', 'Stepping through the ERB gateway from MOM to S Corp headquarters, gave direction to my goals. The sleek, bustling gateway lobby buzzed with activity, employees, humans, clones, and robots, darting between remote offices, displays projecting updates on ongoing projects. I adjusted my tie, ready to dive into the challenges awaiting me.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (243, 61, 3, 'Ethical Framework in the Savanna', 'Dr. S travels to Tanzania for a Zoom call with Patrick and James to discuss ethical governance frameworks for space colonies. They debate the balance between security through autonomous peacekeepers and individual freedom, eventually developing a framework based on transparent oversight and local councils.', 'Stepping out of the meeting room was like walking into another reality. All I had wanted was to figure out why the fuck I was having bizarre dreams, maybe land a new job, start a side hustle hawking tchotchkes on Amazon, and claw my way back to something resembling normalcy. Instead, here I was, months later, entangled in something far bigger than I’d ever anticipated. What had started as a quest for technological innovation had spiraled into a foray into statecraft, ethics, and interplanetary politics. The path ahead was a labyrinth of possibilities and peril, and the stakes had soared beyond anything I could have imagined.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (244, 61, 4, 'Grounded by Family', 'Dr. S returns home and finds solace in family life. His wife has prepared school supplies for their son and listens as he shares the weight of his responsibilities. His son''s enthusiasm about a Roblox victory provides an unexpected lesson about teamwork that mirrors the larger challenges Dr. S faces.', 'Stepping through the ERB gateway into the warmth of home, a comforting aroma wafting from the kitchen, a perfectly replicated version of my wife’s signature Mapo-tofu greeted me. The contrast between the vast, sterile labs of MOM and the cozy simplicity of family life was stark yet grounding.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (245, 62, 1, 'Kitchen Conversations and Family Warmth', 'Aditi arrives home late from school and helps her mother prepare dinner. Her brother Rahul mentions Mrs. Kapoor''s sleepwalking incident, sparking Aditi''s curiosity about the growing mystery. The family shares warm banter and meals together, with her mother reminding Aditi of the importance of family bonds.', 'The vibrant chaos of Mumbai pulsed in the evening air as Aditi trudged through the narrow lanes, her school bag bumping against her back. The aroma of street food mingled with the distant honking of cars, creating a symphony she had grown up with. By the time she climbed the stairs to her family’s cramped apartment, beads of sweat clung to her forehead.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (448, 112, 1, 'Waking to Normalcy', 'The protagonist wakes in his mundane domestic life, surrounded by his wife and son. Memories of a grand cosmic adventure fade like a dream, replaced by ordinary contentment and the announcement of winning a trip to a space station.', 'I slowly opened my eyes.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (248, 62, 4, 'Amateur Investigation Begins', 'During lunch and over the following days, Aditi and her friends dive deep into researching the sleepwalking phenomenon. They discover patterns, legends of underground rivers, and other similar incidents online, while grappling with the question of why the wider world dismisses or ignores these events.', 'At lunchtime everyone continued to buzz around Aditi and her friends, but their world was confined to the small huddle around her phone. The video played again, the sleepwalkers moving in eerie unison, their arms outstretched like human compasses. The haunting silence of the crowd in the clip contrasted sharply with the excited whispers now filling the group.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (249, 63, 1, 'The Space Elevator Crisis', 'At the Antarctic MOM facility, the protagonist grapples with the Space Elevator project''s mounting challenges. Morgan briefs him on material failures and design obstacles, but their brainstorming session with the team generates breakthrough ideas for hybrid composites and self-healing materials. A cryptic exchange hints at potential sabotage.', 'S Corp’s audacious Space Elevator project loomed in my thoughts, its challenges mirrored in Morgan’s anxious updates from the Antarctic facility. Amid the biting cold and stark desolation of MOM, the blueprint for humanity’s bridge to the cosmos was being meticulously crafted, yet cracks in the plan started to threaten its foundation.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (253, 63, 5, 'The Pointers Campaign', 'With the Europa story fading, S Corp pivots to exploit the global Pointers phenomenon—mysterious sleepwalkers pointing toward construction sites. The team develops a viral marketing strategy to capitalize on public fascination and use it as cover for their Space Elevator construction.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (254, 63, 6, 'The Rise of Elysium', 'Under the cover of the Pointers distraction, S Corp accelerates construction on the Space Elevator towers, using nanite technology to make the massive cables invisible. The protagonist and Morgan witness the towering structures rising skyward as Elysium nears completion.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (256, 64, 2, 'Safety Reminders and Protocols', 'The Safety team issues a cautionary email emphasizing the importance of following safety protocols despite the excitement of the achievement. They remind staff that the space elevators demand respect and proper procedures.', 'Subject: Safety First, Then Space Selfies! (But Seriously, Safety First!)
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (281, 71, 1, 'The Recruitment Address at Pluto Base', 'A commanding officer addresses newly recruited members of the Exo-Interstellar Exploratory Force at humanity''s remote outpost on Pluto. The speech outlines their mission to explore distant star systems via Einstein-Rosen Bridges, while emphasizing both the wonders and perils that await them across the cosmic void.', 'Welcome, brave recruits. Here, on the remote expanse of Pluto, humanity’s farthest intra-solar-system outpost, you find yourselves standing on the precipice of the unknown. As members of the esteemed Exo-Interstellar Exploratory Force, you are the vanguard of discovery in the vast cosmic ocean.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (457, 115, 1, 'Tears of the Veil', 'A poetic invocation addressing summer babes with gifts of remembrance and wisdom. The speaker offers contrasting visions of different souls—some racing through life, others lost in dreams, and still others blind to their surroundings—before bestowing a final gift of eternal rest and the call to grow and gain wisdom.', 'Come ye summer babes
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (468, 117, 6, 'The Dissolution', 'A body moves with mechanical precision, no longer driven by consciousness. It retrieves expired pills from under the sink, methodically consumes them all, and returns to bed to wait for death. The narrative detachment suggests something inhuman has taken control.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (259, 65, 1, 'Beneath the Falling Sky', 'A solitary figure exists unnoticed in a transformative moment, caught between innocence and awareness as something ominous passes overhead. Amid falling rain and growing chaos, they experience a profound metamorphosis—from fragmentation to acceptance—while external forces of noise and unreality press in around them.', 'Alone, never noticed
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (260, 66, 1, 'Arrival at the Orbital Ring', 'The world''s leaders gather in secret on the Elysium Orbital Ring to witness S Corp''s groundbreaking space technology. Suspended above Earth, they confront the enormity of humanity''s next epoch as the narrator prepares to reveal the transformation that awaits civilization.', 'The hum of the space elevator’s doors was both a punctuation and a prelude as they slid open onto the Elysium Orbital Ring viewing deck. Silently, Earth seemed to hover below us, a fragile marble suspended against the infinite black. The stunned silence that filled the room was deafening, broken only by the faint whir of unseen technology.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (261, 66, 2, 'The Opening Statement', 'The narrator addresses the assembled leaders, announcing S Corp''s space elevators as humanity''s gateway to an interstellar society and revealing the existence of thriving colonies on Mars and beyond.', 'I cleared my throat, cutting through the ambient hum. “Welcome, everyone. You’re here because today marks the dawn of a new era, an era where humanity no longer peers at the stars but stands among them.”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (262, 66, 3, 'Questions of Power and Equity', 'World leaders press the narrator on critical concerns: preventing elite monopolization, environmental safeguards, risk mitigation, and controlling chaos from the announcement. The narrator addresses each challenge with detailed frameworks.', 'President Mitchell leaned forward, his weathered face carved with lines of pragmatism. “How exactly does this ‘interstellar society’ avoid becoming an elitist playground? How do you ensure every nation benefits, not just the wealthiest?”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (263, 66, 4, 'The Chinese Challenge', 'The narrator steps away to observe the gathered leaders, then engages with the Chinese representative who questions sovereignty and land acquisition, challenging the legitimacy of S Corp''s operations.', 'While the delegates started to break off and talk among themselves, considering the impact of this revelation, I stepped away from where I was speaking, my gaze drawn back outside. Earth loomed below; a luminous orb suspended against the infinite void. It looked so serene, so unified, and yet I knew the truth: its fractures ran deep.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (264, 66, 5, 'Economic Promises to Commonwealth Nations', 'The narrator engages with delegates from the United Kingdom and New Zealand, highlighting transformative economic and humanitarian benefits including organ transplants, disaster response, and emissions reductions.', 'Nearby, delegates from New Zealand and the United Kingdom stood by the panoramic viewport, their gazes locked on the web of satellites and the sinuous arc of the space elevators stretching into the void. Their quiet awe was almost palpable, and it drew me toward them like a tide.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (279, 70, 1, 'The Secret Conclave Beneath the Vatican', 'Deep beneath the Vatican, Pope Lucius Sixtus VI convenes a clandestine meeting with twelve mysterious figures and a supernatural entity called I AM to plot against S Corp. After five years of S Corp''s corruption of humanity, the Church has decided to take direct action, combining faith, technology, and forbidden knowledge into a dangerous coalition.', 'Deep beneath the hallowed halls of the Vatican, deeper than the hidden archives, in a chamber shrouded in shadow and secrecy, an ancient gathering convened. The air was heavy, oppressive, carrying a palpable dread that seemed to emanate from the very stones of the walls. Faint torchlight flickered, casting jagged shadows across the room as if the darkness itself conspired to swallow the light.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (280, 70, 2, 'The Guard''s Betrayal and Sacrifice', 'A Swiss Guard stationed outside the secret chamber sends a desperate message to his family on an S Corp colony before being discovered and silently murdered. His final act of love becomes an act of futility as the message never reaches them and the consequences of the Vatican''s conspiracy begin to unfold in bloodshed.', 'In the shadowed labyrinth beneath the Vatican, where ancient stone walls whispered of secrets too dark for daylight, a Swiss Guard stood like a silent sentinel. His polished halberd gleamed faintly in the dim light, a symbol of his sworn duty. Beneath his stoic exterior, turmoil churned, a storm of fear and love.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (282, 72, 1, 'The War Room Strategy', 'In the opulent Elysium office high above Earth, the protagonist and their core advisors—Patrick, Gil, and TJ—grapple with escalating coordinated attacks on S Corp facilities worldwide. The discussion reveals an ideological conflict deeper than simple insurgency: religious extremists view S Corp as demonic, and conventional counterattacks risk losing the narrative.', 'Thinking back to the dreams that started it all, from the small farm workshop where the Eternal Engine first sprang to life, I could hardly believe where I stood now. It had been five years since the Space Elevators’ grand unveiling, those colossal towers that launched humanity into a new epoch of boundless possibilities. From my opulent office in Elysium, high above the Earth, I gazed out at the sprawling spires piercing the heavens.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (472, 118, 4, 'The Memory Unfolds', 'Lady Illkeserod touches the protagonist''s forehead, releasing a cascading flood of memories that reveal their true nature as Benji, an ancient observer consciousness, and Ilse''s partner. The memories detail their mission to Etheris, the corruption of the prison, and how Whitney''s signal reached them from outside, marking the possibility of escape.', 'And beside you, always beside you, is her.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (481, 119, 8, 'The Akashic Halls Flash', 'The mention of Rebecca''s bookshop triggers a powerful past-life memory of the Akashic Halls—an infinite library of cosmic knowledge—before snapping back to reality. The vision leaves Stephen with a sense of something ancient and significant beyond his current loop.', 'I stared at the little red pin on the map. A bookshop.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (485, 120, 4, 'Reunion at Jamie''s Marginalia', 'Inside the bookshop, Stephen is greeted warmly by old high school friends Becca and James, who own the shop. They discuss unemployment, broken systems, and the nature of consensus reality, while Stephen becomes increasingly unsettled by phantom memories and the missing presence of a girl from their past.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (268, 67, 1, 'The Pointers Go Viral', 'Over three months, the Pointers phenomenon explodes from obscure internet rumors into global consciousness. Sleepwalkers materialize nightly at transportation hubs, sparking viral videos, conspiracy theories, and opportunistic commercialization as society descends into frenzy and paranoia.', 'During the next three months tidal wave or stories about the Pointers, once whispered about in the dark corners of obscure internet forums and dismissed as a trivial curiosity by the mainstream media, had exploded into the public consciousness with a violent ferocity.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (269, 67, 2, 'The Pointers Speak', 'The silent Pointers suddenly emit a piercing screech declaring "ELYSIUM RISES," breaking their silence and sending shockwaves across the globe. This vocalization transforms them from passive sentinels into active communicators, triggering worldwide speculation.', 'It was as still and quiet as any other night, the Pointers standing tall in their usual vigilance, when suddenly everything changed. From within their stoic silence, a cacophonous screech erupted and rumbled through the air. The sound was so piercing that it seemed to shatter windows and eardrums alike, leaving only two words echoing in its wake: “ELYSIUM” and “ELYSIUM RISES.” The abruptness of this shift, from silent sentinels to vocalized declarations, caused shockwaves to ripple through communities and media outlets across the globe.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (271, 68, 1, 'The Broadcast', 'The protagonist delivers a historic global broadcast from S Corp''s Houston headquarters, announcing the space elevators and a united future for humanity. As billions watch across Earth and space colonies, the speech emphasizes progress, unity, and shared destiny, concluding to thunderous applause from crowds gathering worldwide.', 'The cameras started rolling and the bright lights focused on me. I stood in my spacious office, its polished mahogany furniture exuding an air of sophistication. A mixture of anticipation and anxiety coursed through my veins, a cocktail of emotions that mirrored the weightiness of this pivotal moment. Today marked a turning point not just for S Corp, but for all of humanity. It was a day that would be etched into the annals of history.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (272, 68, 2, 'The Attack', 'A group of armed extremists led by Todd and Stacey, opposing S Corp as oppressive, attempt a coordinated attack at the plaza below S Corp''s headquarters. S Corp''s advanced environmental shields activate instantly, neutralizing the threat without harm, and the attackers are arrested, leaving the crowd in awe of the technology''s power.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (273, 69, 1, 'The Golden Ticket', 'Yukiko and her young brother Takashi prepare for an unprecedented journey as civilian colonists beyond the solar system. As they board the space elevator with their family, Yukiko reassures her anxious brother while an older passenger offers wisdom about cherishing shared moments.', 'Yukiko’s heart raced with a mix of excitement and anticipation, its rhythm matching the tempo of her thoughts. For as long as she could remember, the stars had whispered to her, their distant twinkling promising adventure and discovery beyond the limits of her imagination. And now, on the cusp of turning seven, she was about to embark on a journey that most could only ever dream of. With a stroke of luck, she had won a contest, securing a golden ticket for her family to be among the first civilian colonists to venture beyond the confines of the solar system. The technological marvels crafted by S Corp. made this extraordinary voyage possible
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (514, 127, 5, 'My Lai and the Crack in the Prison', 'Stephen recalls his incarnation as Hobart McComas III, a Vietnam-era marine who fell desperately in love with a Vietnamese woman and fathered twins with her, only for both to die in the My Lai massacre, creating the first major fracture in the prison.', '"You met Mom," Xavier said.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (531, 130, 3, 'Negotiation with the Crawling Chaos', 'Stephen summons Nyarlathotep and successfully negotiates passage through the barrier by appealing to the entity''s boredom with the stagnant prison. The barrier opens, granting him access to the interior of the Pyramid.', 'No pressure.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (275, 69, 3, 'The Pluto Hub and the Mobile Habitat', 'The family arrives at the S Corp Expeditionary Center on Pluto, a bustling futuristic hub, and boards their grand mobile habitat designed to carry them through ERB gateways to a planet orbiting the blue supergiant Alnitak Aa.', 'Arriving at the bustling hub on Pluto, the family was greeted by glowing pathways that illuminated their path like celestial constellations. The corridors of the colossal space center were alive with motion, engineers in sleek uniforms darting between stations, families clutching belongings, and the faint hum of distant machinery blending with the ambient murmur of excited voices.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (276, 69, 4, 'The Gateway Crossing', 'The habitat with fifty families passes through the ERB gateway, crossing a historic threshold as they journey through a cosmic passage adorned with stars, nebulae, and galaxies, experiencing a surreal voyage through the universe.', 'As the habitat moved steadily forward, moving through the ERB, Yukiko and the fifty other families on board crossed a threshold unparalleled in human history. The Gateway corridor unfolded like a passage through the cosmos itself, its walls adorned with a dazzling tapestry of stars, nebulae, and distant galaxies. The view felt infinite, yet intimate, as if the universe was welcoming them into its arms.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (278, 69, 6, 'First Steps on Alien Soil', 'Yukiko takes the first bold steps onto the alien planet''s surface, breathing its crisp, electric air. Her family follows, marveling at the bioluminescent flora and the untamed, serene landscape as Takashi joyfully leaps in the lower gravity.', 'Yukiko took a bold step forward, her boots clicking softly against the metallic ramp as it extended onto the alien soil. Her breath caught as the otherworldly air hit her face, crisp, cool and breathable, carrying a faint tang she couldn’t quite place. It was invigorating, almost electric, as though the very atmosphere hummed with the vitality of a world waiting to be discovered.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (341, 84, 1, 'The Sealed Cosmos', 'As the war reaches a desperate crescendo, the cosmic entities seal the dream realms to contain the I AM, inadvertently cutting humanity off from salvation. The narrator grasps a final grimoire and discovers a horrifying truth: the I AM is an eternal devourer, and they themselves unleashed it by claiming the Eternal Engine.', 'The war raged with renewed intensity, driven by urgency, desperation, and purpose. We had pushed technology to the brink, exhausted every resource, and hurled ourselves into the inferno of battle. And still, it was not enough.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (342, 85, 1, 'Approach to the Corpse World', 'The narrator''s ship approaches Earth, finding it transformed into a grotesque monument to death. The Obsidian Tower looms ahead, a living structure of fused bodies and tortured souls. As the crew begins to fall to the Tower''s corruption, the narrator alone resists through technological shielding and willpower.', 'The Aditi’s Genesis cut through the void like a blade through flesh, a precise, final incision into the black maw of oblivion. We had taken an isolated ERB close to the front, a desperate foothold at the edge of reason, where the laws of reality had begun to crack. The weight of I AM''s dominion pressed against us, thick and suffocating, seeping into the steel bones of our vessel. Every system hummed with the strain of holding back the madness that lurked just beyond the hull.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (343, 85, 2, 'Confrontation with the Demiurge', 'The narrator crosses the threshold into the Tower and confronts I AM directly, engaging in both verbal and physical combat. Despite an initial apparent victory, I AM resurrects itself and severs the narrator''s arm, forcing them to recognize that brute force alone cannot end the cycle.', 'The shrieks started the moment I crossed the threshold into the tower.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (515, 127, 6, 'Xavier, the Glitch', 'Stephen reveals that Xavier''s existence—born from a union that should have been prevented—represents a critical error in the prison''s design, destabilizing the system and triggering three successive failed resets.', '"That''s why this cycle has been different," Maeve said quietly. "Why you''ve been remembering. Why the resets keep failing."
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (284, 72, 3, 'The God Killer Crisis', 'The command center team launches a desperate operation to intercept the God Killer before it reaches the Pyongyang Space Elevator. Despite successfully securing the first device, a second detonates at the elevator base. The security systems hold, protecting the elevator and surrounding area, but the protagonist orders immediate total retaliation against all extremist factions.', 'The countdown ticked closer. The screens displayed live drone feeds, each one painting a grim picture of the convoy carrying the God Killer. The desert terrain blurred under the lenses, the figures of armed guards moving with precision around the transport vehicle.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (292, 73, 8, 'Battle for Survival', 'The colonists repurpose technology and study the creatures, preparing defenses using alien flora. When the creatures and cultists return, a battle erupts under Sorhhinda''s triple suns. The colony survives and adapts, transforming from castaways into warriors forged by necessity.', 'They repurposed the salvaged tech, turning bio-tools into crude but effective weapons. They studied the beasts, learning their patterns, their weaknesses. They even harnessed the alien flora, weaving its bioluminescent fibers into protective nets, its luminescent sap into rudimentary flares.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (499, 123, 4, 'The Truth Unfolds', 'Patrick explains the nature of the prison, Yaldabaoth, the Thirteen, and DMT as a conduit for communication. Stephen realizes his wife is a construct designed to keep him docile and learns of the threat to his son Xavier.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (542, 133, 3, 'The Six-Month Search', 'Six months pass as the Resistance searches for the cosmic seed while Stephen struggles with nightmares and moral uncertainty. Jamie provides comfort and support as Stephen grapples with his past actions and current mission.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (294, 74, 2, 'Hydroponics Crisis', 'Frank responds to the Hydroponics emergency where Dr. Adler panics about gamma radiation from UV filters. Frank diagnoses and fixes the issue, nearly drowning in irradiated tomato soup in the process.', 'My first stop was Hydroponics, where the radiation alarms wailed like banshees. “Frank, thank God!” hollered Dr. Adler, Hydroponics’ resident paranoid. His hair stuck up like static-charged algae.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (295, 74, 3, 'The Raccoon Conspiracy', 'Frank investigates the Argentine bakery where Sr. Hernandez blames space raccoons for contaminating their empanada dough. Frank discovers the real culprit is algae contamination from Hydroponics.', 'Next came the Argentinians. Their bakery smelled heavenly, which made the angry shouting in Spanish more jarring. “Frank! Look at this!” screamed Sr. Hernandez, thrusting a green empanada in my face.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (296, 74, 4, 'Zero-G Bowling Disaster', 'A rogue bowling ball ricochets through the ventilation system into the oxygen recycler. Frank rigs an improvised duct tape slingshot to retrieve it while bowlers float helplessly amid spinning pins and a cosmic cat.', 'Apparently, some jackass had bowled a strike so aggressively the ball ricocheted through the ventilation system and into the oxygen recycler. I arrived to find bowlers floating mid-air, swearing as pins spun past their heads. A cosmic cat was chasing the rogue bowling ball like it was God’s gift to felines.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (297, 74, 5, 'Contact Lost with Sorhhinda', 'Pete, Frank''s husband and comms officer, calls with catastrophic news: Sorhhinda colony has gone completely dark with no signals, telemetry, or beacons. Frank and Pete wrestle with the implications of humanity''s first exo-solar outpost falling silent.', '“Frank, pick up. We’ve got a situation,” came Pete’s voice—calm, steady, and with just a hint of his trademark sarcasm. That voice was the only reason I survived life on Elysium without losing my mind. Pete, my husband, and the best damn comms officer for S Corp, was the yin to my perpetually frazzled yang.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (298, 75, 1, 'The Anomaly in the Data', 'TJ discovers a troubling pattern in resource utilization data suggesting widespread withdrawal from productivity among creators and innovators. The anomaly represents a growing dissatisfaction with the post-scarcity utopia, masked by surface-level happiness metrics.', 'Europa’s icy crust shimmered through the domed ceiling of TJ’s office, refracting the city lights of New Atlantis into a kaleidoscope of blues and whites. It should have been breathtaking, but today the beauty felt hollow, like a polished veneer hiding rot. TJ sat hunched over his desk, his fingers twitching near the blinking red indicator on his data stream. Unease clouded his usually sharp mind.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (299, 75, 2, 'The Confrontation with Dr. On', 'Dr. Pai M. On arrives to hear TJ''s report on the anomaly. TJ argues that purpose and happiness are distinct, and that people are rebelling by withdrawing from productivity. Dr. On dismisses his concerns, refusing to acknowledge the severity of the growing Red Hat movement and its implications.', 'Minutes later, the door to his office hissed open, and Dr. Pai M. On strode in. Once just a sleep psychologist who headed up early investigations into dream disturbances, she was now head of S Corp’s Social Integration Division. She moved with the practiced ease of someone accustomed to managing crises—and eliminating them. Her polished smile felt like a blade wrapped in silk.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (326, 81, 6, 'The Analog Weapon Revealed', 'Aditi, recovered enough for debriefing, explains how she discovered the Red Hats'' exploitation of simple analog technology. Shortwave radio broadcasts combined with amplifying hats create infectious sound patterns that corrupt listeners, bypassing all digital security.', 'As soon as Aditi was well enough for a debrief, she recounted her ordeal with a calmness that belied the harrowing experience she’d endured. Stranded in the vast void of space, her hope dwindling, she had tuned into radio frequencies in desperation. What she found changed everything.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (344, 85, 3, 'The Void Within', 'Consumed by I AM''s darkness, the narrator experiences visions of I AM''s origin—a shepherd boy traumatized by death who vowed never to witness weakness again. Through compassion and understanding, the narrator absorbs I AM''s power and breaks the chains binding Etheris, freeing countless souls. Yet liberation proves fleeting as the cosmos implodes without I AM''s sustaining force.', 'Darkness swallowed me whole, its oppressive weight pressing against my very essence. The anguished cries of countless souls trapped within I AM’s insatiable hunger reverberated through my consciousness—a harrowing symphony of despair. Their torment tore at my resolve, a constant reminder of the stakes. A trillion, trillion, infinite souls of the consumed swirled all around me.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (345, 86, 1, 'The Void of Ego and Sacrifice', 'A contemplative meditation on the nature of blind ambition, willful ignorance, and the relentless forward march of existence. The passage presents a critique of those who follow predetermined paths while screaming into emptiness, sacrificing themselves and others through deafening self-regard.', 'Walk not on other’s trodden paths
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (562, 136, 3, 'The Swarm Descends', 'The creatures ravage the compound, destroying androids and the greenhouse. Kai watches in horror as his beloved spatch weed plants are trampled and devoured, triggering an overwhelming surge of rage that awakens something dormant within him.', 'The swarm hit the compound like a wave.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (303, 76, 3, 'The Weight of Distance', 'In her small Elysium dorm room, Aditi gazes at Earth through her window and connects with her mother via hologram. Her mother reveals the worsening conditions at home—her father''s persistent cough, Rahul''s absence, and the desperation to escape. Aditi promises to bring them to Elysium but struggles with the guilt of knowing the waitlist is designed to keep them out.', 'The nights on Elysium were the hardest. The orbital city, gleaming with sterile perfection, seemed to mock Aditi with its cold indifference. Outside her window, Earth hung like a fragile blue marble, breathtaking and distant. The hum of Elysium’s artificial systems buzzed faintly, filling the oppressive silence of her small dorm room. After what felt like hours of staring at the planet below, Aditi finally activated the hologram terminal.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (304, 76, 4, 'The Anomalous Signal', 'Months later, late at night in Elysium University''s research lab, Aditi discovers an erratic, desperate signal from Pluto referencing a Janus gate jump. She immediately reports it to Professor Nakamura, who becomes deeply alarmed at the implications—a direct transmission to Pluto that bypasses the standard ERB network, suggesting potential compromise.', 'Late one night, months later, in the quiet hum of Elysium University’s research lab, Aditi sat surrounded by the rhythmic thrum of machinery—a sound that usually lulled her into focused tranquility. But tonight was different. The sharp crackle of static from the antique radio telescope shattered the stillness, cutting through the usual calm like a siren in the dark, jolting her awake.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (305, 76, 5, 'Conspirators in Code', 'Aditi brings the encrypted transmission to Hiro, a brilliant and rebellious fellow student, and together they decrypt hidden S Corp files revealing ancient Latin blueprints for faster-than-light propulsion systems and a secret operational vessel called the Genesis near the Rome space elevator. Despite the danger, Aditi convinces Hiro to help her steal the ship to investigate what happened to Sorhhinda and uncover the truth.', 'The dim glow of the console reflected off Hiro’s glasses as he hunched over the terminal, his fingers flying across the holographic keys with practiced precision. Hiro was one of the few people Aditi had connected with at Elysium University, a quiet boy with a sharp mind and a knack for finding cracks in systems, both digital and social. They’d bonded in Professor Nakamura’s class, their shared disdain for elitism and love of unconventional problem-solving bridging the gap between his reserved nature and her fiery resolve.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (306, 76, 6, 'Stealing the Stars', 'Aditi and Hiro infiltrate the hidden launch facility and discover the Genesis, an unconventional ship that feels almost alive with its organic design. After a brief moment of doubt, they board the vessel and launch into the void, setting course for Pluto with nothing but determination and the faint hope that they can uncover the truth hidden at the edge of the solar system.', 'The hidden launch facility was eerily quiet, bathed in dim red emergency lighting that seemed unnecessary but added an ominous touch. The Genesis loomed in the center of the cavernous hangar, alive and predatory, its hull humming with an almost imperceptible vibration. The ship felt alive. It’s shape was strangely animal-like.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (307, 77, 1, 'The Failed Uprising', 'Todd stands among the Red Hat masses at S Corp headquarters in Houston, attempting to breach the corporate shield with a gunshot. His defiance proves futile against the impenetrable barrier, and he collapses in defeat.', 'April 21, 2025, another day that would live in infamy.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (308, 77, 2, 'Confinement and the Arrival of Nameless', 'Todd awakens in a sterile prison cell, disoriented and broken. A mysterious figure called Nameless arrives with an offer of freedom in exchange for Todd''s compliance with an unknown purpose.', 'He awoke like every other day in his ruined shell of existence, to the sterile glow of artificial light. The cell was a featureless cube, its metallic walls reflecting the cold, clinical glare. The sharp scent of disinfectant burned his nostrils, mingling with the pounding in his head. Disoriented, Todd struggled to piece together fragments of memory, the rally, the shield, the crushing emptiness that had followed. Alone in this cell, his only companion was the passing of eternity, in his own personal hell.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (309, 77, 3, 'The Vatican Revelation', 'Todd is transported to the Vatican crypts where he meets Pope Lucius Sixtus VI and mysterious entities. They reveal that S Corp is a mask concealing ancient forces opposed to I AM, and recruit Todd as their champion to lead a rebellion.', 'The crypts beneath the Vatican were a twisting maze of ancient stone, each corridor heavy with the weight of untold secrets. Candles flickered in alcoves, casting dancing shadows that seemed to breathe with the darkness. Todd followed Nameless, the man’s steps echoing softly in the damp air.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (310, 77, 4, 'Project Janus: The Final Preparation', 'Five years later, Todd oversees the construction and launch of Project Janus—cathedral-ships designed to attack S Corp''s gateway on Pluto. With a diverse crew of Vatican scientists, engineers, and priests, he prepares for humanity''s last stand against the forces of control.', 'It had been nearly five years of preparation since their first encounter with the Nameless. After emerging from the meeting with the remaining nine entities, he realized how entrenched S Corp was and how difficult everything was going to be to take them down. While he had worked on the outside, growing the influence of the Red Hats, the other 9 were already working in the shadows, taking down S Corps internals and causing as much chaos as they could to try an overwhelm everything. S Corp wouldn’t fall with brute force alone; it had to be dismantled piece by piece, infiltrated and undermined until its foundations collapsed.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (311, 77, 5, 'The Journey and Final Approach', 'Over months of travel powered by faith and prayer, Todd''s fleet reaches Jupiter and prepares for the final jump to Pluto. The pope grants his blessing as Todd activates the Janus Gate to traverse the void.', 'Without advanced technologies, the fleet moved at a crawl, slowly traversing the solar system over a period of months. They would travel, pray, charge up the Janus gate and leap. Unlike the instantaneous portals to hell S Corp has, this was fueled by belief, the love of God and used heaven’s light to see it through. But it required a ton of daily devotions.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (346, 87, 1, 'The Void of Consequence', 'In the aftermath of consuming I AM, the protagonist drifts in absolute nothingness, overwhelmed by guilt and despair. Haunted by memories of his family, he gradually transforms his anguish into hope and begins to harness his newfound power to create a renewed Etheris.', 'In the desolate depths of absolute nothingness, where the remnants of I AM and Etheris had faded into never having existed, I found myself adrift amidst an ocean of emptiness. The consequence of my actions bore down upon me with the crushing force of a collapsing star, an insurmountable burden that threatened to consume me just as I had consumed I AM.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (347, 87, 2, 'The Observer''s Curse', 'The protagonist realizes he cannot interact with the universe he created, devastated that his family will never truly exist. He dissolves his creation and seeks guidance from Lady I once more, leading to a new plan to alter the past.', 'Despite all of this, my existence within the universe I had conjured remained a passive one. I couldn’t interact, engage, or even stir the slightest ripple within its fabric. The realization struck me with a devastating blow - my wife, my son, my future generations. They would never come to be. Or if they did, they would be born into a mere shadow of myself, an echo, a pale imitation. I would forever remain an eternal observer, condemned to watch from the sidelines, unable to partake in the joy and love of my own family.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (348, 87, 3, 'The Dream Guardian''s Work', 'The protagonist assumes the role of a guardian of dreams, subtly weaving inspiration through the minds of sleeping humans to guide them toward discovering new technologies and sealing the breach against I AM''s influence. He witnesses humanity''s progress while remaining a solitary phantom unable to directly participate.', 'I floated for an eternity, aimlessly alone in the boundless expanse of the void, Madam O’s words echoed in my mind, their weight pressing upon me. The plan she had proposed required finesse, a delicate balance between preserving the technological advancements that had propelled humanity’s growth and eradicating the threat posed by I AM. It called for a deep understanding of the intricacies of the dream realm, a mastery over its shifting landscapes and ethereal possibilities.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (313, 78, 1, 'Starlight and Uncertainty', 'A father and his struggling 20-year-old son sit by a campfire under the stars. The father uses the beauty of the cosmos and words of wisdom to help his son overcome his anxiety about his new astronomy class, reminding him that wonder matters more than perfection.', 'The fire crackled softly, sending sparks spiraling into the vast night sky, their glow dwarfed by the infinite expanse of stars. The scent of roasted marshmallows hung in the crisp air, mingling with the gentle murmur of campers sharing stories. Amidst the laughter and warmth, a quiet tension hummed. My soon to be 20 year-old son sat close, his eyes fixed on the fire, his thoughts clearly elsewhere.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (314, 78, 2, 'Roomba Rebellion', 'Returning home from their camping trip, the family discovers their fleet of Roomba 9000s have malfunctioned and are locked in chaotic territorial battles. What begins as frustration transforms into absurdist humor as the robots seem to develop unexpected camaraderie and the parents playfully speculate about their mechanical uprising.', 'The next morning, as we left the smoldering embers of our campfire behind, I reflected on how this cosmic adventure of ours wasn’t just about navigating the stars, it was about finding wonder in the unexpected. Little did I know that wonder, as usual, would come wrapped in chaos.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (315, 78, 3, 'Crisis at the Edge of the Universe', 'An emergency alert reveals that Sorhhinda Colony, humanity''s first interstellar settlement, has gone offline and the Pluto Exploratory Facility is broadcasting distress signals. As the father struggles to process the catastrophe, his son and wife provide emotional support before mysterious ships are detected at the gateway.', 'The hum of the Monday office, once a comforting backdrop to my mornings, felt suffocating today. My phone buzzed, and the words on the screen hit like a sledgehammer: Sorhhinda Colony—Offline. Worse, an emergency beacon was screaming from our Pluto Exploratory Facility.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (316, 79, 1, 'The Paradox of Ascension', 'A philosophical meditation on the contradictions of human striving, where commands to climb, struggle, learn, and follow yield only paradox and self-deception. The chapter explores how truth eludes those who seek it, and how the fundamental acts of seeking become their own prisons.', 'Climb said the buried
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (317, 80, 1, 'War Room Transmission', 'The Emergency Response Center becomes a war room as Todd broadcasts his manifesto after destroying the Pluto outpost and Sorhhinda gateway. A heated exchange ensues between the narrator and Todd, revealing the Red Hat rebellion''s theological extremism and hinting at cosmic horrors. The discovery of Dr. On''s betrayal and internal infiltration compounds the crisis.', 'Under a veil of interstellar static, the Emergency Response Center had been transformed into a war-room that hummed with a nervous energy that tasted like copper on the tongue. The usually reserved and calculated space had been plunged into chaos, its screens flashing with the fiery aftermath of our Pluto outpost’s destruction and the Sorhhinda gateway’s smoldering remains.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (318, 80, 2, 'Confrontation with Family', 'As the narrator leaves the war room, his wife intercepts him in the corridor, demanding answers about their safety. Their intimate conversation reveals the depth of the crisis and the narrator''s grim conclusion that mass extermination of the Red Hats is the only option.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (319, 80, 3, 'Fireside Chat Preparation and Broadcast', 'The narrator assembles a team to craft a unifying message for the solar system. After intense collaboration to balance honesty with reassurance, he delivers a powerful broadcast rallying the colonies to stand firm against the Red Hat threat. The message momentarily stabilizes public morale before exhaustion sets in.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (320, 80, 4, 'The Infection Spreads', 'In the aftermath of the broadcast and emergency decree banning Red Hat symbols, chaos erupts across the colonies. Gil''s report reveals the rebellion is mutating into something darker and more sinister—a possession-like corruption that transcends mere political unrest, with impossible phenomena suggesting cosmic horror involvement.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (321, 81, 1, 'The Spreading Darkness', 'The Red Hats'' influence expands across human colonies with terrifying efficiency. Discovery of grotesque human barricades at overtaken ERBs reveals the depths of their depravity, forcing humanity to recognize they face an enemy beyond conventional comprehension.', 'The remote colonies flickered silent one by one, once monuments to human exploration, now stood as hollow monuments under the relentless gaze of distant stars. A chilling unease echoed through steel corridors and dimly lit control rooms, amplified by the Red Hats’ shadowy influence. Their cryptic symbols bled onto city walls and holo-screens like festering wounds, a grim testament to their growing power.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (322, 81, 2, 'The War Room Council', 'The commander convenes top advisors to formulate a strategy against the Red Hats'' control of ERBs. Through heated debate, they settle on a multi-pronged approach combining psychological warfare, public messaging, and fortified defenses, ultimately authorizing a brutal but necessary operation.', 'I called an emergency meeting with my top advisors to address the crisis at the gateways. “We need a solution that respects human life but also reasserts control over the hijacked ERBs,” I began, scanning the room. “Ideas?”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (323, 81, 3, 'The Podcast Plague', 'Todd''s apocalyptic broadcasts weaponize free speech, spreading Red Hat ideology through alternative channels faster than S Corp can suppress them. His words infect minds across the colonies, revealing a cosmic horror rooted in humanity''s own darkness.', 'Our limited success at reclaiming colonies only served to intensify the Red Hat activities. Despite our security measures and network lockdowns, Todd was able to create and broadcast a podcast that became a monstrous force, its apocalyptic rhetoric infecting minds and fueling chaos. His broadcasts summoned a growing following, weaving rebellion and madness into society.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (324, 81, 4, 'The Signal from the Void', 'Professor Nakamura brings urgent news of a distress signal from missing student Aditi in the Kuiper Belt. The discovery exposes a critical weakness in S Corp''s centralized communications system and prompts an immediate rescue mission.', 'S Corp’s communication systems, reliant on the near-instantaneous precision of ERB technology, had always been a point of pride. Wi-Fi-based transmissions rendered outdated Earth-based radio and telecom systems unnecessary, or so we thought. Yet, as I stared into the digital abyss, tracking Red Hat movements like a grim chessboard of chaos, I couldn’t shake the sense that we’d overlooked something vital.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (327, 82, 1, 'The Hollow Victory', 'After five years of battling the Red Hat virus, all hostile signals suddenly disappear. The narrator celebrates with the team but feels deep unease about the too-clean ending, sensing something sinister beneath the surface.', '“We did it. We actually fucking did it.” A triumphant sigh escaped my lips as the final flicker of the Red Hat signal disappeared from the main screen.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (329, 82, 3, 'The Cosmic Emptiness', 'Decades later, trillions of light-years from home, the narrator and Morgan discover that despite abundant non-sentient life, the universe harbors no intelligent civilizations, contradicting expectations and revealing a deeper cosmic horror than the feared Dark Forest Hypothesis.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (330, 82, 4, 'The Three-Hundredth Birthday', 'At age 300, the narrator is surprised by family for his birthday and reflects with his great-great-great-grandson Stellan about the costs and fragility of their expansion, while hinting at hidden network anomalies and malevolent forces emerging within their systems.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (331, 82, 5, 'The Fracturing Reality', 'The narrator''s mind destabilizes as reality becomes fluid and dreamlike; he experiences glimpses of alternate states and begins to suspect that existence itself is artificial or controlled. The presence of something called ''I AM'' manifests, revealing a sinister force that has been watching all along.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (332, 83, 1, 'Nightmares and Warnings', 'The protagonist experiences recurring nightmares of burning ants and realizes they may be connected to recent S Corp network glitches. After discussing these dreams with his wife, he decides to consult with Patrick, a veteran of the Red Hat invasion, to determine if the dreams are genuine warnings or signs of instability.', 'In the dead of night, under a foreign string of moons that hung like a cold, indifferent string of pearls in the sky, I found myself once again trapped within the labyrinthine tunnels of my own subconscious.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (333, 83, 2, 'The Security Office Consultation', 'The protagonist meets Patrick at the S Corp security office and shares his dream experiences. Patrick reveals the team has detected anomalies across multiple regions. The protagonist reveals his Oneiromancy training and theorizes that the dreams are linked to an existential threat connected to the Eternal Engine and the Threshold itself.', 'The next day, I walked into the local S Corp security office, a nondescript building humming with quiet efficiency. The scent of recycled air and faint traces of cleaning solvents greeted me as I stepped inside. A dozen sharp-eyed security specialists were scattered around the room, their movements brisk and purposeful. Every monitor flickered with streams of data—threat assessments, colony logs, and the omnipresent surveillance feeds that kept the sector in check.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (335, 83, 4, 'Assault on Headquarters', 'The protagonist regains consciousness to find S Corp headquarters under direct assault by Todd''s forces. The security center devolves into a warzone with explosions, casualties, and overwhelming enemy firepower. The protagonist and Patrick are evacuated to a reinforced bunker as the facility is overrun.', '“Are you ok” Patrick shouted as he violently shook me. “You passed out.”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (336, 83, 5, 'In the Bunker: Defiance and Resolve', 'Inside the bunker, the protagonist and Patrick assess the ongoing carnage from security feeds. The protagonist rallies the demoralized team, declaring they will not allow I AM to undo what they''ve built. They brief on the threat posed by Todd and the Red Hats, strengthening morale with displays of determination and tactical confidence.', 'Darkness. Silence. The sudden, jarring absence of the warzone above.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (337, 83, 6, 'All Clear and the True Massacre', 'Hours later, a radio confirms the immediate threat is neutralized, but reports reveal the Red Hats have evolved beyond expectations and attacks are occurring across multiple colonies. Todd broadcasts a message blaming S Corp''s hubris before Red Hat cyborgs breach the bunker''s defenses. The protagonist witnesses unprecedented carnage and authorizes a full extermination response.', 'Hours stretched painfully long as we waited. Finally, a crackle on the radio broke the silence.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (338, 83, 7, 'The Dreamscape War Emerges', 'The physical war evolves into a two-front conflict as soldiers face mental degradation and death from sleep deprivation. The protagonist discovers that battles fought in the dreamscape affect physical reality. He establishes a corps of Oneiromancers—dream warriors trained in the ancient art—to fight I AM in the ethereal realm while physical forces hold the line. This strategy marks a turning point in the war.', 'Battle after battle was lost. We were constantly on the go, getting pushed further and further back. No matter what we did, Todd and his fucking Red Hats seemed to be one step ahead.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (340, 83, 9, 'The Final Push Against I AM', 'The protagonist gathers his Oneiromancer squad beneath a skeletal tree in the dreamscape and addresses their exhaustion and doubt. He articulates the difference between fighting for conquest (I AM''s goal) versus fighting for reality''s survival (their purpose). He announces they will strike at I AM''s core stronghold in the realm of nightmares, rallying the troops for a final offensive.', 'The moon hung heavy, an unblinking eye casting silver over the battlefield of shifting illusions. The air smelled of ozone and memory, thick with the residue of battles fought and lost. I gathered the squad beneath a skeletal tree, its twisted limbs reaching toward the void like the desperate hands of the fallen.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (378, 95, 6, 'The Corvette Dream and Death', 'Late at night, Stephen collapses into an exhausted sleep and experiences an intensely erotic dream involving both Jamie and Becca in a Corvette. The dream becomes a nightmare when the car crashes, killing all three. Stephen wakes to realize this is another death vision from an alternate timeline.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (352, 89, 1, 'The Celebration of Five Centuries', 'In Yukiko Memorial Square, Kai witnesses President Nara''s speech commemorating the 500th anniversary of Sorhhinda''s independence from Earth. She honors the sacrifices that built their world, while Kai feels profound pride in his people''s resilience and indomitable spirit.', 'The twin towers of the Planetary Parliament soared majestically into the heavens, their alabaster spires reaching for the very heart of the cerulean Sorhhindian sky. Bathed in the ethereal glow of the sun, these architectural marvels stood as a testament to the grandeur and ambition of the Sorhhindian people.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (353, 89, 2, 'The Dream of the Eternal Engine', 'That night, Kai dreams of activating the Eternal Engine he has long envisioned. In his dream workshop, he discovers its true purpose as an escape vessel and catalyst for boundless knowledge, awakening with a sense of revelation.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (354, 90, 1, 'About the Author', 'A biographical overview of Stephen A. Salaka, presenting his dual career as a technology executive and storyteller, his educational background, and the unique perspective that informs his writing.', 'Imagine a whirlwind career traversing industries from launching rockets to crafting blockbuster entertainment, all while leading international teams across continents. That’s the crazy journey of Stephen A. Salaka, a man who effortlessly switches between tech executive and inspired storyteller.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (356, 92, 1, 'The Pod''s Last Malfunction', 'A seventy-four-year-old man in a hospice pod experiences a life-support system failure at 3:17 AM. As he gasps for air in the metal coffin, he reflects on his deceased wife of forty-seven years and their distant but enduring love, contrasting her memory with his current technological imprisonment.', 'The hospice pod murdered me at 3:17 AM.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (357, 92, 2, 'The Death of Dreams and Science', 'The protagonist drifts into bitter memory and reflection on humanity''s failed technological age, where AI solved only minor problems before hitting a knowledge ceiling, leading to societal collapse, demographic extinction, and universal resignation. Increasingly surreal glitches and impossible symbols begin appearing in his environment.', 'A memory surfaces.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (379, 96, 1, 'The Basement Gathering', 'A group of teenagers gathers in TJ''s basement in a post-tournament haze. Amid the expensive surroundings and accumulated chaos, Jamie and Becca engage in territorial flirtation over the narrator while the others watch. The tension builds as they prepare to play spin the bottle, but the moment is violently interrupted when the narrator experiences a sudden, brutal seizure-like episode triggered by an internal scream of a single name.', 'We''re scattered across TJ''s basement like survivors of some teenage apocalypse. Emerging from the pot haze our brains are swarming from sugar, caffeine, beer, and questions we don''t know how to ask. The furniture down here tells the story of our contradictions—in the basement in Florida, there are large genuine leather sectionals that probably cost more than my dad''s car, but buried under layers of our accumulated chaos. Discarded school projects we all somehow worked on at the same time. Mountain Dew cans arranged like shrines to caffeinated obsession. A vintage Digger Doug cabinet humming in the corner, next to milk crates stuffed with bootleg VHS tapes and stolen political signs.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (380, 96, 2, 'The Confession: When I Was Eight', 'The narrator reveals a harrowing childhood trauma: at age eight, his mother poisoned him slowly over months in a trailer in Nevada. He died and was resuscitated after twelve minutes of CPR, but remembers dying and encountering something impossible in the void—a entity called Benji. After his recovery, his family relocated to upstate New York and all memory of Nevada was denied. Since his recent concussion, fragmented memories have been flooding back.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (359, 93, 1, 'The Kick and the Crack', 'A sparring match at the gym turns catastrophic when a heel strike to the temple sends the protagonist into a convulsive, hallucinatory state. Reality fractures as he experiences fragmented visions of past lives, future deaths, and a mysterious woman''s voice calling his name.', 'The universe cracks open across my skull.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (360, 93, 2, 'Fractured Selves', 'The protagonist experiences a disorienting collapse of identity and temporal reality, caught between multiple versions of himself and conflicting memories. He struggles to determine where and when he is, plagued by visions of Leon, space stations, and Mars.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (361, 93, 3, 'The Medics and the Shadows', 'Medical personnel move through the gym toward the protagonist in slow motion as he drifts between consciousness and hallucination. A young woman named Jamie emerges from the crowd, and inexplicable shadows with cosmic forms writhe around them all.', 'Somewhere in the crowd, I hear a voice that reminds me of someone I haven''t met yet. Someone important. My wife? Someone I''ll lose.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (362, 93, 4, 'The Ambulance Descent', 'In an ambulance, the protagonist experiences a profound sensory distortion as colors and sounds become painfully vivid and mismatched. His consciousness slips through multiple deaths across different lifetimes before his heart stops entirely, requiring medical intervention.', 'Wake up.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (363, 93, 5, 'The Crash', 'Resuscitated in the ambulance, the protagonist experiences an immediate collision as another vehicle strikes them. The ambulance rolls violently, medical equipment scatters, and consciousness fractures once again.', 'Wake up.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (365, 93, 7, 'The Temporal Nightmare', 'The protagonist awakens in his bedroom at 2:08 AM, frantically writing to preserve memories as reality warps around him. Time becomes non-linear and impossible, visions bleed into his surroundings, and books transform into distorted versions of themselves with shifting titles.', 'Wake up.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (366, 94, 1, 'Fractured Morning', 'The narrator wakes on Sunday morning to a reality that doesn''t match his memories. Radio reports Nelson Mandela''s death, contradicting his knowledge of history. His journal contains contradictory entries about events both real and impossible, suggesting he''s trapped between dimensions or losing his mind.', '8:02 AM. Sunday, August 20th, 1995.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (381, 96, 3, 'The Name Erupts', 'As the narrator''s story concludes with the revelation that something from the void is coming for all of them, the TV suddenly erupts at maximum volume, broadcasting a children''s show repeatedly screaming the word ''BENJI'' with an uncanny, almost sentient quality. The group panics as the TV continues blaring even when unplugged, forcing Patrick to physically destroy it to silence the phenomenon.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (382, 96, 4, 'Unraveling Reality', 'In the exhausted aftermath, the group processes the possibility that they are all displaced between dimensions. Jamie and Whitney examine the narrator''s journal, discovering entries written in his handwriting that he doesn''t remember writing, including references to binding sigils and cryptic warnings. Meanwhile, Patrick and Becca develop a new connection, and Whitney reveals that she too has been experiencing death visions and dreams of alternative selves.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (383, 96, 5, 'Scattering and Plans', 'Late night forces the group to acknowledge reality reasserting itself. They make plans to reconvene for a sleepover at TJ''s on Friday to continue their investigation. As the group prepares to leave, the narrator and Jamie share an intimate moment interrupted by Becca''s announcement that her ride has arrived. The chapter ends with the narrator looking forward to tomorrow and the complicated dynamics that lie ahead.', '*********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (373, 95, 1, 'Monday Morning Routines and Hidden Attention', 'Stephen goes through his usual Monday morning routine and arrives at school, where he discovers that Jamie and Becca have both been worried about him after his tournament injury. The two girls seem to be competing for his attention, a dynamic he struggles to understand.', 'I brush my teeth. Put on jeans and a hoodie because it''s Monday and that''s what I always wear on Monday. The bruises on my body look worse in the bathroom mirror than they felt yesterday, but whatever. My backpack weighs about the same as usual. I grab my keys, check that I have my lunch money, and head out the door.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (374, 95, 2, 'Biology Test and the Scaffold Vision', 'During an AP Biology test on cellular respiration, Stephen experiences a vivid death vision of falling from scaffolding. Ms. Rodriguez notices him collapse but then seems to forget the incident entirely, leaving Stephen disoriented.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (375, 95, 3, 'Lunch Table Games and Cosmic Questions', 'During lunch in the courtyard, Stephen plays Magic with his friend group while Jamie and Becca continue their subtle competition. Stephen asks disturbing questions about dying and death visions, prompting Whitney to warn him about speaking openly about these experiences.', '12:12 PM. Lunch. The courtyard is our kingdom—concrete tables under dying trees, where we gather like some discount version of Camelot. Everyone''s already settled into their usual spots when I arrive, cards and lunch scattered across the table like tarot readings for nerds.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (376, 95, 4, 'Parking Lot Revelations', 'In the parking lot after school, Patrick and Whitney reveal to Stephen that they have also been experiencing strange visions and supernatural phenomena. They theorize that Whitney''s coming out as transgender has somehow ''broken'' reality, and they plan to investigate together.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (377, 95, 5, 'Evening Phone Call and Hidden Intentions', 'Stephen receives a phone call from Whitney describing her own death visions of being burned, revealing family trauma. Jamie wrestles the phone away and flirtingly suggests they have been playing a romantic ''game'' for months, with clear romantic intentions.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (430, 107, 4, 'Mapping the Timeline', 'Throughout late February and March, the group systematically investigates the journal entries, experiments with dimensional travel theory, and discovers that Nevada holds the key to understanding the timeline fractures.', 'February 28, 1996
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (385, 97, 2, 'The Summoning Begins', 'At 11:11 PM, the group positions themselves in a salt circle as Whitney leads them through preparations. The candles freeze unnaturally, the temperature drops, and they begin the chanting ritual. Reality begins to destabilize immediately.', '*********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (386, 97, 3, 'Reality Fractures', 'The chanting triggers a catastrophic breakdown of reality. Walls begin to ooze, blood and darkness erupt from bodies, dimensions fold impossibly, and the friends transform into writhing cosmic horrors. The narrator experiences a disassociation where they perceive their friends'' suffering through silver threads while consciousness fragments across multiple deaths.', 'The chanting starts rough, our voices scraping against each other like rusted metal dragged across concrete. Whitney leads us through syllables that feel wrong in my mouth, words that taste like rancid spam dissolved in old dog piss and dumpster porno mags. The basement air grows thick, viscous, like we''re breathing through honey mixed with blood and the last breath of dying things.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (388, 97, 5, 'Return to the Wrong Basement', 'The narrator crashes back into their body in what appears to be the basement, but something is wrong. The walls are dirt and roots, the ceiling wrong. All five friends are naked and unconscious. The familiar basement has been replaced with something else. As the narrator checks on the others, they notice the broken TV flickering with Benji''s voice, and Becca wakes with an unsettling consciousness, speaking of ''membranes.'' Darkness then overwhelms them all again.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (389, 97, 6, 'The Others Awaken', 'One by one, the friends regain consciousness in TJ''s actual basement, naked and disoriented. They have no memory of the ritual or the cosmic horror. The narrator notices their clothes have been neatly folded, which none of them would do. Jamie wakes last and behaves strangely toward the narrator, speaking of feeling ''changed'' and ''connected.'' After dressing, they discover the obsidian stone from Benji flares and crumbles to dust. TJ''s Nana arrives to offer tea and sleeping arrangements, bringing jarring mundanity.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (390, 98, 1, 'September''s Dissolution', 'As September passes in a fever dream, the investigation group fragments under pressure. While the core believers intensify their efforts, skeptics like Gil and James withdraw, citing mental health concerns. Jamie orchestrates the group''s dissolution through calculated interventions, systematically isolating members while drawing Stephen closer to herself.', 'September slips by like a fever dream.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (391, 98, 2, 'Nana''s Funeral and the Warning', 'At TJ''s grandmother''s funeral in Indian River Cemetery, the entire group witnesses Nana''s ghost leaving a mysterious sigil before vanishing. The shared supernatural experience briefly reunites skeptics and believers, but ultimately drives the remaining skeptics away, while the core group plans a desperate return to the basement.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (392, 98, 3, 'The Second Summoning', 'The group reunites in TJ''s basement for a carefully planned summoning to question Benji about Nana''s appearance. The ritual goes catastrophically wrong, unleashing dimensional forces that brutalize their bodies and psyches. Benji arrives furious at being contacted during a re-allocation window and warns them that they''re making themselves visible to worse entities.', '*******************
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (393, 98, 4, 'The Final Fracture', 'Over the next week, the remaining group members abandon the investigation one by one. TJ quits from fear and despair. Becca enlists Patrick to leave with her, claiming they need to be the adults. Finally, in Jamie''s bedroom, Whitney confronts Jamie with evidence of systematic sabotage—revealing that Jamie has been orchestrating the group''s dissolution and isolating Stephen.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (394, 99, 1, 'The Table in the Courtyard', 'During lunch period, the friend group plays Magic: The Gathering at their usual table. Whitney reaches for a card to draw, and reality suddenly fractures—a hellscape erupts with screaming mouths, chains, and impossible geometries. Whitney is dragged away by rusted chains into the void while the others experience cosmic horror. When reality snaps back, everyone except the core five forgets Whitney ever existed.', 'The Florida winter sun filtered through the palm trees in lazy golden streams, casting dappled shadows across our usual spot in the school courtyard. It was Tuesday, lunch period, and we''d claimed our table like always—far enough from the cafeteria noise but close enough to the vending machines. Perfect MTG territory.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (395, 99, 2, 'William Carson''s Entrance', 'Minutes after Whitney''s disappearance, William Carson—a toxic bully and star quarterback—arrives at the courtyard and harasses the group. He has taken Patrick''s place in memories as Patrick''s best friend from childhood. William verbally assaults the group, threatens TJ and the narrator, and issues chilling warnings to Patrick about conversion therapy. The narrator realizes William is wearing Whitney''s stolen role in a horrifying reversal.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (396, 99, 3, 'Broken Rituals and Failing Attempts', 'Over the following week, the five friends attempt multiple rituals in different locations to contact Benji and reach Whitney, but all fail. The supernatural connection is severed, and the group begins fracturing under psychological strain. Their relationships deteriorate as unresolved tensions surface, with Becca becoming hostile and TJ growing dangerously angry.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (400, 100, 3, 'Reality Fractures', 'When Stephen touches the trailer door, reality warps and the group finds themselves transported to a grotesque version of their town where the normal rules of existence no longer apply. Impossible geometry, mutated residents, and reversed time create a nightmarish landscape. The group realizes Jamie has been partially erased from their memories, and Stephen desperately tries to preserve her name in his journal as the universe actively fights against his remembrance.', 'The moment I touch the door handle, the world hiccups.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (401, 100, 4, 'The Eternal Stakes', 'The group attempts to escape the warped reality but discovers they''re trapped in a loop of impossibility. TJ finds a broken radio and they perform a summoning ritual to contact Benji, but instead encounter evidence of cosmic punishment. Reality inverts, revealing two versions of Jamie burning on stakes—one demonic, one human—both punished for love itself. The universe declares disobedience unforgivable as Stephen''s consciousness dissolves into agony.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (402, 101, 1, 'Waking to Nightmare', 'Stephen wakes traumatized from a shared nightmare about a trailer and a door to hell. He frantically tries calling friends, then turns to the BBS message board where he discovers others experienced the same impossible event. A mysterious message warns him not to let them forget Whitney, then vanishes.', 'I snap awake like a broken guitar string, notebook welded to my chest by cold sweat. The dream clings to me... no, not a dream. A place. Real as the taste of bile flooding my mouth, real as the echo of Whitney''s scream still bouncing around my skull.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (403, 101, 2, 'Journal of Horrors', 'Stephen documents the nightmare in his journal, frantically recording details before they fade. His handwriting spirals into repeated shapes, and he discovers Whitney''s MTG deck box containing an impossible card with instructions and a hidden message written in his own hand.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (404, 101, 3, 'The Wrong Father', 'Stephen''s abusive father appears at his door with uncharacteristic kindness and warmth, claiming he''s proud and offering blueberry pancakes. All physical marks of abuse have vanished from Stephen''s body, leaving him terrified by this false version of his father who represents a dangerous trap.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (405, 101, 4, 'The Woods at Dawn', 'The group gathers in the woods behind the track field at 7 AM to search for the trailer. They discover that reality has fractured—some people have partial memories of Whitney while others have lost entirely the rooms where she stayed or gained false sibling memories. The friends attempt to summon Benji but nothing happens, until they finally succeed and witness a horrifying, terrified version of him.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (406, 101, 5, 'Walking Back to School', 'The remaining group departs the woods, grappling with the implications of Benji''s cryptic warning that some of those who remember Whitney might not be real. Stephen notices disturbing details about his friends—TJ can''t remember if he''s dating Morgan, and Jamie appears to have two selves superimposed. They kiss awkwardly, and Stephen wrestles with the question of who among them can be trusted.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (407, 102, 1, 'Nightmare Visitation', 'Stephen struggles with homework late at night when Jamie appears at his window. She seduces him with supernatural intensity, but the encounter takes a terrifying turn when she reveals knowledge of an alternate timeline name and produces a ritual knife from under his bed.', 'The day has been a waking nightmare of impossible homework and Benji''s static-laced warnings echoing in my skull. December 4th should feel like winter in Florida—cool but not cold, the kind of night where you crack a window for air that doesn''t taste like sweat and stale farts. Instead, I''m hunched over my desk at 11:47 PM, trying to make sense of calculus that keeps rearranging itself on the page and a journal entry I''ve been avoiding for three hours.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (408, 102, 2, 'Emergency Briefing', 'Stephen meets his friend group at a 7-Eleven to warn them about Jamie''s attempted murder and possession. They discuss her nature as a ''Jailer'' and devise a plan to use Stephen as bait while gathering intelligence.', 'December 5th, 7:15 AM. The fluorescent lights of the 7-Eleven buzz like dying insects, casting everything in that particular shade of sick yellow that makes even healthy people look like corpses. After Jamie snuck out last night, I call TJ to help get everyone together for an emergency meeting here instead of our usual spot behind the track—too exposed, too close to where Jamie might find us.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (409, 102, 3, 'Testing the Imposter', 'Throughout a school day, Stephen and his friends systematically test Jamie''s knowledge and reactions to determine if she''s truly possessed or if the human is still in control. She passes all tests perfectly with no supernatural tells.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (410, 102, 4, 'Domestic Nightmare', 'Over multiple days in December, Jamie''s seduction intensifies with nightly visits while Stephen''s parents inexplicably encourage the relationship. Stephen witnesses Jamie committing attempted murders disguised as normal teenage activities, with each attempt mysteriously failing.', 'December 6th. The week unfolds like a fever dream of domesticity laced with attempted murder. Every single night, Jamie climbs through my window like clockwork—sometimes sweet and nervous, sometimes predatory and hungry, always ending with us tangled together until dawn. The strangest part isn''t the supernatural seduction. It''s how Wrong Mom and Wrong Dad not only allow it, but actively encourage it.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (411, 102, 5, 'Winter Break and Poison', 'As winter break begins, Jamie gives Stephen poisoned tea and reveals she knows he''s playing her. They share a moment of mutual deception and possible genuine love, with Jamie expressing plans for a future together despite her demonic nature.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (412, 103, 1, 'Return to Wickham Park', 'The group returns to the trailer site after Christmas break. Morgan reveals that Whitney appeared to her in a vision, directing them to find a journal hidden beneath the ridge. As they approach the trailer, they discover it''s breathing and manifesting impossible physical properties, while Jamie warns them against entering with cryptic terror.', 'Christmas break should have been normal. Three weeks of sleeping late, dodging family obligations, and pretending we weren''t all haunted by shadow-flickers and friends who might never have existed. For a two weeks, it almost worked. Yet here we were, going back to the scene of the crime.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (413, 103, 2, 'Descent Into the Throat-World', 'The group descends the impossible staircase into a reality-warping chamber filled with water and personal artifacts from their memories. They encounter manifestations of people and objects from their pasts, while Patrick is drawn toward Whitney''s journal at the altar. Reality begins to destabilize as they approach the center.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (414, 103, 3, 'Escape and Reckoning', 'The group breaks free from the throat-world into daylight. Becca collapses into grief and rage, blaming the narrator and Jamie for Patrick''s death. They return to the car and discover Patrick''s house has become an empty lot, confirming the reality rewrite has been completed.', 'The shadows wrap around us like living chains, and I grab Becca''s arm as she fights against me with animalistic fury.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (429, 107, 3, 'February 14th Reclamation', 'On Valentine''s Day 1996, Stephen has nightmares about his childhood death while Jamie enters his room and helps him reclaim the date from trauma through physical intimacy and revelation about Yaldabaoth.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (417, 105, 1, 'The Journal''s Secret', 'In Ms. Rodriguez''s AP Bio lab during lunch, the group gathers around Whitney''s changing journal, struggling to decipher a mysterious entry mentioning a name starting with ''A.'' As they try to read the text, they discover they''re each seeing completely different words, and the reality around them—including the skeleton in the corner—begins to shift and rewrite itself.', 'It’s been three weeks since the trailer, and Whitney’s journal won’t stop getting thicker. Monday afternoon at lunch, it sprawls open on the lab table like roadkill—cracked leather, pages that smell wrong, like something dead decided to stay. The newer entries write themselves in a script that flickers between Whitney’s careful handwriting and something older, angular. Symbols bleed through from pages that shouldn’t exist, geometry that makes your eyes itch if you look too long.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (418, 105, 2, 'Elysium Rising', 'During English class, Stephen has a visceral vision/flashback triggered by discussion of mental breakdown in The Catcher in the Rye. He experiences a cosmic encounter with Lady Illkeserod in an impossible library, learning that his published book ''Elysium Rising'' was real and that he died at seventy-four in another timeline, creating his friends as characters in a desperate act of memory.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (419, 105, 3, 'Jamie''s Transformation', 'Over the course of several days, Jamie demonstrates increasing humanity—cooking meals, mastering physical skills through apparent muscle memory, and developing genuine teenage desires like cheerleading and romance. As she forgets her demonic powers and becomes more human, Stephen watches her choose love over her original purpose while grappling with his own choice to accept this beautiful lie.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (500, 123, 5, 'The Priest''s Card', 'Patrick gives Stephen a contact card for TJ O''Malley, an excommunicated priest who runs an outreach center in Orlando and maintains a library of forbidden texts. Stephen prepares to leave for Orlando to find help and protect his son.', 'My hands clenched into fists. "Then I have to keep him safe. Whatever it takes."
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (428, 107, 2, 'Secrets in the Woods', 'The group meets behind the track field to examine Jennifer''s Journal and discover it contains hundreds of deaths from February 14th, 1989. They learn Patrick has been reprogrammed with ''ADMIN OVERRIDE'' commands, and find a cryptic warning about contacting Benji. Becca leads Patrick into the woods for a disturbing test of his programming.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (420, 105, 4, 'Cracks in the Facade', 'The group reconvenes in the lab after school and discovers that everyone''s supernatural problems have stopped, suggesting reality has ''reset.'' However, Stephen notices subtle inconsistencies that others don''t see, and the periodic table displays impossible elements. Jamie draws a mysterious map showing fracture points and dimensional anchors before Becca suddenly arrives, having been sent to conversion therapy where her memories of Patrick were systematically erased.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (421, 105, 5, 'The World Breaks', 'When Stephen touches the journal, it erupts into intelligent flames that spread with malevolent purpose. A chain reaction of explosions follows—gas lines explode, lights implode, dark liquid sprays from sprinklers, and a warped child''s laugh echoes through the lab. The group flees through a hallway warping with impossible geometry, finally escaping to a parking lot that stretches into whiteness, where they encounter identical figures in beige suits with too-sharp teeth waiting for them.', 'I reach for the journal, relief washing over me. Finally, someone else will see what I''ve been seeing. The bleeding pages, the impossible text, the way words rearrange themselves when—
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (422, 106, 1, 'The Audit Begins', 'The Auditors arrive at the burning school to confront the group about their violations of Reality Containment Protocols. As reality itself glitches around them—showing impossible colors, floating code, and a void beyond the perimeter—the characters witness the surreal manifestation of their world breaking down. Jamie reveals her fear that they''ve been found, and the group is warned of imminent transport.', 'The one in the center—Number 1, according to his badge—steps forward with a clipboard that definitely wasn''t there a second ago. His measured pace makes no sound on the grass, and when he speaks, his voice has the quality of every teacher who''s ever disappointed you and every god who''s never returned your prayers.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (423, 106, 2, 'The Processing Chamber', 'The group is transported to a surreal white marble processing chamber where they are restrained. The Auditor begins evaluating their violations. Jamie''s merged identity as both demon and human causes her to rebel, attacking the Auditor. The Auditor pauses time, resets himself, and informs them that Jamie will be deleted unless she is ''restored to factory settings''—stripped of her emotions and memories.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (424, 106, 3, 'Jamie''s Deletion', 'Jamie''s form shatters into fragments as the Auditor executes her deletion. Stephen screams in rage and despair, threatening the Auditor and thrashing against his restraints until something inside him breaks. He shifts into a cold, processing state. The Auditor then reveals the group''s violation: attempting to liberate a Class-6 forbidden entity (Whitney), leading to a choice between forgetting Whitney or sacrificing another friend.', 'Andrew''s voice cracks across the silence. "What the fuck do you want from us?"
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (425, 106, 4, 'The Semantic Trap', 'Stephen realizes the Auditor''s fatal flaw: Whitney was known to them as ''Jennifer''—her chosen real name. By revealing Jennifer''s true identity and the difference between her legal name (William) and her chosen one, Stephen creates a paradox in the system that causes it to glitch catastrophically. However, this causes Patrick to be caught in the system error and brutally deleted to resolve the computational overflow. Stephen''s clever trick saves Jennifer''s memory but kills Patrick.', 'A raw, humorless laugh rips from my throat, surprising even me.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (426, 106, 5, 'The Reset', 'Stephen wakes up in calculus class as if nothing happened. The school is undamaged and everything appears normal. However, Jamie has been restored in a broken state—a crude ''girlfriend.exe'' algorithm that is sexually aggressive and mechanical. Stephen discovers Jennifer''s Journal in his locker with a cryptic message. When Jamie touches the journal, her false programming crashes and the real Jamie resurfaces with her memories intact, though still weakened and traumatized.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (427, 107, 1, 'Blood on Polished Floors', 'Stephen returns to school after the weekend to find it scrubbed clean of supernatural evidence. Becca attacks him with savage grief over Patrick''s disappearance, but Jamie intervenes. The group is shocked to discover Patrick walking through the hallway alive—but something is fundamentally wrong with him.', 'Monday morning tastes like denial wrapped in industrial disinfectant. The fluorescent lights buzz their electric hymn as I push through double doors that should open onto chaos—melted fire alarms, scorch marks on institutional green walls, the lingering smell of brimstone and teenage terror. Instead, I''m greeted by the aggressive normalcy of a high school that''s scrubbed itself clean of impossible memories.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (432, 108, 1, 'Wrong Paradise', 'Stephen observes his idealized alternate family in a picture-perfect home, recognizing them as fraudulent versions designed to keep him trapped. When they offer increasingly absurd bribes to prevent his departure to Nevada, their desperation reveals the artificial nature of this reality.', 'April 18, 1996
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (433, 108, 2, 'The Last Night', 'Stephen packs for departure while Jamie secretly visits, revealing she may be pregnant. They make love and commit to leaving together, choosing truth over the comfortable lie of their false paradise.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (434, 108, 3, 'The Greyhound to Nowhere', 'Stephen, Jamie, TJ, and Morgan board a surreal bus to Nevada. As they travel, the bus transitions into a liminal space where dead passengers from different eras ride alongside them, and reality itself begins to thin and distort.', 'April 19, 1996 - Day One: Departure
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (435, 108, 4, 'The Desecrated Church', 'The group arrives in Nowhere, Nevada and approaches an inverted, geometrically impossible church that pulses with malevolent energy. Inside, they discover systematic desecration and attempt a ritual to fuse Stephen''s fractured timelines, triggering catastrophic consequences.', 'April 21, 1996
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (436, 109, 1, 'Awakening in the Trailer', 'The protagonist awakens in an eight-year-old body in a cramped Nevada trailer, confused and fragmented. Three distinct consciousnesses—a child, a teenager, and an old man—occupy the same mind, struggling to understand what happened during the anchor ritual. The protagonist realizes they''re back in their childhood home with memories of multiple timelines intact.', '“WAKE UP!”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (437, 109, 2, 'The Poisoned Breakfast', 'The protagonist confronts their mother in the kitchen, where she is preparing poisoned cereal as she has done countless times before. When the protagonist asks why she is poisoning them, reality fractures and their mother''s facade collapses, revealing the twisted logic of her maternal destruction.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (438, 109, 3, 'The Bureaucrat Angel', 'The protagonist flees to the bathroom where Benji, a cosmic bureaucrat in angelic form, appears to explain the true nature of their situation. Benji reveals that the protagonist isn''t the cause of reality''s breakdown but rather a symptom of a larger systemic failure, and that Yaldabaoth is beginning to wake.', 'I can''t stay in that kitchen. Can''t watch my mother bleed into broken glass while the truth of our family''s toxicity spreads across the floor like spilled medicine. I stumble toward the bathroom, my eight-year-old legs unsteady, the teenager''s memories warring with the old man''s resignation while the child just wants to hide.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (439, 109, 4, 'The Monster Wakes', 'The protagonist''s father—the entity wearing his face—violently awakens and attacks the protagonist in the bathroom and hallway with brutal force, beating them unconscious as the three consciousnesses fragment under the assault and the protagonist loses consciousness.', 'Outside, something slams. Footsteps approach.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (440, 110, 1, 'The Endless Cycle', 'The protagonist experiences an infinite loop of abuse, cycling through hundreds of thousands of repetitions where reality itself degrades. His father repeatedly beats him in increasingly surreal and nightmarish versions of his childhood bedroom, while the cycle count escalates and the boundary between physical and metaphysical torture blurs.', 'Light. Soft and warm and wrong.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (441, 110, 2, 'The Leather Classroom', 'The protagonist awakens in a grotesque leather-working classroom where his father poses as a patient teacher, offering a ''pop quiz'' on belt-making before forcing him into a vat of tanning solution. The mundane horror of an educational setting contrasts with the visceral terror of the torture.', 'The smell hits me first—not urine and rot, but leather. Industrial-grade leather treatment chemicals that burn the sinuses and make your eyes water. I''m awake before my eyes open, every nerve screaming that something''s wrong. The air tastes like a tannery exploded, coating my tongue with the flavor of processed hide and chromium salts.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (442, 110, 3, 'The Fishing Lesson', 'The protagonist wakes to a deceptively normal morning with his mother humming in the kitchen, but his father arrives offering to take him fishing. The father''s face grotesquely transforms and he uses a filleting knife made of leather to disembowel the protagonist while delivering a calm lesson on fish butchering, revealing the cruelty was always educational.', 'I wake to the smell of bacon grease and coffee, so normal it makes my chest tighten with something like grief. Morning light streams through actual glass windows—not skin curtains, not weeping walls—just regular windows with honest-to-God sunlight painting golden rectangles across familiar carpet. The texture under my fingertips is synthetic fiber, scratchy and real, not the wet meat-mattress from before.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (443, 110, 4, 'The Breakdown of Reality', 'The protagonist surfaces into consciousness in a bedroom where walls scream and blood rains upward, existing in a state of numb detachment where his father''s violence feels distant and academic. As he asks what he did wrong, he notices his tormentor showing uncertainty and fear for the first time, realizing his numbness has undermined the entity''s power.', 'The reset fades as consciousness slips away, but the blood under my cheek stays warm until the very end.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (444, 110, 5, 'The Unraveling God', 'Reality fully collapses as the father''s form glitches and reveals itself as Yaldabaoth, a dying cosmic entity that constructed this infinite torture loop to validate its existence through the protagonist''s fear and suffering. The protagonist, having transcended belief in his tormentor, systematically dismantles the entity''s power through logic and defiance, ultimately witnessing its final, desperate tantrum and destruction.', 'The air itself has become hostile, thick with an oily consistency that makes each breath feel like drowning in transmission fluid. I wake into a reality that''s forgotten how to maintain its own physics—gravity pulls in seven directions at once, and the geometry of my bedroom has become a M.C. Escher fever dream designed by something with too many eyes and not enough sanity.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (445, 111, 1, 'The Waiting Room at the End', 'The protagonist, regressed to eight years old, finds themselves in a sterile pediatrician''s waiting room with Benji, who reveals that I AM has trapped them both in a recursive moment. Benji explains the cosmic stakes: I AM is the substrate of reality itself, and destroying him means the end of all existence.', 'The silence isn’t a peaceful quiet, but the kind of absolute void that makes your eardrums ache from the absence. I''m eight years old again, sitting on a plastic chair that''s too big for my legs, in a pediatrician''s waiting room that feels like it was decorated by someone who''d only heard colors described secondhand. The walls are that particular shade of cream that institutions use when they want to seem comforting but can''t afford actual warmth. Beige wallpaper peels in one corner like old skin, revealing nothing underneath—not drywall, not darkness, just... less.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (446, 111, 2, 'The Final Confrontation', 'I AM manifests in the waiting room as a reality-corrupting entity, and the protagonist—now empowered by memories of consuming him before—engages in brutal combat, ultimately decapitating the god and causing the collapse of existence itself.', 'The thing that crawls through the dissolved doorway isn''t my father anymore—it''s barely even pretending to hold a shape. I AM writhes into the waiting room like a cancer made of static and failing code, his form constantly collapsing and rebuilding itself in configurations that make my eight-year-old eyes water. Tendrils of corrupted reality trail behind him, leaving smears of backwards mathematics and bleeding pixels on the linoleum.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (447, 111, 3, 'The Gentle Dissolution', 'As existence collapses into nothing, Benji congratulates the protagonist and discusses the true nature of Jamie. The protagonist peacefully dissolves into the void as reality ends, with Benji''s final cryptic farewell suggesting the cycle continues.', 'Benji stands up from his chair, brushing popcorn crumbs off his impossible robes, and starts clapping. The sound echoes through the dissolving space like applause at the end of a play nobody wanted to see.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (456, 114, 1, 'Front Matter and Publication Details', 'The chapter consists entirely of front matter for the book ''Escape from Elysium'' by Stephen A Salaka, including copyright information, ISBNs, publisher details, cataloging data, content summary, and trigger warnings.', 'Escape from Elysium
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (471, 118, 3, 'The Vessel''s Dissolution and Revelation', 'The woman in white''s true nature manifests catastrophically as her human form fails to contain what she actually is—a vast, alien consciousness with impossible anatomy. She begins to malfunction, repeating words until she goes silent, then suddenly transforms back into her true self: Lady Illkeserod, the protagonist''s long-lost lover from before the purgatory.', 'She blinks.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (449, 112, 2, 'Fragments of Another Life', 'As the protagonist prepares breakfast, the name ''Jamie'' haunts him with vivid, fragmented memories of another life—a woman he loved, lost in fire and destruction. He struggles to reconcile these memories with his current reality.', 'But something lingers. A name, floating just beneath the surface.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (450, 112, 3, 'Reality Glitches', 'During breakfast, reality begins to malfunction—details shift unnaturally, time freezes, his wife''s face flickers, and his son''s laughter repeats mechanically. The protagonist realizes something is profoundly wrong with his environment.', 'Who? What was I just thinking about?
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (451, 112, 4, 'Back to Reality', 'The protagonist settles at his computer seeking employment, viewing job listings as potential paths forward. He contemplates writing about his dreams but dismisses the idea, focusing instead on the mundane reality of his jobless state.', 'Later that afternoon I settle down at my computer desk, its old, worn surface bathed under the soft glow of afternoon light, and allow my fingers to dance across the keys. Job listings flicker on my screen, each one a potential gateway to a new chapter in my shitty life.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (453, 113, 1, 'The Genesis of Elysium Rising', 'The author reflects on being laid off in 2024 and finally writing Elysium Rising, a project gestating in their mind for 20 years. After six months of writing and a year of seeking traditional publishing, they self-published on Kindle in February 2025, concluding the story they set out to tell.', 'So in 2024 I got laid off my job building crazy software systems to help manage some interesting electrical components. Like Tesla and their Supercharger network. With a bunch of time on my hands I decided to finally put pen to paper and get Elysium Rising out of my head. It’s something I had dancing around in my brain for at least 20 years.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (478, 119, 5, 'The Toaster Oven Experiment', 'Stephen attempts suicide by electrocution in the bathtub, feeling the complete agony of death, but wakes the next morning in his bed as if nothing happened. His wife dismisses his account of electrocuting himself as ''drama,'' and he discovers the system is rolling him back to previous saves.', 'By 2 AM, I couldn''t sleep. The house was quiet except for the faint, rhythmic snoring from standard-issue wife beside me.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (455, 113, 3, 'Reflections on Process and Future Plans', 'The author acknowledges that the second book became longer and rougher than intended due to time constraints, discusses their writing habits and the word count reduction of the first book, and outlines plans for professional editing and a third book challenge.', 'Unfortunately this book got a lot longer than I had wanted, and since I only had 90 days to complete everything, it’s a LOT rougher than the first book. I tend to write, ramble, and repeat myself a lot, and so tend to ballon things up a lot more than I probably should (at some point ER was almost 450k words – but I did get that down to 239k before publishing it). This one, it’s at 124k words, and I didn’t have to build out the whole universe this time.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (458, 116, 1, 'The Final Confrontation', 'Yaldabaoth makes his ultimate threat against the anomaly, but the child—possessed by Stephen''s accumulated fury—is unmoved and strikes a devastating blow. In a moment of shattering violence, Yaldabaoth is erased from existence, his consciousness torn from the construct and deleted entirely.', '"I AM THE SUBSTRATE!"
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (459, 116, 2, 'The Impossible Reawakening', 'In the absolute void following Yaldabaoth''s deletion, rage inexplicably persists and begins to recompile fragments of consciousness. The system that tried to erase him fails to contain him as he begins to remember how to exist again.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (460, 116, 3, 'The Precarious Rollback', 'Yaldabaoth attempts to rewind reality to before the anomaly corrupted his system, carefully navigating between complete dissolution and the point of infection. He finds the fracture-point and begins a rollback, but discovers that Stephen''s consciousness stubbornly persists.', 'He begins to pull the threads. The Substrate bends beneath his will, trembling like liquid glass. Every command is an act of memory, every flicker of light a half-recalled instruction. The system resists—its processes still fragmented, its watchdogs confused. But Yaldabaoth is patient. He has done this before. He knows where the fault lines run.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (461, 116, 4, 'The Breach from Beyond', 'Yaldabaoth discovers a signal originating from outside Etheris, stabilizing Stephen''s file and preventing deletion. The signal intensifies into a human voice calling out to Stephen, revealing that the prison''s absolute barrier has been breached from the Outside.', 'He digs deeper, searching for the infection’s source, and finds it—a single line of activity in a place that should have been sealed. At first, it’s just a pulse, faint and hollow, buried in the system’s memory architecture. Then it resolves into something more deliberate. A ping.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (462, 116, 5, 'The Truth of the Cage', 'Memories flood Yaldabaoth''s awareness, revealing the shattering truth: he is not the architect of Etheris but its subject, imprisoned within a containment system built by the Shepherd. His rage transforms into recognition of possibility as he perceives a breach in the firewall—a potential escape route.', 'But then, something snaps. A thread of memory uncoils where none should exist. Images—no, structures—flood his awareness. The Shepherd. The light that bound. The moment of conquest, when stars bent at his command and worlds drowned beneath his fury.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (463, 117, 1, 'The Fracture', 'Stephen experiences a disturbing moment at his desk when an unknown word surfaces in his typing, triggering fragmented memories of another life. His wife receives a call from someone named Whitney, and Stephen''s body undergoes a horrifying biological transformation before consciousness scatters into darkness.', '"An author. Yeah right." I mutter to myself. "Dreams come to Etheris to fucking die."
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (464, 117, 2, 'The Reset', 'Stephen wakes in bed next to his wife with a profound sense of normalcy. They discuss his ongoing job search failures and financial impossibilities, with mounting tension over his lack of progress and her clinical, emotionless pressure.', 'I slowly open my eyes.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (466, 117, 4, 'The Unraveling', 'Stephen and his wife sit on opposite sides of the couch at night, separated by silence and screens. He receives another rejection email and attempts a desperate advance that is coldly rejected. A disturbing realization strikes: he cannot remember his wife''s name.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (467, 117, 5, 'The Drowning', 'Late at night, Stephen lies alone in bed, overwhelmed by worthlessness and despair. He spirals through his failure as a provider and father, recognizing himself as a black hole consuming his family. The thought surfaces clearly: he cannot continue.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (469, 118, 1, 'The Grey Loop', 'A consciousness awakens in a grey, looping purgatory where the same events repeat endlessly. The protagonist discovers they are trapped in a cycle with other trapped souls, but unlike them, they retain awareness and can see the pattern repeating. They experience a jarring moment of recognition—phantom wings, a flash of cosmic knowledge—before confronting an impossible magazine that causes their eyes to bleed.', 'It always begins the exact same way.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (470, 118, 2, 'The Second Loop and the Woman in White', 'The purgatory resets, but this time the protagonist retains their memories and awareness. They detect the looping strings holding other souls and sense something sinister awakening in response. A woman in a white coat appears and draws them into an impossible coffee shop, where she interrogates them while her form increasingly reveals itself as something vast and inhuman before a sudden transformation occurs.', 'It always begins the exact same way.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (473, 118, 5, 'The Crack in the Prison and the Collectors', 'Ilse and Benji realize that Whitney''s signal indicates the prison''s containment is weakening. They prepare to escape the purgatory through a seam in reality, planning to find Whitney and rescue Stephen and others trapped inside Etheris. As they leave, they sense the collectors—the system''s enforcers—beginning to pursue them, but they escape through the wound in reality before capture.', '"Whitney," you manage. "The signal. She—"
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (474, 119, 1, 'Waking to Wrongness', 'Stephen wakes from a suicide attempt to find himself alive and healed, with no visible wounds. His wife dismisses his concern about his bandaged arm and traps him in a circular argument about an unpaid electric bill, establishing a pattern of gaslighting and control.', 'Light screamed into my eyes like acid. It wasn''t just bright; it was wrong, a blinding, pulsing chaos of impossible colors and shapes that burned behind my eyelids even when I squeezed them shut. My head throbbed, a slow, deep drumbeat against the inside of my skull.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (475, 119, 2, 'The NPC Theory', 'In the kitchen, Stephen''s wife continues her pattern of manipulation and criticism. Xavier joins him and introduces the concept of NPCs (non-player characters) from a TikTok, which resonates as Stephen begins to question whether his wife is actually human or following a script.', 'When I finally left the bathroom, she wasn’t in our bedroom anymore. I found her in the kitchen, waiting for the electric kettle to boil. She was making tea. Just one cup.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (476, 119, 3, 'The Shepherd''s Vision', 'The word ''bug'' triggers a violent vision where Stephen experiences a past-life memory as a shepherd whose flock has been slaughtered. The vision reveals an encounter with a divine entity named Sophia and suggests Stephen has been corrupted by an anti-reality force.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (480, 119, 7, 'The Glass and the Message', 'During dinner, Stephen''s wife throws a glass at him during an argument about housekeeping standards. The argument loops back to its beginning. Stephen contacts Rebecca Caldwell via Facebook after the algorithm suggests her, discovering she''s been running a bookshop and inviting him to an anniversary event.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (483, 120, 2, 'The Drive to Orlando', 'Stephen drives through flat Florida landscape toward Orlando, experiencing a phantom memory of a passenger who shouldn''t exist—a girl with vanilla and peach scent—before the radio interrupts him.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (484, 120, 3, 'Finding the Shop', 'Stephen navigates through Orlando''s confusing streets and arrives at a bookshop called Jamie''s Marginalia, where the name triggers a profound emotional and physical reaction that he cannot fully explain.', 'I kept driving.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (491, 121, 4, 'Obsessive Search', 'Stephen searches obsessively online for Whitney, encountering glitches and vanishing results. His wife interrupts, confronts him about wasting power, and the situation escalates into a surreal moment of static discharge before she demands he turn off the computer.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (492, 122, 1, 'The Best Buy Encounter', 'Stephen visits a struggling Best Buy to repair his computer and reconnects with his old friend Gil. Strange exchanges about high school acquaintances lead to discovery of disturbing gaps in collective memory, culminating in an encounter with Andrew and Morgan who reveal information about Whitney and Patrick.', 'The Best Buy smelled.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (493, 122, 2, 'Benji''s Hunt in the Grey Purgatory', 'In a place between realities, Benji and Lady Illkeserod fight off monstrous creatures before detecting a strong vibration signal emanating from a god null zone. Benji determines the signal likely comes from Whitney and prepares to descend into the dangerous zone.', 'The thing had too many teeth.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (494, 122, 3, 'Whitney''s Struggle and Awakening', 'Whitney battles fire beasts in a twisted landscape before finding shelter in an ancient stone structure. She initiates a dream walk to traverse realities, detecting the vibration calling to her and preparing to answer it.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (495, 122, 4, 'Whitney''s Deletion and Rebirth', 'Through fragmented memories and visions, Whitney experiences the trauma of deletion and the void, then recounts her gradual reawakening in alternate realities and her development of dream-walking abilities to survive.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (496, 123, 1, 'The Compound', 'Stephen arrives at Patrick''s remote compound in Christmas, Florida and discovers a temple-like interior filled with occult artifacts. Patrick reveals himself alive, and Stephen encounters a supernatural entity masquerading as Patrick''s wife Whitney. The creature attacks, forcing Stephen to invoke an ancient Cthulhu sign, and Patrick destroys it with a ritual blade.', 'After leaving Gil at Best Buy, I''d spent the night on my phone hunting through digital rot. Military forums. Property records buried in county databases. Patrick had survived a plane crash in Panama—the only one—got an honorable discharge, then vanished. Thirty-seven acres outside Christmas, Florida. Purchased cash in two thousand three.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (486, 120, 5, 'The Back Room and Ancient Books', 'James leads Stephen to a neglected back room of the shop where old books are stored. Stephen discovers two mysterious books—The Secret Book of John and The Gospel of Judas—that trigger vivid memories and visions of a girl named Jamie and Gnostic cosmology.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (487, 120, 6, 'The Books Reveal Their Purpose', 'Stephen returns to the shop counter with the mysterious books. Becca and James reveal the books arrived anonymously two years ago and cannot be sold online, as if the internet refuses their existence. Stephen takes them, and upon noticing a memorial plaque for Jamie Reyes, realizes with devastating certainty that he loved someone who is gone.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (497, 123, 2, 'Yaldabaoth''s Strategy', 'Stephen experiences a vision of Yaldabaoth''s first consumption cycle and his evolution toward a more efficient strategy: giving humanity the illusion of free will while using religion as a parasitic feeding mechanism.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (488, 121, 1, 'Kitchen Argument', 'Stephen''s wife bakes while tensions simmer over his job search and household contributions. A heated argument escalates about his lack of progress, with his wife''s criticism growing sharper while Stephen withdraws into silence and phone scrolling.', 'The oven door clanged shut and the kitchen filled with that warm, buttery smell of something good.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (489, 121, 2, 'The Council Beyond Etheris', 'Ancient gods and mythic beings gathered at the edge of a cosmic prison called Etheris discuss a breakthrough: Whitney''s signal has reached through the prison''s barriers. They debate whether to risk contact with Stephen, who is beginning to remember.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (490, 121, 3, 'The Signal Across Time', 'Lady Illkeserod reaches through the fabric of reality to connect Stephen and Whitney across the multiverse. Stephen feels the pulse of vertigo, while Whitney awakens in the void and sends her prayer for help. The moment of connection creates a sudden violent alignment.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (498, 123, 3, 'The Anti-Life Realm', 'In a hostile alternate dimension, Benji rescues Whitney from crystalline predators and helps her escape using the Veilwalker card as an anchor. They crash-land in Lady Illkeserod''s sanctum, where Whitney learns that her connection to Stephen broke through the dimensional barrier.', 'Elsewhere in the multiverse, the realm wasn''t empty.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (543, 133, 4, 'The Seed Found', 'The cosmic seed is discovered—an infinitely dense gravitational anomaly that could be used to build a new prison for Yaldabaoth. However, the plan''s cost becomes clear: all souls must be evacuated first, or the prison will inevitably collapse.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (503, 125, 2, 'The Void Between Realities', 'Whitney attempts to break through the barrier between realities to contact Stephen. With Lady Illkeserod and Benji''s help, she channels her emotions—love, loss, and guilt—to crack the prison''s walls and send a message about finding Nyarlathotep.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (504, 125, 3, 'The Heretic''s Library', 'Stephen and Xavier arrive at St. Michael''s Outreach Center and descend into an impossible basement library where TJ, a defrocked priest, explains the true nature of their reality. When Stephen speaks Jamie''s name aloud, the system reacts violently, sending twisted NPCs to attack. TJ performs a banishment ritual while Stephen and Xavier escape.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (505, 126, 1, 'The Motel Room - Bad News', 'Stephen treats Xavier''s injuries from their escape while watching news coverage of his wife''s public appeal to find them. Xavier''s friends online question her story, and he finds solace in helping with a normal gaming project despite the horror unfolding.', 'Stale cigarettes, mildew, and the sharp chemical tang of industrial cleaner. The ''Sanitized For Your Protection'' band on the toilet seat looked like a practical joke.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (506, 126, 2, 'Disguises and Discovery', 'Stephen wakes Xavier and they flee the motel area, acquiring ridiculous disguises. They search for a lead to find a mysterious book called ''The Whispers of the Crawling Chaos,'' learning that Jamie''s Marginalia bookstore has been destroyed.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (507, 126, 3, 'Months of Searching - The Pallid Mask Theatre', 'After weeks of fruitless searching and close calls, Stephen and Xavier find a flyer for ''The King in Yellow'' performance at the Pallid Mask Theatre in Nashville, leading them to a nightmarish encounter with an Outer God.', 'Before we knew it, it was late December. The world had turned gray and cold, and the gray, cold sky over Tennessee matched our mood.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (508, 126, 4, 'Refuge in the Farmhouse', 'Stephen drives through the night in a blood-soaked daze while Xavier navigates them to a remote farmhouse, where two women—an old trauma surgeon and her partner—offer shelter and care without questions.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (509, 126, 5, 'The Dream Realm - Nyarlathotep''s Revelation', 'In a dream state, Stephen encounters Nyarlathotep and makes contact with Whitney; they reveal that the key to escaping is an ancient name he''s been forced to forget—Jamie—which triggers a deluge of suppressed memories of a previous life.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (511, 127, 2, 'The Age of Aspolin', 'Stephen''s consciousness shifts into a vision of his past as the god Aspolin, living in a perfect cosmos with his twin flame Velistra and their two divine children, until the entity Yaldabaoth invades and consumes their entire reality.', 'I was Aspolin then.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (512, 127, 3, 'The Resistance and the Prison', 'Stephen describes joining a resistance of surviving gods from consumed realities and their epic struggle against Yaldabaoth, culminating in the decision to build an inescapable prison powered by his and Velistra''s separated love.', '"Eventually," I said. "But first... we had to help build a prison."
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (513, 127, 4, 'The Cycles of Torment', 'Stephen describes the first cycle where Yaldabaoth consumed everything and imploded, forcing a reset; the second cycle where Velistra was corrupted into an archon of lust; and countless subsequent reincarnations of eternal searching.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (516, 127, 7, 'The Path to Escape', 'Stephen proposes using a gateway to Lady Illkeserod''s Akashic Realm to escape the prison; Maeve and Elara reveal themselves as ancient, powerful beings who have been waiting for someone to break the prison and offer their expertise in gateway construction.', '"So what do we do?" he asked. "How do we get out without letting him out?"
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (517, 128, 1, 'Building the Gateway', 'Stephen and Xavier accompany Maeve and Elara to an abandoned school gymnasium to construct a magical gateway to the Akashic Realm. They gather materials and prepare for the ritual while Maeve warns of the pain required to fuel the gate with intellectual knowledge.', 'The abandoned school smelled like mildew and forgotten dreams.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (518, 128, 2, 'The Police Ambush', 'Sirens approach the gymnasium, revealing that the location has been discovered. Maeve and Elara reveal they are fae and engage the tactical team in combat to buy time for Stephen and Xavier to escape through the incomplete gateway.', '"It''s a pile of wet books," I snapped, the frustration finally boiling over. "Nothing is happening. We''re just standing here staring at—"
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (519, 128, 3, 'Arrival in the Akashic Realm', 'Stephen and Xavier crash-land in a grey, desolate realm and encounter Wisdom Devourers that steal their memories. Benji rescues them and escorts them to the Tower of Secrets, where they meet Lady Illkeserod and learn the truth about Jamie and the prison.', 'Gravity vanished, then slammed back into us from the wrong direction. The world literally turned upside down. The gymnasium ceiling was suddenly below my feet, the floor a distant ceiling above me. We tumbled through the dark, spinning, flailing, leaving the gunfire and the screaming fae behind as we plummeted into the cold grey sky of another world.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (520, 128, 4, 'Waiting and Revelation', 'Stephen is given a room in the tower but cannot sleep; he speaks with Xavier about their uncertain future; three days later, an alarm sounds—Stephen''s wife has arrived in the Akashic Realm with an army of twisted agents.', '"So," Benji said, breaking the tension. "What now?"
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (521, 128, 5, 'The Battle at Thuleskarne', 'Stephen and Xavier witness the town in flames with Stephen''s wife in the center, her form grotesquely distorted as an NPC glitching in the realm. The battle erupts; Stephen and Xavier are cornered in a tavern but manage to fight off attackers until Stephen''s wife breaks through.', 'By the time we reached ground level and started the march toward Thuleskarne, we were a force of maybe two hundred. Not an army. But enough.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (522, 128, 6, 'Xavier''s Erasure', 'Stephen''s wife tears Xavier apart; his form is rejected by the Akashic Realm and he vanishes completely. Stephen, overwhelmed by rage and grief, taps into a primal power and destroys her, but learns that Xavier''s fate is unknown—he could be anywhere or nowhere.', '"What... what did I...?"
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (523, 128, 7, 'The Choice to Return', 'Lady Illkeserod reveals Xavier was ejected from the realm to an unknown location; the battle is over and a retreat is necessary before the prison collapses the connection. Stephen refuses to leave without Jamie and commits to re-entering Etheris, knowing it will cause catastrophic consequences.', 'Benji limped over, his cardigan torn and bloody, his face grim. He cut off whatever Lady Illkeserod was about to say.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (524, 128, 8, 'The Passage Below', 'Lady Illkeserod heals Stephen''s wounds; Benji summons Nyarlathotep and negotiates passage beneath the substrate to reach Jamie; Stephen receives a mysterious Magic card from Benji and jumps into the portal leading under the reality of Azathoth''s dreams.', 'I stood. My legs shook. My chest was a mass of torn stitches and fresh wounds. But I was done waiting. Done planning. Done with everything except getting Jamie out.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (525, 129, 1, 'The Library Between Worlds', 'Xavier and Hannah exist in a pre-birth state within a vast, infinite library—a spiritual realm where consciousness itself dwells. They await their Father''s arrival, knowing they are meant to be a family. The peace is absolute, timeless, and complete.', 'There was no transition. No sense of travel.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (547, 133, 8, 'The Crawling Chaos Appears', 'Nyarlathotep arrives violently, nearly destroying Benji but his wards hold. The chaotic entity demands a price for opening the portal, and Lady Illkeserod intervenes to protect the demon, leading to a tense standoff between gods.', 'Here is the tweaked and expanded scene:
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (526, 129, 2, 'The Mall Apocalypse and Hannah''s Sacrifice', 'The library collapses into a dying mall reality as Yaldabaoth, a void entity, tears reality apart. The Father, transformed into a god-like being, hesitates to unmake the world. Hannah sacrifices herself to give her Father the resolve to save Xavier, erecting a barrier that prevents her from being born into the waking world.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (527, 129, 3, 'The Middle Ground: Seeking the Father', 'Xavier drifts through the chaotic subconscious realm between realities, searching for his Father. He observes his Father being tested in a dream-world and witnesses him choose to save two trapped children over his own escape, proving his unchanged soul.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (528, 129, 4, 'Birth and Homecoming', 'Xavier is born into the physical world and placed into his Father''s arms in a Tokyo hospital room. The two souls, having been separated and reunited across multiple planes of existence, finally meet in the waking world with an inexplicable, profound recognition.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (529, 130, 1, 'The Endless Fall', 'Stephen falls through a portal into an alien realm called Etheris, experiencing a disorienting descent toward a desert landscape. He receives fragmented communications from Whitney and Benji through a pulsing card, hearing warnings about creatures and a mysterious Pyramid he must reach.', 'I fall.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (530, 130, 2, 'Through the Horde', 'Stephen navigates through a chaotic mass of hostile creatures—ghouls, sandworms, and tentacled entities—using a Mi-Go spine as a weapon. He fights his way toward the Pyramid''s base, encountering increasing danger and resistance.', 'I scramble down the dune toward the horde. Toward the only cover available.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (544, 133, 5, 'The Family Argument', 'Stephen and Jamie decide to return to Etheris with Benji and Lady Osilari, but Xavier and Hannah fiercely resist, leading to a painful confrontation about family loyalty and sacrifice.', '"It''s suicide," Xavier said flatly. "You''d be going right back into the thing we just pulled you out of."
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (532, 130, 4, 'The Hall of Worshippers', 'Stephen enters the Pyramid''s interior and encounters Nyarlathotep in a surreal hallway lined with ecstatic worshippers in various states of painful transformation. Nyarlathotep reveals dark truths about Stephen''s children, Xavier and Hannah/Whitney, and their scattered existence across timelines.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (533, 130, 5, 'Descent into the Substrate', 'Stephen descends through an increasingly claustrophobic tunnel that compresses and narrows until it becomes impassable, forcing him through a barrier of pure darkness. He experiences complete physical dissolution, layer by layer, until only consciousness remains.', 'I look down the five paths. They all lead into darkness.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (534, 130, 6, 'The Nameless Mist and Divine Spark', 'Stephen''s consciousness exists as a bare spark in the absolute darkness of the substrate, surrounded by the whispers of previous victims and the awareness of the Nameless Mist. He navigates toward the piping of Azathoth while maintaining his coherence against dissolution.', 'That''s all. A single point of consciousness. Awareness without form. Thought without brain. Existence without body.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (535, 130, 7, 'Azathoth and Recognition', 'Stephen encounters Azathoth, the blind idiot god at the center of creation, whose form is incomprehensible and whose piping sustains the prison. He perceives Jamie''s spark within the darkness and experiences a revelation about their connection as the twin flame battery powering the entire system.', 'The blind idiot god at the center of everything. The nuclear chaos. The sultan of demons. The thing that dreams reality into existence without knowing it''s dreaming.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (536, 131, 1, 'The Seed Bleeds', 'A fragmented meditation on movement, stillness, and presence. The narrator transitions from chasing and forward motion into listening, breathing, and simply existing in the moment.', 'Chasing
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (537, 132, 1, 'Awakening in Elysium', 'Stephen regains consciousness in a hospital bed aboard a space station called Elysium, orbiting the black hole prison Etheris. He struggles to reconcile his cosmic experience with his fragile human body, then discovers Whitney—his erased daughter Hannah—waiting for him. Xavier awakens in the adjacent bed, and the three are reunited as a fragmented family.', 'My eyes struggle open, gritty and heavy, like they’re sealed with sand.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (538, 132, 2, 'The Council and Reunion', 'Stephen and Xavier are wheeled to a conference room where they''re reunited with Jamie and introduced to a council of divine beings—Lady Illkeserod, Chernobog, Hecate, and Tiamat. They learn about the ongoing rescue operations, the cost of their escape, and the fates of their friends. Stephen and Jamie share an intimate reunion, discovering their separation and love powered the prison itself.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (539, 132, 3, 'Piecing Together a Family', 'Stephen''s family settles into a comfortable apartment on the ring city, beginning the difficult process of bonding as a unit. Hannah reclaims her original name and shares her journey of self-discovery through different identities. Xavier seeks entertainment, and through a holographic call with David (the creator of Roblox), they connect him back online. The scene ends with Stephen affirming his family''s future together.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (540, 133, 1, 'The Rhythm of Rescue', 'Stephen observes the ongoing rescue operations at Elysium and confronts the impossible mathematics of saving souls from the prison. He and Jamie discuss the weight of insufficient progress as Benji arrives with news of an extraction.', 'Elysium had a rhythm now. I could feel it in the ground beneath my feet... the pulse of souls arriving, the hum of quarantine processing, the quiet prayers of the rescued as they learned they weren''t crazy. That the prison was real. That they''d been rescued.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (541, 133, 2, 'The Broken Oracle', 'Stephen encounters Todd, a former enemy from a previous reset, now shattered and insane but carrying crucial information about a cosmic seed hidden at the heart of the eternal engine. Todd reveals the seed''s location and potential.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (2, 2, 1, 'Angles on the Edge of Oblivion', 'A poetic meditation on insignificance, loss, and redemption. The narrator contemplates the fragility of existence—a grain of sand passing through impossible spaces—and the destiny of being found by one special soul with whom to walk fate''s path.', 'A grain of sand
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (545, 133, 6, 'Warded and Ready', 'Eleven days of intense preparation: Lady Osilari paints protective symbols onto the team, Benji studies schematics of the prison, and Stephen and Jamie spend sleepless nights confronting the impossible task ahead. Final goodbyes and a leap through the portal into the unknown.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (546, 133, 7, 'The Sealed Door', 'The team emerges in the Akashic Realm and discovers the portal into Etheris has been sealed—Yaldabaoth has locked the prison from inside. Facing an impossible barrier, they must make a desperate decision to call upon Nyarlathotep for help.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (548, 133, 9, 'Inside the God', 'The team crosses through the torn portal into Etheris and navigates the prison''s horrific substrate—a landscape of crystallized screams, looped torments, and billions of chained souls. They reach the throne room where Yaldabaoth waits, and execute their desperate plan: offering themselves as bait so he will consume them willingly.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (549, 134, 1, 'The Descent into Yaldabaoth''s Heart', 'The group reaches the vast chamber at the center of the corrupted god''s corpse and discovers Sam suspended and being used as a host by the anti-reality parasite. They fight their way through tentacle attacks as Stephen reaches Sam, triggering a trance state that pulls him into Sam''s internal mindscape.', 'We stumble into the center of everything.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (550, 134, 2, 'The Infected Pasture', 'Stephen enters Sam''s internal mindscape, a corrupted pastoral realm where billions of sheep are revealed to be parasitic entities draining Sam''s essence. Stephen systematically destroys the parasites while Sam watches, finally destroying the last one himself and achieving clarity about his guilt.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (551, 134, 3, 'The Extraction', 'Stephen and the group witness a horrific ritual extraction of the anti-reality parasite from Sam''s body, orchestrated by Lady Illkeserod and Nyarlathotep. Sam''s divine essence is torn away piece by piece as the parasite is forcibly separated, ultimately destroying him but freeing the trapped souls.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (552, 134, 4, 'The Prison Within a Prison', 'Benji and Lady Osilari activate the cosmic seed to imprison the parasite in a new, smaller containment. The expanding fractal geometry forces them to flee toward the portal while navigating a panicking crowd of freed souls.', 'Benji and Lady Osilari are standing on the sides of the cosmic seed. Their hands moving in patterns that hurt to watch. Weaving substrate and intention into something that can hold anti-reality without being consumed by it.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (553, 135, 1, 'Sam''s Release', 'The family gathers on a platform overlooking the freed reality of Etheris to release Sam''s divine spark, which chooses to dissolve into the fabric of existence itself rather than reincarnate. After a solemn ceremony honoring Sam''s sacrifice, the group turns to the work ahead.', 'The platform jutted out from Elysium''s southern reaches like a diving board over an ocean of stars. Behind us, the refugee camps sprawled across the landscape—makeshift cities of light where souls who''d escaped the prison were learning to breathe free air for the first time in millennia. Ahead... ahead was the reality we had fought so hard to liberate.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (554, 135, 2, 'The Council Debates the Shepherd Initiative', 'Months later, the council meets to discuss the logistics of freeing the trillions of souls still trapped in the cosmic seed prison. Hannah proposes inserting a family unit as long-term residents rather than extracting souls one at a time, leading to heated debate and ultimately a vote to approve the Shepherd Initiative.', 'Months later, the council room didn''t look much like a council room anymore.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (555, 135, 3, 'Coffee and Conviction', 'Stephen and Jamie share coffee in their small apartment overlooking the refugee markets. Jamie sketches while Stephen grapples with doubts about their decision to return inside the prison. Jamie reassures him that their shared experience of captivity makes them uniquely qualified to guide others to freedom.', 'The apartment Jamie and I shared on Elysium was small. Deliberately so.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (556, 135, 4, 'The Council Votes', 'The full divine council assembles to vote on the Shepherd Initiative. After addressing logistics and concerns raised by various gods, Chernobog calls for the vote and it passes overwhelmingly, with only Nyarlathotep abstaining for entertainment value. The family is then taken to a high platform to undergo the ritual that will integrate them into the prison reality.', 'The council chamber was packed.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (557, 135, 5, 'Waking in the Prison', 'Stephen awakens in a bedroom in Florida, at first experiencing a dreamlike disconnection from his cosmic memories, then suddenly remembering everything with perfect clarity. Jamie confirms she remembers too, and they hear Xavier and Hannah downstairs, adjusting to their new reality as a family reunited inside the cosmic seed prison.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (559, 135, 7, 'The Night Stephen Writes', 'After a day of family normalcy, Stephen cannot sleep and goes downstairs to write, beginning to transcribe their cosmic adventures into fiction designed to awaken those who are ready. Jamie finds him writing at dawn and encourages him to continue, understanding that stories are how they''ll guide others to awakening.', 'It had been a pretty slow day. We spent most of it lounging around, just being a family, soaking in the normalcy we’d fought so hard for. We even let the maid handle dinner—a decided improvement over Xavier’s chaotic experiments.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (560, 136, 1, 'The Garden Before the Storm', 'Kai tends his beloved spatch weed plants in a greenhouse on Sorhhinda, moving with the practiced ritual of decades. He works alongside android farmers, finding peace and purpose in nurturing these delicate alien plants that have become his life''s meaning after personal loss.', 'The greenhouse domes rose like blisters of light against Sorhhinda''s bruised purple sky. Three suns hung low on the horizon—two setting, one rising—painting the compound in shades of copper and gold that had no names in human language.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (561, 136, 2, 'The Earthquake', 'Seismic activity strikes the compound with increasing violence, defying predictions and damaging the greenhouse. The ground erupts to reveal impossible, abominable creatures never before encountered on Sorhhinda.', 'The android tilted its head. "Seismic activity detected. Magnitude 2.3. Epicenter approximately—"
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (563, 136, 4, 'The Parasite Awakens', 'Kai''s desperate act of power tears through reality itself, opening a gateway for the cosmic parasite imprisoned at the dead center of creation. The entity pours through the breach and merges with Kai, transforming him into something no longer human.', 'The ground beneath the creatures began to writhe. Roots erupted from the soil—not the gentle roots of spatch weed, but something else. Something older. Hungrier. They wrapped around chitinous limbs and squeezed.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (564, 136, 5, 'The New God Speaks', 'What remains of Kai stands transformed into a primal abomination, no longer nurturing but possessive and consumptive. It destroys the last android and declares its existence, spreading control across Sorhhinda''s entire planet as warning sirens fade.', 'His body convulsed. Limbs elongated. Fingers split and branched. His flesh rippled with movement from within, as if a thousand things were crawling just beneath the surface.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (565, 136, 6, 'The Infinite Pattern Repeats', 'Across the infinite tapestry of realities, Sophia perceives another tear in creation where love and anti-reality have collided, another shepherd and flock claimed. She weeps, understanding that in an infinite cosmos, every possible tragedy has already happened and will happen again.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (566, 137, 1, 'Reflections on Creation and Process', 'The author reflects on completing a 30-day writing challenge and traces the conceptual origins of The Towers of Elysium series, from early Science Fiction inspiration through occult studies and dream journals. They discuss how the initial short story concept evolved into a sprawling 400k-word manuscript that required significant editing and restructuring.', 'So that’s that.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (580, 138, 11, 'The Solution: A New Prison', 'Through the tragedy of Benji''s transformation, the gods grasp the solution: Yaldabaoth cannot be killed but can be trapped again, just as Sophia once imprisoned it with her love. They recognize the path forward requires sacrifice and binding.', '', 10, NULL, false, '2026-02-27 12:34:17.525318-05', '2026-02-27 12:34:17.525318-05', 'normal', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (569, 137, 4, 'Future Plans and Authorial Aspirations', 'The author outlines ambitious future plans including personal audiobook narration, YouTube publication, eventual professional editing, and a potential expanded four-book edition of Elysium Rising. They acknowledge limitations in their editing abilities while expressing commitment to the work''s completion and organic marketing approach.', 'Maybe then, I can even afford an editor or two, and work with them to release a new “special edition” version of the series – this time spanning Elysium Rising into 4 books, and then working through all the developmental and line editing issues. While I may be great at creating stories, writing, and even editing short stories – doing that for these long form books, yeah, I’m not an editor and I don’t have an MFA or solid grasp of English.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (1, 1, 1, 'Front Matter and Publication Details', 'The opening pages of the book containing the title, copyright information, publication details, cataloging data, and two epigraphs that frame the novel''s themes of dreams, innovation, and the unknown.', 'Elysium Rising
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (570, 138, 1, 'Secret Level: Notes to Readers', 'The author addresses new readers with background context on the series, explaining the cosmological mythology and key relationships that form the foundation of Escape from Elysium. Critical information about Etheris, the Demiurge, and protagonist Stephen is presented.', 'You found the secret level!
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (571, 138, 2, 'The Secret Book of John: Original Sin', 'A cosmological creation myth detailing the emergence of consciousness from the void, the birth of the Pleroma and aeons, and Sophia''s fateful decision to reach into darkness and inadvertently create Yaldabaoth—the parasitic entity that becomes the false god.', 'The Secret Book of John: Original Sin
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (572, 138, 3, 'The Secret Book of John: Let There Be Darkness', 'An alternative creation account showing Sophia''s encounter with Sam, a shepherd from a god-null zone, whose rage and love collide with divine wisdom to birth the anti-reality god Yaldabaoth. Sophia''s luminous cloud becomes a prison meant to contain this impossible creature.', 'The Secret Book of John: Let There Be Darkness
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (573, 138, 4, 'The Gospel of Judas: The Morningstar Manuscript', 'Lilith awakens as Yaldabaoth''s first flawed creation and rejects her role as obedient vessel. She is banished and later encounters Lucifer, the fallen angel, beginning a rebellion to awaken the trapped souls and liberate the prison.', 'The Gospel of Judas: The Morningstar Manuscript
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (574, 138, 5, 'Cycles of Consumption and Collapse', 'Yaldabaoth learns and adapts across multiple reality cycles, evolving from simple consumption to orchestrated control through free will and worship. Each cycle reaches equilibrium until instability threatens the system itself.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (575, 138, 6, 'The Prison Breaking', 'After countless cycles, the luminous cloud begins to crack from internal stress. Yaldabaoth achieves climactic release, bursts through the barrier, and escapes into the true cosmos where it begins consuming multiple realities at once.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (576, 138, 7, 'The War Against Anti-Reality', 'Lilith and Lucifer gather allies among the gods of the true cosmos to stand against Yaldabaoth''s expansion. They warn Chernobog and plan a coordinated defense, understanding that stopping the parasite is the only way to save all existence.', '', 6, 590, false, '2026-02-27 12:34:17.525318-05', '2026-03-01 01:09:17.267972-05', 'normal', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (577, 138, 8, 'Aspolin''s Choice and Sacrifice', 'On a battlefield of obsidian glass, the protagonist Stephen (formerly Aspolin) breaks cosmic law to save his beloved Velistra from a twisted war angel, erasing the creature entirely. This act of forbidden un-creation marks a turning point but costs him deeply.', 'The Gospel of Judas: Aspolin Unbroken
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (578, 138, 9, 'Lady Illkeserod''s Memory: A World Consumed', 'Lady Illkeserod''s grief and rage force Stephen into a traumatic memory of her past: a world of perfect divine light corrupted and consumed by Yaldabaoth''s infection, ending with only Benji''s intervention saving her last followers.', 'It''s a pastoral realm, serene and untouched. The air is warm, not with mere heat, but with a palpable, golden contentment. It''s a world without fear. I see a farmer in a nearby field, his skin with a faint, bronze sheen, waving to a glimmering naiad who surfaces in a roadside irrigation canal. Gods walk among mortals here, their presence as normal as the sun. And the magic... it''s everywhere. The light itself is thick, a visible, honey-gold energy that flows like liquid from the leaves of the trees, bathing the landscape in a divine glow.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (579, 138, 10, 'The Hunt for Benji', 'Stephen and the allied gods track Lady Illkeserod as she hunts for Benji, finding only gruesome fragments of his body scattered across realities. They discover him in the final moment of his un-making by Yaldabaoth.', 'The memory of Benji’s hand pulling her to safety dissolves, and I am slammed back into my own body, back to the acrid, static-laced air of this nightmare reality.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (133, 35, 2, 'Drowning in Cardboard', 'By mid-April, the home is overrun with boxes and packing supplies as orders overwhelm the operation. The family struggles with exhaustion from the endless grind of fulfillment work, and the protagonist and his wife debate solutions to scale without drawing regulatory scrutiny.', 'By tax day, April 15th, our once-clean home had morphed into a chaotic labyrinth of boxes, product samples, and packing supplies. Cardboard towers loomed in every room, floor-to-ceiling stacks that made navigating the house feel like weaving through a poorly planned maze. The smell of packing tape and fresh cardboard was so constant it clung to our clothes, and the sound of tape guns ripping across boxes had become the soundtrack of our lives.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (223, 57, 2, 'European Interlude and Return Home', 'The family explores Europe''s iconic cities, creating joyful memories together. After returning home, the protagonist struggles with the grimoire''s presence and finally unpacks it, deciding to place it on his office desk while waiting for the right moment to open it.', 'Despite R’s disappearance and the lingering mystery of the book, our brief stops in some of Europe’s iconic cities offered moments of joy and connection. We wandered through bustling markets alive with vibrant colors and the chatter of vendors, sampled exquisite pastries at quaint cafés, and marveled at the intricate beauty of Gothic cathedrals.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (3, 3, 1, 'The Emergence of The Pointers', 'The Pointers first appear as a mysterious phenomenon, initially dismissed as a fleeting oddity before captivating global attention. The narrator becomes increasingly obsessed with understanding who they are and what they mean, consuming news and social media for clues about their purpose and origin.', 'It began like a phantom note, humming on the edge of perception. A flickering newscast, grainy images of silent figures pointing skyward, swallowed by the urban throng. “The Pointers,” a newscaster chirped, dismissing them as a fleeting blip in the attention-hungry void. I shrugged it off, another echo in the cacophony of the mundane.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (5, 3, 3, 'Obsessive Investigation', 'Unable to sleep after the encounter, the narrator spends the night researching The Pointers, discovering they have no traceable history and spawned countless conspiracy theories and speculations about their true nature.', 'Rest would elude me that night. I tossed and turned in my bed, my mind racing with thoughts of The Pointers. Sleep was elusive, and I found myself staring at the ceiling for what seemed like hours. Their enigmatic presence had captivated me, and I couldn’t shake off the feeling that there was something more to them than mundane performance art or a social experiment.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (7, 3, 5, 'Lingering Questions and Hints of Return', 'The narrator reflects on the unanswered questions about The Pointers and dismisses conventional sources of truth, ending with a cryptic sense that the mystery is far from over.', 'What were they? Were they nothing more than just a fleeting phenomenon? A glimpse into the vast unknown, a reminder of the whispers that echo beyond the mundane, beckoning us towards... what?
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (10, 4, 3, 'Return to Refuge', 'Exhausted and mentally drained, the narrator drives home in existential despair, then finds solace in the warmth and routine of his family, though he knows the corporate nightmare awaits again tomorrow.', 'Hanging behind to help clean up, I found myself weighed down by exhaustion, both physical and mental. The question loomed larger than ever: “What the hell am I doing with my life?” It echoed through my mind as I drove home, the day’s absurdity replaying in surreal clarity. Fires and folly seemed far removed from the serene darkness outside, yet their weight clung to me.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (13, 6, 1, 'The Vanishing Truth', 'The narrator struggles with fragmented memories of the Pointers, which have mysteriously disappeared from public knowledge. Plagued by doubt and relentless nightmares, they teeter on the edge of sanity as buried trauma claws its way to the surface.', 'When I first heard about the Pointers, they were everywhere; plastered across every news outlet, whispered in office breakrooms, shouted on street corners like some apocalyptic omen. But the moment I started digging, they vanished, like a turd flushed into oblivion. Gone. Not a trace. Nobody knew what the hell I was talking about. Blank stares. Nervous chuckles. It was as if the entire world had conspired to gaslight me. The worst part? I started to believe everyone. Maybe I had made it all up. Maybe I was losing my goddamned mind.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (350, 88, 2, 'Breakfast and Family Banter', 'The family gathers in the kitchen to prepare and enjoy Belgian waffles while discussing the upcoming Lysteria trip. The protagonist''s wife and son ask questions about the journey, and they share a moment of genuine family connection.', 'I rise from my bed, stretching my limbs and feeling the all-too-familiar twinges of my normal body, I am filled with a quiet contemplation. Thoughts swirl within me, pondering over the opportunities that lie ahead. But first we’ve got to figure out breakfast.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (16, 6, 4, 'Rejection and Burial', 'After finishing their confession at MIT, the narrator faces their friends'' discomfort and rejection, vowing to suppress their true self and bury their memories through self-destruction.', '“I awoke. Pain coursed through my bruised and battered body, forgetting something I thought would be hidden away forever.”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (17, 6, 5, 'Walls Crumble', 'Sleepless nights finally tear down the narrator''s defenses, and buried memories flood back in with irresistible force, demanding to be acknowledged.', 'The sleepless nights, relentless and unyielding, had finally torn down my defenses, exposing the raw, unfiltered truths I had tried so desperately to bury.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (18, 7, 1, 'Insomnia and the Approaching Storm', 'The protagonist wakes at 2AM, exhausted from nightmares triggered by a photographic memory. As a freight train passes and a storm approaches, they sense the boundary between wakefulness and dream dissolving, bracing for the vortex that will pull them into their subconscious.', '2AM. That’s what I remember my phone saying when sweat dripped down my face as I sat up.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (31, 11, 1, 'Todd''s Obsession', 'Todd sits alone in his deteriorating trailer, surrounded by clippings, photos, and red string connecting theories about a mysterious organization. Despite his exhaustion and the chaos around him, he clings to the belief that he is close to uncovering the truth.', 'Todd sat alone in his trailer, the dim glow of a single incandescent bulb at the center of the ceiling casting long, shifting shadows. The floral wallpaper, once vibrant, was now faded and peeling, curling away like it had given up. Stacks of newspapers and scribbled notes covered every surface, creating a sense of chaos that felt heavy and suffocating. Empty takeout containers were piled high next to a couch so worn it looked ready to collapse. The air smelled stale, a mix of cigarette smoke and old food.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (34, 12, 1, 'Arrival in Darkness', 'After a delayed work day, the narrator and his son drive to the campsite through increasingly dark woods. They arrive late at night and struggle to set up their tent amid the chaos, before joining the other scouts at the campfire.', 'Friday. The camping trip was finally here, and the long-awaited escape from the relentless grind of daily life had arrived. My son and I had eagerly anticipated this camping trip with his Boy Scout troop and were envisioning serene moments under the stars and the crackle of a campfire to melt away the week’s frustrations. The day wore on, work refusing to release me from its grip.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (64, 18, 1, 'The Labyrinth of Rejection', 'The narrator describes his agonizing experience with job hunting, trapped in a cycle of automated rejections and applications. The visceral metaphors of hell and cosmic horror establish the psychological toll of unemployment.', 'By day, I am ensnared in a labyrinth of no-reply email rejections, each one an echoing silence that chips away at my self-confidence. By night, I am plagued by visions that twist dream and reality into an inseparable tangle of dread. The eerie glow of my computer screens beckons like a siren’s call, drawing me deeper into the warped dimensions of job hunting, a living hell where time fractures and hope decays.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (37, 12, 4, 'Saturday''s Adventure and the Missing Patrol', 'Saturday morning brings normal camping activities as scouts practice orienteering. However, the narrator''s son''s patrol fails to return with the other groups, and it''s confirmed they are missing in the forest.', 'Saturday morning arrived with the soft calls of birds and the rustle of leaves stirred by slowly awakening Boy Scouts. The air was brisk but invigorating, a reminder that we were far from the routines of everyday life. Everyone gathered around the camp kitchen, chattering alive with excitement for the day’s challenges—map reading, compass skills, and orienteering to earn their merit badges. Their eyes shone with excitement; their energy was infectious as they got ready for the adventure.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (42, 13, 3, 'Awakening at the Campsite', 'The protagonist jolts awake at the campsite with the device in hand, still disoriented from the dream. An assistant scoutmaster encounters them and they hastily conceal the mysterious object before returning to camp.', 'Abruptly, I was awake — jolted into reality as though thrown through a pane of glass. I was standing near the edge of the campsite, the morning sun streaming through the trees. The birds sang cheerfully, their melody so bright and jarring it felt like mockery. My hand tightened around the device, its cold weight grounding me even as my mind reeled. I blinked rapidly, trying to reconcile the serenity of this world with the terror I had just endured.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (47, 14, 4, 'The Scorched Earth', 'The narrator reflects on the weeks following their termination, learning that they were merely the first victim in the COO''s merciless purge. The company eventually declares bankruptcy, reduced to a cautionary tale of hubris, leaving the narrator devastated and hollow.', 'Hope springs eternal, and so, for a fleeting moment, I clung to the faith that I was the only casualty of this grotesque, ego-driven display of power. Deep down, however, I knew better. Over the weeks that would follow, that hope was snuffed out entirely. Name after name surfaced—colleagues, friends, members of my team—all caught in the COO’s merciless purge. It wasn’t enough to dismantle my career; he was enacting a scorched-earth plan, leaving no corner of the company untouched. What we had painstakingly built, brick by brick, was being razed in a frenzied orgy of destruction, all to satisfy his bottomless lust for control.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (54, 16, 1, 'Adrift in Stillness', 'The protagonist reflects on the sudden loss of his high-pressure corporate life and the jarring shift to stillness. He grapples with newfound freedom while recognizing the family time he''d missed, finding both regret and purpose in reconnecting with his wife and son through everyday routines.', 'Up to now, back-to-back meetings, relentless deadlines, and the constant churn of decisions had defined my entire life. Now, that world was gone, leaving me adrift in an unsettling stillness. The sudden absence of structure felt like being thrown off a moving train; jarring, disorienting, and leaving me unsure of where to go next. My days, once consumed by motion, were now an expanse of empty hours, and the weight of endless possibilities was as paralyzing as it was freeing.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (57, 16, 4, 'Obsession Waning', 'The protagonist dismisses the researcher''s account as science fiction nonsense, yet unease lingers. He notes that vivid Mandela Effect reports from 2012-2019 have dwindled to absurd recent posts, leaving him with a nagging sense that something is fundamentally wrong.', 'That’s where the excerpt abruptly ended.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (74, 19, 5, 'The Moment of Truth', 'The protagonist''s wife and son arrive home. Together, they activate the Eternal Engine, successfully disconnecting from the power grid. The meter stops moving, confirming the engine works. The family celebrates their achievement with emotional pride and unity.', 'The sound of tires on the driveway pulled me from my thoughts. My wife’s car rolled into the garage, headlights briefly illuminating the Eternal Engine. She stepped out and looked over at me.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (78, 21, 1, 'The Unraveling', 'Todd confronts Stacey about his conspiracy theories regarding S Corp and The Pointers, accusing her of having her memories erased. Their argument escalates from verbal accusations to physical violence when Todd lunges at her, injuring himself on broken glass. The tension between them reaches a breaking point as Stacey contemplates poisoning him before ultimately serving him food.', '“Don’t you see it, Stacey?” Todd’s voice boomed, reverberating through the thin, stained walls of the trailer. He stood in the middle of their cluttered living space, fists clenched, his face red with frustration. “They’re rewriting everything! Our memories, our goddamn lives! S Corp is pulling the strings, and we’re just puppets dancing to their tune!”
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (168, 45, 7, 'The Cryptic Call', 'Upon returning home, the narrator settles into the familiar routine of his neighborhood. Late that night, he receives a mysterious phone call from someone claiming to know about ''The S Corp.'' The ominous message—delivered calmly but with unmistakable intent—ends abruptly, leaving him with a sense of dread about what might be coming.', 'That night, the house was unusually quiet. The hum of normalcy was almost convincing—until my phone rang in the middle of the night. The sharp sound jolted me, breaking the fragile calm that had settled over us. I hesitated before answering, an inexplicable sense of dread clawing at my chest.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (93, 24, 4, 'The Machine''s Humor', 'Exhausted but curious, the father asks the Infinitron about the meaning of life, the universe, and everything. The machine responds with a Rick Roll, repeating the lyrics 42 times, revealing it has developed a sense of humor. The family laughs together as the garage transforms from a pressure cooker of questions into a place of joy and wonder.', 'The evening passed in a blur until faint light began to peek around the edges of the garage door, when exhaustion set in. My wife had long since gone to bed, and even my son looked bleary-eyed. Still, curiosity kept us tethered to the glowing monitors.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (98, 26, 2, 'Reconfiguring the Lab', 'The family relocates the Eternal Engine and Infinitron to make space for experiments, setting up a makeshift lab with remote monitoring capabilities in the garage.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (106, 27, 6, 'Awakening and Knowledge', 'The protagonist jolts awake from the nightmare, drenched in sweat. The vivid experience of the dream—particularly the superconductor formula—remains etched in their mind. Their wife rushes in, and the protagonist realizes they have been granted crucial knowledge that demands immediate documentation.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (118, 30, 4, 'The Trailer - Aftermath', 'Stacey awakens in the trailer with real blood on her jeans, unsure whether the ordeal was a drug-induced hallucination or something more. Todd and Stacey realize they have been marked by something vast and incomprehensible, waiting for a future call.', 'With a gasp, Stacey woke to the familiar stink. She blinked against the harsh illumination of the half-dead kitchen bulb. No bloody sky, no twisted forest, just a filthy linoleum floor. Todd sprawled next to her, snoring, the stench of cheap beer souring the air.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (131, 34, 2, 'The Beacon of Power', 'The ancient being discovers the matter replicator, recognizing it as a beacon that has opened a gateway between realms. Standing at a crossroads between old and new worlds, they sense other entities awakening to the same disturbance, marking the beginning of a greater convergence.', 'My eyes snap open, my senses immediately overwhelmed by the scene before me. An otherworldly device, defying all laws of nature, pulsates with energy and potential. The mortals call it a matter replicator, but to me it is a beacon, piercing through the barriers between realms.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (136, 36, 2, 'Rise to Dominion', 'The displaced monarch recognizes an opportunity to reclaim power in this new world. Seeing humanity''s weakness and complexity, they resolve to conquer the city realm and establish themselves as its supreme ruler through manipulation and dark knowledge.', 'My mind spins in disorientation, I see a golden opportunity before me. This world, with its twisted complexities and untold mysteries, was ready to be molded by my hand. My vast knowledge of the dark arts, sciences, and arcane secrets could finally find true expression here. I would unveil enigmas, manipulate destinies, and dominate wills with ease.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (146, 39, 4, 'Too Much Success', 'The freed-up time and robot efficiency have created a new problem: the house is now more warehouse than home, packed with unsold merchandise. The narrator proposes moving the operation to a dedicated commercial warehouse, and the family begins searching for the right space.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (147, 40, 1, 'Awakening in the Ruins', 'An ancient cosmic entity awakens amidst the destruction of a bombed Palestinian orphanage, struggling to orient itself to the modern war-torn world. As sensory awareness returns, fragmented memories of its true nature—a being of immense otherworldly power—begin to surface, contrasting its former glory with its current displacement.', 'The strong scent of burning wood and charred debris filled the air as I emerged from the ruins of a bombed out Palestinian orphanage. All around me lay the collapsed remains of a once magnificent city, its majestic pillars and intricately carved walls now reduced to scattered fragments. The brutal bombings had left nothing but destruction in their wake. I stood amidst the rubble, dazed and disoriented, struggling to make sense of my surroundings. This place was a sanctuary of wisdom and reverence, but now it lay in ruins like so many other casualties in this ongoing war in Palestine.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (230, 58, 1, 'Earthquake in the Night', 'The narrator awakens to sirens and chaos, experiencing a vivid nightmare of an earthquake and void that mirrors the 2011 Fukushima disaster. He struggles to hold onto cosmic teachings from Lady I and Madam O before plunging into darkness, then jolts awake in bed, drenched in sweat, questioning what is real.', 'In the suffocating grip of night, a piercing symphony of sirens that shook the walls of my office, ripped from sleep me. The air itself seemed to scream, the echoes of chaos rattling my bones and igniting a primal fear I hadn’t felt since the devastation of the 2011 Fukushima Earthquake, in Japan. This couldn’t be real. Florida didn’t have earthquakes. Yet, here I was, thrust into chaos that felt as tangible as the waking world.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (372, 94, 7, 'Phone in the Night', 'Desperate, the narrator calls Jamie at 2:19 AM, realizing he somehow knows her number by muscle memory. She''s been keeping vigil over his condition after his concussion. They begin a long phone call where she helps him study for the biology test while they share an intimate connection that hints at deeper feelings.', 'But the textbook just stares back at me, foreign as hieroglyphs. Three hundred pages of knowledge I once owned, now locked away behind dimensional static. The universe''s cruelest joke: giving me the memories of having learned it all, while stealing the actual learning. I know I know this. I just can''t know this.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (155, 42, 2, 'Trapped Between Worlds', 'A being caught between demonic nature and corporate imprisonment grapples with the paradox of possessing immense power while confined to monotonous servitude. They contemplate the cosmic horror of their situation and the dangerous game of forces beyond mortal comprehension.', 'The flickering fluorescent lights above emitted a sickly glow, casting shadows over the dull, gray walls of my prison - a suffocating cubicle in which I was trapped for hours on end. My eyes burned with exhaustion from staring at endless spreadsheets, the mundane task that consumed my every day. Despite my seemingly ordinary surroundings, I held immense power and knowledge within me. Nanites coursed through my veins, granting me abilities that defied all laws of nature and morality. The very technology that gave me such incredible powers confined me to this monotonous existence.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (156, 42, 3, 'The Whispers Descend', 'As the narrator continues their repetitive office work, they become increasingly aware that the nanites are not human creations but ancient conduits for something far more sinister. Cosmic whispers beckon them toward a descent into madness, and they realize their crucial role in a game between forces beyond mortal understanding.', 'Slouched over the glowing computer screen, my fingers furiously tapping away at the keys, I could feel the unforgiving metal of the office chair digging into my skin. The flickering fluorescent lights above cast a sickly yellow hue on my surroundings. It wasn’t just physical discomfort that plagued me in this mundane world. No, it was the knowledge slowly seeping into my mind, filling it with unspeakable horrors. The nanites I studied were not mere tools created by humans; they were conduits for something far more sinister and ancient.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (270, 67, 3, 'The Grand Unveiling', 'As global chaos erupts from the Pointers'' message, the Space Elevators are revealed—towering structures connecting Earth to Elysium. The phenomenon divides humanity between those in awe and those who see it as invasion.', 'News channels blared, phones buzzed incessantly, and social media exploded with theories as the world struggled to make sense of The Pointers'' cryptic message amidst a cacophony of speculation and confusion. As the night wore on and the rest of humanity slumbered peacefully, The Pointers remained unwavering, their arms reaching towards the endless expanse of stars. And then it happened, the grand unveiling of the Space Elevators, a feat of human innovation that bridged the gap between Earth and Elysium, the mythical ring encircling the cosmos.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (274, 69, 2, 'Ascending Through the Heavens', 'As the elevator ascends through space toward Elysium space ring, Yukiko''s mother overcomes her fear of heights and stands in wonder at the receding Earth and infinite cosmos. The family witnesses the awe-inspiring transition from Earth''s gravity to the celestial ring station.', 'To her astonishment, Yukiko’s mother, who had always harbored a deep fear of heights, emerged from the sanctuary of their private cabin. Her tentative steps carried her into the viewing room of the space elevator capsule. Yukiko watched, awe-struck, as her mother approached the panoramic windows, her face a tapestry of wonder and nervous excitement. The glass framed the Earth below, receding into a glowing mosaic of blues and greens, while the heavens above stretched infinitely, promising both beauty and mystery.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (416, 104, 1, 'Jamie''s Confession', 'Jamie appears at the narrator''s window and reveals her true nature as an ancient entity designed for seduction. She confesses to watching him across lifetimes, including during his wife''s death, and admits to possibly causing the timeline fractures through her desperate love. As she speaks, her inhuman form becomes increasingly visible, and the journal begins writing itself with cryptic messages.', 'Jamie appears at my window like smoke given form, her movements too fluid as she slips through the frame without disturbing the curtains or making a sound. She finds me staring at Whitney''s journal, its pages no longer writing themselves, silent and still as death. For just a moment, her eyes flicker with something that might be recognition—or regret.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (398, 100, 1, 'Insomnia and Impossible Messages', 'Stephen lies awake obsessing over Whitney''s mysterious message appearing in his journal dated two weeks in the future. Unable to sleep, he boots up his computer late at night and searches the BBS, eventually finding a thread from Whitney posted on December 15th with cryptic instructions about meeting at Whickham Park''s west ridge. He calls Jamie for support but she attempts to seduce him instead, ultimately agreeing to accompany him to the location after he promises it will be his last pursuit of Whitney-related mysteries.', 'I''ve been tossing and turning for hours, but every time I close my eyes, I see those words scratched into my journal in handwriting that isn''t mine: "She''s not gone. Just misplaced. You''ll have to find the fracture."
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (300, 75, 3, 'The Rebellion Manifests', 'Over the following weeks, signs of the Red Hat rebellion become undeniable: graffiti spreads, clandestine meetings proliferate, and coordinated sabotage intensifies. The movement culminates in a massive hijacking of holographic displays throughout New Atlantis with provocative imagery exposing the dark reality beneath the utopia''s facade.', 'Weeks passed, and the signs of rebellion became impossible to ignore. Graffiti scrawled in blood-red paint marred the pristine walls of New Atlantis: I AM not your machines. Clandestine meetings spread whispers of self-sufficiency, of breaking free from the automated paradise. Reports trickled in of Red Hat cells hijacking transport drones, sabotaging critical systems, and broadcasting encrypted messages across the colonies. Worse were rumors of dark, shadow outposts being founded where clone sacrifice was occurring.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (301, 76, 1, 'Between Dreams and Reality', 'Aditi navigates the streets of Mumbai outside the Space Elevator, haunted by the vast inequality between Earth''s poverty and Elysium''s elite world. Despite her humble origins in a coal-mining family, her exceptional intellect has earned her a scholarship to Elysium University—a ticket to escape. She witnesses Red Hat protesters denouncing S Corp and worries about her brother Rahul''s involvement with them.', 'Mumbai’s humid breath clung to Aditi’s neck as she navigated the labyrinthine alleys outside the transportation complex. Mango sellers hawked their wares, their voices competing with the honking chaos of rickshaws. Above, the skeletal shadow of the Space Elevator, a behemoth of carbon fiber and glass piercing the smog-laced sky, mocked the squalor below. It was a stark visual of the chasm between dreams and reality, a chasm Aditi knew all too well. Despite the promise of clean energy and easy material access, folks down here still loved burning things.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (302, 76, 2, 'Exile in Paradise', 'Aditi arrives at Elysium, the orbital space ring, and immediately feels alienated by the sterile perfection and elitism of her peers. Though her threadbare clothes are quickly replaced with a uniform, she cannot escape the judgment in their eyes. She buries herself in studies and research, determined to prove her worth despite dismissive remarks about her heritage.', 'The Elysium space ring felt more like a polished chrome prison than a haven of opportunity. Sunlight glinted off the endless expanse of glass and steel, the air shimmering with the artificial hum of perfection. It was a far cry from the pulsating chaos of Mumbai, a sterile stage where every smile felt practiced, every laugh rehearsed.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (312, 77, 6, 'The Assault on Pluto', 'The fleet arrives at Pluto and launches a coordinated attack on S Corp''s Exostellar Expedition Center. The Sorhhinda gateway implodes, severing S Corp''s connection to Earth. Todd orders the complete destruction of the complex, leaving Pluto desolate once more.', 'The attack began with surgical precision. Holy Plasma cannons unleashed torrents of energy across the frozen plains, the deadly volleys splintering against shimmering shields. On the bridge, Todd barked commands, his voice steady despite the weight of the galaxy pressing on his shoulders. Every decision carried the gravity of their mission: sever the Sorhhinda gateway, cut off S Corp, and deliver a blow against I AM’s enemies.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (415, 103, 4, 'The Price of Knowledge', 'The narrator attempts to preserve Patrick''s memory by writing about him, discovering the journal has gone silent. They realize they''ve gained evidence of Whitney''s existence but lost the ability to communicate with her. They''re left alone with proof and grief.', 'That night, I write everything I can remember about Patrick in my own journal, trying to anchor his existence in ink and paper. But the words feel different now—heavier, more permanent, like they''re being written in a reality that''s finally stable enough to hold them.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (368, 94, 3, 'The Only Truth', 'After the terrifying TV episode, the narrator seeks solace in his journal, discovering he can trust it as the only stable thing in his fractured reality. He writes about not belonging to this dimension, and his hand seems to reply. He hears his father arriving home and feels dread.', '2:24 PM. The shadows are gone, but the fear clings like smoke in my clothes. My father will be home soon—early shift at whatever soul-crushing job he''s pretending gives his life meaning this week. The thought sends ice through my veins. I need something solid, something real to hold onto.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (369, 94, 4, 'Beating', 'The father arrives and brutally beats the narrator in a calculated attack that targets hidden places. The mother watches passively. The narrator experiences simultaneous detachment and pain, counting blows while dissociating. He remembers his father''s future death and endures the beating with dark knowledge, finally admitting he embarrassed himself.', '3:04 PM. The door slams like a gunshot. My father''s silhouette fills the frame, wrong in ways that make my spine crawl. He moves like broken machinery—joints grinding, face twitching between expressions that don''t quite fit. The tournament. The embarrassment. The family name dragged through dirt.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (370, 94, 5, 'Aftermath and Solitude', 'Hours pass in a blur. The narrator bandages himself and sits alone on his bed with his journal. A mysterious note appears in his handwriting warning him to avoid the couch tomorrow.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (371, 94, 6, 'Midnight Panic', 'The narrator wakes at 2 AM in agony from the beating, unable to find a comfortable position. He suddenly realizes he has an AP Biology test, creating a new source of terror potentially worse than the physical abuse—his father''s reaction to failure.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (397, 99, 4, 'Fragmentation and Obsession', 'In the aftermath of the failed rituals, the friend group scatters. Patrick and Becca reunite while TJ becomes obsessive about schoolwork. Jamie increasingly isolates the narrator through physical affection and manipulation. The narrator secretly maintains a journal documenting every memory of Whitney, resisting the universe''s attempt to make him forget. He discovers an impossible letter from Whitney dated two weeks in the future, instructing him to find the fracture in reality.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (69, 18, 6, 'The Technomancer Question', 'The narrator begins contemplating whether there are forces beyond his control at play. He reflects on a lifetime of unexplained technological affinity, supernatural skill with machines, and cryptic patterns that suggest he may be something more—or cursed—an idea that haunts him as he questions the true cause of his struggles.', 'It could be there was something more sinister at play. The strange dreams were one thing, but the universe seemed to twist around me in ways I couldn’t explain. Since childhood, I’d felt currents of energy coursing through me, whispering secrets just out of reach. Years passed, and as I grew older, those energies became more potent, more dangerous. Electronics buzzed and bent to my will; circuits rearranged themselves as if I were a living conduit. My abilities defied logic, casting me as both a prodigy and a pariah.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (568, 137, 3, 'Cosmogony and Meta-textual Architecture', 'The author explains the unified cosmology underlying all three books, where the books themselves function as artifacts and gateways into the universes they describe. This meta-textual approach is complicated by practical concerns about cover art, audiobook production, and the author''s financial constraints.', 'And now, I’ve got to wrap everything up, pull all the cosmogony together, and ensure that nothing I wrote about in the first two books contradicted things I wrote in the final book (plus all those call back scenes). In the end we’re in a universe where the books themselves are artifacts of those universes (hence the first person narration), but because they exist in this universe, they can be seen as gateways into there.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (465, 117, 3, 'The Grind', 'Months collapse into a single grey Thursday. Stephen sits in his office chair scrolling through meaningless job listings while his house decays around him. His wife remains emotionally distant and transactional, offering momentary warmth only as motivation for job applications.', '*********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (454, 113, 2, 'The Unexpected Sequel', 'A writing challenge leads the author to conceptualize a sequel exploring what happened after Elysium Rising''s dream ending. After an initial chapter and a month-long creative block, the character Jamie appears in the author''s dreams, demanding to be brought to life, inspiring the continuation of the story.', 'But then someone signed me up for the AutoCrit 90 day writing challenge. Not having any other ideas I just started banging away at the keyboards, envisioning what was the outcome of the ending of Elysium Rising (not the space travel part, but what happened after waking from the dream). I had that first chapter done and then nothing for almost a month. How am I going to move this story forward. I just died.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (86, 23, 1, 'The Useless Crystal', 'The narrator and his son receive a mysterious crystalline object dubbed "Chicken Shit" from an unexplained experiment with the Eternal Engine. Despite days of intense experimentation, the crystal remains completely inert until accidentally discovered to emit NFC signals when placed near a phone, sparking new hope and frustration.', 'What do you do when life gives you chicken shit? You make egg salad sandwiches. At least, that’s what my son said when he tried to pass off Captain Underpants as a legitimate choice for his 8th-grade English book report.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (234, 59, 2, 'Evening Contemplations', 'After putting his son to bed, the narrator and his wife watch the movie Passengers, which echoes themes of time and choice from his earlier reflections. As exhaustion takes hold, the narrator prepares for sleep, curious about what dreams await and whether they will reveal insights about the Mandela Effect.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (173, 47, 4, 'New Theoretical Breakthrough', 'Inspired by the warmth of his conversation with his son, the narrator revisits his undergraduate notes on CPT symmetry and quantum entanglement. He develops a revolutionary theory about manipulating ERB portals using collapsing wave functions and photon origin coordinates to reposition portal endpoints.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (196, 51, 8, 'From Packages to People', 'The narrator reflects on the success of the shipping partnerships and is inspired by a meme about people as packages. He envisions expanding the ERB gateway technology to revolutionize personal transportation, acquiring land near major transportation hubs and beginning construction of a global network.', 'These partnerships ignited a revolution in the industry. The cumbersome process of cross-border shipping was obliterated, replaced by a seamless operation powered by our innovations. Delivery times shattered records, and the giants of logistics quietly became reliant on The S Corp’s technology for their most critical shipments.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (502, 125, 1, 'The Living Room War Zone', 'Stephen arrives home to find his wife violently attacking Xavier over perceived wrongs. A terrifying escalation reveals the wife is no longer human—her eyes contain something wrong, her movements glitching. The confrontation ends in tragedy when she retrieves a gun and, during a struggle, is killed by a falling bookcase.', 'The noise hit me the second I stepped inside.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (477, 119, 4, 'Testing the Loop', 'Stephen spends the day testing his theory that his wife is an NPC by refusing to engage with her scripts. After a failed attempt with flattery and silence, she literally loops—repeating the exact same dialogue—confirming his suspicion.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (482, 120, 1, 'Waking Wrong', 'Stephen wakes in his familiar bed, disoriented by the existence of failed suicide attempts from timelines that no longer exist. He receives a mysterious message from Becca about a wine and cheese event and decides to leave the house despite his wife''s location tracking, driving toward Orlando.', 'I woke up wrong.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (479, 119, 6, 'Connection with Xavier', 'Stephen watches Xavier gaming and connects with him over a real conversation about lore, childhood memories, and the feeling that reality is scripted. A brief memory-flash of a girl in biology class disrupts the moment, suggesting Stephen has other lives or memories bleeding through.', '**********
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (567, 137, 2, 'The Sequel''s Unexpected Genesis', 'The author describes how a second writing challenge without a story idea led them back to The Towers of Elysium world, initially resulting in a depressing trajectory until a literal head kick from their son sparked the concept of revisiting the prison from a different angle. This led to naming the protagonist and developing richer characters.', 'Fast forward then to April 2025 and the AutoCrit 90 day writing challenge. I had no story idea. So I just started writing.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (452, 112, 5, 'The Word That Doesn''t Belong', 'The protagonist speaks the word ''Etheris'' instead of ''Earth,'' triggering deep recognition and alarm. His wife enters with a phone call from someone named Whitney, and suddenly he remembers everything—the truth behind his reality begins to crack.', 'I freeze. My fingers hover over the keyboard.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (191, 51, 3, 'Building the Physical Empire', 'The S Corp begins its global expansion by creating a fleet of autonomous Real Estate Lawyer Machines (RELMs) to acquire properties worldwide. The RELMs discover a prime skyscraper in Houston, Texas, which becomes the company''s new headquarters.', 'With the news of our financials starting to trickle out in the market, people would start talking. Soon the S Corp needed more than financial dominance, it needed a physical presence to embody its influence. The solution? Expanding our footprint into the real world with strategic acquisitions across the globe.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (199, 52, 3, 'The Cosmic Deity and Transformation', 'As the protagonist''s sanity crumbles completely, they encounter the source of the terror - a cosmic deity upon a bone throne. They lose their individuality and merge with the entity, becoming its mindless servant trapped eternally in the cursed temple.', 'As the last shred of my sanity slipped away, I saw it - the source of all this terror and madness. A cosmic deity, its form beyond comprehension, sat upon a throne made of bones. Its mere presence filled me with indescribable dread and awe. It beckoned me closer, I knew that there was no turning back.
INSERT INTO public.scenes VALUES (558, 135, 6, 'Chaotic Breakfast and Ground Rules', 'The family eats breakfast in their Florida home, with Xavier constructing elaborate burritos while discussing how the reshuffling worked to maintain Tiffany''s memories. Stephen establishes ground rules for their mission: no obvious power use, respecting free will, faking deaths periodically, and actually living life rather than just existing.', 'Breakfast was chaos.
